window.INNKEEPER_CHAPTERS=(window.INNKEEPER_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2401,"title":"Chapter 2401: How did it happen?","paragraphs":["For once, the time before the beginning of the next torture cycle was longer than a brief moment, if only to increase the mental torture Lex was going through. The name of the last cycle was Infinity, but it would last for a total of one second.","So then, why was it named as such? It was because within that one second, Lex would be exposed to the absolute and inalienable personification of infinity. Within that one second, he would experience unending time. In theory - at least as Lex understood it - there was no technical end to it. Time would go on forever.","This time, the torture cycle gave him plenty of time to completely fathom what he was about to face, as if pushing him to his very limit. Maybe the trick would be to break out of it somehow, or maybe it would just keep on going until the retribution ran out of energy or...","There were too many possibilities, but all of them were incredibly haunting. This torture cycle, too, was specifically designed to exhausted Lex’ spirit while preserving his body and soul so the parasite could take over his body.","Unfortunately, the parasite had been crushed by Lex’s instincts. Lex himself did not even know the details regarding the parasite, except the feedback he got from his soul about activating his instincts. Though, he also felt something when the parasite appeared, and the name of the torture cycle itself was enough for him to understand what might have happened.","Regardless, that’s how he’d known that there had been a parasite hidden within the necklace, ready to take over his body and soul.","As for the specific details, there was no way Lex could ever learn or even guess them. At the moment, he was not concerned about that at all. Instead, he could not help but laugh. Eternity, but that was it. Finally, Lex could take this moment to rest and recover. Of course, after he recovered his spirit, if he was forced to endure eternity, his mind would become exhausted once more, or maybe he’d just eventually reach a point of wanting to kill himself.","But it was also true that it would give him an endless amount of time to figure things out. He’d find a solution one way or another. When had he ever given up?","Besides, he still had that egg shell waiting for him to absorb, and that ability of his to unlock from the feedback given to him by the Disaster Rose. The Disaster Rose was still slowly channeling its energy into the necklace, and would probably take a couple of decades at this point.","Regardless, Lex was not daunted by the thought of facing Infinity in the least. If anything, knowing about it put him at ease. An infinite rest that actually only lasted 1 second? He could not have asked for anything better.","Of course, he was aware that there were secret, hidden aspects of the torture cycle too. He’d just deal with things as they came.","No sooner had he finished that thought that the torture cycle began. Lex saw endless darkness, all around him, for all of eternity, and a flow of time that didn’t make sense to him.","He furrowed his brows, but before he could figure anything out, a second passed and the torture cycle was over.","What had happened? Neither Lex, nor the Gilded Hollow could understand at all. He had successfully entered the cycle of Infinity, but instead of being exposed to infinity, Lex only felt the regular flow of time. That wasn’t supposed to happen.","Lex was just as surprised as the Hollow, though his disappointment was not as great. He could only think about his plan of resting for a long time reluctantly, as if he was not resigned to giving up his break.","Yet Lex had no time to rest, or regret. Whether he was prepared for it or not, whether he understood how it happened or not, the eight torture cycles were over, and thus he was immediately kicked out of the Hollow!","Though he was kicked out, he did not immediately return. Instead, he seemed to feel like he was undergoing a long range teleportation that wouldn’t be over so soon. Lex furrowed his brows and began to check himself, suspecting that he might be in some kind of illusion. How could the last cycle have finished so soon?","What Lex didn’t realize, or even notice, was a soft, warm light being emitted from the center of his projection’s forehead - exactly where Lex had created a seal on his real body. After a few seconds, the light disappeared, as if nothing had happened at all.","No matter how Lex checked, he could not find any signs of any deceit or illusion. Could this actually be happening, or was the last torture cycle the perfect illusion?","His instincts told him that was not the case, and that he had genuinely survived somehow. It was just that he wasn’t aware of how he had done it.","While he kept wondering, Lex also began thinking about the Nexus event. There were only a few months left before that happened, and he had to make the most of it. But first, a nice, healthy dose of long-awaited revenge. He was going to pay back his stalker for everything he had been through and more - regardless of whether it was the stalker’s fault or not.","When Lex disappeared, the corpse sitting in the ruins that had been ’watching’ him did not move. How could it? It was dead. But soon enough, a figure appeared in front of the corpse, and then looked in the direction he was looking at. There was nothing there.","The figure studied the corpse a little more, but upon being unable to discover anything of value, the figure moved on without a word.","Elsewhere in the Hollow, Romulus felt Lex’s energy leave, and he couldn’t help but curse. He knew that human would be okay, one way or another - he was the one who needed some serious help."]},{"number":2402,"title":"Chapter 2402: The way of rumors","paragraphs":["The obelisk. Velma looked at the obelisk with impassive eyes, unimpressed and unaffected by the alluring lies it told. She knew many of its secrets already. Even if she didn’t have access to an information database of the Humanoid Alliance, just by looking at it with her eyes she would have learned most of its secrets.","She couldn’t pry into its deeper secrets, naturally, but the surface level secrets were all bare for her to see. Besides, how could she hear lies and not recognize them? Velma was completely unaffected by Obelisk’s lies, and passed her Spirit tribulation with frightening ease.","When her tribulation ended, she returned to her location looking completely unbothered. Her armor had suffered not a single scratch by her Major tribulation, despite the fact that she had just endured a Major tribulation to enter the Celestial Immortal realm!","Her rise had been meteoric, to say the very least. To be specific, her rise began the moment she heard about Z getting kidnapped. She faced almost no obstacles in her cultivation, not just because her mastery of laws related to rumors and information was so frighteningly high, but also because of how in sync she was with her tenet.","In fact, her mastery over her tenet was so advanced that the very moment she entered the Celestial Immortal realm, she felt like she could continue to climb the ranks, but now was not the time. After all, she wasn’t alone.","All around her, countless members of the Humanoid Alliance stood looking extremely uncomfortable. Though they all held weapons in their hands, they held them loosely, as if they were looking for a reason to drop them.","How could they not? Which one of them was not close friends with Velma? Which of them had not cried their hearts out to her, and which of them had not sought her out for guidance. Which of them had not...","Thus, not a single one of them wanted to face her here, like this. But the situation was... unusual.","Not an ounce of emotion flickered through Velma’s as her gaze swept across them, and focused on the one Celestial who she had been working with so far - Ur Weiss.","Ur was, for all intents and purposes, a very good boss to work for. He had also helped build a very positive impression of Celestial Immortals for Velma - present circumstances not withstanding.","It was unfortunate, then, that they had reached such an impasse.","The armor she wore - made entirely out of a type of golden silk that was rare beyond rare - was gifted to her by Ur. Though the intentions had not been made clear at the time, she understood that the gift was his request that she keep working for her, and a subtle confession that he had developed feelings for her.","Velma was not impressed, to be honest, but she politely accepted the gift back then. She was used to people falling in love with her, so that a Celestial would do the same did not surprise her at all.","\"Velma, I have told you time and time again - we knew nothing of the attack,\" Ur spoke with a voice filled with endless patience. \"I don’t even need to tell you! You can see it with your very own eyes. We knew nothing of it, and we’re doing our best to remedy the situation!\"","What Ur said was the truth. Velma’s mastery over her tenet was at such an extreme that her tenet alone granted her powers, allowing her to hear the secrets of whoever she looked at, see them, know them. Naturally, she was not powerful enough to learn all secrets, but it also wasn’t easy to hide things from her, especially now that she had reached the Celestial Immortal realm.","\"Your best? Will your best bring Z back to life if something happens to him? Or will your best punish those who ordered the attack?\" she asked, her voice so strongly filled with an iciness that those who heard it shivered.","Ur did not respond, because this was the very issue that they had been arguing over for so long already.","\"Velma, this can still be managed. I can protect you. I can-\"","Finally, a hint of emotion appeared on Velma’s face, and it was that of amusement.","\"You? Protect me? You cannot even protect yourself. Mark my words Ur, the Humanoid Alliance will forever regret its actions. The only thing left for you to do now is decide - decide whether you want to waste the last of the favor you have with me trying to stop me, or will you stand aside and let me pass.\"","Ur took a deep breath, feeling somewhat disappointed with how the conversation was going. Even now, though, he remained entirely composed as he looked at Velma - such was the confidence of a Celestial. She would see reason - she had to.","\"Velma, you used your position to steal confidential information from the Humanoid Alliance. As long as you stay here, I can give you the clearance for that information as my special assistant, but if you try to leave you will automatically be deemed a criminal. We’ve had a long, fruitful cooperation so far. There’s no need to end things on such a note.\"","Velma shook her head, all emotions once again disappearing from her expression.","\"Make your decision Ur. Will you attempt to stop me, or will you make the wise choice,\" she said, before she began to walk forward.","Ur grit his teeth, and made the difficult decision to detain her first. He did not want Velma to be branded a criminal - if that happened, it would be too difficult to redeem her. He needed to offend her a little, if only for her own good.","He made a move, but his every action was laid bare in front of Velma. She not only saw his intentions, but she saw the finer details of how he weaved his laws, so much so that she knew exactly how to break his Lawcraft. She did not even need to attack - she simply waved a finger, shifted a law and his Lawcraft broke before it could even be launched.","That simple exchange was what triggered the chaos. It wasn’t that everyone attacked Velma, nay. Instead, the dwarf standing on the side heard a whisper in his ear about the person who had stolen his family’s brew recipe. An elf heard the name of the perpetrator who burned his forest. An Oolin heard the name of the person who slept with his girlfriend. An Angel heard about a lover who was only with them on a dare, and a Devil learned about a groupchat dedicated to making fun of him.","One after another, secrets were revealed and spread across not just the room, but the entire alliance building. With the war going on, and the situation tense, Velma knew exactly where all the Dao Lords were, and what it would take to attract their attention, and this wasn’t it.","By the time Ur recovered what he saw was madness. All his workers were fighting, but they were not fighting Velma. Instead, they were fighting each other as if they had encountered their worst enemy!","Not only had she revealed their secrets to the ones they were trying to hide them from, she also spread them across the base, thoroughly humiliating them. If they could have pretended previously that their honor wasn’t marred, and that they weren’t humiliated, now they had to deal with the fact that everyone knew.","Everyone knew their deep, dark secrets, their humiliating moments, moments of weakness, and everything they wished to hide.","Many of them were immediately triggered, unable to control themselves as they attacked whoever had betrayed them. Others had no choice to defend themselves as they were attacked. Others still acted only because if they didn’t, they would lose all face! They had to make it seem like they were fighting to reclaim any lost honor or get revenge for whatever wrong they had suffered.","Ur was shocked. It had been a second - no, not even a second. How had she...","The formation in the room that was preventing Velma from accessing her tavern shut down, and when he looked over he saw that all she had done was give it a simple kick.","Velma Nyxheart turned to look at Ur in the eyes one last time. Working for the Humanoid Alliance had actually been a genuinely educational and insightful experience. This last lesson they taught her, too, was one she would remember for a long time.","Ur tried to stop her, but discovered to his abject horror that his body was filled with a strange, pink energy he had never noticed before. The energy in his body was being guided by the pink energy in completely random and chaotic ways, entirely beyond his control.","Such was the way of rumors. They would take on a life of their own, growing and spreading far beyond what anyone could control. Ur was learning that through his own body.","By the time he looked back up, she was gone.","Velma returned to the Midnight Inn, garbed in her golden armor that made her appear more angelic than even angels, and more fearsome than warriors and soldiers who had lived entirely on the battlefield.","She wasted no time in taking control of the House she had founded and spreading out her orders.","\"I have uncovered the details of the conspiracy behind why Z was captured, and the location of the realm of the one known as the Grand Conqueror. Ready the Midnight Battalion. He has been away for long enough - it’s time to bring him back.\""]},{"number":2403,"title":"Chapter 2403: The Nyxheart I","paragraphs":["A meeting was called including all the senior and upper level managers and members of the Midnight Inn. That naturally included the usual faces, such as Luthor, Gerard, Velma, Anita and so forth, but also a lot of the newer members of the Inn who had received promotions in the past few years.","The topic of this meeting was incredibly serious, which is why they all sat in silence, waiting to be briefed. Velma, however, could plainly see the hints of curiosity wafting from Gerard and a few other of the older members as they looked at her. They didn’t need to ask - she would explain everything on her own.","\"I’ll start from the beginning so that there is no confusion,\" said Velma as she addressed the room. \"From the moment I learned that Z had been kidnapped, I began to focus on using the Humanoid Alliances information database to locate him or any information about him. At first, my only motive was to leverage the alliance’s massive size and network. However, it was not long before I discovered that the kidnapping had been orchestrated, from the very beginning, by an anti-Midnight Inn faction of the Humanoid Alliance itself!","\"Officially, these actions had been conducted in secret and went against the larger agenda of the alliance, so the perpetrators were given what I can only call a token punishment. Moreover, the punishment wasn’t because Z had been kidnapped, but because their actions would make it more difficult for the alliance to form agreements with the Inn in the future. Z himself never came within their considerations at all.\"","She took a moment at this point, and sighed.","\"From that moment on I realized that I could no longer trust any organization other than the Midnight Inn, and formulated a plan to get any and all information on Z before leaving the alliance. For this, specifically, my tenet played an immense role, and it’s also the reason why I was able to reach the Celestial realm so easily.","\"You see, back when I became an immortal, I created my tenet on a whim. It’s not something as simple as gossip, or rumors, or gathering secrets. My tenet is... a concept I came up with on my own. It involves wanting to hear the most interesting gossip and learn the most incredible secrets, but I also don’t want to be malicious and steal people’s secrets that they don’t want to share.","\"Thus, my one, single tenet involves the concept of learning information, but only the things people want to share. In fact, after sharing, they feel much better about it, as if a burden has been lifted from their hearts.","\"Well, that was the original concept of my tenet, and over the years of using it, my understanding and application of my own tenet became so advanced that it kept growing. While the original core of the tenet has remained the same, what I can do with it has advanced so much that my cultivation journey seems to have deviated from everyone else’s.","\"Normal humans use their tenets to manipulate laws. I, on the other hand, simply apply and use aspects of my tenet, and the tenet itself manipulates the most optimal laws to achieve what I want. It has grown to the point where I can no longer be constrained by the original limitations of my tenet.","\"So, naturally, I used my tenet to find information about Z. I reversed the order, no longer looking for information that others wanted to share so that they would not be harmed, but looking for information others were hiding to harm my interests. In doing so, I learned the truth about what happened to Z, all the finer details. At the same time, my tenet grew so much that I was able to elevate my cultivation to this level.","\"Previously, I was always suppressing my level since I’ve heard growing too fast wasn’t good for you. Now, that’s no longer a concern I’m worried about. The reason I’m sharing all these details with you... is because none of this was taught inside the Temple of Fasting. It’s almost as if the Temple itself is unaware of this method of cultivation. I hope that by sharing this with you all, I can help you move forward on your cultivation path and grow stronger. Everyone of us needs to grow stronger, because in this universe, when you start trusting others to protect your interests, you make yourself vulnerable to them as well!\"","Everyone paused, and could not help but marvel at Velma, who seemed to have created a whole new path for human cultivation out of sheer compatibility with her own tenet! That was incredible. Also, it was a reminder that while many cultivation paths already existed, that did not mean that there couldn’t be more or better ways.","\"Another reason I told you all this was so that, moving forward, we’re on the same page to avoid any confusion or misunderstandings. During the time while I was at the alliance, I already planned out everything, from the method of our attack, information about the enemy, how we will rescue Z and more.","\"However, this is not a mission that has been sanctioned by the Innkeeper. I have been unable to contact him and ask for permission, so everyone needs to make a choice whether to participate in my plan or not for themselves. I will, of course, shoulder all responsibility for this mission, but I cannot, in good conscience, force anyone to act alongside me.","\"Please, make up your own mind about what you want to do. I will sincerely apologise to the Innkeeper for acting without his permission, but I believe he will not blame me for this. We have seen, from the very beginning, that the Innkeeper has always been very protective of us. I believe that this is exactly the kind of thing he would want to see from us - protecting one another in his absence, so that he can carry out his own work without having to worry about us.\"","Velma was prepared to give everyone time to ponder over what to do, but as soon as she was done speaking, Gerard put a hand on her shoulder and looked at her fondly.","\"You have endured much alone for the sake of the Inn, but this is not a burden you need to carry alone. We will all help. Just tell us what to do.\"","Velma looked around and found that there was not a single look of doubt or hesitation in the room. None could keep secrets from her eyes, so if they were only acting but secretly begrudged her for putting them in this position, she’d know. Yet, as always, the members of the Inn were extremely united, especially when it came to their resolve to protect one another."]},{"number":2404,"title":"Chapter 2404: The Nyxheart II","paragraphs":["Finally, after countless weeks, Velma’s icy expression finally broke, and a warm smile could not help but appear on her face. There really was no place like home.","She took a deep breath, and immediately began to reveal the contents of her plan.","\"The rescue operation consists of four phases - and yes, it’s important to remember that this is a rescue operation, not a revenge operation! The first phase is preparation. We cannot just get up and go because we know the destination. We need to properly equip ourselves, not to mention we need to mobilise our allies for a coordinated attack.\"","Velma created a projection in front of the members of a large realm, including its terrain, key features, population, defensive positions and so on.","\"This is the layout of the realm controlled by the person who kidnapped Z, known as the Grand Conqueror, based on reconnaissance carried out by certain members of the alliance. While they have not been able to firmly locate the realm, I have already discovered a method for us to enter it.\"","She pulled out an entire list of Devils who had made deals with not just the Grand Conqueror, but other members of the realm as well. It seemed like the concept of quickly gaining strength through external means was a common theme within this realm.","\"Devils are notorious for not betraying their deals, but that also doesn’t prevent them from making new deals. Making a deal with them is not hard at all. For a long time, Devils were the largest demographic inside the Inn, and I know most of them.","\"I already have over a hundred Devils who have infiltrated the realm on my behalf, making deals with the residents while also ready to smuggle in the Snowglobe tavern at my command. I have also, using information as payment, requisitioned a battalion of 300 million demons who will attack across the realm at the same time as us to serve as a distraction.\"","A stunned silence filled the room as everyone listened, and tried to comprehend the words Velma had spoken. 300 million demons? To attack alongside them? Was Velma herself aware that this was a rescue and not a plot for revenge?","\"Do not be swayed by that paltry number,\" said Velma, picking up on the fact that everyone was stunned by her preparations. \"We are attacking an entire realm - one that is constantly preparing for war. Their armies, while consisting mostly of mortals and low level immortals, stand in the billions. These demons really are nothing more than a distraction. A battle between realms is nothing like normal battles.\"","The simple and direct words from Velma stunned most, for although they conceptually knew how vast realms were, they had never considered what it meant to raid a realm to rescue Z.","\"I have also made a tentative list of powers and forces we can galvanize to help us during this attack,\" Velma continued as she pulled up a large list. A mere glance was all it took for Gerard to recognize that most of these forces were from the Origin realm, and had a strong and positive relationship with the Midnight Inn. The Jotun Empire and the Iron Heart pirates were examples of just a few, though Gerard did not feel like the pirates were strong enough to take part in this endeavor. Maybe there was something Velma knew that he didn’t.","\"I’ve also devised a number of ways in which we can quickly strengthen a number of our workers using some of the practices the alliance employs. Oh, and I have a small gift for you Gerard,\" she said, before raising her right hand.","Nothing immediately appeared within her hand, but the strained expression on her face revealed that she was putting quite a bit of effort into summoning whatever it is she was talking about. A few seconds later, however, beads of deep red blood began leaking from her nails and gathering into a ball floating above her hand, terrifying a lot of people.","\"What are you doing?\" demanded Nurse Jubilation as she rushed up to Velma.","Velma, in turn, did not respond until the ball of blood was as big as a snooker ball.","\"The Regalia Bloom bloodline,\" she said in a somewhat exhausted tone. \"It is no longer useful for me at all, and is just a waste for me to have. So I thought I’d give mine to you. You always were the best at utilizing the bloodline.\"","She spoke, she encased the ball of blood in a glass orb and tossed it to Gerard. What she had summoned was not actual blood, but the very core of the bloodline that was bound to her body. She had not lied when she said it was not useful for her, because she intended on forming her own bloodline based on her tenet.","She had even thought of the name for the new bloodline she was going to form. It was going to be called Nyxheart. For some odd reason, ever since she entered the Celestial realm, she got a strong feeling that she needed to continue to enhance her tenet, as well as clearly define its power and limitations.","\"Anyway, preparation and infiltration are the first two phases,\" Velma continued to speak, turning her attention back to the matter at hand. \"The third, and actually difficult phase, is the rescue itself. Getting current and reliable information from within the realm is actually quite difficult so...\"","Velma continued to elaborate her plan to the rest of them as she broke down everything they were going to do. The Midnight Inn... was going to war. The last time they did something like this was when Lex needed help rescuing his sister in the Origin realm. Now... their capabilities were far more terrifying.","Somewhere far away, on the other side of the universe, Lex finally finished teleporting out of the Gilded Hollow. Yet he did not return to the palace he had entered the realm from. Instead, he appeared in a room, sitting in a chesterfield that looked far too familiar. Also, why was he wearing a velvet coat and a wooden pipe? Hey wait a minute, the smoke from the pipe actually smelled quite nice.","Wait a minute, wasn’t this the place from that vision he saw of himself? The one where he...","\"Ah child, I must thank you. After witnessing the death of a universe, I feared I would never feel normal emotions ever again. Who could have predicted that I would run into you, and rediscover the feeling of anxiety?\""]},{"number":2405,"title":"Chapter 2405: Doppelganger","paragraphs":["Lex followed the strangely familiar voice - the very same voice that had told him to exit the Hollow before the Nexus started - and found sitting opposite to himself was... himself?","Lex started at the dashingly handsome Lex, wearing a purple velvet coat with a yellow ascot with purple polka dots. He had a wooden pipe in his right hand as he sat comfortably in a chesterfield, and near his left hand was a smooth, black cane with an ivory known in the shape of grandfather clock.","He was wearing cufflinks in the shape of an hour glass, which was very on brand with the time based theme that seemed to be going on.","Lex looked away from the other Lex and studied the room, and found that they were sitting in a corner of a library - one that was absolutely filled to the brim with books.","\"I find reading is a great pastime,\" the Lex with the cane spoke, commenting on his library that he seemed to be quite proud of. \"It’s also quite educational, so it’s a two for one kind of deal. Not bad, eh?\"","Lex blinked, and then turned his gaze back to his doppelganger.","\"What was it that you said about helping you rediscover anxiety, again? Oh and, I’m terribly sorry about this, but your name seems to have slipped my mind.\"","Doppelganger-Lex chuckled upon hearing genuine-Lex’s words, entirely unbothered by them.","\"Actually, we never actually got around to sharing my name with you. The consensus we reached the last time we met was that you’d be much safer if you know as little about me as possible. That’s the reason I am appearing to you like this - it’s safer for both of us that way.","\"We did, however, reach a small agreement. Unfortunately, due to the dangers posed by the exact details of the agreement, we also agreed to seal your memory about it until such a time that you need to act upon the agreement.\"","Real-Lex nodded, as if everything doppelganger-Lex had said was entirely reasonable, and was exactly how he would act.","The doppelganger, though, naturally saw through Lex’s reservations. He was not causing any issues because he was convinced that the fake was a Dao Lord, and so even if the fake Lex said that lightning was wet and pizza was icecream, Lex would not argue.","\"You do not need to be concerned too much with safety when it comes to me. In fact, among the terms of our agreement, one of the terms is that I need to actively protect you from any and all time related anomalies that you may encounter.","\"I, naturally, agreed, but at the same time I did not want you to abuse our relationship, and so you agreed to accept a time related inhibition which would instinctually inhibit you from learning or experimenting with time related laws. I even helped you a bit in your last torture cycles. See, we’re on the same side.\"","Real-Lex nodded reluctantly, as if accepting that answer.","\"So what was the reason I was causing you so much anxiety again?\" asked Lex.","The doppelganger-Lex sighed.","\"You see, Lex, we agreed on a number of terms, not just one or two. The reason we did so was because I have been trapped in this book called the Fable of Time for far too long. The book is designed so others cannot find it at all, but somehow you bypassed that restriction. I had no choice but to make a deal with you, but in exchange, I also offered you many benefits which you agreed to accept.","\"The thing is, while I have many other powers, I lack the ability to see the future. Thus, not even in my wildest dreams could I have imagined all the extreme and creative ways in which you regularly almost get yourself killed. Sealing your memories was also to avoid putting any pressure on you.","\"If you die, I would likely need to spend another unknown number of years before an anomaly like you can find the Fable of Time. Or if that Sovereign discovers the seal in your forehead and opens it, everything will be ruined. Or if you...\"","The Doppelganger-Lex was getting worked up as he spoke, but then caught himself and just sighed, shaking his head. For some reason, real-Lex actually felt kind of guilty, feeling bad for stressing out doppelganger-Lex. Then again, it wasn’t like any of that had been on purpose - or that Lex had known about it.","\"So you’ve been sealed inside my forehead all this time?\" Lex asked, quite a few concerns rising up.","The doppelganger nodded, and then hopped up off his chesterfield and motioned Lex to follow.","\"Yes, I have. I told you as much before I took residence there. Since we were establishing a cooperative relationship, you clearly felt the need to establish some boundaries so that I don’t spy on you while I was staying there. But I couldn’t avoid monitoring you and watching out for time related dangers at the same time, so you came up with a number of guidelines. Here they are, feel free to peruse them yourself.\"","Doppelganger-Lex brought the real one to a dedicated library shelf which was filled with books, kind of like the volumes to old encyclopedias. They were bound with matching covers, all titled: Rules for living in Lex’s Body I, II, III, IV and so on.","The entire cabinet was filled, from top to bottom, with such books.","\"You spent almost three weeks writing these down. I must say, you were quite thorough considering the limited time. I, naturally, found some loopholes you left behind, but in the spirit of honest cooperation, I did not use them and adhered to the intention behind these restrictions rather than abusing their ultimate flaws.\"","Lex was... somewhat astounded. He had worked with quite a number of Dao Lords before. All he could say was that they all had unique personalities. Yes, very unique.","\"Any way, I realize that you wanted to use that previous torture cycle to rest up, but you may as well use this place to relax and recover a bit. Time flow here is so slow it’s basically not moving at all. When you feel you’re recovered, we can discuss your latest situation.\"","Lex raised an eyebrow and looked at the doppelganger-Lex.","\"My latest situation? What’s that? I should have exited the Gilded Hollow, so I shouldn’t be in any danger,\" he said, trying to recall if he had forgotten something important. Considering his own history of apparently keeping secrets even from himself, who knew what he’d forgotten."]},{"number":2406,"title":"Chapter 2406: Lex’s Heart Demon","paragraphs":["\"Getting directly into the thick of things, I like it,\" said the doppelganger-Lex with a nod. \"Although, I suppose it’s completely natural to be curious about the latest death threat on one’s life. You sir, are behaving completely as one normally should.\"","Real-Lex stared at his doppelganger, unsure of how to respond to that statement.","\"Uh, thank... you?\" he said awkwardly, to which his doppelganger simply nodded.","\"Excuse me if my conversational etiquette isn’t what it used to be,\" said the doppelganger as he began leading Lex deeper into the library. \"I’ve been quite alone for many years now, and the only conversations I’ve encountered are the ones from my books. But I have no way of gauging whether those are even coherent, or appropriate talking patterns in this day and age.\"","Made sense, at least to real-Lex.","They walked into an open area of the library with a large table and a coffee bar. Doppelganger-Lex slipped behind a coffee machine and began to brew some locally grown galactic super coffee - or at least that’s what Lex decided to call it after smelling it.","\"Due to the extensive rules you laid down, I’ve been careful to avoid watching you during your specifically decided private moments. But, as it turned out, meeting your parents didn’t count as one of those according to the guidelines, as well as the spirit of the agreement.","\"Regardless, I remember you had a small conversation with your mother about Dao Bodies - do you remember? I am talking about the conversation where she told you that a Dao Body’s tribulation happens once every thousand years. You remember it now?\"","Real-Lex nodded, showing no expression about whether the conversation bothered him or not.","\"Are you saying I’m about to face a Dao Body tribulation? It’s not been anywhere close to a thousand years since I started,\" said Lex dismissively.","The doppelganger-Lex nodded to agree, but with an incredibly exasperated expression on his face.","\"Do you know that I am exceptionally adept at the laws of time, but the law of time in this universe is exceedingly irritating at times. The ruling law of this universe is Chronos - meaning linear time. That in itself is quite irritating for me, but what’s happened with you is yet another reason I don’t like it.","\"A common belief dictates that if a person has a clone, and they both experience the same amount of time, that should not double their age. Technically, they have been alive the same amount of time, even if the clone means they experience that same time twice. The name linear time also insinuates such a thing.","\"Unfortunately, the reality of the situation is quite different. A clone means that the amount of time you’re being exposed to, for a set unit of time, is actually doubled since both clones are independently experiencing linear time. Now, since my book is sealed inside your forehead, and your body is actually your soul, my book is present in everyone of your clones.","\"That means you, Jack, and the necklace are all experiencing time individually, but according to the universe the amount of time you’re experiencing has tripled. By my estimate, the time you’ve endured is nowhere near a thousand years even when tripled.","\"Although we have to take note that due to various different flows of time, the accumulated amount of time experienced in a set unit of time according to a Mature realm is not always tripled, but may in fact be more! Anyway, at some point, you crossed a threshold to experience a Dao Body tribulation.","\"I don’t know why the time period you have between Dao body tribulations is shorter than regular, but that’s the case. However, since a part of you was inside the Gilded Hollow, the Dao Body tribulation was being blocked from happening. Unfortunately, now that you’re out, that’s no longer the case.","\"Thus, the moment you leave this place, you will trigger the Dao Body tribulation. As for what will happen when that occurs, I cannot say. However, this Dao Body tribulation... is a problem.\"","Lex heard everything, but at the same time he blanked out, unable to process what the doppelganger was saying. He almost developed a heart demon!","He was experiencing time at a tripled rate? But... he was only 26. No, how could this happen? He was... just turned 26. He couldn’t be older. The doppelganger must be mistaken. No wait, the universe was the one that decided he was ready for the test. The universe must be mistaken! These kinds of things can only be expected from an immature, incomplete universe. Yes, that’s it.","The build up to the Heart Demon disappeared.","Now that he finally recovered from the mental shock of what he heard, he could focus on the rest of what the doppelganger said.","\"A Dao Body tribulation? You think that thing will kill me?\" Lex asked, looking at his doppelganger.","The other Lex puffed his pipe a bit before answering, as if to calm his nerves.","\"Honestly, I don’t know. It should , at the very least, put you out of commission for a while even if it doesn’t kill you. But even that’s not the point. A normal Dao Body tribulation can last for years, and you don’t have that kind of time. You see, the time for you to keep your end of your bargain is coming up.\"","Lex raised an eyebrow, as if that in itself was enough to express his question.","\"Don’t worry about it - the task is something you’re completely capable of doing, otherwise you would not have agreed to it. The problem is, if the tribulation begins, you’ll be occupied for months, and you’ll miss the build up to the Nexus event. I’m sure you have your own plans for that as well. So it’s in our best interest to do something about it.\"","Lex furrowed his brows, considering everything his doppelganger told him. To be honest, he wasn’t sure how much he trusted this handsome fellow, but he was used to it.","Lex had an uncanny habit of getting involved with people far beyond his level. Whether it was Ballom, Nuwa, Eclipse, Romulus, Wu Kong or any of the other Dao Lords he encountered regularly, any one of them held his entire fate in their hands. He could not resist at all, so he didn’t bother with it either.","Instead, he just chose to believe whatever the doppelganger told him, regardless of how likely he thought it actually was.","\"I take it that you have some kind of plan for this,\" said real-Lex as he waited for the doppelganger to respond. This was a very serious matter, for he really did have plans leading up to the Nexus event."]},{"number":2407,"title":"Chapter 2407: Dao Body tribulation","paragraphs":["\"Actually, I have a dozen or so plans and proposals regarding how to face this situation, but we really need to sit and talk through which one of them to implement. After all, the plan that is most ideal for me is not necessarily the most ideal plan for you,\" said the doppelganger Lex.","Real-Lex suddenly understood why his doppelganger wanted him to get some rest first. This might take a while. The one benefit, at least, was that the doppelganger seemed to have spoken the truth about the flow of time. His connection to Jack wasn’t cut off, which is why he could sense that the entire time he had been here, not a second had passed for Jack.","Although, he could not help but wonder if that was a feature of this place in general, or if his doppelganger had made it so for their meeting.","The doppelganger took a seat, laying his cane beside him as he took a deep puff from his pipe.","\"The most effective and practical solution I have is to affect your time, and make it so that the Dao Body tribulation will occur after the Nexus event. However, if I do that, the tribulation will only become more difficult for you to overcome. On the surface, that’s a good thing for me because you’ll have completed most of your end of the bargain, and if you die I won’t need to fulfil my end.","\"However, I am a being of honor. I would not compromise you for my own personal gain if we have a standing agreement. That is why I said, make yourself comfortable. Relax, recover, and once you’re in the right frame of mind, we can tackle this issue properly. Maybe we can even figure out why your Dao Body tribulation came early.\"","Lex did not respond, though he had a pretty decent idea of why it came early. He hadn’t noticed at first, but ever since his Dao Body reached 51% he’d noticed how it was making itself apparent in his spirit and soul. The issue with his Dao Intentions hadn’t occurred, mainly because he was living as a necklace and not as a proper human, so he hadn’t been relying on his tenet.","More important than that, however, was the fact that the Dao Body and his Primordial aura seemed to be in perfect harmony. Since it was, in fact, his entire being that was being converted, he theorized that his Dao Body and Primordial aura were fusing.","At this point, he didn’t even want to call it Dao Body anymore - calling it Primordial Dao Being might be more accurate. But this was firmly heading into unfamiliar territory, and it would be best not to make claims he did not even understand.","The point was that Lex suspected that it was the Primordial nature of his Dao Body which had triggered a premature Dao Body tribulation. Since it was already here, it was more important to figure out what he’d be facing rather than dwelling on the how or why.","\"Do you know what I can expect in a Dao Body tribulation? And what delaying it will do it to?\" the real Lex asked.","In truth, he’d done his own research on the topic, but it couldn’t hurt to ask. This fake version of himself seemed quite knowledgeable, at least based on the number of books in the library.","\"In truth, a Dao Body tribulation is actually not so frightening,\" doppelganger-Lex said. \"Although Dao Bodies are not common, based on the records I’ve read, most don’t face any serious issues in their first 10 or 20 Dao Body tribulations. Considering that these tribulations come at fixed internals until the Dao Body is complete, I think Dao Body tribulations are more like check marks to be able to determine how great your progress is. The truly difficult trial is the Fate tribulation you will face as your Dao Body moves from 99% to 100%.\"","All of this was something Lex already knew, but he couldn’t take the information at face value because his situation was unique. While others may face a relatively safe tribulation, he had no way of knowing how difficult his own would be.","\"The specific details, as far as I know, of the Dao Body tribulation are quite interesting actually. The recipients of the tribulation all live through the same scene which many historians think is a recreation of a certain, significant event. There are no records of the event, though.","\"All in all, you’ll be faced with a behemoth of a race that is no longer known, and during your first tribulation it will strike you once. During your second, it will strike you twice, and so on and so forth. If your Dao Body is sufficiently strong, you’ll survive, or else you’ll die, for that creature’s every strike carries with it a subtle Dao aura.","\"While in theory this is easy and straightforward, it’s an extremely time consuming process, not only because of the grave injuries you’re likely to carry afterwards, but also because of the feedback from the tribulation. Being occupied for years or even decades afterwards is completely normal.\"","Lex looked at his doppelganger, and was tempted to ask some personal questions, but then decided against it. The copy had already told him it was best for Lex to know as little about him as possible, so it wouldn’t do to ask questions. Otherwise he was going to ask if the copy really didn’t know about the event that happens in the tribulations.","After all, he seemed to be very old, and have some kind of relation with time.","But, for his own health, he moved on. Others may have a safe tribulation, but the same could not be said for himself. Delaying it might really be the best option, but...","\"How much more dangerous will the tribulation be if it’s delayed?\" the real Lex asked.","The doppelganger puffed for a while without answering, as if he too were calculating the result.","\"Depends on the amount of time. Considering we’d be delaying it for months, I think the tribulation would become absolutely lethal. That is why I have other suggestions prepared as well.\"","Lex, however, was not intimidated by the news.","\"You said the tribulation is a test for how developed the Dao Body is. What percentage do you think is safe for the first tribulation if it’s delayed?\"","While Lex remained relaxed, the doppelganger was not. In fact, the very same anxiety he had mentioned earlier began to return as he regretted even mentioning delaying the tribulation. That was only meant to be a bad example to make other alternatives look good, so why was Lex focusing all his attention on it?"]},{"number":2408,"title":"Chapter 2408: Morrow","paragraphs":["Despite whatever feelings he felt inside, the doppelganger did not reveal it externally. Instead, he thought about the real-Lex’s answer for a moment before answering.","\"There’s no fixed percentage, but generally speaking, I think everyone who usually takes the Body Tribulation is around 5% during their first tribulation. If we account for the increase you may face for delaying it, a safe percentage would be around 20%.","\"But you need to understand, it’s not as simple as surviving a difficult tribulation once. If you do this, then every subsequent tribulation you experience will kick off from the same level as the one you experienced last. In short, you’d be making your own future tribulations permanently more difficult, and reducing the amount of time you have to reach the peak.\"","Real-Lex nodded, but internally he was thinking of something else. This doppelganger... something was off about him. Not in the sense that he was trying to fool Lex or conspire against him, but that his emotions were... easy to sense.","He didn’t think too much into it. Instead, he focused on his tribulation. Even if it was harder than normal, and the current safety net was at 20%, then even if he doubled it, it would at most reach 40%. With a 51% Dao Body, Lex felt like he’d be safe.","Lex was not as averse to this option as his doppelganger expected, but it would be foolish to decide when he hadn’t heard all his options. So, after sufficiently deliberating on this option, Lex began to discuss his other options with his doppelganger.","He felt no rush either, delving into detail about each possible plan. Unfortunately, the option to allow Lex to experience the tribulation then bring him inside the book so that he could finish processing the result within this flow of time was not possible.","Allowing Lex to enter and exit the Fable of Time, which is where they were, wasn’t so easy. It required them to rely on certain conditions that the doppelganger could not recreate on his own. Traveling out of the Hollow just incidentally fulfilled those requirements which is why he had been able to intervene.","After several hours of discussion, Lex decided to get some rest. He didn’t sleep, but he got about as close to sleeping as he possibly could as a necklace. He entered a state of deep meditation, cycling through his cultivation technique as he recovered his spirit and stabilised the space within the necklace.","His strength had reached a whole new level now, and Lex couldn’t wait to have a faceoff against his stalker. Then he could finally return to the Inn and relax for a bit.","Knowing his luck, he’d get sucked into some universe-wide plot of some kind, but at least it was nice to imagine returning home to the Inn. It had been far too long since he’d returned.","Of course, if Daekol had done something to his body by this point...","Lex did not dwell on such a thought. He’d deal with things as they came. Besides, even if the shield around his body broke, getting something from his body wasn’t all that simple or easy. Lex’s cultivation technique was unique - getting anything from his body or soul would require far more effort than his stalker would have expected.","Once Lex was thoroughly recovered, he checked his condition and then made up his mind. Many of the alternatives his doppelganger presented him were much safer than delaying the tribulation, but they came with considerable drawbacks.","To others, the drawback of a more difficult tribulation would be the most significant one, but that wasn’t the case for Lex. With that, he made his decision. Now it would be up to his doppelganger to actually make such a seemingly impossible thing happen.","\"I must say, you’re still very much on theme with giving me intense anxiety,\" said the doppelganger, though his tone was relaxed and somewhat amused. \"I never even imagined that this was the option you would pick, even if it was my idea to begin with. But, since we have reached an agreement, I will honor it. Are you sure you don’t want to stay longer?\"","Lex shook his head.","\"I have too many things I need to do. I have already thoroughly prepared for them to the extent of my abilities, and spending more time won’t meaningfully increase my strength or ability to handle them. In that case, waiting around will just be delaying things unnecessarily, I won’t be able to truly relax. I’d rather leave and get things done. What do I need to do to delay the tribulation?\"","The doppelganger took a deep puff, and then shook his head.","\"You don’t need to do anything. I’ll take care of everything. Once you leave from here, the Dao Body tribulation won’t trigger. I suspect you’re on the verge of a Major tribulation, though, and you should be able to suppress that on your own.\"","Lex nodded. He could feel that he was on the verge of triggering a tribulation to enter the Celestial Immortal realm. He could likely delay it until he returned to his main body, but no more. He was already pushing the limit of what a Heaven Immortal should be able to do in every sense, and that was before having access to his main body.","Regardless of anything else, even if the necklace could allow him to show great strength, it could not replace that his main body was the core of his being. No matter what, his greatest strength would always come from it. Once the necklace returned to his main body...","Lex narrowed his eyes in anticipation of that moment. With nothing else left to say, the doppelganger waved goodbye to Lex, and then sent him away.","Lex disappeared, and for a few moments the doppelganger remained the same. Then, however, his appearance changed to that of a scruffy looking teenager who immediately fell to his knees as if he was extremely drained or exhausted.","\"Are you alright, master?\" asked the cane with the grandfather-clock shaped handle as it floated up beside him.","The teenager looked up, and though his body was trembling and his skin was pale, his expression was that of utter excitement!","\"We did it, Morrow. I think we managed to fool him,\" the teenager said as he grabbed the cane and with wobbling hands used it to help himself stand up. \"That was so cool, wasn’t it! That was actually Lex, the Bulldozer, Williams! In our library! Ah, I was so tempted to ask him for his autograph!\"","The cane, also known as Morrow, looked at the teenager with an exhausted expression and resisted the urge to sigh. He failed."]},{"number":2409,"title":"Chapter 2409: Good to be back","paragraphs":["Instead of continuing to worry about the hopeless child, Morrow channeled some of his energy into James. The exhaustion the cane felt wasn’t only mental - it was a very literal exhaustion caused from using up a tremendous amount of power to delay Lex’s Dao Body tribulation.","James himself, however, didn’t even seem to notice the energy flowing into his body, helping him recover from the fatigue of pretending to be someone powerful and mysterious. Instead, he pulled up his holographic interface - something he had built himself after spending endless years within the library studying its books.","The interface was tapped into the laws of the universe, and delivered information to the library much in the same way Dao Lords stayed in touch with whatever was happening in the universe. Of course, the only reason James could build something that touched upon the laws in such a way was due to the inherent power of the Fable of Time.","\"Look, this is what I’m talking about! Lex, the Bulldozer, Williams, an S tier worker of the Midnight Inn,\" said James as he pulled out a picture of a collective card. The image was a picture of Lex holding a missile and threatening the soldiers of the Henali alliance from back when he went to rescue the Midnight Battalion.","Besides the picture, and the title, the card contained bits of other information. For example, the card gave the user +4 strength, +3 endurance, + 2 speed, + 1 intelligence as well as a ’forever alone debuff’.","There was also interesting flavor text which was a direct quote of something Lex said to a guest inside the Inn during the early days of the Inn: ’You can take a man out of a suit, but then the man would be naked.’","Morrow looked lamely at James, and said nothing, mainly because he knew that when he got like this, James wouldn’t listen to anyone.","\"He’s one of the only characters from the Midnight Inn series of the Mages Gather cards that has multiple versions. There’s Lex the Bulldozer, Lex the Wrecking Ball, and finally, Lex the Bombastic Bazook! But these cards are incredibly rare - according to the Mages Gather forum, only 20 Lex cards have ever been opened across the universe!\"","Morrow, the cane, flew away to the bar and made himself a very strong drink. By the time he returned, James was still talking and geeking out about Lex without ever realizing that he had ever left.","\"James, you should really go and stabilise some more Fractured time. At this rate, it won’t be long before Lex unlocks the seal on the Fable of Time so you should make the most of this time,\" said Morrow when he eventually couldn’t take any more.","James, who had been rambling on and on, finally broke free from his excitement.","\"Good point. But I’m going to go nap first - all that acting really wore me out,\" responded James as he waved to the cane and made his way to the corner of the library he treated as his bedroom. As he walked, he could not help but lament his own sorry state, and how different it was from a celebrity like Lex.","Once upon a time, James was a normal teenage human who used to write online fanfiction for his favorite books. Then one day he wrote a fanfiction called the Fable of Time, and, well, somehow provoked the actual Fable of Time.","As absurd as it sounded, that’s the story of how he got trapped inside this book, except that the Fable of Time wasn’t really a book. It was a legacy left behind by some dude known as the Timekeeper. This legacy was made from the remnants of his Dao before he died.","The original purpose of the Fable of Time was to act as a sort of trial. Anyone who mastered the legacy, even a little bit, could become the master of the book Fable of Time, and inherit everything else the Timekeeper left behind inside the book.","Unfortunately, the Timekeeper was from a universe known as Pentagal, and time worked differently there. Thus, within this universe, his Dao didn’t work properly, causing a glitch in how the book worked.","Thus, James had been stuck inside this book for hundreds of years already, his age, mentality and even cultivation frozen in time, unable to grow. The only way to fix the legacy was to smuggle a certain amount of the trapped, fractured time within the book.","When, many years ago, Lex stumbled on the Fable of Time, Morrow convinced James to pretend to be the Timekeeper and strike a deal with Lex to help them smuggle out the fractured time. They just never imagined that Lex, who had somehow managed to resist the book’s inclination to avoid people, would grow to become so powerful.","Fortunately, his uniqueness allowed them to use him to smuggle out much of the stabilised, fractured time trapped within the book.","James himself was just a mortal, so pretending to be a secret badass in front of an actual badass like Lex was quite tough, and he had to rely on Morrow’s power for that. Morrow, being the original Timekeeper’s cane, was naturally super powerful.","Once the issues with the Fable of Time were fixed, James too would be able to cultivate. He couldn’t wait till he had his own adventures across the universe, and the Mages Gather did a series on him.","Unfortunately, he could not get his hands on any of the cards in here, so he had to resign himself to just looking at their pictures.","Just as James retired to his ’room’, he received a notification from his holographic interface. One of his online friends had pinged him. Apparently there was a new set of Mages Gather cards being released!","James quickly opened the live stream and watched him unpack the latest pack. The first card he saw was that of a fairy! How rare!","\"The Pocket Calamity? Sounds intimidating,\" he said as he lay in bed and watched the rest of the unpacking.","From a different corner of the library, Morrow sighed once more. There was a time where his very presence inspired awe and terror. Now he was a babysitter to a perpetual teenager. How times change.","Lex suspected nothing close to the truth about his doppelganger, but he had a strong feeling that his copy wasn’t being entirely honest, nor was he as formidable as he claimed to be. That did not mean he did not wield incredible strength, for Lex felt tremendous pressure coming at him from the pipe and the cane he carried.","At least it was good to finally know a bit of what was hidden in his forehead. Only a few seconds after he left the library, he found himself back in the Joro realm. Although it wasn’t the location he had entered the Gilded Hollow from, he recognized the laws of the realm at least.","For a moment, he felt the laws of the realm - no, the laws of the universe lock onto him almost as if a tribulation was about to be triggered. The feeling, however, did not last.","Lex nodded. It seemed that his doppelganger really had the means to delay his tribulation. Maybe he really was very strong, and it was just his personality that was a little... off.","Lex took in a deep breath, taking in all the fresh air from his own universe, allowing himself to feel the touch of familiar laws. It felt great!","\"I’m back!\" Lex yelled in excitement, not expecting how great it felt to be in his own universe. It was the kind of thing one wouldn’t realize that they would miss until it was gone. Now that he was finally back, he felt that the spiritual energy from this universe was cleansing him out, as if he was filled with contamination!","No sooner had he had that thought that a whirlwind of energy started to form around him as it flooded into his system, washing out all the energy he absorbed from the Hollow. Fortunately, replacing the energy did not make him any weaker, and kept him at his peak strength.","Lex began sensing his surroundings as he began considering when and how to return to his main body. Almost as soon as he began, Lex felt the familiar aura of River and Pearl, and saw that they were in a bit of a bind.","He could not help but smile. Since he was living out the cliche of guiding them from the necklace, he might as well show up at the last moment to save them.","He began to chuckle as he imagined it, but then froze. His expression, his thoughts, everything froze alongside of him as he tried to make sense of what he was sensing.","This... didn’t make sense. This had to be wrong. Why could he sense the aura of... Z’s blood?","His bright eye began to slowly darken, and the grin on his face began to slowly withdraw as he checked again, and again, and again. Unfortunately, no matter how much he checked, the result was the same, so he summoned his Karmic Bead, and tried to activate the Karmic Clone he left with Z.","It wouldn’t activate."]},{"number":2410,"title":"Chapter 2410: One opportunity - suggested song: Royalty by Ezgod","paragraphs":["River stood in front of Pearl defensively as they looked up at the group in front of them, not that it would make any difference. River and Pearl were both Earth Immortals, and though their little trip into that strange place filled with treasures had allowed them to grow much stronger, they were nothing compared to the Celestial Immortal in front of them.","There were three Celestial Immortal humans, all three of them wearing disgruntled expressions as they looked towards the one, terrifying being in front of them. Mentioning that beings’ cultivation realm was unnecessary, for the being was from the Celestial realm!","Helplessness filled the young couple, though at least they were fortunate enough that the ones in front of them were from the Humanoid Alliance. Even if they suffered some injustices, they would at least preserve their lives... hopefully.","\"Do not cause any more problems,\" said the Celestial Immortal in a commanding tone as it looked at the three humans. \"We’re cut off from reinforcements so we need to regroup and strengthen our defensive positions.\"","The three humans, though, did not exactly look pleased by those orders.","\"Abandoning the realm and regrouping is the wrong move. This realm is full of heritages for humanity! We have an advantage - as long as we keep discovering them and use them to our advantage, we can route all enemies. Look at these two humans - no discernable talents or latent bloodlines, yet their power index is far greater than the norm.","\"If we can get them to lead us to whatever heritage they encountered, we can use that to rapidly increase the strength of our forces. Even if we’re cut off, this doesn’t need to be a defensive battle!\"","One of the three Celestial humans looked towards River and Pearl with an intense glare, as if blaming them for not already disclosing the details of everything they had encountered.","The Celestial glanced at the young couple, and that mere glance was enough to nearly buckle their knees and drop them to the ground. Fortunately, the Celestial was merely looking at them, and had no real intention of interrogating them.","\"Your actions are the very reason we have been cut off from the main forces. Do not exacerbate the situation by prioritising your personal agendas. So long as you act under the banner of the alliance, you will obey!\"","River and Pearl both started to get tense because they had no idea how they got caught up in this mess to begin with.","\"Obey? I’m not obeying crap from you,\" responded the human derisively. \"It’s an alliance, not a dictatorship. You can’t control our actions. You want to keep us humans weak and docile so you can maintain your leverage over us. Well, we don’t have to take your orders, we’re not from the same camp as you anyway.\"","After saying that, the human turned his gaze towards the young couple, clearly looking for some targets to vent his anger towards.","\"And you two? What the hell are you waiting for? I want the full details of your experiences and all heritages you’ve encountered so that we can best supplement the strength of the human race appropriately. Or are you two double agents, working for the enemy to weaken the human race from within?\"","River and Pearl tensed. It was clear that there was some high level conflict going on between camps within the Humanoid Alliance, and they had somehow stumbled in between it. If they truly had encountered some great heritage, they wouldn’t mind handing them over to the alliance. The problem was, they didn’t want to compromise Cliff and Karev, who had played a fundamental role in them gaining their strength.","\"We’re members of the Humanoid Alliance and have protected rights towards any cultivation aids acquired in enemy territory,\" River said, looking from the human to the Celestial, hoping that the latter would step in.","The Celestial did not intervene just yet, but the human did not seem pleased with that answer.","\"These are not ordinary times. We are in a war for survival, and all personal matters need to be set aside for the greater good,\" the human responded, his anger quite evident in his tone. \"The fact that you can’t see that tells me that you must have made some kind of shady deal to get where you are. Tell me, how many resources did you get for betraying the human race?\"","Panic and horror began to fill River’s heart as he felt his body freeze under the Celestial Immortals terrifying gaze. There was absolutely no logic in the words of the other human, but he didn’t seem to care about that either. He either felt greedy for whatever opportunities the couple had, or a much more likely scenario was that he just wanted to use them to vent his anger of frustration.","The young couple could not move, but the Celestial was within the scope of their vision so they focused on him, hoping for some help. He, at least, seemed to care about the rules of the alliance. They saw a subtle change in his expression, almost as if he was about to intervene.","The human, almost as if expecting to be interrupted, smirked and began to channel an attack. Reality, however, did not follow the script any of them had imagined.","A loud, deep sound rang ominously across the skies, almost like an especially large war horn, alerting reality itself to a proclamation that could not be ignored. Light itself changed with the proclamation, tinting the world in a dark maroon hue.","The clear skies were, in a single moment, filled with thick, impenetrable clouds which were thick with a baleful aura that seemed to almost resonate with the crimson air.","The wind blew, and how. It ripped and snatched at their clothes and bodies as it raged, lashing at them with the utmost ferocity, threatening to shred them to pieces. Yet unlike the sky, it was not filled with ferocity or balefulness. Nor was the wind filled with the smell of rain that often accompanied such thick clouds. Instead, the wind smelled only like fear.","It was not anger that caused the wind to attack them so ferociously. No, it was caused by a fear that permeated across the entire horizon, as if it was a rightful inheritance bequeathed upon all of reality. The air itself wanted to escape.","Lightning, its body entirely red contained within a thick border of black, fell from the sky. Yet this lightning lacked the swiftness that it was usually known for. Instead, the thousands of streaks of lightning fell from the sky at an agonizing crawl, searing everything they touched.","Heavy. Everything felt so incredibly heavy that not a single one of them could even breath, and yet the space around them felt so thick and viscous that they could not fall to the ground even if they could not support themselves under that indescribable weight.","River and Pearl had not moved, now terrified for entirely new reasons, when the both of them suddenly noticed a new figure standing in the air - a figure that was all too familiar, and yet entirely alien.","For so long, they had felt like the clothes that Cliff wore were so strange. They knew now that what he wore was called a suit, and it was a certain type of clothing common among some humans.","For as long as they had known him, Cliff always appeared extremely proper - his shirt always tucked it, his tie always up to his collar, his suit buttons always closed. Now, though, he did not look like that.","His shirt was tucked out, and his loose tie flapped in the raging wind. His hair ruffled and his open suit hung loosely. Yet his unkempt appearance did not make him appear shoddy - far from it. No clothes, no attire, regardless of how they appeared, could take away from the majesty that radiated from every fiber of his being.","None who laid their eyes upon him could deny the regal bearing he possessed, nor the undeniable aura of royalty that exuded from his being.","His presence was entirely unique, and could not even be equated to the presence of Elders or Sages. After all, there were many Sages and even more Elders, but there could be none other like him.","Seeing Cliff like this, an absurd thought ran across Rivers’ mind - though the thought did not seem so absurd now. Could it be that... all the stories he had told them about himself... were real?","Lex looked at the young couple, and then the Celestial. A palpable indifference filled his eyes when he looked at the Celestial - not a slight, but a mercy. That much became abundantly clear when his gaze finally fell on the human who had been speaking so far.","No words were spoken yet, but they all felt it - it was the unmistakable sensation of facing a tribulation of absolutely colossal proportions.","The Celestial could not understand why a mere gaze from a human felt like a tribulation - wasn’t that the domain of the universe itself? Then again, if he was going to start picking out the anomalies of their given situation, that feeling would hardly be the first on his list.","\"I am going to give you one opportunity,\" Lex said, his tone calm, his pace unhurried, as he imparted the absolute privilege of that one, single opportunity. \"Explain to me why I can sense the aura of Z’s blood on you.\"","No threat was uttered from Lex’s mouth. Then again, such a thing was not needed. The clouds above them began to weep, but its tears were mistaken for rain."]},{"number":2411,"title":"Chapter 2411: Gathering the prey","paragraphs":["Lex had plans. He was going to return to the universe and find a way to face his stalker. He was beaten up pretty badly by the stalker, and so he planned to seek revenge, and was looking forward to sharing his own growth with him. Then he was going to go back to the Midnight Inn and thoroughly spoil Almira, and maybe take some time to relax.","Realistically speaking, he was aware that he might encounter some issues here and there, so he was ready to face some obstacles. He was ready for the universe to have descended into absolute chaos. He was... he was also ready for the fact that he may have been too late.","Hoping for the best was one thing, but he did not deny himself from considering that he had taken too long, and that his stalker had managed to get his hands on Lex’s system. He was ready to face a reality wherein the Midnight Inn was...","Thus when he returned, and one of the first things he sensed was the aura of Z’s blood, an overwhelming, all encompassing rage filled his very being, but he was no longer the inexperienced 25 year old that he used to be. Rage, no matter how severe, did not blind him, nor did it control him.","On the contrary, it provided him with a level of clarity that a calm mind just could not achieve. Everything of value became so much easier to distinguish from everything else that normally felt significant, but was merely a nice addon. Almost immediately, all of his priorities became clear.","From the moment he decided on the fake realm design inside his necklace, and the system that governed it, he had a very set and specific idea of how he wanted it to work. Now, that didn’t matter. It just needed to work, however that may be.","When he entered the Dream realm, the Dream tavern brought with it a tiny piece of space with it, forcefully attaching that to the laws of the realm while retaining its own set of rules. Why did Lex need to pull anyone inside his necklace, and increase the burden on the necklace itself, when he could just bring that fake realm outside and impose it upon wherever he was?","He traced the aura of Z’s blood and found the person carrying it. Without hesitation, he summoned the fake realm from within the necklace, and superimposed it upon the Joro realm. Instead of replacing the realm itself, it became like a filter upon that reality, turning that section of the Joro realm into his personal realm - where his whim and will were law!","Yet he did not attack just yet. He did not vent his anger, for the clarity brought about by his rage was so much more potent than even his Flow state. Instead, he investigated. He needed to know if the Midnight Inn still existed. He needed to know if his home had been destroyed. He needed to know... if this was his fault.","Thus, the moment he arrived, he asked a question. Of course, Lex was not really relying on their answer to learn the truth. Instead, as he stood there, his gaze looked not at the people in front of him, but at their karma, at their fortunes, and even through their spirits. Their cooperation was entirely unnecessary for his interrogation.","The group of Celestials looked up at Lex, unquestionable, unfathomable power radiating from his very being, and knew that they had run into trouble. So far, despite kidnapping Z from the Inn, the Humanoid Alliance hadn’t actually faced any fallout directly from the Inn. Yes, their cooperation had been temporarily disrupted, but that was all.","Who knew that the first to face some kind of repercussion would be them? Little did this group know the actions Velma had already taken.","\"We are members of the Humanoid Alliance,\" the human spoke after gathering up his courage. \"How dare you-\"","The human did not get the opportunity to complete his words, for Lex had already seen through the truth. The Midnight Inn was fine. It had not been destroyed - the alliance had merely broken faith with the Inn.","With that weight off his shoulders, Lex gave himself a fraction of a moment to decide his next steps. He had to be careful not to offend anyone, for the Inn couldn’t afford any enemies. Or rather, the Inn had been thoroughly offended, and so he could not afford to take a step back, lest anyone assume the Inn was actually weak.","Thus, when he took a step forward to attack, Lex was not venting his anger. Not at all. It was a strategic move. This was completely... strategic!","The Celestial Immortal human could not complete his words because Lex appeared in front of him and clamped his mouth shut with a single hand, crushing not just his face, but his entire body as he did, leaving only the human’s soul trapped within Lex’s hand.","\"How dare I ?\" Lex repeated slowly, calmly, without the slightest hint of any loss of control. \"A mere Humanoid Alliance - not even your patron cares to look after you. I gave you a single opportunity to explain yourselves. How dare you waste it by trying to threaten me?\"","Despite the calm tone, Lex’s words rang louder than thunder. The other human Celestial Immortals retreated, trying to build some distance between themselves and Lex, as futile as it seemed considering how slow they moved.","River and Pearl felt their comprehension of reality shatter as they could not wrap their heads around what they were witnessing.","Yet it was not them, but the member of the Celestial race who was most strongly affected by Lex’s words, and not just because his voice itself seemed to be a spiritual attack. What had he said about the patron of the alliance? Why had he treated the entire alliance as insignificant? Could he really know the truth behind certain matters?","None of that mattered at the moment, though. He needed to quickly decide - was he going to try to save those humans, or should he escape and save himself.","No sooner had he thought about saving the humans that Lex turned his gaze towards the Celestial, and he found himself frozen still.","\"Now I will give you one opportunity. Convince me that the alliance has done everything in its power to right this wrong, or else you might discover that you all are just as disposable to the alliance as you think Z is to the Inn.\"","The rain was slowly turning into a storm, for with each passing moment, Lex was devouring the information inside the soul of the human in his hands, getting up to date with everything that had happened in his absence.","The other humans, finally freed from the devastating mental pressure they felt while Lex looked at them, regained enough of their mental faculties to call for help, entirely unaware that the only reason they were able to do that at all... was because Lex wanted them to bring his prey to him. It would be so much easier to deal with them if they came to him themselves."]},{"number":2412,"title":"Chapter 2412: I dare - Song Recommendation: Warriors from 2WEI","paragraphs":["Author’s Note: For Chapters with song recommendations, I recommend playing the sond at a low volume on repeat in the background for maximum immursion.","\"Be at ease, the Alliance has taken this transgression extremely seriously,\" spoke the Celestial, forgoing all intentions to fight against this enraged agent of the Midnight Inn. It wasn’t because he felt like he couldn’t put up a fight, but because he honestly did not support the kidnapping of Z to begin with. In fact, the Celestial court itself had commented on the foolishness and shortsightedness of this action.","Lex looked from the Celestial to the human soul that he was holding. Due to the fact that he was a Celestial Immortal, the soul itself was strong enough to take on the shape of the body, making it look like he was still clamping his mouth shut.","\"Oh? How seriously? Has Z been returned to the Midnight Inn? According to his memories, that does not seem to be the case,\" said Lex as he raised the soul in his hand. Immediately, the expression of all the others distorted as they realized that Lex was searching through his memories.","Naturally, his memories were protected by seals and formations set in place by the alliance, however that seemed to be no obstacle for this human. He hadn’t even shown any signs of struggling with them, nor had any of the contingencies of a memory search been triggered.","In truth, it wasn’t that Lex was some kind of expert at reading memories or navigating the spirit. It was just that the brute force of his energy, augmented through his partial Primordial Dao Body, completely and directly tore through all restrictions in his mind.","The only thing that Lex wouldn’t be able to tear through was a seal placed by a Dao Lord, and he was smart enough to steer clear of that. There were quite a few of those in the human’s mind, but even avoiding them he’d gotten a pretty good idea of what had happened.","First he was kidnapped, then enslaved to use for the sole purpose of attracting a legacy. Dammit, even Lex had never worked Z that hard.","\"The alliance has sanctioned the Dao Lords responsible for planning these actions and...\"","Lex snorted, his disdain extremely apparent on his face as he heard those words. The Celestial wasn’t even worth talking to anymore if that’s what he considered ’taking very seriously’. To begin with, Lex wasn’t actually interested in talking to him. Instead, he was waiting for the human reinforcements. He had, on purpose, allowed that call to go out. He had, on purpose, not hidden his location.","He looked towards the other two humans and felt like their request for backup wasn’t urgent enough, so he put some more pressure on them.","\"Tell me, have you ever experienced a slave collar? The kind that you had put on Z?\" Lex asked.","That question alone caused the two humans to immediately pull out a defensive treasure, encompassing them in a metal sphere to protect them from Lex’s influence. Yet Lex peeled apart that sphere as if it was made of foil.","What awaited him was an attack, yet before it even reached Lex’s body, the attack sizzled away.","Lex was deliberately slow in his attack, letting the humans savor in the inevitability that was their forthcoming demise. The more they struggled against him, the more they felt afraid rather than reassured. They couldn’t understand why everything they did was so ineffective. How could the gap in their strength be so great? They were all peak Celestial Immortals!","Lex raised his left hand and one of the humans was pulled into his grasp despite how far he was. Lex had said nothing, he had done nothing, yet the human was pulled in without being able to put up the slightest resistance.","\"What the hell are you?\" the human muttered in horror. Unfortunately, he did not live long enough to hear a response.","Through his hand, Lex channeled the law of Anchor with such intensity that not only did it immediately destroy his body, it also eviscerated his soul. This one Lex did not need to save since he already knew what had happened.","Lex looked at the soul in his right hand - the one who was stained with the aura of Z’s blood. This one would not get such an easy end, so he curled up his soul and tucked it away inside the necklace, leaving only the one Celestial, the one very frightened human, and the young couple.","Fortunately, the human’s reinforcements finally arrived, and they were not a few. Four other Celestial Immortal humans, and a dozen other Heaven Immortals appeared in the team, all fully equipped to deal with Lex.","The moment they arrived, though, all their previous confidence vanished. Feeling the oppression in the air alone let them know that what they were dealing with was far from a normal threat.","\"He’s from the Midnight Inn!\" the human yelled desperately as he rushed to hide behind the group. \"He’s after Z!\"","Upon hearing the words the group seemed troubled, but the advantage of numbers gave them a bit of confidence. In the back, the Celestial shook his head, and slowly distanced himself from the group. The summation of all the wisdom accumulated across his life as a Celestial led him to believe that if he tried to defend the alliance any further, or provoked Lex in any way, he would seriously regret it.","Lex, however, looked at the new group as if they were already dead. Their biggest mistake wasn’t bringing too few people. Their biggest mistake was bringing another person with the aura of Z’s blood on them.","\"There’s no need to fight between us,\" said one of the reinforcements cautiously as he observed Lex. \"I can see you’re a very powerful human. In that case, you should understand the difficulty our race has had to endure due to our weakness. What we did was for the sake of the human race. Your friend’s contribution can bring our whole race a bit closer to once again reclaiming our spot in the universe.\"","He was appealing to the struggle Lex no doubt endured as a fellow human.","\"The Humanoid Alliance is working for the betterment of the entire human race. Do not make a mistake that you cannot take back. Your situation can still be salvaged if you stop fighting and agree to work with us. But if you persist in your current actions, the alliance will not let you off.\"","River, Pearl and even the Celestial looked at the speaking human as if had suffered head trauma.","\"For the sake of the human race?\" Lex asked, his voice hardening a little as he finally let loose the strict control he’d had over his anger. \"I alone am enough to restore the glory of the human race. And you... you are the personification of the rot and corruption that has stained the legacy of humanity.\"","With every word he spoke, Lex stepped closer to the group, and with every word his voice rose until the ground shook and the skies trembled.","\"As for the Alliance? My name is Lex William of the Midnight Inn, and I dare the Humanoid Alliance to not let me off, because no matter what, I will not let off those whose hands are stained with the blood of my family.\"","Lex was a regular sized person, but for some reason, in that moment, the entire group could not help but imagine Lex as some infinitely massive behemoth because the rage that oozed off his body was so intense, it froze the group, leaving them unable to respond or retaliate in any way. All they could do was tremble.","Even in the grip of his anger, everything Lex did was tinged with strategy. He could not show an ounce of weakness. He could not show the slightest hint of restraint. Lex needed to show the universe exactly what kind of nightmare they would face... if they crossed the Midnight Inn!","\"I DARE ,\" Lex bellowed, his voice alone shattering the bones of the group who had come and threatened him, \"the Humanoid Alliance to send their Dao Lords one more time! Let the universe see the dawn of the day the Midnight Inn is no longer neutral. Let them taste the fear of knowing that nowhere is safe.","\"Where will you hide? In what corner of the universe will you cower after provoking the Innkeeper one more time, knowing that he will always find you? What formations will you use, what realm will you hide in where the Innkeeper cannot reach you?","\"When you discover that your allies can no longer save you, and that even your worst nightmares run away to hide, you will know you have entered the darkness of midnight, and there will be no one to save you.\"","With those words echoing far and wide, Lex finally attacked. Yet he did not attack to kill, not yet. Death was too easy an escape. They needed to live, or else how could they become examples?"]},{"number":2413,"title":"Chapter 2413: Not even a fight","paragraphs":["It was not a fight. It could not be called a fight. If it was absolutely necessary to describe it, an ass whooping could be used, although calling it total decimation would be more accurate. Even before venturing into the Gilded Hollow and upgrading the necklace, Lex had the strength of a Celestial Apex. Now he was on a whole new level.","The battle ended almost as soon as it began. Lex captured the souls of all who were even slightly stained with the karma of Z, and let the others live.","It was strategic. He didn’t spare them out of kindness, but because he needed to show that the Midnight Inn was not blindly making an enemy out of the entire Humanoid Alliance. Even though he postured and proclaimed how the Innkeeper would fight them, he was careful to say that he would only do it if they were offended again.","No matter how angry he was, Lex had not lost his self-awareness. The key was to intimidate the opponent and make them think a confrontation would cost them too much, while to also show them proof that they were not in an undeniable conflict. The trick was to balance how serious and severe his reaction needed to be to show sufficient strength, yet enough restraint to make them think that the issue could be resolved without an all out war.","At any other time, Lex would be far more cautious about his actions, but considering the whole universe was at war and Major realms kept blowing up like balloons, the alliance had their hands full with other problems. Pushing them at this point was actually ideal, since they were already defending themselves from many other enemies. If they began to fear that the Innkeeper could get behind their supply lines and attack them in critical locations, they would be too afraid to challenge him.","As for what the ideal outcome from this situation was, Lex had no idea. He did not know Z’s condition, or his location, nor could he predict what direction the universe would grow in. He did not know how he could put an end to this conflict, or where he was supposed to go from here. He had none of those answers.","He would just have to handle this the old fashioned way - the way he used to do things before he matured, and realized that planning and preparing usually lead to better outcomes. Yes, he would have to wing it. Good thing he was a pro at it.","Lex turned towards the Celestial who seemed to be waiting for him. He was wary of Lex, that much was true, but he still did not reveal an ounce of fear. Then again, if this is all it took to frighten a Celestial, they would not really live up to their reputation.","\"Are you willing to talk now?\" the Celestial asked cautiously. \"I assure you, the action taken against the Midnight Inn was not sanctioned by the alliance, and many of the leading factions are not pleased with it. It’s just that as leaders, we cannot avoid due procedure like others.\"","Lex glared at him, but slowly withdrew the realm he had superimposed upon the Joro realm, causing the reddish tint to dissipate. The pillars of lightning that were falling from the sky also faded away, and the air of oppression that was suffocating everyone finally eased.","\"You can use whatever excuse you wish - those who intend to break the rules never care about them anyway. The only ones you’re restricting are yourselves. The ones who will have to suffer the repercussions in the end will also be you,\" answered Lex, his voice filled with immense gravity.","\"I have been away from the Inn for a long time so I do not know what they are considering, but I assure you of this, if Z is alive but harmed your alliance will pay a dear cost for his pain. But if his life is lost, then the entire alliance will bear the burden of the repercussions. Your due process, your systems, your niceties will not exempt you from responsibility.\"","Lex looked at the Celestial with nothing but disdain and contempt, and then turned his gaze towards River and Pearl, revealing nothing on his face. If a connection between them was realized, especially after what had just happened, the young couple could get pulled into danger. It was best not to involve them - especially since he was not yet returning to the Inn.","Without another word, Lex vanished, leaving only the young couple and the Celestial unharmed. The others, despite having their lives spared by Lex, lay on the ground, gravely injured.","The full extent of their injuries was not something that could be discerned right now. Heck, even their life was not guaranteed at the moment since the Joro realm was still technically classified as enemy territory.","\"Come on, we need to retreat to the base,\" the Celestial said, looking at the two young humans. \"That fight won’t have gone unnoticed. Enemy forces will converge on this location soon enough - it would be best if we were long gone by then.\"","River looked at the Celestial and nodded.","\"Exactly. This fight won’t have gone unnoticed, which is exactly why no one will come here any time soon - at least not until they can gather an army of Celestial Immortals. I’m safer here than with you. The Humanoid Alliance... does not inspire the same trust and sense of security that it used to.\"","The Celestial frowned at the humans, but then shook his head. He couldn’t blame them, for the actions of the other humans really had made them feel unsafe. They were right - the Humanoid Alliance was slowly descending into chaos. It was the anchor weighing the Celestial race down, preventing them from reaching their true height, which is why the enemies of the alliance never wanted to see it actually destroyed.","But... since that much was already apparent, surely the Celestial court had thought of some kind of solution. For now, he just needed to follow orders.","In another corner of the Joro realm, Lex breathed out a long, exhausted sigh. He just wanted to come back and beat up his stalker. Why did things need to be so complicated? Now he wouldn’t be able to enjoy himself with that fight.","The situation of the universe wasn’t so great either, and only a few months were left until the Nexus event. He needed to quickly plan things out.","He looked up at the sky and sensed his impending Major tribulation. Just as he’d taught River and Pearl, he’d use it to beat up a powerful opponent - mainly because he had no other choice.","Lex pushed away all unnecessary thoughts from his mind and focused on his next immediate task: reaching his original body."]},{"number":2414,"title":"Chapter 2414: The Forgotten Age of Heroes - Song recommendation Moonlight Sonata Epic Trailer Version from Hidden Citizens","paragraphs":["Author’s Note: Guys, please do try to find the right version of the song. It’s on youtuibe and spotify :)","Lex found a secluded corner of the Joro realm to create a temporary abode for himself wherein he sat down and did a thorough self analysis. It had been many years already since he lost his body and had been living as a necklace.","The absurdity of the situation needed no extensive elaboration. When he had stepped onto the path of cultivation, he never imagined himself as a fairy, let alone a necklace. And yet here he was.","Once, abstract concepts of the universe confounded him and stopped him, but with experience and exposure he opened himself up to the limitless possibilities of the universe which is actually why he was able to even create a fallback for himself such as this necklace.","Yet even in the abstract, and even in the limitless possibilities of the universe, there was a rule book that governed all of reality - even if he didn’t understand all its complexities just yet. He wasn’t just referring to the Ruling laws, but something deeper and more fundamental that controlled even them.","He had no idea what it was, but he was certain it existed. Lex remembered that the first time he saw a statue of the Human Kings within the Temple of Fasting, he heard a voice telling him about other lists, other ranks than the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum. Back then he had no idea who had been speaking to him, or why, but he knew now.","The voice had belonged to Nuwa, and she had told him that only by adding his name to one of the other rankings in the universe could he actually become a real performer - a real player on the universal scale. Well, even now, he wasn’t sure his name was on any of the lists she had been talking about back then - surely the Celestial Apex list, or the highest bounty list weren’t the types of lists she was talking about.","Regardless, Lex had a feeling that these lists and ranking controlled and governed the universe just as much as the ruling laws, just in different ways. That’s why there was so much emphasis on Elder and Sage races, while other powerful races disdained to join them altogether - such as the Celestial list.","All of this reeked of secrets he did not know yet. The reason he was thinking about all of this now was because... he had a massive obstacle in front of him. He needed to not only find his real body once more, after his stalker had made it increasingly difficult to find it, he needed to regain control of his body.","The irritating competence of his stalker made that task incredibly difficult. Difficult did not, however, mean impossible.","The images of a few different figures flashed through Lex’s mind. From Nuwa, to Eclipse, to various other extremely dangerous beings that came in the form of Mythical beasts, monkeys, dragons and so on... all powerful beings, all of whom he had met under various identities. In meeting them, regardless of which identity he used, Lex formed karma with them, regardless of how deep or subtle it may have been.","For various reasons, the source of that karma was hidden, whether it was by his system or someone else. That didn’t change the fact that it existed, and it was fused to his karma!","He wasn’t thinking of all their specific names because he was now back in the main universe and he did not want to attract their attention for not all of them were on such good terms with it. That didn’t change the fact that they had a connection, no matter how hidden that connection was.","So why was Lex thinking of that connection now, while also thinking about the mysteries of the rules that governed the universe?","He looked up, and though he saw the ceiling of the abode he had temporarily created, what he was actually looking at was his impending tribulation. It would not trigger until he reached his main body, but how could the universe differentiate between his lesser forms and his main body?","Heck, why did he exist as a human and a fairy, both with different cultivation levels at times? They had the same soul, so shouldn’t the cultivation realm be the same as well? If the necklace that fused with his soul could also act as his body because of the unique nature of his soul, why didn’t the universe itself treat the necklace as the main body, and was instead waiting for him to return?","Lex did not have a specific answer to those questions. What mattered, however, was that those distinctions existed, and the universe not only acknowledged them, but functioned according to them.","The reason his Major tribulation was not being triggered was either because the universe couldn’t identify where his main body was, or because the growth of his soul hadn’t yet synchronized with his real body. Yet the very fact that the universe was waiting also proved that his body still existed, and that there was a deep, intrinsic connection between his soul and his main body which could not be cut off by his stalker no matter how well he hid it.","Lex closed his eyes and dismissed the projection of his body, leaving only a single necklace floating in the air. A swirl of energy began to form around the necklace as he gathered his energy, allowing that swirl to slowly and gradually become larger and larger. He did not care about being discovered.","Everything he did now need not be hidden. In fact, he was depending on it being as obvious and evident to everyone as possible. Though no words were spoken, this would be a message to the Humanoid Alliance as well.","A small, black Go bead appeared above the surface of the necklace, as if deliberately placed there. When the entire universe itself was a massive Go board, placing the bead upon his necklace was a purposeful move.","The swirling energy around the necklace tore through the roof of the abode as it turned into an energy storm, gaining a momentum that transcended simple energy. What Lex was gathering now was not just the entire sum of energy that he could control - no, he was gathering the total sum of his karma, regardless of where or who it came from. Even the karma forcefully hidden for various reasons had to contribute the weight of its existence today.","Honestly, Lex himself did not know just how massive his karma was. He had met too many powerful beings, encountered too many secrets, ventured into too many forbidden zones. The seal on his forehead was one thing he had forgotten about - who was to say there weren’t more of such things?","Far away, Nuwa looked towards Lex and for once... for once, she was not exasperated by him. That was because he was not making a mistake, or doing something unintentionally. He was fully aware of the risks, and was taking action boldly.","She did not cover for him, nor did she try to interfere. Instead she only watched, even though her gaze seemed to transcend the boundary of time and look back upon a period that had, once, been known as the Age of Heroes. Now, with its history forgotten, it was called the Primordial Age.","It seemed like alongside that history, the universe had collectively forgotten what it meant to be a hero. For all the endless troubles Lex had caused her, this one single moment that reminded her of that forgotten age... was worth it.","Nuwa was the first to notice Lex, but she was far from the only one."]},{"number":2415,"title":"Chapter 2415: Who he would become - Song recommendation Protectors of the Earth from Two Steps From Hell","paragraphs":["Lex himself did not know that among the eight of the beings above the Dao Lord realm that inhabited his universe, he had met four, and had connections to five!","A tornado of energy and karma surrounded the necklace, growing at such a spectacular speed that it could not be ignored. Even those immortals who did not know or understand karma within the Joro realm could sense it. Even the mortals who could not sense laws could sense the depth and enormity of the energy tornado that was rising in a random corner of the Joro realm.","If even Immortals and mortals could sense it, how could the Dao Lords remain ignorant of it? How could they not investigate? How could they not put a stop to it? The answer was simply because Lex had directly thought of the names of Nuwa and Eclipse before beginning!","Though the observers could not know, could not properly sense what was so terrifying about that karmic storm, they knew full well that this rising storm had already touched upon something they did not want to get involved with.","If only the universe were not so mired in war, if only realms were disappearing left and right, if only Dao Lords weren’t being killed every day, maybe someone would have had the courage to experiment. Yet in this universe, ’if only’ was entirely irrelevant. The only thing that mattered was the ground reality of the situation, and the ground reality was that no one wanted to mess with the unknown.","Eclipse, sitting on her throne within her realm, could not help but look over at Lex, and could not help but let out a fond smile. She really appreciated Lex’s courage, and his lovable stupidity. She felt something akin to a grandparent watching a newborn baby trying to bite a bagger laced with poison. Although she had no grandchildren of her own, she supposed this is probably what it felt like.","Yet while Eclipse watched with amusement and fondness, not all were like her. Lex was summoning, or at least trying to summon all the karma connected to him. He did not, fortunately, have the ability to actually fully succeed. He did, however, make some progress.","Ventura, another entity above the Dao Lord realm, looked towards the Joro realm in confusion. What about that realm was attracting him? Even he did not know.","Asho, another such being, looked over and spotted Lex - the human born in the Origin realm, and suspected son of the Innkeeper. Why had he suddenly felt the urge to look at him? Asho himself did not know.","Within the Primary realm, Death looked over while working on his Nether portal, and saw not the Joro realm, but something blocking his vision. He snorted, unable to determine who was blocking his vision, and began working on his portal once more.","That was four of beings above the Dao realm who Lex had encountered one way or another. Yet far away in the universe, within a sarcophagus being pulled by nine, skeletal dragons through the void, Divine opened his eyes. He looked over at the Joro realm and looked at the rising, karmic tornado with confused eyes.","Yet before he could ponder over it, he immediately closed his eyes and concealed his existence when he sensed the gaze of the others . He had nearly been fooled by their trap. Fortunately, he was quick enough or they would have been able to trace his location.","With such a terrifying collection of gazes falling upon the karmic storm, the Dao Lords within proximity of the storm did not try to intervene. Instead, they evacuated as quickly as they possibly could, afraid that this might be a prelude to the terrifying phenomenon of mysteriously destroyed Major realms!","Lex did not know, nor did he care. He had walked those lands which even Dao Lords feared, spoken to beings forgotten by history itself, and done things that should have been impossible. He had wanted to live cautiously until he was strong enough, but if the universe was intent upon depriving him of that option, then he would throw caution to the wind. He would unleash all that he was worth and let the cards fall where they may. Whatever the repercussions may be, he would deal with them.","Within the darkness, Regix looked over. He could not see Lex, protected by too many of his means. He could sense it though - something significant was happening.","Within the Midnight Inn, Mary’s new body was not yet complete but the body’s eyes began to twitch, as if something deeply connected to it was calling out to it. Mary herself, imprisoned by the laws of the system, sensed nothing save the Primordial energy leaking into the core of the system. Her focus remained unwavering - right now, nothing could distract her.","Within her mirror, Moon looked out as she felt a pull of blood she had not felt in a long time. With Arch-Heaven, Mango trembled, and the scale it used to write down important things began to heat up.","Within the Tyrannum realm, Alexander and his group stood in front of the barrier, looking out at the army of Dao Lords attacking it, trying to break in. The soldiers standing by them, humans one and all, did not even flinch as they watched the attacks fall, and fail to break the barrier.","The group sensed something and looked at one another, all thinking of a single name. In this grave moment, why would they think of Lex? They did not know.","Across the universe, in the darkness and in the light, mortals, immortals and Dao Lords alike all felt like something strange was going on. So many of them had never even heard of Lex, let alone have a connection to him. How then could they imagine that what they were sensing was the pull of his karma?","They had benefited from him, from his Inn, from the feedback of his tribulations, from the enlightenment of the phenomenon he had caused across the universe time and time again. Knowingly or unknowingly, they had benefited from him, so how could they deny him now when he called upon all the karma that was connected to him?","The storm grew larger and larger, its vibrations transcending the limits of the Joro realm, growing into a force that could not be contained nor controlled. No one understood what was happening, but many of them began to understand who was responsible.","From the start, Lex had not attempted to hide himself, or his actions, so it was only a matter of time before it was realized who had caused this storm. The eyes that fell upon the strom from the Humanoid Alliance were mixed with complex emotions.","How could this be caused by a human? Why was it someone from the Midnight Inn? What was he trying to do? They did not know, but they watched, for the answer was forthcoming.","Within the storm, the black bead was trembling from the force of the massive karmic storm. It was beginning to heat up to such an extent that it felt like the bead may explode. In truth, the storm had quickly grown far beyond the point where even Lex could properly control it.","Then again, control was never his goal to begin with. He wanted, instead, to challenge his stalker, and see whose methods were stronger.","Although he could not control the karmic storm, he could channel it towards a general direction and let it take over from there, so he did just that. With the full force of the entire karma Lex had ever accumulated, he locked onto his tribulation, as if to force it out.","Lex wanted to see whose means were better - his own, or his stalkers? Lex wanted to see who he would become when he let go of all his inhibitions.","The massive, overbearing, overwhelming karmic storm suddenly and abruptly vanished, bringing with it the karmic bead and necklace."]},{"number":2416,"title":"Chapter 2416: Miss me, b****? Song recommendation Back in Black","paragraphs":["Daekol had to admit, this human had turned out to be more challenging than expected. Being challenging did not mean that Daekol would have avoided doing this had he known - it just meant that he had come to acknowledge that beating him wasn’t nearly as simple or easy as he had expected.","After the last time the body woke up, Daekol had gone all out, leaving nothing back. Now that he was through the barrier, and especially now that he was putting in so much effort to cleanse the body of its curses, he could not afford any mistakes. He did not want to encounter the very cliche predicament of putting in so much effort to purify the body, only for it to be reclaimed by its original owner.","The problem was, it was becoming increasingly clear that such a thing could actually and genuinely occur, so Daekol committed his all to ensuring that would not happen. He utilized every system reward he had been saving to increase their isolation and keep them from being discovered.","He utilized his personal Sovereign authority until it actually exhausted him, causing him to need to rest for months and months. He used every item and resource available to him through his own contact network, and everything awarded to him by the Path of Chaos.","Although many of the means he used were one-time use items, meaning he could never get them back, he did not regret it. Strengthening his foundation and increasing his chances of entering the Dao Lord realm were far more important than anything else.","Every price he paid, every resource he utilized could be earned back once his strength grew, or once his system evolved into the next level. However, if he lost the body for any reason, it was much more difficult to correct.","Then, after so much preparation, and after paying such a massive cost, he finally began purifying the body. Once that was done, Daekol wasted no time trying to get his hands on the system within the human’s soul.","The body and soul themselves were extremely difficult to control, especially once all the curses had been lifted, but that was not the biggest hurdle Daekol faced. Instead, it was the system itself.","It seemed to have gone into some kind of dormant state, and so it wasn’t responding to him or his means at all. Even his Sovereign command received no response.","When he saw that, Daekol got a foreboding feeling that something was going terribly wrong. That was not a feeling he liked at all, because he could not figure out what the source of that danger was.","It took him many more months until he got a hint of the problem. First off, the system in the human’s soul was of a higher rank than his own, which is why his own system had no authority over it. A higher rank system had some power over weaker systems, even if they couldn’t generally interfere with each other.","That made it much more difficult for him to understand what exactly was going on with the system in the human’s body. Eventually, however, he discovered a hint of a Primordial aura and immediately triggered an emergency quest!","The quest dictated that the targeted system was absorbing Primordial energy, and that he had to stop it at any cost! The quest was automatic with excellent rewards and severe punishments for failing.","While he didn’t like being forced into a quest, it did explain what was going on. The source of the danger was the Primordial energy that the system was absorbing.","Thus, instead of trying to gain control over the system, which was his original goal, he began trying to stop it from absorbing more Primordial energy. He figured that once he stabilized the situation, he could try to take control of it.","At the same time, he suspected that the Primordial energy that the system was absorbing was of the human’s last contingencies in case he ever lost control of the system in his soul. Clearly he was aware that not absorbing the system made him vulnerable to external threats, and so had prepared this as an unpleasant surprise for anyone who tried to take it from him.","It was a bold and dangerous move, and Daekol could not help but respect the human for it.","Since then, he had been working on two fronts. On one hand, he had been trying to pressurise the system and prevent it from absorbing more Primordial energy. If he knew where the energy was coming from that would have helped, but he couldn’t figure it out so he had to stop focusing on that.","On the other hand, he kept trying to take control of the system. As it turned out, his own system also couldn’t directly absorb the one in the human’s soul because it was compromised with Primordial energy which had activated some kind of automated self defense mechanism, preventing his system from absorbing the other one.","Thus, taking control of the system through the human’s own soul became the last option left to Daeko. It was a tough one, but one he intended on seeing through.","When he focused, time lost meaning, and he stopped paying attention to external things. With step by step progress, he was certain he could gain control of the system within a hundred years - a paltry amount of time.","Unfortunately for him, that was not meant to be.","Daekol suddenly frowned and looked up, confused as to why he could sense an approaching tribulation. That shouldn’t be-","Before he could complete the thought, a bolt of deep maroon lightning tore through the defensive barrier he had set up, boiling with far more power than Daekol could take undefended!","He was shocked, but that didn’t prevent him from raising a hand to erect a barrier above him. Even on short notice, he could create powerful enough barrier to-","For the second time he was taken by surprise when he felt something grab onto his arm. He looked down and saw the human, looking up at him with a massive, mad grin.","\"Miss me, bitch?\" Lex yelled as he kicked his stalker straight in his shocked and surprised face. Oh how long he had waited to do just that. Unfortunately, Lex did not have the time to savor the feeling of retribution for his Major tribulation had been triggered in the most aggressive way throughout the history of the entire universe.","In short, the main target for that maroon lightning bolt was his own face!"]},{"number":2417,"title":"Chapter 2417: A facial","paragraphs":["The Dream Master was humming a splendid tune while working. Their plan, which had been in the works for over an Age, was going along smoothly. In fact, due to several unforeseen incidents, the plan was going even smoother than they expected.","Instead of interference from Sage races, like they expected, their progress was actually sped up because the Sage races were using this opportunity to forward their own plans. The Primals had let Elizabeth loose, and the rate at which she killed Dao Lords contributed greatly to the reduction of the strain on the universe.","Then there was that whole incident with the Innkeeper, and his teleportation which caused the Path of Chaos to develop a means to isolate the universe from his reach. That had really helped them hide traces of their activities far better than they had planned.","While on the surface, it seemed like the destruction of the Major realms was causing the Dream realm to become weaker, what people didn’t know was that a majority of the living beings from those destroyed realms were being funneled into the Dream realm.","The Dao Lords were being put to sleep and used to manufacture Dao Essence, which was helping them move their plan along even further. The Dream realm had really thought that planning against the entire universe would be a whole lot harder than it actually turned out to be. Heck, no one had come even close to figuring out the Dream Master’s identity, origins or motives.","It was no wonder the Dream Master was humming. Yet suddenly, the Dream Master looked in a certain direction in surprise.","\"Oh?\"","It couldn’t be helped. All beings from across the universe were trying to figure out ways to exit the Dream realm. This was actually the first time the Dream Master had seen someone break into the Dream realm, and in such a spectacular fashion as that.","\"Shall I go take care of it?\" asked a shadow that appeared behind the Dream Master. After a moment, though, the Dream Master shrugged. A single glance was enough for the Dream master to understand the intricacies involved in Lex’s actions.","\"Nah, it’s fine. It’s just some children playing. Besides, he’s doing a good job at distracting the Humanoid Alliance, not to mention he’s the son of the Innkeeper. Just let him do his thing.\"","The shadow disappeared, though a box of popcorn appeared in the Dream Master’s hands. There was no reason not to enjoy such a good show.","Within the Joro realm, River and Pearl had finally gotten settled into a Humanoid Alliance base, but they could hardly focus on that. They, much like everyone else, looked in the direction of the energy storm that had shaken the whole realm!","Just like everyone else, they were looking up Lex Williams, trying to figure out who this person really was and why he was so strong. At the same time, they could not help but take stock of his amazing strength. Time and time again, he had told them that their results were unsatisfactory, but they just assumed he was just trying to motivate them to work harder.","Now they finally understood that they really did need to work harder because... the standards of their teacher were far beyond what they could hope to achieve by normal means.","Within the Midnight realm, an army was getting ready. From deep within the halls of the Midnight Tailors, the sounds of an evil, maniacal laughter could be heard while in other corners of the Inn workers prepared themselves to go to war.","Moon and Velma were supposed to have a meeting, but that had been paused because too many of them had sensed the same thing. Lex was doing something big. While they didn’t know just yet what that big thing was, it was good to know that he was alive and well.","While these few did not know what was happening, Marlo looked up at the massive screen in the middle of the stadium and watched an image of Lex appear, getting smashed in the face by a lightning bolt.","\"Oh lawd, did he just try to eat that lightning? Doesn’t he know that lightning is not food?\" asked the Drama-cat sitting on Marlo’s right shoulder.","\"Nay, my ill informed companion, he is not partaking in the consumption of lightning. What you are seeing is a medical procedure called a ’facial’ which is meant to rejuvenate and energize the skin on the patient’s face,\" said the other Drama-cat.","On the screen, when the smoke around Lex’s body disappeared, what was revealed was half his skull with his skin burnt off, and the other half with some skin still left. Of course, the skin was also rapidly growing back - looking fresh and energized, just as the Drama-cat had claimed.","Marlo, as usual, ignored the other two and just looked at Lex on screen. Suddenly, he couldn’t help but feel like his own path of Prime wasn’t nearly as impressive as he had originally thought.","He could not help but think back to that one time he had been invited to join the Inn. If he had accepted back then, instead of rejecting, what would things be like now? Would he also be... that strong?","Lex, of course, knew nothing about what all the others were thinking or doing. He had accompanied the karmic storm as it empowered his Major tribulation into searching for his body. But there was one issue.","The momentum of the storm was too great. The tribulation was further empowered by the karmic storm so it struck the very first moment it detected him, and alongside that lightning bolt came his necklace as well.","When the lightning bolt broke the barrier around his stalker, Lex immediately regained control of his original body. He used that opportunity to kick his stalker in the face, both to vent some of his frustrations, and also to build a bit of distance between the two of them.","The distance was the real important thing, because when the lightning came, what had truly caused it to turn maroon was his own necklace. The thing that slammed into his face, and burnt off his skin, was not the lightning bolt, but the force of his own necklace slamming into his face with the momentum of a storm that had transcended realms!","Yet when the necklace and his body finally reunited, Lex immediately absorbed the necklace into his own body. It was no longer useful as a hidden backup since its existence had already been exposed. In that case, the best use for it was to absorb the necklace, and to strengthen his main body alongside it.","The moment the fusion took place, the absorption rate of the Double Yang Disaster Rose skyrocketed! Lex’s connection to the phoenix aspect of his own being began to increase, and fortunately, that allowed him to heal the burnt off skin on his own face.","Now, it was time for some payback."]},{"number":2418,"title":"Chapter 2418: Try to resist - Song recommendation Thunderstruck by AC/DC","paragraphs":["Daekol found it hard to believe, but he was forced to nevertheless. The human had somehow found a way back. He clearly had countless contingencies in place, proving that he was a formidable enemy that should not be underestimated. If that wasn’t the case, he would not have survived, and he certainly would not have been able to take back his body despite all of his preparations.","Daekol did not get angry, though admittedly he did feel frustration at his repeated failures. He suppressed that frustration as quickly as it appeared, however. Instead, he used the momentary respite to analyse the situation and discover his mistake.","From the start, it seemed like his greatest mistake was to underestimate the human. It seemed to Daekol that the human had anticipated that Daekol would underestimate him, and used that to his own advantage.","Since that was the case, he would no longer make the same mistake. All it took was a split second for Daekol to analyse why everything had gone wrong, and to fix the mistake. He would no longer try to take control of the system. Instead, he would use the human to stabilize the leaking Primordial energy within his own system, and once that was done, he would...","No, if he used the human to fix the Primordial energy, he’d have to give back the access to his own system, which was dangerous. In that case, he’d need to suffer a loss and accept that he couldn’t get the optimal outcome from this system. Still, just by selling it to the system-hunter groupchat, he could make a significant profit and upgrade his own system that way.","Such a path would give him the least benefits, but that was, ultimately the result of something the human had forced upon Daekol. Respect. The humans incessant attempts to interfere with Daekol’s plans, to the point of success, had earned Daekol’s respect.","Only the strong deserved respect, and at that point they warranted caution too. Daekol had grand ambitions in life, and he would not let paltry things such as arrogance and greed bar his path.","Daekol looked at the human, his face slowly being reconstructed, and then up in the sky. For the first time since targeting Lex, Daekol finally encountered something that caused him to pause.","\"Did you... use a tribulation to find your real body? And you triggered it?\" Daekol asked, feeling profound confusion. \"Before initiating a big fight against me, a fight you have already lost once, you felt like triggering a tribulation that would only make it that much harder for you to fight?\"","In truth, Daekol didn’t really care if Lex did stupid things. The issue was... if Lex died during the tribulation, then the system would be lost! Was this... the ultimate contingency? To what extremes was the human willing to go?","Daekol’s evaluation of Lex shot through the roof as he realized that he was not fighting a mere human, but a genuinely formidable enemy!","Lex, meanwhile, was not even considering the tribulation as a serious threat at all. The reason his face was damaged was not because of the lightning, but because of the damned necklace! In a way, it could be stated that it was not the tribulation, but Lex himself who blew half his face off!","He’d even been through a damn, Primordial Major tribulation. How could an ordinary Major tribulation even register as a threat to him any more?","\"What the hell are you talking about? Using tribulations to fight is my signature move,\" said Lex with a smile, looking particularly terrifying with half his skull exposed. \"I must really thank you for taking such good care of my body while I was away. Allow me to share some of my hospitality with you.\"","Daekol was no longer listening. He was calculating the perfect battle strategy to incorporate the tribulation into his own attacks to target Lex and...","Daekol’s eyes narrowed when he realized that he lost sight of Lex. Out of sheer instinct, he dodged just in time to avoid the razor edge of Naraka, keeping his neck. Honestly, a simple sword should not have been enough to cut him so he didn’t know why his instincts had warned him.","No, he did know. Lex was clearly much stronger than before.","Daekol threw out all unnecessary thoughts and focused on the goal.","\" Slow ,\" he commanded using his Sovereign authority to influence Lex, but something unexpected happened. Instead of Lex slowing down, a strange red tint spread out from Lex’s body enveloping the entire region.","\" Kneel ,\" Lex commanded using Supremacy, alongside the fake Sovereign authority he had within this superimposed realm. His command, with the impact of a sledge hammer, crashed into Daekol’s body and caused him to temporarily feel weak in his knees. Without even realizing it, he had almost kneeled!","Shock finally appeared for the first time within Daekol, yet there was no time to dwell on it for Lex, unfortunately, no longer planned on savoring this battle as much as he had originally wanted to. With Z’s whereabouts unknown, and the condition of the Inn in question, he could not justify wasting time beating up a stalker.","Lex teleported right in front of Daekol, his hand already grasping his stalker’s neck. After working on Lex’s body for so long, he had developed an immense amount of karma with Lex, and now all of it was going to be used against him.","Daekol could not see, but in Lex’s eyes there were countless threads between him and his stalker. Each one of those threads was a weapon in Lex’s hand.","\"Are you ready?\" asked Lex as he raised Daekol’s body up in the air. \"Try to put up some resistance. It would be a shame if I prepared so much to face you, and you end up not being worth it at all.\"","Before Daekol could respond in any way, the next lightning bolt from Lex’s tribulation struck down, slamming through Daekol’s body.","That... was much too fast for a normal tribulation. Ordinarily, the tribulation needed to build up energy for each strike. This time, however, Lex personally collected so much energy for the tribulation to strike him with.","Moreover, since the tribulation judged that Daekol was interfering with Lex’s tribulation, it increased its lethality by a lot. Normally, he’d be able to use his Sovereign authority to avoid this kind of disaster, but the red tint coming from Lex’s body seemed to be suppressing his Sovereign nature.","Daekol narrowed his eyes and ignored the damage he had accumulated. Instead, he pulled out his weapon, a large sledge hammer the same size as his body. This had long since transcended the point of being a joke.","Author’s Note: Many readers are confused so I thought I’d reiterate this within the text of the Chapter. Innkeeper release is 2 Chapters on weekdays, 1 Chapter on weekends, all released at 1 am + 8 GMT time (or 1 hour after reset on web.novel). Also, I usually leave a message in the discord if the Chapter will release later than scheduled."]},{"number":2419,"title":"Chapter 2419: Betting pool","paragraphs":["\"What are you watching?\" asked Cide as he walked into the theater and joined Agemo and the others, looking at the screen displaying two figures standing face to face with their weapons drawn.","\"It’s the latest live stream on Daoflix,\" replied Agemo without looking back. Daoflix was a streaming service that was only accessible to Dao Lords for it was transmitted via waves only Dao Lords could access. For the low, low price of 1 drop of Dao Essence per ten millennia, any Dao Lords could access the streaming service.","Other than a lot of entertainment material, Daoflix was filled with latest updates, research, and confidential information making it worthwhile for many Dao Lords.","In this case, Cide, Agemo and several other Dao Lords were living inside a vast ship they had created that forever traveled the Void while remaining hidden. They had run away from their Major realms when they started to be destroyed, committed to hiding until the universe stabilised once more.","They had brought alongside with them countless minor realms in which they carried their followers and families, and enough resources to last them a long time. This was not to mention that their ship absorbed chaos energy from the void to constantly produce a very comfortable environment within the ship for them.","With not much else to do, many of the Dao Lords began producing Dao Essence, or went to sleep, or just watched Daoflix to pass the time.","\"That one, the one with a hammer, is a Celestial Apex from the Path of Chaos, and a Sovereign with a very high bounty. The one with a sword is a human from an organization called the Midnight Inn with a suspected prestigious lineage, but there’s no proof of that yet,\" explained Agemo.","Cide watched the screen for a few moments, and then looked at his companions in confusion.","\"Why are we watching some Celestial Apex fighting when there are literal realm wars going on?\" he asked in confusion. Yeah, maybe this fight was good, but could it compete with actual realm wars? Unlikely.","\"Because of the betting pool,\" Agemo said without looking away from the screen. \"I don’t know if you heard about the Primordial Tea party, but that was a big thing that happened a short while ago. Well, a lot of Dao Lords who attended it set up a betting pool, and all of them bet a tremendous amount that the human will win. It’s become so massive that someone has bet an Edolix shard on the human human winning.","Now countless Dao Lords are betting against him just to get a chance on winning that shard. The total value of the betting pool has surpassed the theoretical value of an entire Major realm. Did I mention that the fight started only four seconds ago? There’s no guessing how big this betting pool is going to become.\"","Cide’s jaw dropped and he looked back at the screen in horror. An Edolix shard? What the hell was the background of this human?","\"How the hell are they certain that no one will interfere in the fight with a betting pool like that?\" Cide asked.","\"The Dao Lords from the Tea Party have taken charge of that, led by Ventura. Regardless of who wins or loses, no external Dao Lords will be able to interfere.\"","Cide did not know how to respond to such an absurd situation. How was it that in a universe where Major realms were literally being destroyed left, right and center, the biggest entertainment event was somehow a fight between two Celestials... no wait a minute, was the human undergoing his Celestial Immortal tribulation during the fight?","Cide himself did not know when he sat down to watch the fight, but all his attention was now focused on the fight, and the betting pool. There was a grand conspiracy involved in this, he was sure of it. But who cared? It wasn’t like his money was involved in this.","Lex, entirely unaware of the extent of attention his karmic storm had caused him to attract, looked at Daekol. Defeating him would not be an easy task, and killing him would be even harder. However, he did not doubt for a moment that he could do it.","First, he had to dismantle the universal feedback and nourishment that a Sovereign received constantly. He had done his research on how to kill a Sovereign in the time he was away, so he knew exactly what to do.","Lex’s figure suddenly vanished once again, and Daekol realized that Lex was not only moving at speed that made him too fast to follow, but that within this red tinted realm he could no longer see or speak to the laws Lex used.","\" Hit ,\" Daekol commanded as he waved his hammer, no longer attempting to speak to external laws, but the laws within his hammer. The hammer itself never made contact with Lex, but the moment Lex targeted a law touching Daekol’s body, the full force of the hammer seemed to transmit through the law onto Lex!","And yet... Lex lost not an iota of momentum. To influence even just a 51% Primordial Dao body, the amount of strength and the intensity of the laws that were required far surpassed what Daekol had imagined! That was merely to influence it. To actually stop it...","Daekol stumbled back, mainly from the shock his own hammer gave him, just in time to feel a seething blade cut through something far more intimate to him than his own flesh! Lex’s blade cut at his Sovereign authority - or rather, the connection between his authority and the universe itself!","The connection between a Sovereign and the universe was bound from the most pure law of Tether, meaning that it was not a subsidiary law like karma or fortune. It was Tether itself which tethered Sovereigns and the universe together. To even touch such a connection, let alone cut at it, required a level of power most Celestial Immortals could never hope to achieve.","Lex, however, was neither a Celestial Immortal, nor did he hope to cut that connection. He was just a man who let go of all his inhibitions, and let his Dao Intentions resonate with the core of his very intent!","The suddenness of the pain, and the severity of it caused Daekol to grunt and stumble back. For the first time in a long time, Daekol tasted blood in his mouth. It tasted like... weakness.","Daekol narrowed his eyes and activated a Lawcraft, enveloping his body in a purple aura, isolating his laws from Lex’s reach.","When Lex tried to cut at them again, he felt the purple light singe his very soul, causing him to jump back as he analyzed what had caused even the slightest hint of harm to his newfound body and soul. It was a Lawcraft made from pure Hollow."]},{"number":2420,"title":"Chapter 2420: The Red Moon rises - Song Recommendation You’re going down by Sick Puppies","paragraphs":["Although he was nowhere near completing his Dao Body, Lex knew that it wasn’t so simple to damage him anymore. The reason he’d been hurt by the tribulation was because of his necklace. The actual tribulation itself was completely negligible to him.","He had reached a level that most Celestial Immortals across the universe weren’t even qualified to hurt him. It was straight up impossible for them even if Lex just stood there and let them do whatever they wanted. Yet his stalker had immediately found a way to counter him after clashing with him just once.","Considering how far he had been able to push Lex in the first place, he expected nothing less of him now. If he had merely relied on his identity as a Sovereign to face his enemies, he would have never reached his state today. Clearly, he had other skills and abilities within his arsenal.","It was extremely rare for a Lawcraft to be made of such pure laws, for most Lawcrafts were complex and built up an entire working system of laws interacting with each other. The purple hue surrounding the stalker, however, was almost entirely made up of the law of Hollow.","\"For the accomplishment of making me take this seriously, I honor you with the knowledge of who will defeat you,\" said the stalker as he slowly lifted his hammer and pointed it towards Lex. \"I am Daekol, the Seraph of Calamity, killer of Sages, and I will grant you a worthy death.\"","Lex snorted.","\"Tough luck buddy. I ain’t no Sage. But I am Lex, Herald of legendary asskickings, and you’re about to find out why I got that name,\" said Lex, his every syllable carrying an immense amount of Anchor - the very ruling law that governed the physical forces of the universe.","The Hollow and Anchor laws clashed as Lex’s words themselves carried his Dao Intentions, manifesting into an attack.","Lex moved again, not heading for Daekol but targeting laws instead. Attacking his body, for now, would be moot so long as the connection to the universe wasn’t fully severed. The laws, too, were protected by that purple hue, which is why Lex carried Anchor in his attacks, using one Ruling law to counteract another one.","Daekol, in turn, unleashed his own counter attack. A fight of this level and scale no longer took the same form as fights Lex had fought previously. The body and core of the enemy weren’t nearly as important to target as their surrounding laws, their area of control, and the level of their influence on laws themselves.","That was why, compared to lower level fights, immortal battles took so much longer. If Lex was significantly stronger than Daekol, he could ignore all these things and harm Daekol directly using brute force.","Unfortunately, that was not the case, as Lex had learned when Daekol had used that purple hue to protect himself.","The fight became much more complex and strategic than before, yet his inexperience in such types of fights did not put Lex at a disadvantage at all. He was long used to looking at everything from the perspective of a Go board, where every move had direct and indirect consequences.","Gaining and losing territory required both skill, rhythm and intellect. The strength to do all that was merely the most basic prerequisite to even fight on such a level. The problem with such a fight, however, was that it was so complex that even the slightest mistake could cause a sudden shift in the direction of the fight.","Daekol had much experience in such fights and almost immediately he was able to hone in on Lex’s temperament and strategy style. As long as he was able to resist Lex for long enough, he could turn the tables in a decisive moment. Or so he thought.","Just as he was convinced his plan would work, a shift came and Daekol’s eyes narrowed. The critical mistake - the one that was usually hours, days or even weeks in coming - he had made from the very first moment he assumed Lex was targeting him.","His bluster, his confident demeanor, his anger and arrogance - all of it had been a masquerade. From the very first moment he arrived - or probably even from long before then - Lex was not fighting against Daekol, he was setting the stage.","In the future, a system of his own creation would be able to perform the set up for him. For now, though, he needed to set the stage himself. Superimposing the fake realm was the first step. Spreading his influence, taking control of the laws, and turning the battlefield into his own personal territory was what came next.","Domains were a technique used by immortals where they take control of a region by pushing out the influence of all other laws and allowing only the laws they controlled to work. Well, Lex was taking it one step further by turning by taking control of all laws and making them obey only him. He called it his Absolute Domain.","While it appeared to Daekol that Lex had been fighting him, Lex was in truth using every law, every technique he had learned to turn this area into his own Absolute Domain. While the law of Anchor cleared all obstacles, Firmament allowed him to spread his influence to what constituted space within this portion of the Dream realm.","Every step he took, every word he spoke, every law he manipulated was all for the purpose of spreading his karma around this region. He stained this region with his sweat, colored it with his fortunes, influenced it with his will, all in a step by step manner as if everything had been planned by him long ago.","Every clash against Daekol, every struggle, every law used and failed... all of it was to distract from his true goal of establishing his Absolute Domain, all within the territory of his superimposed realm.","Daekol looked at Lex and suddenly saw through his smiling exterior, his cavalier behavior and puerile remarks, and what he saw was a terrifying, calculating calm, holding a tsunami of anger at bay.","Suddenly he remembered the one request Lex had made of him. ’Try to put up some resistance,’ he had said, lest all his preparations be wasted. The words he had originally dismissed as mere bluster now rang in his ears once more, each word laden with a chilling gravity.","Daekol suddenly found himself standing in a nightmare with a massive, with a red moon slowly rising in the sky above him, tinting all of reality in the color of blood. Some of the killing intent Lex had revealed to the Humanoid Alliance earlier finally began to leak out, and Daekol for the first time saw who... or rather what Lex had returned as after his defeat at his own hands.","\"I wonder,\" said Lex, his voice filled with such authority that it pressed down on Daekol’s body, once again pushing him down, trying to force him to kneel. \"Which do you think is superior, your Sovereign authority, or my Supremacy?\"","Though it was a question, it came with its own answer. The Celestials of the Humanoid Alliance had merely seen the first stage of what Lex had planned on. This red tinted nightmare was merely the second stage. Lex would see how many stages Daekol could witness before succumbing to his Supremacy.","Daekol, meanwhile, realized that he had been fooled from the very beginning, and found himself in a troublesome situation. Yet it was when he was in the most danger when he himself was the most dangerous. The outcome of this fight was far from decided."]},{"number":2421,"title":"Chapter 2421: Return of the Inn","paragraphs":["Actually, the terrifying, calculating perception Daekol gained of Lex wasn’t entirely accurate. That wasn’t to say that he wasn’t calculating, or calm, or that all of this hadn’t been a part of his plan. It was just that he also hadn’t faked his curses, and he really had been excited to beat up Daekol.","The reason why, at the moment, he looked so terrifying was because he had to use a lot of his focus and energy while turning his second phase from a mere concept into reality. The immense shock caused by Lex onto Daekol caused him to evaluate Lex’s behavior into the same categorization as himself.","Thus, in every one of Lex’s actions and behaviors, he saw a deeply sinister intent.","Lex, meanwhile, was checking the state of his Absolute Domain. One very important reason that he had changed his original plan of pulling Daekol into his self created realm was simply because of how easy it was to destroy realms.","Lex could shatter space even before he became an Immortal, and that was for a naturally formed, extremely stable realm. If he fought inside his own self created realm, he’d need to divert a significant amount of his attention on keeping the realm stable.","If he superimposed it upon other realms, he could piggyback on their stability. The trade off, however, was the extent of his control over the region of his fake realm lessened, and as did the magnification of his own Supremacy to the point of reaching Sovereignty. That, however, could be fixed by developing his own territory in steps or phases.","The deployment of his fake realm, and its subsequent development during each fight was a complex process, and he needed a name for it - if only for himself. The Absolute Domain was what he established within his territory, so that’s not what this entire process could be called.","Since his enemy in this case was a Sovereign, and his own goal as well was to become a Sovereign within this space he created, Lex instantly decided on a name that would sufficiently... honor his current opponent.","Just in case the sarcasm wasn’t detected, Lex would make sure that Daekol understood that he chose this name to taunt Daekol!","It barely took Lex a mere moment to think all this through. Of course, Daekol watched the silent, brooding Lex and assumed that he was planning something terrifying. With the blood red moon hanging directly above Lex, Daekol couldn’t really be blamed for misunderstanding him.","\"My Sovereign authority against your Supremacy... that is a challenge you may regret issuing,\" said Daekol as he equipped his armor and got ready for an intense fight. It had been a very long time since he was in such a disadvantaged position.","\"I can sense your confidence wavering,\" said Lex with a soft smirk, noticing how Daekol had said he ’may’ regret it. \"Then again, that’s the kind of thing that happens when I deploy my... Sovereign realm.\"","The moment Lex’s words ended his body disappeared, and Daekol and Lex clashed once more, but this time in a very different way. This time, Lex attacked Daekol’s body directly, while the Sovereign realm itself worked on severing and subduing the connection Daekol had with the universe.","Why did Lex need to restrict himself to just one method and target of attack? He could target several targets all at once - he just needed to be tactical about it. The thing that allowed him to increase his own Supremacy, and suppress Daekol within his Sovereign realm was incrementally populating the place with laws, skills and abilities that he excelled in.","Daekol wasted no more effort exchanging words - it was pointless unless his goal was to distract his opponent. Such a thing would not work with Lex. Instead, he focused on absolute domination. He no longer even thought about capturing Lex or acquiring the system.","The severity of the situation demanded that he give it his all.","He summoned his strength, honed his authority, equipped all his tools and began to utilize all his powers. A small white ball appeared in front of his hammer, seemingly entirely of white light. The purity of the light cut through even the tint of the red moon and directly struck at the Sovereign realm.","He smashed the hammer into Naraka, but the part that made contact was the ball of light suddenly causing a quake in the very laws of the Dream realm itself. Lex coughed out a hint of blood as the damage to the Sovereign realm caused a backlash at him, though his eyes remained fixed on the ball of light.","That was... the theoretical opposite of a black hole - a white hole. That thing not only caused issues with any laws it touched, but disrupted time-space itself!","Daekol looked up into Lex’s eyes, his entire being defiant and ready to face whatever Lex threw at him.","Lex exerted his control over his Sovereign realm, restored it, and resumed the fight. Daekol slammed his hammer one more time, but this time the hammer actually made contact with the white hole and then... traveled through it as if it was an illusion. Except now, the surface of the hammer was covered in a white light as if the white hole had changed shape, and had now itself become the hammer!","Lex wasn’t intimidated in the slightest, attacking once more with Naraka, the white light of his sword intent competing against the white hole for which shone brighter! The weapons clashed, but this time there was no disruption of laws. In fact, Daekol felt as if he hadn’t touched Lex’s sword at all.","Yet the faint, white drizzle that began to fall from the sky said otherwise. Lex’s sword intent did not attack, but instead became a part of the Sovereign realm, adding a new color to it and bringing it into the next step.","The suppression on Daekol became greater, but there was no time to dwell on that. Daekol attacked again, this time his attack rising at the same time as the lightning of Lex’s tribulation fell.","Lex smirked as he activated the next step of his plan, and entered the first proper form he ever unlocked - the Lotus form!","Lightning struck Lex but there was no bang - no thunder at all. It was as if the lightning itself got lost inside a limitless well. The World Seed Lotus, later having evolved into a Realm Seed Lotus, was the master manipulator and devourer of all energy, from the Primordial Origin Lotus series.","That naturally included the energy from a tribulation, as well as the energy from a mythical white hole or white hammer, or whatever else!","With his left hand Lex caught the hammer, and in the moment the Sovereign was shocked, with his right hand he stabbed Daekol. Long before he exited the Hollow, Lex felt confident enough to face his stalker. Yet he continued to stay, and he continued to grow stronger. The true extent of Lex’s power, even he himself did not know yet.","\"I think this is sufficient setup for a special gift I prepared for you,\" said Lex as Daekol retreated, pulling his hammer free. Lex’s eyes began to shine as he channeled the tremendous amount of energy his Lotus form had gathered into one of his latest Lawcraft, inspired directly by the Gilded Hollow.","The laws of the Sovereign realm began to bubble as a massive structure appeared around Lex and Daekol, swallowing them inside.","\"Welcome to the Abaddon Inn ,\" Lex said as he used a Lawcraft that was supposed to never exist outside the absurdity that was Abaddon itself. But within the Sovereign realm, where his Supremacy was meant to be uniquestioned and he had absolute control, he could forcefully recreate the required madness for this technique.","This wasn’t even the Lawcraft he had designed using the eight retributions specifically to fight Daekol. Nay, this was something he just realized his Sovereign realm should enable him to do if he played his cards right. As for whether Daekol could actually live long enough to see all the cards Lex had prepared... they’d just have to find out.","Daekol dismissed his white hammer form - one of his most powerful techniques that usually allowed him to break through any and all of his enemies Lawcrafts. Lex’s current strange state allowed him to absorb energy more easily than anything Daekol had ever seen, so the white hammer was absolutely useless against him. He would have to try something else.","But first, he needed to protect himself from the horror of this Inn. He could feel it sapping at the sanity within his spirit, devouring it as if it was starved of reason.","Dark scales emerged from Daekol’s body, the lines between the scales filled with thin lines of flowing, blue magma as the hammer was filled with the aura of a flame Daekol himself had created.","The technique that Lex thought he had lost began to slowly work, trading its absorbed reason for madness, as it attempted to capture the horrors Lex had once experienced.","Oh, and while that happened, the soft drizzle of sword intent ate at Daekol’s energy and strength, attacking slowly but unceasingly. As for Lex...","Naraka flashed once, its strikes replacing the sound of thunder that Lex’s tribulation failed to cause."]},{"number":2422,"title":"Chapter 2422: The best","paragraphs":["Lex was entirely and totally focused on his match. Even with his best instincts, though, there was no way of knowing that he was being spied upon by countless Dao Lords from across the universe. Not only could he not sense it, he could not have even imagined that so many Dao Lords would be interested in watching him.","Previously Nuwa used to hide him, and after that he had the Masterless technique to hide him. But using the Masterless technique himself would be useless after pulling a stunt like the karmic storm, which is why he had stopped using it when he did that. The last thing he wanted was to let the Dao Lords who notice the Karmic storm notice that he had a technique that could cause them to overlook him.","As a result, when he unleashed his long lost technique, he had not imagined that countless Dao Lords were watching him, eating snacks and betting on the fight. The mere name of the technique, however, caused some information that had successfully stayed hidden for ages to spread across the universe in an instant.","\"Abaddon?\" muttered Cide as he watched the fight. He had no idea what the significance of the name was, but he could feel that it was not normal. There was a massive secret involving the name. The strange thing was... how could a mere Immortal know about a secret that alluded him?","It was fine if he didn’t know about it before, but how could it stay hidden from him even after he learned of its name and tried to look into it?","Cide was not alone. So many Dao Lords suddenly became curious about Abaddon, though no one could say whether that was a good thing or bad.","Just out of the sheer novelty of an immortal knowing a secret even Dao Lords did not, many placed bets on Lex’s victory. Not to mention, this was a piece of direct and irrefutable proof of Lex’s deep background.","The fight, meanwhile, continued. Despite the direct clashes, the increasingly abstract nature of their fight could not be denied. For example, what Daekol had previously summoned was not really a white hole - more like he had relied and used the concept of one. Similarly, Lex did not materialize a physical building out of nothing when he revealed his technique.","They were manipulating laws, tapping into powerful concepts and using them for their own advantage. Thus, Lex tapped into the strength of Abaddon with his technique and relied on it to affect Daekol’s sanity while Daekol used his blue flames to infect Lex’s techniques.","This blue flame of his did not create heat, but instead spread out a strange kind of corruption in the same way that heat spread. This corruption targeted not just Lex’s control of laws, but the function of laws themselves.","This was not the kind of flame Lex could resist since he was not the target to begin with. Instead, each and every law that felt the corrupting influence of the blue flames started to misbehave. Moreover, they became even more active than they were normally, so that reality itself began to warp.","Let alone Lex’s Sovereign realm, even the Dream realm itself could not resist the influence of Daekol’s flames. A solemn expression filled Lex’s eyes, for while he expected Daekol to put up a fight, he had not anticipated something like this. Those flames, if found independently, would be at least a Dao level resource!","The thin lines of blue magma spread throughout his scales became Daekol’s biggest defense, protecting him from any laws that targeted him, while the flames that enveloped the hammer became his greatest weapon.","If Lex didn’t find some way to stop the influence of the flames, it would only be a matter of time before the Sovereign realm would dissipate, let alone the Abaddon Inn. The two locked eyes, and then clashed again.","This time, the lightning from the tribulation struck at the same time as their clash, and Lex had to admit that the lightning was finally beginning to tingle. Or maybe that was just the laws that bound his body together beginning to misbehave under the influence of the blue flames.","Lex’s Lotus form was useless when the obstacle in front of him had nothing to do with energy, and instead was solely a result of the action of laws. He did, however, have a form which could help with that.","Lex and Daekol clashed, the hammer and Naraka clashed, and with each single clash both of them suffered injuries on their bodies to say nothing of the Sovereign realm itself. It was not so easy to harm Lex’s new body, but Daekol managed it nevertheless. Similarly, Daekol had spent a considerable amount of time strengthening his body, but the immense strength packed within Lex’s body made him a living, breathing embodiment of Anchor making it hard to resist his strength.","They both stood near the absolute peak of power beneath the Dao Lord realm, so naturally their every clash caused an immense amount of destruction. To help the realm survive, and also to aid it in surviving the presence of the unusual blue flame, Lex began to include his understanding of defensive laws to the Sovereign realm.","But considering how quickly the realm was unraveling, Lex would need to do something about the blue flame first!","Naraka trembled in Lex’s hand, not just because of the immense strength contained within Daekol’s hammer, but also because the blade itself was filled with intense fighting spirit. It, too, wanted to demonstrate the versatility of Lex’s power. The issue was, Lex had a very diversified fighting style which is why he had never focused on one specific tool or technique. His vision was always broad. Thus, Naraka did not have as much of an opportunity to shine.","But, since the blade yearned for it, Lex was not above listening to it. He channeled his energy into his sword so that the next time he clashed against Daekol, it caused an explosion, sending the two of them away from each other momentarily.","That momentary relief was all Lex needed. He exited his Lotus form, and quickly entered into... the best form!","Coincidentally, that was also the form in which his control over the Sovereign realm was maximised, not to mention improve his control over laws, improve his naturally good looks and solve all his problems.","Dragon-Lex grinned as he flapped his wings, rocketing forward towards Daekol at a breakneck speed. The sword and hammer clashed once again, but this time... the blue flames seemed to bend away from the blade, as if they were exposed to something that could naturally resist their corruptive influence.","\"You are pretty good, but I ... am the best,\" said Dragon-Lex as he saw his Domination able to push away the blue fire.","\"That is questionable,\" muttered Daekol as he twirled the hammer and slammed it towards Lex’s face. Lex blocked with his sword, but in the process, lost sight of Daekol for a moment. When he lowered his sword, he found that Daekol had vanished entirely. His entire aura was gone, and even using his control over the Sovereign realm he could not sense the Sovereign.","Dragon-Lex raised an eyebrow, and casually looked around the area, sure that the enemy would not just run away so easily. Then again, he also wasn’t sure where he had gone, and how he had vanished.","\"I do not blame you for running,\" Dragon-Lex spoke into emptiness, the absolute certainty carried in his voice translating into a torrent of Dao Intentions like never before. \"It is the burden of having a visage as glorious as mine - it inspires insecurities in all who bear witness.\"","His Dao Intentions roared like a vicious animal as they spread across the territory, aggressively and forcefully implanting insecurities in anything and everything - alive or not.","Daekol himself remained entirely immune to such an attack, and he focused on his attack. The very laws of the attack he was building, though, weakened just enough for Dragon-Lex to detect it.","The smirked widened, and instead of attacking Dragon-Lex spread his wings and opened his hand, making himself a massive target.","\"Come. Attack. Let me feel with my body just how strong you are, Daekol ,\" he roared. Of course, as he did that, he also strengthened his control over his Sovereign realm, imbuing his Domination into the very fabric of the realm. At the same time, the structure of the Abaddon Inn, which had been weakened by the blue flames, began to rumble and grow behind Dragon-Lex.","If Daekol did not stop him, the influence of the structure would become too massive to ignore, which forced him to attack even before he was ready.","A dart made azure flames slammed into Dragon-Lex’s body, causing the scale on his body to slightly crack and threatening to shatter his form and return him to his regular state. Yet Dragon-Lex seemed not bothered in the slightest. Instead, he just grinned even wider.","\"Damn, I’m just too good,\" he whispered before flapping both his wings.","Daekol’s eyes suddenly narrowed as his body screamed danger. Yet Dragon-Lex moved too fast. Daekol only barely sensed the danger before Dragon-Lex was already behind him."]},{"number":2423,"title":"Chapter 2423: Revealed secrets","paragraphs":["Daekol was good, of that there was no doubt. Dragon-Lex wasn’t looking down on the fellow. There was no doubt that he was, in fact, the most formidable enemy Dragon-Lex had ever faced. Did that mean that Daekol got special privileges, such as performing sacrilegious acts? Never!","What else was it when Daekol used a unique type of flame in Dragon-Lex’s presence? Sacrilege and nothing less! To have the audacity to flaunt flames in front of a dragon? It was as if Daekol had gone out of his way to specifically request death at Dragon-Lex’s earliest convenience.","If Dao Intentions resonated with every action that Lex took in his normal form, then in his Dragon-Lex form the effect was much more pronounced. Thus, when Dragon-Lex flapped his wings, his Dao Intentions aided in increasing his speed, adding to the element of surprise.","Moreover, when he appeared behind Daekol, even though he hadn’t acted yet, the Dao Intentions were already resonating with his intentions of challenging Daekol’s flames directly.","Dragon-Lex unleashed his Golden Inferno, unleashed a torrent of brilliant, golden flames at point blank.","While the flames themselves carried a destructive force that could cause even stars to destabilize, the true danger in the flames was caused by the Dao Intentions. Daekolo, even cut off from the universe, had experience in law manipulation that non-Sovereigns just couldn’t get.","His self made blue flames directly attacked the most fundamental parts of the universe, causing laws themselves to misbehave. That was not the kind of thing just anybody could pull off. He could cause damage to Lex’s body, even if it was only minor damage, despite him having a 51% Primordial Dao Body. The number of Immortals who could achieve such a thing in the universe were... who knew? But certainly it was not many.","It was an undeniable fact that Daekol was extremely formidable, and not just because he had been born with an incredible advantage. It was his dedication, hard work, and wisdom that had allowed him to get this far. Oh, and there was one more thing that helped him along the way.","When the golden flames incinerated their way to him, threatening even to burn his blues flames that were supposed to distort laws themselves, Daekol did something he had never done before. He used his system to help him in a fight.","His body was suddenly garbed in a thin, protective robe that looked more like a bathrobe than armor. That didn’t change the fact that the flames were entirely resisted by them.","Things like pride were an obstacle in the pursuit of goals, at least in Daekol’s opinion. That had not prevented him from avoiding the direct aid of his system in a fight before today. But when the need arose, there was no resistance or delay. He used it just in time to protect himself from suffering significant harm.","Daekol looked at his system interface and read its title: the Debt System. Anything and everything in the universe had a price, whether that price was literal or metaphysical. Whether he himself was the debtor or the creditor, the limit of things which could be borrowed or loaned were limited only by his system’s rank. His current S ranked system allowed him to borrow or lend many things, but it wasn’t enough to satisfy him. Moreover, the rewards of his quests were also limited by the rank of his own system.","For example, this robe he wore was merely a one time use item that could protect him. It was good enough for now.","He looked at his system, and borrowed the knowledge required to handle and counter a Dao Body from the catalog of things he could borrow. The knowledge itself, naturally, could not be returned so to pay off this debt he would need to pay with something of equivalent value - or accumulate enough debtors to take on the burden of his debt in his place. Regardless, that was a matter for later.","For now, he looked at Lex and immediately understood that the effects of his Dao Body were beyond a normal Dao Body. It didn’t matter.","Daekol activated an ability called Forced Debt, and transferred his own debt to Lex.","Dragon-Lex, who was in the middle of breathing fire, suddenly paused as he did something he hadn’t done since he stepped onto the path of cultivation. He hiccuped, and with great force.","Confusion filled his eyes as he looked at Daekol, and felt a strange weight in the center of his chest - as if his very soul had picked up an invisible weight.","\"I will admit, of everyone I have faced, you really are the best,\" said Daekol as the silk robe on his body faded away. \"Now you will have to face the consequences of being so great.\"","The fight suddenly entered into a whole new territory, because Dragon-Lex could not understand what it was that Daekol had done. Of course, such a feeling also gave him a clear answer as to what it could be. Daekol had just used a system.","All across the universe, countless Dao Lords were watching the fight. Lex’s utterance of the word Abaddon had been heard across the universe, spreading knowledge of a secret that had been hidden for too long.","For some strange reason, though, Daekol’s use of his system remained entirely undetected by almost all the Dao Lords. It was as if they sensed nothing unusual with his actions at all, and instead they saw perfectly reasonable and explainable sequences of events.","The only Dao Lords who did sense something unusual were the ones with systems themselves, Eclipse and only a very few other Dao Lords who already happened to know of the existence of systems for various reasons. What had been so easily missed by so many other Dao Lords was as plain as day to them, as if there was some secret at work that only they could see through.","If only Daekol knew that he had inadvertently revealed one of his greatest secrets."]},{"number":2424,"title":"Chapter 2424: Forced to fight normally","paragraphs":["The battle, in the beginning, was following the trend of Lex gaining overwhelming momentum. No matter how Daekol tried to fight back, his attempts were too feeble to affect Lex. His ultimate weapons, which would have otherwise greatly affected Lex, only barely harmed Lex.","On top of that, Lex’s own attacks kept pushing Daekol to the point where he genuinely felt like he was in danger. His techniques were seen through, his defenses failed him and his life was in danger. It wasn’t a fair fight at all.","Yet the moment Daekol began to use his system, the momentum of the fight changed, and quite drastically at that. Accruing debt suppressed Lex on a fundamental level. The fact that Daekol was his debtor automatically made all of Lex’s attacks against him weaker by a fixed and undeniable 20%.","Lex was more sure than ever that a system had been used against him, but the issue was that he didn’t know the details of how it had been done. He didn’t know if what he had done was repeatable. A strict 20% deduction in his attack damage was something Lex could bear, but if the percentage continued to increase then he’d be in real trouble.","If the percentage doubled to a 40% deduction in his attack power, Lex would directly have to retreat! This was not a video game or novel where sheer willpower could allow one to overcome such immense odds. If his attack power was nearly halved, Lex wouldn’t even be able to damage Daekol anymore, so what would be the point of fighting?","Of course, Lex also wasn’t going to just sit around and wait for Daekol to attack him. Based on his experience with the Galactic Sovereign turtle, and other, weaker system users, he knew that others could externally influence a system. Since that was the case, there was no reason Lex couldn’t influence Daekol’s system too.","In fact, the stronger his Sovereign realm became, the greater his chances were of influencing Daekol’s system, whatever it was.","Dragon-Lex narrowed his eyes and unleashed his Domination in full. Domination, which was originally inspired by Dragons Might, was naturally much more powerful in his Dragon form.","\"You gain the slightest bit of ground, and suddenly you’re filled with confidence,\" said Dragon-Lex as he put away Narka and raised his fists. \"I have the cure for that too though.\"","The reason Dragon-Lex opted to fight barefisted was not just because it would be so satisfying to punch that face.","No, he needed Domination to be as thick and condensed as possible to affect Daekol’s system, which is why he needed to fight as close as possible. That, of course, increased his own risk as well but that was a price he was willing to pay.","At the same time, Dragon-Lex could not help but smile. Since he had been weakened, he’d need to punch him a lot more to do the same amount of damage. That meant he could enjoy beating him up much longer.","The fight resumed, and though it appeared as if they were exchanging physical blows, it also took place in the realm of laws and Lawcrafts. Lex was much too used to ending a fight in a couple of hours because of how overwhelmingly strong he was. But against Daekol, every step needed to be measured, every advantage needed to be snatched with great effort and retained with careful consideration.","For the first time ever, Lex was facing an opponent who was forcing him to adhere to the usual format of fighting among immortals.","While all of that was happening, Lex was also trying to use his Domination to suppress Daekol’s system, all the while continuing to build more Karma between them for an ultimate upset later on. Yet Daekol too was slowly building up debt for his counter attack.","Even if it wasn’t so simple to directly transfer all his debt to Lex, he could take on debt to help him gain the advantage in a fight. He had the patience to continue this fight for a long time. The process did not matter - only the result.","No matter how this fight would end up, it was quickly becoming obvious that it would not reach a resolution quickly. Even though Lex was in a hurry because he wanted to go find Z, he would not let that rush him and lead him into making a mistake.","As it happened, however, within the Midnight Inn, two armies had finally gotten ready to go and rescue Z. Considering the faster flow of time, they had much more time to prepare than Lex, however this mobilisation was still quite rushed.","If it hadn’t been for Velma’s critical intel supplemented by Anita’s battle experience and Hera’s logistical expertise, it would have been difficult to make everything happen so quickly. Of course, just because these three women were leading the administrative charge for the upcoming rescue, it did not mean the men had nothing to do.","The first army ready to rescue Z was, naturally, the existing Midnight battalion. A second, temporary battalion had also been formed during this time, all under Gerard’s oversight.","While Gerard took up the position as battalion leader for the temporary battalion, Luthor adopted a much more specialised role. He was a team leader for a small yet powerful strike team. Leadership was never Luthor’s strong point anyway - his strengths were better demonstrated on the field.","Many, many others had also helped. Brother Chen and Lily, some of the earliest guests of the Midnight Inn, and owners of one of the largest businesses inside the Guild room, openly and readily sponsored the second battalion, using up many of their personal resources to contribute to the army.","Of course, each army member had far more wealth than they knew what to do with, and were more than willing to contribute as well. However, their wealth was mostly in the form of MP. Brother Chen and Lily, however, directly contributed in terms of resources.","Geeves was more than happy to accept those resources, for his requirements for the suits to be worn by the battalion were skyhigh. He even used up his personal stock of rare resources that he usually gathered to use in suits for Lex.","The entire Midnight staff took to heart Brother Chen and Lily’s contribution, even if they claimed it was just their way of repaying the Inn for everything that they had gained from it. Their aid and generosity would not be soon forgotten.","Countless others had also helped, and now the two armies stood ready to depart. Velma, however, was not there yet for she was meeting with one more person who wanted to help them."]},{"number":2425,"title":"Chapter 2425: The woman she had become I","paragraphs":["The Midnight Inn had many allies, and even more who wished for an opportunity to ally with the Inn. Velma had kept a tight lid on the goals and intentions of the Inn, but she had purposefully let some information leak to the right people.","She understood better than most how information traveled. By telling the right people the correct news, she could pass long hidden messages without even the messengers knowing what exactly they were doing. As such, the Henali, Devils, Elves of the Origin realm as well as the Marzu of the Origin realm had all tacitly agreed to lend the Midnight Inn some aid when they took action.","Everything was discreet for now, and the forces moved were such that their displacement would not attract attention. In fact, many more forces were willing to help, but Velma had to turn them away because their movement would attract attention. The dragons of the Origin realm were a notable example of this.","The humans who had fled Earth and used one of the Minor realms within the Midnight Inn were also extremely motivated to help, especially because Z was so extremely popular among them. However, they were too weak to contribute directly, so they instead contributed in terms of resources.","While the Midnight Inn itself was not lacking for resources, the upper limit of the resources the realm could naturally produce was limited to the Earth Immortal realm. Yet they did not, for one moment, feel like they were limited in resources.","The Infinity Emporium practically threw themselves at Velma offering up to 90% discounts on certain items.","Never before was the fondness and love for the Inn felt so strongly by the workers, causing them to feel extremely touched.","Yet all of this had been taken care of before. Velma now was in a meeting with someone she wasn’t sure how to respond to.","\"You do not need to be concerned. At most , I would merely lose this mirror if something unexpected were to happen. No actual harm would come to my body,\" said Moon from within the reflection in the Dreamy mirror.","Velma did not respond, however, as she considered the situation from various angles.","\"If you’re worried about me being an inconvenience to your soldiers, I have already proven that the aid I can provide more than makes up for any inconvenience carrying the mirror causes. The things I can do, no other cultivator can do.\"","The more that Moon spoke, the more troubled that Velma felt. In truth, she was no longer as ignorant as she once was. A single glance was enough for her to understand that there was something incredibly special about Moon - far more than even Lex’s other sister, Liz, who had bonded with a Sovereign.","The breadth of her abilities was so vast that no matter what explanation Velma came up with, she could not pinpoint exactly what the source or origin was. Thus, she also felt that bringing her out was a much greater risk.","Even if it was just through a mirror, bringing Moon out left the chance of exposing her existence and abilities. If even Z could be kidnapped from within the Inn, then Moon was no safer. Hiding her and keeping her out of view was the best way to keep her safe.","Thus, she wanted to deny Moon’s request to go out on the rescue. This was especially since Lex himself wasn’t around either. But Moon was no child. She was a fully grown adult, and a powerful one at that. Her strength could not be limited by things such as cultivation realm any more. If she was willing to go out, then Velma should honor her wish.","Yet she could not reconcile that with her protective instincts either. If Moon was Lex’s sister, then Velma treated her like her own sister. How, then, could she...","\"To be quite frank with you, asking you is only a formality,\" Moon finally said with a sigh, seeing right through Velma’s internal conflict. \"If I want to join, I can.\"","Velma, too, sighed, and then nodded.","\"I hope you understand. It’s not that I want to stop you, it’s just that I don’t want to put you at risk,\" Velma said.","Moon nodded softly, the reflection in the mirror changing from her appearance to the day Lex had appeared to save her. It showed her world. It showed the Immortals who came to kidnap her, and the Jorlam they encountered during their escape.","\"I know just how hard my brother has tried to protect - better than anyone else,\" said Moon from within the voice. \"I don’t want to waste his efforts, but I also refuse to live a life where I do nothing when my friend is in trouble. For all those who helped when I was in need, I cannot just sit back and do nothing when they need me. Staying alive, staying safe, they’re important, but they’re not everything.\"","Velma smiled softly, and genuinely regretted the fact that she hadn’t spent more time talking with Moon. She was such a... splendid young woman.","\"Forgive me, you’re right,\" said Velma as she gently lifted the mirror. \"Welcome to the army. I’ll keep you with me for the greatest coordination. You let me know when you feel like you can aid a situation.\"","Moon nodded, and said nothing else. Velma paused, and wondered if she should tell Moon about her other sister, Belle. Among all the siblings, she was the one with the most unique personality to be sure.","She was doing fine the last time Velma looked up her information, so it was probably best not to mention it for now. She wouldn’t want to distract Moon from the mission. In the meantime, she would look up some effective anger management techniques to share with Moon for whenever she had an opportunity to meet Belle again. It couldn’t hurt... probably.","The distraction lasted only a moment. Velma reappeared in front of the two armies, mirror in hand, her gold silk armor equipped.","Everyone looked to her, including Gerard, Luthor, Anita and all the others. From the very start she had been leading this mission, and the impression everyone had of her evolved very quickly during this time.","She had very quickly gone from that harmless, cute little girl who liked to gossip and chat with everyone to the fearsome, dependable woman who would infiltrate a Dao level organization and organise a raid on another realm to rescue her friend. The gap between those two identities was huge, but even that could not begin to encompass the change Velma had shown during this period.","\"It’s time,\" Velma said, her simple words carrying over to the two armies. She should give a small, motivational speech first though, right?"]},{"number":2426,"title":"Chapter 2426: The woman she had become II","paragraphs":["The two armies were not large - especially when considering that they were about to raid an entire realm. The entire population of that realm, according to the data Velma had collected, was around 3 billion.","Of that, there were around 600 million combatants, most of them in the mortal levels. Naturally, as the cultivation level rose their numbers dwindled, but quantity had its own advantage.","Apparently, the population of the realm used to be far greater, well over 20 billion. However, the realm had suffered from a prolonged war between countless tribal warlords, from among whom the Grand Conqueror had emerged. By the time he unified the realm, the population had dwindled severely.","This 3 billion now was a result of active efforts to regrow the population.","The Midnight Inn wasn’t short of people either. Since they handled billions of guests, the number of workers naturally had to be increased.","Before she became an immortal, Velma never questioned these things. However, after becoming an immortal, and especially after reaching the Celestial Immortal realm, Velma became clear of many things. She and many of the workers of the Inn hadn’t been born naturally.","They had been born directly from the Innkeepers power, even if she did not understand the specific details of how it was done. Whether it was through the DNA of people who were long gone, or through some esoteric spirit or Dao techniques, none of it actually mattered.","What mattered was that most of the workers of the Inn were like her. Such things weren’t entirely uncommon inside the universe. However, the extent of freedom of expression they had been given was very unlike what most organizations did after specially creating workers like them.","Typically, a specific training routine would be followed to indoctrinate them and mould their personalities to the specific needs of whoever had created them. Nothing like that had been done at the Inn, so even though the Inn too had hundreds of millions of workers by now, they had all sorts of personalities.","Since they grew up in a stable and safe environment, most of them were actually not very combative either. They, instead, usually focused on cultivating so that they could be better hosts!","Thus, the number of workers at the Inn, despite also being massive, could not make an army nearly as large as the ones to be found in the realm they were about to invade. In terms of quality, though, there was no equal.","Velma knew that for a fact. Across the entire universe, there was no collection of humans with as much potential as the Midnight Inn. That potential simply needed to be tapped. The Innkeeper chose to tap into that potential for the sake of hospitality. Today, however, they would, of their own violation, channel that potential towards a different kind of hospitality.","\"It’s time,\" she said, her voice carrying a certain kind of power that infected the very bones of all who heard it. \"We have all lived our lives for the sake of welcoming the guests of the Inn, and showing the universe the boundless graciousness and hospitality of the Midnight Inn. We have lived that life, and we have shown the universe our character. In return, so many of our guests have aided us in our time of need - as you all have already seen.\"","The members of the armies nodded subtly, thinking back to everyone who had aided them in preparation for this event.","\"But the universe is a vast place, and alongside those with wisdom, there are those who lack it entirely. The hospitality of the Midnight Inn has been tested. One of our own was taken from within our very homes. It was taken for granted that we, as gracious hosts, would say nothing while others come in and make a mockery of our hospitable nature. Well, now is the time to show the universe what we are like... when we are crossed! No mercy !\"","Velma’s last two words thundered across the Midnight Inn, carrying within them the anger and grievance of one who had been accosted.","\"We go to those who took advantage of us, to those who took one of ours and enslaved them. We are not marauders or bandits, but we are also not lambs who will only bleat while we are slaughtered. To those who have harmed the houses of Midnight, we will show no mercy ! Do not hesitate. Do not hold back. Today, we march with purpose, and the universe needs to feel the depth of our purpose!\"","As Velma’s words echoed, the armies were filled with an unbreakable resolve. There was no hooting, no screaming, no war cries just yet. They were not acting in the heat of passion - no, they were about to carry out a highly strategic and precise set of actions, and that required cooled heads and clear minds.","They were marching today for a purpose, and everything they did now was in service to that purpose.","\"It’s time,\" Velma whispered, repeating the words once more as she sent a signal to the devils awaiting her command. She was the first to vanish, but she was hardly the last. One by one, all the soldiers began to disappear as they were carried over by the devils to the realm they were about to invade.","Luthor, who was standing in one corner, suddenly discovered that... Velma was actually pretty scary. No one else had felt it as clearly as him, simply because he was the one most familiar with Conceptualized Torment - the seed of a hell. The torment itself was irrelevant in this situation. What was more relevant was that Luthor had an in-depth understanding of the deep, more esoteric versions of things like killing intent and bloodlust.","When Velma said ’no mercy’, he could feel the extent of her anger, and he realized that while everyone was incredibly impressed with everything she had achieved so far, in truth she was holding herself back. The moment she stopped doing that and unleashed her anger, they would truly realize what it meant that hell hath no fury like a woman scorned. Or, well, in this case a woman whose younger brother was kidnapped.","Her own nature was that of a friendly, chirpy, happy young girl. It was the universe which had forced into the woman she had now become - and someone was going to pay the price for that dearly"]},{"number":2427,"title":"Chapter 2427: Already taken care of","paragraphs":["Gilded Hollow","Hemzy, the porcupine, opened her eyes and took a deep gasp, coming back to life once more. This was around the fifth time she had been killed by Mithon, and she was running out of cultists to replace her death. She needed to-","Hemzy paused, her mind going blank, as she looked at the angel of death in front of her. Although that was mostly just an expression, the humanoid figure with angel wings, drenched in so much blood that only the color red was visible, standing in front of Hemzy really did look like an angel of death.","Belle looked at the many Seraphim corpses around her, and then at the porcupine beast. She was sure that thing had been dead, but now it had come back to life. She didn’t know what the deal with that thing was, but it was better to be safe than sorry.","\"No, senior, wait!\" Hemzy screamed as she tried to save herself, but it was no use. Belle killed Hemzy with a single slash, and then quickly left the area. She still had a location marker on her, which meant more Seraphim were probably on the way to kill her. Before then, she needed to raise her strength further and maybe set a good trap or two.","A few hours later, the porcupine reattached her head and looked around with an unresigned expression. She needed to quickly find a way out of here and initiate more people into her cult of dopamine cleansing, or else she might really end up dying one of these days.","*****","Conquest Realm","It was an average day in the Conquest realm. Ever since the Grand Conqueror had unified the realm, peace had finally returned, if only within the realm itself. The Grand Conqueror would often go out of the realm to continue his conquests, wage war, win trophies and resources, and continue to grow.","Such things naturally enriched the realm itself, even if it simultaneously put a strain on the realm to produce more warriors. Thus, while there was peace on the surface, an air of intense competition and desperation gripped the lands. Everyone worked day and night in the hopes to become strong, for only the strong had any rights within the Conquest realm.","Mortals... didn’t even have the right to a name. They were identified by the name of the place they resided in, followed by a serial number. Only after becoming Immortal could they have the honor of choosing a name.","Even then, they could only take on a surname by becoming a Heaven Immortal. That, too, was the bare minimum convenience for true prestige, honor and rewards were granted only to capable warriors.","Thus, despite having achieved peace, the mood in the Conquest realm was always tense and filled with a sense of urgency and desperation.","An orc kneeled in front of an altar and completed a ritual, opening a portal and allowing the Devil that the orc had been dealing with to enter.","\"I have done as you asked, oh devilish one. Please, aid me in healing from my injuries faster. If my bones do not recover their former strength, then I will surely fail tomorrow’s monthly combat assessment.\"","A smiling devil, dressed extremely sharply, stepped out from the portal and looked at the orc fondly.","\"Don’t worry Buro-112233, I promised to help you resolve the assessment issue, didn’t I?\" the devil asked warmly. \"It’s just that, rather than healing your bones, I was considering a different solution.\"","Buro-112233 looked at the devil in confusion, unable to understand what he was getting at? If he wasn’t healed, how could the issue of the assessment be resolved?","Before he could ask, a breathtakingly beautiful woman stepped forth from the portal, garbed in golden silk armor.","She glanced at the orc for a brief moment before turning her gaze to the rest of the realm.","\"As per our agreement, the contractor who summoned us here is off limits,\" the devil said with a smile as he looked at Velma. \"I still have my own end of the bargain to fulfil after all. Everyone else... is fair game.\"","Velma glanced at the devil and nodded to him with a polite smile.","\"Pleaure doing business,\" she said before her figure disappeared.","By now, Buro-112233 had caught onto what was happening, but he was too horrified to react. Had he just... allowed enemies to infiltrate the realm?","As if to answer his question, a massive explosion occurred far off in the distance.","\"Come on Buro-112233, let’s grab a good spot to watch the show,\" said the devil as he patted the orc on the shoulder. \"Trust me, there’s no way you’re going to fail any assessments after this.\"","Within the capital of the Conquest realm, the Grand Conqueror immediately opened his eyes when his system gave him an emergency notification.","He wasn’t being notified that the realm was being invaded - no, that’s what would have happened if someone else had attacked. But since this was Velma, a master of manipulating information, the emergency notification that he got was that the system was no longer able to minotaur the realm!","Across the entire Conquest realm, a number of formations were being activated by hundreds of devils, disrupting all monitoring as well as flow of information. These formations had been custom designed by Velma using the Humanoid Alliances formations, and they were specifically for the purpose of disrupting communication during a realm invasion.","Since Velma knew she was doing this, she naturally took advantage of the alliance’s deep history by collecting information about how they usually handled such situations and used the information for herself. Blocking information was, perhaps, the most important thing during a war.","The beautiful thing about Velma’s custom designed formations was that disrupting information was merely the first step. The real fun would only begin after the enemy finally figured it out and began destroying the formations.","Even though this was a major invasion, and even though they were grossly outnumbered, Velma felt not a hint of urgency. Instead, she remained completely calm as she began collecting information from the realm to find Z’s location.","Meanwhile, all across the realm, members of the Midnight Inn were beginning to arrive. They wasted not a single second, for they already had their orders.","Such an invasion was naturally not a secret at all for the Dao Lords of the universe. The members of the Humanoid Alliance, and especially those who were responsible for backing Z’s kidnapping, all realized what was happening.","Before they could even react, a certain message traveled from the Origin realm to the Humanoid Alliance, causing their Dao Lords to pause. None of them had the time to intervene anyway, but just in case any of them felt like it, Velma had already employed defensive measures to protect their invasion from the interference of Dao Lords."]},{"number":2428,"title":"Chapter 2428: Slave legions","paragraphs":["Velma stood in the air high above the Conquest realm, watching and controlling the invasion from a distance. Even though she had the realm infiltrated long ago, and had made thorough preparations, she hadn’t been able to discover Z’s location, which is why she had to search for him now.","That meant countless streams of data were channeled to her every moment, and she had to sift through them. So far, it seemed like all her preparations were useful and meeting her expectations.","Upon that thought, she couldn’t help but think back to the most critical preparation she had to account for: ensuring no Dao Lords interfered. At the Humanoid Alliance, Velma had truly come to learn and understand what level of existence Dao Lords truly were. Exposure to the Innkeeper had made it so that her understanding of the scope of their power was inadequate.","It was not an exaggeration to say that Dao Lords literally did not need anyone else to do anything they needed. People believed that Dao Lords relied on the Immortals in their organization to manage their territories and do menial work, and that’s how they contributed to the empires and forces of Dao Lords.","That was inaccurate. Sentiment and prestige were probably the only two reasons due to which most Dao Lords kept anyone else around. Doing all their work themselves would lower their prestige, so Immortals could do their work for them. Or they could carry sentiment for their families and friends despite becoming Dao Lords themselves, which is why they kept others around.","There could be any other number of reasons, but the point was that they did not need anyone else. Any random Dao Lord could create a ridiculous number of weaker clones to replace immortals to do their work assuming the work had to be done far away. Within the vicinity of their spirit sense, they would not need anyone to do anything at all. Their will alone was enough to make anything and everything they wished come true.","Of course, in the broader scope of things, organisations that spanned entire races had considerations like nurturing more immortals to have more Dao candidates and to slowly and steadily increase the ranking of their race on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum.","No matter how powerful and resourceful Velma was, there was nothing she could personally offer to a Dao Lord to win their favor or get their help. Of course, there was no shortage of Dao Lords willing to sell a favor to the Innkeeper, but she would never use the Innkeeper’s name without his permission.","Thus, she could only rely on a combination of factors to achieve her goal. The Henali already had a good relationship with the Midnight Inn. Moreover, they were a powerful race.","However, even powerful races needed help in growing stronger, and there was no such thing as being too rich.","Among many aspects of their cultivation power, one of the critical things within Henali was bloodline purity, which could be divided into three tiers. Henali with the most basic bloodlines had appearances similar to scorpions. If their bloodline purity grew to an advanced tier, they would grow wings. However, the highest tier bloodline purity changed their appearance altogether.","The growth of their bloodline purity was not associated with lineage or parents, but the cultivation of the spirit. Velma volunteered the entire dataset she had captured of the Humanoid Alliances spirit training techniques, regimen, treasures and so forth to the Henali, including various methods that could be employed within the Origin realm.","She had not dared to bargain or make a request - she directly donated it. It was only afterwards when the Henali contacted her that she expressed her hopes that the Henali might be able to assist her with her problem. It was a mere hope, not a request. She dared not make a request of Dao Lords.","But, considering the relationship between the Henali and the Midnight Inn, they were quite happy to assist. No one made any mention of the Innkeeper. Instead, this entire deal was focused on Velma’s donation, and the future potential she showed.","After Lex, she was the first member of the Midnight Inn who attracted significant attention from the Henali.","That potential alone was enough for the Henali to invest in her by supporting her like this - not to mention it would improve their relationship with the Midnight Inn even more. They were unlike the Humanoid Alliance who would spit on a good deal. Instead, from the earliest days of their relationship with the Innkeeper, they had maintained a firm stance to remain on good terms with him.","Thus, the moment the invasion began, the Henali also sent their letter to the Humanoid Alliance. Alongside the letter was the location of a certain Henali Dao Lord within the Joro realm. If the alliance interfered in the matters of the Conquest realm, then the Henali would interfere in the matters of the Joro realm. This was not a threat but a promise!","Within the alliance, anger grew. The anger was not targeted towards the Henali, but towards the faction that had acted against the Midnight Inn. Their seemingly insignificant action from back then was repeatedly putting the alliance at a disadvantage in an extremely critical time.","At a time when they finally needed to cash in the reputation and prestige they had built across the ages, the stain of that one action made everyone look at them with distrust! Even if they really wanted to, no one was free enough to go interfere in the matters pertaining to an immature realm. Yet not only were they being doubted, one of their greatest allies was silently taking precautions against them!","Velma did not know the details of the exchange that had happened, nor was she bothered with it.","\"Critical intel gathered,\" Velma said, her voice echoing in the minds of millions of Inn workers. \"Z was a member of a Slave Legion. Within the Grand Conquerors army, there are 21 confirmed Slave Legions. This narrows down our search area. Everyone, begin gathering information on the where these legions are posted.\""]},{"number":2429,"title":"Chapter 2429: Massive secret","paragraphs":["Cide had never thought that he’d actually get invested in a fight between two Celestials - not since he became a Dao Lord - but the fight between Lex and Daekol had an intensity that had him on the edge of his seat.","Wherever either of them gained an advantage, the other would pull out some trick to quickly turn the tables, turning their fight into a competition for who had more secret cards. Moreover, they could also see that both fighters were silently preparing for a greater confrontation. It was too thrilling, especially since the level of their power was at the absolute peak beneath the Dao realm. Of course, the true reason that the match felt intense was the immensity of the betting pool!","Even though the actual prize pool would be divided among all who bet on the winner, the sheer size of it was ridiculous. The amount of wealth bet on two Celestial Immortals had to have set some kind of record.","The Edolix shard, especially, attracted a lot of attention.","While watching the fight, a popup suddenly appeared showing an entirely different fight.","\"What’s that?\" Cide asked, and Agemo immediately responded with a laugh.","\"Hah! That looks like another fight going on by the same force that Lex belongs to. They’ve been made a part of this bet. This is crazy!\"","Cide raised an eyebrow, and looked at the leaflet which contained information on both parties, meaning Daekol and the Path of Chaos behind him, as well as Lex and the Midnight Inn behind him.","\"I thought the Inn was supposed to be peaceful. Why the hell are they invading a realm? Did a guest run away without paying the bill?\" Cide asked, confused.","Fortunately, the information on the leaflet was updated in real time.","Agemo glanced at it, and suddenly found it incredibly interesting.","\"Ho ho, look at that. Betrayed by the Humanoid Alliance? For a single Immortal they invaded an entire realm? Is it because he’s special or more specifically to send a message to all who would deign to attack the Inn?\"","As if to answer his question, the leaflet updated once more. On top of that, the leaflet also added a bit of additional information.","\"Oh my, it seems they’re very protective of their own,\" said Cide as he read the leaflet. \"I wonder how they’ll react when they learn the location of the immortal they’re looking for.\"","Suddenly, Agemo felt an itch... and itch to place a bet as well. He wanted to bet... that this matter was far from as simple as it seemed, and whoever was streaming the fights seemed to know something.","There was a conspiracy at play, and there was nothing more exciting than getting involved!","*****","Conquest realm","From the moment the Grand Conqueror had gotten his hands on his system, his system had not failed him even once! It had always been perfect, granting him miracles beyond his imagining and exposing him to a whole new realm of possibilities.","While he dared not be arrogant in front of a Dao Lord, beneath the Dao realm he really didn’t take anyone seriously - at least not with his system to support him. Who the hell could mess with him as long as he had his system?","He still didn’t know, because his system seemed incapable of connecting to the entire Conquest realm at all! It was as if there was some kind of interference between the system and the realm that it could not break through.","Not only could he not access the systems surveillance of the realm, he also couldn’t ascertain the situation with at least 30% of his armies. It was fortunate that he did not completely rely on the system for gathering information, although he did use it for most of it so at the moment he was severely handicapped.","\"Mobilize all forces, deploy all defenses, activate all the... what is it?\" the Grand Conqueror asked as he looked at his assistant who was staring back at him in confusion.","\"Sir you... you always deploy the defenses yourself. No one else knows how to do it,\" the assistant answered, feeling extremely confused.","The Grand Conqueror suddenly went quiet. He’d always directly controlled his army deployments, defense activations and all other war related actions directly from his system interface. Everyone was used to his magical and mystical ways of doing everything, to the point where they did not know how to behave without it.","It was only in that moment that the Grand Conqueror realized just how dependent he was on his system.","\"The enemy has employed some kind of means to interfere with my surveillance and communication systems,\" the Grand Conqueror explained, gathering his thoughts. \"The soldiers are trained enough, they’ll defend themselves until they get other orders. What we need to do is figure out how I’m being blocked and stop it. The fact that the blockage is not 100% effective means that there are gaps in the enemies methods.\"","The assistant nodded and quickly went to gather the nearby soldiers while the Grand Conqueror looked at his system. While it was disconnected from other things, his own augmentations could still be implemented.","What neither the Grand Conqueror, nor Velma herself realized was that the suppression of the system surveillance and many of its functions were not a deliberate plan implemented by Velma. They had inadvertently encountered a massive mystery or secret of some kind.","Velma herself had no knowledge of systems, so how could she plan to suppress it? The actual suppression of the system happened because Velma was utilizing customized versions of formations used by the Humanoid Alliance during wars and invasions.","It was her own customizations which reduced the effectiveness of the formations against systems. Had she used the authentic thing, the system would have been suppressed entirely.","But there was no way for Velma to know such a thing because there was no mention of it in the Alliance’s data records, and the annotations of the formations did not mention this specific use either. It was as if a huge secret was being kept by the alliance, or that the alliance itself did not realize that during its wars, it suppressed systems.","Of course, Velma had customized the systems because it would be too difficult to use them as they were, not to mention they didn’t necessarily suit her needs perfectly.","Meanwhile, the Grand Conqueror’s strength was not only severely curtailed, but he also became a lot more cautious in his actions, unsure of what his enemy had in store for him."]},{"number":2430,"title":"Chapter 2430: Ministry of Order & Discipline","paragraphs":["Lex was caught in a fight he could not quickly resolve, nor could he avoid. An enemy as dangerous as Daekol, who kidnapped Almira to lure Lex out, and one who knew about him having a system, simply couldn’t be allowed to live. Unfortunately, Daekol did not share Lex’s opinion and refused to die easily.","The Midnight Inn, too, had initiated their invasion. Due to the massive size of the realm, even if it was an immature one, it would take them a while to find Z’s location. It might take them even longer to rescue him due to the fact that they might need to go across the realm to do it depending on where he was.","Both were involved in extremely serious and potentially dangerous endeavors, but just because they were busy did not mean the rest of the universe had taken a break. With each passing day, the situation in the universe became more and more complex.","The feeling of dread - the one that accompanied the destruction of a Major realm - became unnervingly common. The problem became that no one could figure out which were the realms being destroyed since no information was being leaked.","Until, one day, a realm owned by an Elder race was invaded. That is the day the universe learned that the suppression and prestige of Elder races was only impressive for those below them. Whoever was masterminding this universal turbulence clearly had no regard for them, and had many ways of dealing with them.","They fell with the exact same speed as the other realms, but no one knew how or why. Let alone things like Daoflix, even powerful divination and deduction techniques utilized by expert Dao Lords failed.","The mood in the universe was becoming darker and darker, to the point where the spirit energy of the entire universe slowly started to get infected by a subtle aura of death, yin and things of such nature.","For now, only some more astute Dao Lords could sense the difference, but the fact that it could be sensed at all demonstrated how severe the situation was. A trend of ghosts, spirits and undead suddenly appearing began to increase across the universe, and many discovered that it was easier than ever before to embark onto the path of necromancy.","Unbeknownst to most of the universe, the number of destroyed Major realms crossed another major threshold, prompting the laws of the universe to react once more.","The first time, the universe unleashed the Tribulation Fiends that appeared anywhere and everywhere, targeting any and all with sins against the universe. This time, however, the universe rumbled, and all the excess energy that was released from the destroyed Major realms was gathered and channeled into Arch-Heaven.","Within Arch-Heaven existed the Heavenly Court, and many who lived in Arch-Heaven had official positions recognized by Arch-Heaven. The highest available position, up until then, was that of Lord.","However as the energy was gathered from the universe, it all channeled into a certain building, causing it to grow in size rapidly. Outside it, massive marble statues began to gain golden armaments and gained a hint of presence that hinted at them being more than just statues.","In front of the building some characters appeared in a language that had never existed before, but could be read by anyone. It read: Ministry of Order & Discipline . More and more energy flowed into the building, giving rise to various marble statues, in the shape of various Sage and Elder races.","Right in the center of the building, on a throne, an ethereal figure appeared in the shape of a Celestial garbed in ministerial robes rather than armor or anything else of the sort. The aura exuded from the figure was unusual and complex. It did not have any hint of Dao, and instead appeared to be entirely made up of laws - yet the depth of laws was far beyond what even Dao Lords ordinarily controlled.","It was as if the figure shared its origins with the laws that governed the very core of the universe.","The moment the figure opened its eyes, all the statues in the building stood up straight with their heads bowed low, as if awaiting orders.","\"Crimes are being committed. The universe is in disarray. Amend the situation,\" the figure spoke softly.","The response, however, was thunderous. All the statues saluted in unison, before fading away from Arch-Heaven and appearing within the universe itself. Each statue had an aura similar to, but weaker than the minister, in the sense that they lacked any relation to Dao, but had immense power nevertheless.","It only made sense - their powers came directly from the universe itself, so they had to be strong.","The appearance of the ministry attracted so much attention, that almost no one noticed that the leftover energy was diverted from the ministry and absorbed into the crystal dome where Dao Lords were being imprisoned.","Perhaps at any other time, such a thing may have been noticed by others. Yet for now, all the attention was directly focused on the adjudicators of the ministry who marched as a single, unified army. Despite not having any Dao aura, together all thousand of them represented a force stronger than an army of one thousand Dao Lords simply because all of them shared the same source of power.","Many wondered where they would go first, but not a single one expected that their first stop would be the Primary realm, and to be specific, the Ruins of Ascension within the primary realm.","Without holding back, the unified army of adjudicators attacked without any forewarning!","Yet the territory of the Ruins of Ascension was under the watch of the Primals. How could it be so easily damaged?","Without displaying even the slightest hint of being burdened, the Primals deflected the attack, and locked onto the adjudicators with great prejudice. If they showed any signs of attacking again, the Primals would not hold back.","For a few, silent seconds, the two parties stood at an impasse. Then, the adjudicators left the realm entirely, as if they weren’t the least bit concerned about what had happened."]},{"number":2431,"title":"Chapter 2431: The merchant","paragraphs":["Something unprecedented happened right after the attack by the Ministry of Order & Discipline. For the first time in history, a major organisation on a universal scale completely abandoned a Major realm.","They directly, and without hesitation, forcefully harvested any resources from the realm and then abandoned it. All Dao Lords, as well as many powerful Immortal families abandoned the realm and escaped within a Void ship, hiding from detection, effectively disappearing.","With most Dao Lords missing or gone inside the Dream realm, and many others caught up in war or unable to provide support due to the disconnected state of the universe, they decided it was better to give up the Major realm than to try to hold it.","Thus, without any war or fighting, a Major realm became ownerless. No one even went to claim it. In fact, after the first realm was abandoned, many other powers also began to copy them.","The vast and wide universe suddenly started to feel hollow, for too many Dao Lords started to hide or were already missing.","Yet... not everyone’s means were effective enough. What originally appeared to be a strategic retreat was merely a result of Dao Lords trying to hide because they were already anticipating that the Ministry would come after them!","Though they tried to hide, their means were ineffective, leading to fights breaking out in the Void. Yet the 1000 member strong army of adjudicators could not be resisted by merely a few Dao Lords huddled together. Whether they were killed or imprisoned was unknown to all, but the certainty of their defeat was shared by all.","Slowly and steadily, time passed, though each passing second was extremely eventful. Eventually, a single month remained until the Nexus event. Jack opened his eyes, a solemn expression painting his face. His fight against Daekol had gone on much longer than expected, and he didn’t have nearly as much leverage as he would have liked. Daekol’s system kept interfering.","If Lex’s own system was working, and he could have used his Butter Knife, then the fight would have been much easier. Then again, a Butter Knife could only be used on Inn territory.","Jack originally had a few things planned that he wanted to do before the Nexus event to take advantage of his Destiny resetting, but now he had to abandon all his plans and focus on helping Lex.","It was not perfect yet, but Jack had, to a large degree, mastered the art of sending things between his souls. For now, it seemed like only divine items could make the trip, but that was good enough for him.","What Jack was sending now was a tiny speck of Divine ore containing an augmentation from his Paladin powers. Jack seemed to have benefited from Lex’s 51% Dao Body as well, not to mention his new Heaven Immortal realm. His paladin powers, thus, were on a whole new level.","His attack and defense were, obviously, strong but not nearly as strong as Lex’s. His augmentation, however, was suddenly critical. The interference from Daekol’s systems had reduced Lex’s attack power by 32% which was a massive reduction considering they were close to each other in strength.","If Jack could cause that percentage to drop at a critical moment, it could change the flow of battle.","Seeing as how it was not time yet, Jack closed his eyes and began reinforcing his augmentation which was contained within that tiny piece of divine ore. When that critical moment came, he would be ready.","Within the Dream realm, Liz was frozen from fear, and not even Nemo on her cheeks dared to move. They had been on a mission from the Path of Order, and in the beginning everything had been going fine.","Even when they faced trouble or difficulty, they at least avoided dead ends. But today, when trouble came, it came without restraint. The Dream realm had separated her from her group all of a sudden, even though they were supposed to have protection against that.","As if that was not enough, the place where she was teleported to was not somewhere she could hope to escape or survive in on her own. She was transported right inside one of the Dream Master’s bases.","Fortunately, with Nemo’s help, she had been able to hide her presence entirely. After that, she hid herself underneath a sofa, pushing herself as far as she could manage to stay out of sight. Her hiding spot could have been discovered by a five year old, but since most high leveled cultivators trusted their spirit sense, they didn’t really pay attention to a hidden corner where their sense said nothing was hidden.","Not long after, some scarily powerful beings entered the same room as her to discuss certain sensitive topics.","\"Have you calculated the strain? It’s been decreasing at a steady pace,\" said one of the people in the room.","\"Yes, it’s just as we predicted. In fact, everything is going incredibly smoothly. I can recommend that, at this rate, the optimal universal strain will be reached in five years. Anyone wishing to undergo a Dao tribulation should initiate it at that point - they’ll have the highest chances of success.\"","There was a long silence, which probably meant that they were talking about something using their spirit sense. Eventually, though, they all stood up.","\"We have an agreement then. As long as you can stably provide nourishment potions for mortals at a rate of 1 trillion vials per hour for mortals, and 34 million vials per hour for Earth Immortals, we will purge your sins before the adjudicators of the ministry can find you,\" answered one person sounding happy.","The group seemed happy with the agreement and they left the room... except for one person who sat back down on the sofa right above Liz. A heavy silence once again filled the room, and Liz dared not even breathe.","\"You know, you can come out from under the sofa young lady. I won’t harm you,\" the person suddenly said, his voice freezing Liz’s heart. The being was so powerful that even Nemo did not dare try anything funny. All things considered, it only made sense that she was discovered.","Liz’s mind raced as she thought of ways to resolve her situation, the person brought his head down and looked at her with a warm smile.","\"My name is Oaka, and I am a merchant. You do not need to be afraid of me - maybe we can even come to a deal,\" he said, sounding almost inviting. Liz did not exactly believe him, but she didn’t really have a choice either."]},{"number":2432,"title":"Chapter 2432: Snake stereotype","paragraphs":["Although fear gripped her entire being, being looked at by Oaka strangely made her feel reassured. If someone so much more powerful than her wanted to harm her, it was unlikely that he would try to talk to her nicely, right? They could directly just do whatever they wanted.","Even Nemo seemed to agree with her, considering that he too felt afraid of the snake merchant. It was strange. Other Celestial Immortals could not intimidate him the way the mere presence of this merchant could.","Seeing that nothing was happening, Liz slowly scooted out from under the sofa and sat opposite to the snake, ironing out the wrinkles in her clothes as she did.","\"I would show you my wares, but I left them back at my shop,\" Oaka said as he let out an awkward laugh. \"These days, the things that are selling the most are deals, which is a shame because many of the items in my shop will expire in a few months.\"","Though Liz still felt intimidated, her mind was racing as she tried to find her way out of her predicament.","\"What kind of deals are you selling then? Anything I might be interested in?\" Liz asked, keeping up with the conversation.","The snake used the tip of its tail to rub the area under its mouth, almost as if it was rubbing its chin while in thought.","\"Well, I can offer you a few generic deals, but it would be a whole lot better if you either told me about yourself and your interests. If you’re unwilling to do that, there’s a way to anonymously check what deals I can offer you. You simply have to place your hand over this crystal ball and think about what you want most. I won’t learn any actual details about you, but I’ll be informed of all the deals I can offer you that are relevant to your needs or desires.\"","Liz looked at the snake, and then at the orb. She could not help but wonder if it would be a bit speciesist or stereotyping if she operated under the assumption that the snake was out to harm her.","\"Try the orb, I have a good feeling about it,\" said Nemo whose eyes shone with excitement.","Despite Nemo’s excitable personality, he was extremely reliable regardless of how ridiculous his desires were.","Oaka glanced at the tattoo on her cheek but said nothing. Instead, he merely pushed the crystal orb towards Liz so that she could easily reach it.","She glanced at the snake, pushed away her concerns about stereotypes, and placed her hand on the orb. Her eyes closed on their own, and without her even realizing, Liz began to think about all the things that concerned her most.","She thought about her family, she thought about the Midnight Inn, about Nemo, about her cultivation and many more things she never even knew she valued. The taste of a fresh apple pie, the smell of freshly baked bread, the taste of warm milk with a massive dollop of honey, grilled fish marinated in butter and lemon... okay so most of it was about food but that was mainly just because she hadn’t had a decent meal since she ventured out on this mission.","She did not feel time pass at all, for she was solely focused on thinking about everything she cared about.","When she opened her eyes back up, she found that Oaka was placing an entire feast on the table in front of her, a particularly noticeable look of pity in his eyes.","\"Oh, are you done already? Please, have a snack while I present you with the offers. The food is free, so don’t worry about it,\" said Oaka.","Before Liz could even pretend to say no out of formality, Nemo jumped out of her cheek and began chomping on the calamari!","\"Dish ish very goosh, thanksh yoush!\" Nemo managed to utter in between bites, its size literally growing with every bite it ate. The food was all normal, mortal food. There was no spiritual nourishment in it - he was only eating for the sake of eating. That did not, however, stop him.","Liz froze as she stared in horror, and then quickly grabbed a drumstick before Nemo ate them all. She wanted to remain polite, but Nemo was genuinely eating so fast that it put immense pressure on her. She merely gave a thankful glance at Oaka before she began eating!","The fact that Nemo was eating them meant that they wouldn’t harm her either - she did share many of Nemo’s immunities after all.","Oaka shook his head, and then sat back down before pulling out two files and placing them in the air in front of Liz.","\"I have a number of deals I can offer you, but I think these two will be the most relevant to your current needs. Actually, even I myself don’t know the details of what’s in the folders yet, so feel free to look through them. Only if you wish to pursue this deal can you share its contents with me and we can move forward. Otherwise, you can simply discard the files and no one will ever know their contents.\"","Liz very reluctantly looked away from the alfredo pasta and glanced at the files. She knew that if she didn’t eat the pasta now, Nemo would get to it first. However, logic prevailed over her gluttonous desire, and she grabbed one of the files.","She was shocked to learn that the file talked about a war ongoing between the Midnight Inn and a mysterious immature realm owner. Her hunger died completely as she quickly went through the file that briefly mentioned the state of the war, and then gave much more emphasis on how Oaka could help, and what she would need to pay for such services.","The help he could offer was great, but the price was much greater. She couldn’t accept it at all. She’d rather go there and help out personally.","Yet now that she knew what one file contained, she quickly grabbed the other one and opened it.","This time, she was stunned as he wrote down the details of Lex’s fight with another Sovereign. Helping him out was also expensive, far, far beyond what she could pay. However, there was nothing stopping her from offering up her own deal to Oaka as well based on all the help he offered in this file.","Liz put down the file and channeled all the diplomatic training she’d received in Ventura.","\"I have a counter offer,\" she said, discarding both files so that Oaka would never know what was in them - assuming he had told the truth."]},{"number":2433,"title":"Chapter 2433: Lucky Bourdow","paragraphs":["Bourdow’s infiltration into the Dream realm remained entirely undetected. Not a Dao Lord alive could sense his movements, of that he was sure. It wasn’t Bourdow’s mastery of some arcane, invincible technique that granted him that confidence, nor an unsurpassed Unique Dao.","It was simply the one, single law he had dedicated his life to - one for which he even held a Major Dao! It was the law of Luck, and the Dao of Lucky Break. It wasn’t that he had the best technique to hide in the universe - it was just that he was destined to be lucky for his entire life.","Wherever he went, whatever he did, he was always tremendously lucky. He’d discover long forgotten secrets that would teach him exactly what he needed. His enemies would suffer from gut wrenching food poisoning right in the middle of fights. There was once a time he was ambushed by a Dao Lord, but right in the middle of the fight, the enemies Dao fractured.","To this day, Bourdow didn’t know why that Dao fractured and that Dao Lord died. All he knew was that it was a Lucky Break, because he benefited greatly from that Dao Lord’s death.","Yes, he was destined to be lucky his whole life - he knew as much because he’d literally made a deal with Destiny to change his destiny like that. In exchange, he worked for her, completing tasks no one else could.","As far as he was concerned, even working for her was a Lucky Break. It allowed him to get in touch with secrets no one else knew. It allowed him to secretly prepare his own Seat of Power without attracting attention, all in preparation for the day he too could rise above the Dao Lord realm.","But those were all things for much, much later. For now, working for Destiny allowed him to venture into the Dream realm and get his hands on that treasure everyone was coveting. By now, everyone already knew that the treasure was some kind of massive platform - they just didn’t know what its function was.","Of course, there was no guarantee of him discovering the use of the platform, let alone getting it for himself, but with his luck, and Destiny on his side, what other outcome could there be? Destiny herself had told him that she was less interested in the treasure, and more in the Dream Master and his identity. Or rather their identity, because even Destiny could not learn anything about them, including their gender.","Such a severe flaw in the workings of destiny had to be addressed immediately. Once she understood how the Dream Master had hidden from her for so long, she could improve the associated law, and grow all that much stronger.","As far as he was concerned, that had nothing to do with him. He was just here to get a Lucky Break.","\"I’ve infiltrated the place, but I can’t make anything out,\" said Bourdow. \"I sure as hell wouldn’t mind if I stumbled onto something that’ll help me find the key to the platform’s secret.\"","While Bourdow waited for his words to take effect, and for his luck to come to him, he connected to Destiny.","\"I’m in, but I’ll need a distraction or two,\" he said while tossing a cashew nut into his mouth. \"The amount of loose luck within the Dream realm is strictly controlled - I feel like they’re harvesting it as well. I can’t rely only on luck to break in, I need sufficient disturbances.\"","After a few moments of silence, a slightly irritated voice spoke in his ear.","\"Isn’t the destruction of Major realms and the descent of the Ministry of Order & Discipline distraction enough? The whole damn universe is on edge because of that.\"","Bourdow shook his head and popped in another cashew.","\"Not really. The Dream realm hasn’t been affected in the slightest because of that. Everyone keeps saying the destruction of realms has affected the Dream realm, but I’m in here telling you it’s growing stronger with each passing second. We need a distraction that will affect the Dream realm, or at least the Dream Master.\"","This time, the silence that followed was even longer, but Bourdow didn’t mind. He stumbled, even though he wasn’t walking, and when he looked up he saw Wu Kong and Elrand fighting.","So the Lucky Break he needed to find the treasure was one of them? But which one?","He would have to think about it a bit.","\"I don’t know what will distract the Dream Master,\" Destiny finally said. \"I’m sending you a lucky draw. Pick out a few options - we’ll proceed accordingly.\"","Bourdow wasn’t surprised. This was something they had done often in the past. Destiny would randomly write a bunch of options of pieces of paper and toss them in a bowl for him to pick from. There was no sophistry about it - it was as simple as a mortal lucky draw. What mattered was his luck.","It would always pick out the option luckiest for him, and more often than not it gave them what they wanted or needed.","\"If I’m going to use up my own luck for this draw, I want a little something extra afterwards. A few races. I want your help usurping the lucky destiny of the Leprechaun and Kitsune races,\" Bourdow said without a care that he was talking to Destiny. He knew for a fact she would agree.","\"The Leprechauns have been weakened enough, but the Kitsune have dozens of Dao Lords. As long as you kill them, I’ll help you absorb their destiny,\" Destiny said before a crystal bowl appeared in front of Bourdow.","He clicked his teeth. Such an unreasonable request.","\"Fine, fine, we’ll see how things go,\" Bourdow responded as he plunged his hand within the bowl and drew three slips.","The slips read Humans, Marina realm and Time Stones.","The Marina realm was a realm that used to be controlled by Mermaids before they were driven to the point of being nearly extinct, and Time Stones were valuable crystals which were used for various purposes including, but not limited to, Time acceleration, reality fragmentation and more.","Neither of them could understand why this would affect the Dream master, but they didn’t care either.","\"I suppose it’s finally time to thoroughly crush the destiny of humanity,\" said Destiny with a cold voice. \"The Marina Major realm is under control of the Hydra race. I’m not sure what’s so special about it - it has a very mediocre destiny - but I’ll make sure it’s destroyed in the war. As for Time Stones... I’m not sure what the hint could be. I’ll just send you a bunch of Time Stones and you can do with them as you wish.\"","Bourdow shrugged and locked onto Wu Kong. Erlang’s personality was annoying, he’d rather latch onto Wu Kong instead.","\"What do you want me to do once I discover what the platform actually does?\" he asked.","Once again, Destiny responded after a long silence.","\"Don’t get ahead of yourself. Ask me once you’ve figured out the details of the platform. And be careful. Avoid doing anything stupid. The Dream Master is not an enemy we can treat lightly. Operate under the assumption that he already knows you are there.\"","Bourdow rolled his eyes and simply grabbed the Time Stone sent by Destiny before focusing on Wu Kong. The one in front of him was merely a clone, he could tell that much. In fact, even Elrang seemed to be using a clone. So where were the real ones?","It may be a secret for others, but Bourdow had no doubts that he’d be able to find out easily enough. As for Destiny’s warning... it wasn’t that he ignored it, but that he needed to act in certain mannerisms to maximise the effect of luck, so there wasn’t much he could do.","He closed his eyes and then threw his body right in the middle of the fight without any hesitation. Luckily, at that exact moment, a sudden change occurred within the Dream realm that caused a disturbance between Wu Kong and Erlang, temporarily stopping the fight.","In truth, many Dao Lords had already discovered the location of the treasure, but exploring its secrets was easier said than done. That was why Bourdow had opted for this indirect method.","As it turned out, the disturbance that had been caused was due to the very platform he was here to explore. Two Dao Lords had fought on the platform, which wasn’t strange or unusual. What was unusual was that the Dao Lords were both much more vulnerable on the platform than they would have been otherwise.","One of the Dao Lords was killed far too easily, and the platform suddenly began to absorb all the energy within the corpse, turning it into Dao Essence left to be claimed by whoever encountered it.","Horror and excitement spread throughout the realm. This... changed everything!"]},{"number":2434,"title":"Chapter 2434: Eight Retributions: Crucible of Karma","paragraphs":["One dead Dao Lord. Three thousand litres of Dao Essence. A Dao Field would allow one Dao Lord to make one drop of Dao Essence in a hundred years. Without a Dao Field, it would take one hundred Dao Lords one thousand years to produce one drop, meaning it would take 100,000 years for each Dao Lord in that group to get one drop!","Even though they were immortal and time was plenty, that was a lot of time to spend for a single drop of Dao Essence. Yet it was worth it because of how valuable Dao Essence was. It was for that very reason that the Runeking and other Dao Lords did not want the Innkeeper to join the Humanoid Alliance.","The number of resources were fixed, and more players meant more competition. It wasn’t personal, it was merely a matter of resources and benefits.","That is also why, the moment a Dao Lord died on top of the platform in the Dream realm, all eyes from across the universe focused there. A single Dao Lord died, the platform absorbed his energy, and in return produced three thousand litres of Dao Essence.","That was approximately 60 million drops. Without a Dao Field, it would, on average, take a Dao Lord 6 trillion years to gather that much Dao Essence.","Greed. GREED!","Like an unstoppable virus, greed spread across the universe faster than logic or common sense would allow, overcoming any and all restraint. Nothing - nothing - in the universe at that moment was more valuable than the platform in the Dream realm.","That one, single revelation was destined to change the course of history for the universe forever. Not only did the platform make Dao Lords far more vulnerable than made sense, it also allowed one to exchange a Dao Lord for three thousand litres of Dao Essence, basically allowing them to save six trillion years of time!","Bourdow began to hyperventilate, and neither Wu Kong nor Elrang paid attention to why a random Dao Lord had appeared in the middle of their fight. In fact, the fight effectively ended as the clones disappeared.","Luckily for Bourdow, he managed to leave a tracker of Wu Kong’s clone before it vanished, allowing him to trace it as it traversed the Dream realm.","Across the universe, many wars spontaneously ended. Literal Major realm invasions stopped, and many forces simply stopped defending irrelevant Major realms.","Except for the absolute most core Major realms controlled by the races or organizations, all Major realms across the universe were suddenly left undefended as every free and available Dao Lord made their way into the Dream realm.","Killing one Dao Lord saved 6 trillion years, two would save 12 trillion, and three... The amount of wealth being talked about was entirely inconceivable.","The mere idea that so much Dao Essence was on the table to be taken gripped them all. The best part was that the platform made it so easy to kill Dao Lords, who otherwise had no way of being killed. Thus, countless Dao Lords who had been trapped or imprisoned were brought along as well.","Their sacrifices would not be forgotten any time soon.","Whether it was Destiny, or Death, or Chaos or any other, they too paused all their plans and thoughts and looked towards the platform, trying to understand its secrets. If they could replicate it...","Especially with the Nexus event coming, all could be forgiven. They could absolve themselves from any carried debts. If they could only figure out how to copy it...","An uncontrollable madness spread among the Dao Lords of the universe, leaving most major forces crippled since there weren’t many Dao Lords left to command them. At the same time, a slaughter unprecedented since the Primordial Age began to unfold.","The blood of Dao Lords was shed easily, baptizing the Dream Arena - as many had taken to calling the platform - in one of the universe’s most sacred liquids.","Only a very, very few watched in horror. Cide and Agemo trembled within their ship as they tried to understand what crazy madness, what vile disease or plague could infect so many Dao Lords to the point beyond reason.","Although they too understood the value of Dao Essence, they were not driven crazy by it. They could not understand why they were spared while others were not, but it was apparent at a glance that this was far beyond normal.","The bet on Lex, and his match, or even the ongoing war in the Conquest realm could no longer interest them. All eyes were on the Dream Arena.","Naturally since Cide and Agemo could be spared, many others were as well. Even though many Sage races sent in their armies to the Dream realm without restraint, they were not driven to madness. Similarly, Destiny and the others were still cautious.","They sent in their subordinates, but remained hidden themselves.","Destiny took this opportunity to advance her other plans as well. The destiny of humanity needed to be crushed. A good portion of it was centered in the Midnight Inn, but she didn’t want to touch that for it seemed too closely connected to Oblivion and Eclipse.","Besides that, the Tyrannum realm seemed to attract a lot of humanities destiny. She might as well start from there.","She picked up a piece on a chessboard and placed it casually, uncaring that the destiny of an entire race would be affected by it.","Within the Dream realm, Dragon-Lex was still caught in the fight, an incredible weight pressing down on his chest. Yet no matter how heavy the weight was, Dragon-Lex did not care.","Up close, his Domination suppressed Daekol until the Sovereign too coughed out blood in frustration. In fact, there came a point where Lex didn’t even care about winning the fight - he just enjoyed frustrating the hell about Daekol.","The stupid Sovereign was too composed - it wasn’t fun beating him up. Only in moments where he finally let his frustrations show would Dragon-Lex finally enjoy himself a bit.","Yet for all his enjoyment, Lex suddenly got a very strong feeling that something terrible was about to happen. He wasn’t sure what, but his instincts were warning him that this was very, very dangerous!","This unknown danger far outweighed whatever danger Daekol represented towards him, which is why he needed to finish this fight off quickly.","\"You’re nervous,\" Daekol suddenly said, studying the fluctuations in Dragon-Lex’s Domination. \"Something has happened, and whatever it is has made you nervous. You put up a good fight, but the moment you lost your composure, you also lost the fight.\"","Dragon-Lex snorted.","\"No, it means that your time is up because I’m done playing with you,\" he said before punching Daekol. But Lex’s punches lacked the impact that they used to have.","Even though the effects of the Dao Body were still there, they suffered from a harsh decline in effectiveness.","Personally, Lex was not yet done setting everything up for his confrontation with Daekol, but time waited for no man.","He had been fighting Daekol for a long time already, and step by step, he had managed to strengthen his Sovereign realm. It was not deployed to its utmost, but it was sufficient. Daekol had taken him by surprise, and given him a lot of trouble. But that was all.","Even if it was a system, Dragon-Lex did not fear it.","\" Pause operations ,\" Dragon-Lex whispered using Supremacy, a malevolent grin painting his face.","Daekol’s eyes constricted as he saw, for the first time, his system responding to someone other than himself. It did not actually pause operations, but it did pause for a bit, as if it too was confused.","That pause was enough. Dragon-Lex finally used the one Lawcraft the pain of which he had personally felt with every fiber of his being.","\" Eight Retributions: Crucible of Karma ,\" Dragon-Lex uttered, his very voice tinged with power and Domination, as he unleashed one of the most powerful Lawcrafts Lex had ever encountered.","The Lawcraft was far from perfect just yet, but having experienced everything within it himself, he could still manifest it well enough. Yet he could also change it. Pain was not enough. Pain was the perfect crippling and torture tool, but against an opponent like Daekol, it was not enough.","Thus he changed it. Not only did he want Daekol to suffer through all the pain he had ever caused, Lex also wanted to continue infecting Daekol with karma, down to his very core, so that when Lex struck his final blow, there was no escaping it.","Thus, when Daekol felt the first feeling of pain from the first pain he had ever caused, Lex saw it too. The first pain he’d ever caused... was to his mother. It was not the pain of childbirth, but the pain of abandonment. Daekol was born a superior being, a Sovereign of the universe, destined to stand at the very peak, and his mother was a mundane beast who had not even awoken proper intelligence.","That did not mean she did not feel the pain of being abandoned. For some inexplicable reason, that first pain stunned Daekol, and seemed to affect him even more than the behavior of his system."]},{"number":2435,"title":"Chapter 2435: It’s about time","paragraphs":["It was not the knowledge of his mothers pain that stunned Daekol, despite what some may assume. From the moment of his birth, he knew he was different and things like emotional connection and solace were entirely irrelevant. As a Sovereign, he understood the cruelty of nature far better than others, and he adapted to it.","No, what stunned him was the unfiltered sensation of pain. As a Sovereign, he could even command the universe, let alone his own body, so he had long diluted the sensation of pain to avoid distraction.","It wasn’t like he was bothered by it - he had the strength of mind to ignore it. But there was also no need to excessively feel pain either. Now, though, he seemed to be feeling pain without any reduction or dampening.","The shock was from the fact that Lex seemed to have overwritten his command over his own body somehow.","\"Daekol,\" Dragon-Lex called out to the Sovereign, his voice filled with something alien. It almost felt like... empathy. \"I see you never had much of a relationship with your mother. In that case, allow me to give you something most get from their mothers. I call it... character development.\"","He increased the speed at which Daekol’s karma triggered pain, as there was no reason to go one by one. Lex didn’t quite have the same strength as the Gilded Hollow which meant that Daekol might find a way out of this Lawcraft if given the opportunity.","In that case, it was best not to allow him such an opportunity to begin with.","When the pain came, it no longer came one by one, and incrementally. It came all at once, with countless pieces of karma working together. Even though Daekol could resist the pain, he knew that if this continued it would distract-","Dragon-Lex grabbed Daekol by the throat and lifted him in the air, just in time to use Daekol’s body to block the lightning bolt!","By now, his tribulation had grown enormous. Oddly enough, the lightning bolts did not turn into Farham, like they usually did. Maybe it had something to do with the egg shell. Regardless, each lightning bolt struck him with increasingly devastating force, to the point where it was no longer constricted by the limitations of normal lightning. The Dream realm itself began to burn from wherever the lightning crossed. This was no longer something Lex could just blindly tank - each bolt genuinely hurt him a lot.","Then again, considering that the tribulations were also the process by which he evolved to the next level, would he even get any benefits if the lightning couldn’t harm him? Though technically, the lightning only grew stronger and stronger because Daekol was considered to be interfering with it.","Fortunately for him, that also served his purpose of using his tribulation to fight Daekol as well.","The brutal, singeing sensation of his skin being burnt to a crisp by the tribulation woke Daekol from the stupor of the pain he was feeling. Although his tolerance for pain was immense, his unfamiliarity with it caused his mind to slow down when he was dealing with it. This was a flaw he was unaware that he had, but that could be dealt with later.","The fact that Lex had initiated the next stage of the fight meant he was getting impatient. He just needed to continue holding out and Lex would get increasingly desperate. Desperation leads to mistakes or drastic measures, both of which would give him an opening.","But for that, he needed to first survive, and so he needed to step it up as well. He grit his teeth and looked at his system. It was lagging even now. Although it still responded to his command, Lex’s previous order to pause operations felt like it was being initiated every second, causing it to stutter.","He looked at a certain command called Debt Seizure, but before he could even activate it, the Crucible of Karma seemed to react to his actions. It suddenly skipped over a lot of his other karma, and directly began reacting to all karma associated with Debt Seizure.","This was an additional ability Lex added to his Lawcraft. Since pain alone probably wouldn’t stop his enemies he would be facing at this point, he configured the Lawcraft to react to any attacks, skills, abilities or Lawcrafts his opponents used.","Naturally, the pain associated with such abilities should be far greater. Moreover, since Lex was reading his opponents karma, he’d also learn about the opponent’s abilities. Before even being attacked, he’d know what to expect.","Speaking of alterations to the Lawcraft, Lex thought that the idea of having the retributions appear sequentially was a waste. They’d be much more effective if they were stacked.","\" Eight Retributions: Prison of Gluttony ,\" Dragon-Lex whispered before Daekol could even initiate his Debt Seizure system ability.","Like the previous retribution, Lex had altered this one too. When he suffered from this retribution, and his body devoured itself, the Gilded Hollow healed and restored his body time and time again. Lex had no intentions of doing that for Daekol, or anyone else who suffered from this for that matter. He would let their body cannibalise itself, let the soul and mind do the same. Why would he waste energy healing them?","Daekol let out an angry roar as he activated Debt Seizure. Lex had, by now, amassed a considerable debt which was not easy to pay off. Daekol would have preferred increasing the debt a whole lot more before taking it back, but the situation didn’t allow it.","The system lagged, but it still worked. Lex had many assets which could pay off the debt he had accumulated, but it was the creditors choice what to take, and Daekol chose Lex’s soul!","Lex felt something connecting to the massive weight he had been feeling inside his chest, and then pull. A massive chunk of his scales, skin and muscles from his chest disappeared, showing his beating heart, partially missing bones and other, damaged organs.","The damage was extreme, far beyond what even the tribulation had done, but it was nowhere near enough to threaten Lex’s life.","Daekol’s eyes narrowed in complete, genuine shock for the first time as he struggled to understand what his body had to do with his soul and, more importantly, how valuable his body was for such a small part of it to offset such a massive debt.","Unfortunately for Daekol, while the Debt Seizure had inflicted damage onto Lex, it also freed him from debt, returning his strength to full.","Dragon-Lex’s fingers dug into Daekol’s neck as he brought him closer to himself.","\"It’s about time to end this, don’t you think?\""]},{"number":2436,"title":"Chapter 2436: The ballads of my glory - Suggested Song: Blow me away by Breaking Benjamin","paragraphs":["With pain clouding his mind, anger clouding his judgment, an unquenchable hunger eating away at his sanity and Dragon-Lex’s terrifying gaze causing Daekol’s body to feel a fear he had never felt before, the Sovereign let go of all reason and unleashed everything and anything he had been holding back.","Gravity Crack. Void Eruption. Debt Acquittal. Enhanced rebirth. Memory of Shagufta. Law’s rending. Sovereigns Sacrifice .","One attack after another unleashed itself onto Lex’s body. A Major tribulation punished him from up above, and a terrifying force of nature wreaked havoc on him from close by, but not an ounce of doubt or hesitation flickered through Lex’s resolve.","He could feel it in his bones - the universe was not at peace and something terrible was happening. No matter what price he had to pay, he needed to end this here and now .","With his Sovereigns realm partially deployed, and only two of the eight retributions unleashed, Lex wasn’t fully ready, but he would make do.","\"It is your honor, Sovereign Daekol, to push me so far,\" said Dragon-Lex, ignoring his bleeding body and the storm of attacks ripping at his flesh. \"When the ballads of my glory are sung, your name will be mentioned for making me bleed.\"","Fury filled Daekol’s eyes as he summoned his hammer once more, its body covered in scars and faint cracks, and smashed towards Lex’s face. He’d had enough of his talking.","Yet Lex ignored him entirely. With his right hand he gripped Daekol’s neck, his fingers digging into the neck itself. With his left hand he summoned Naraka and used it to cut into Daekol’s body, forming an effective clamp so that he could not escape.","Holding nothing back, Lex unleashed Golden Inferno right at the Sovereign’s face, burning whatever Sovereign authority he had to spare. The hammer came down, and though it smashed onto Lex’s face with enough force to crack a planet, it could not stop him. It merely rang Daekol’s own death knell.","The brilliant, golden flames shot past Daekol’s face, burning him and everything else it touched, before taking the form of a dragon and turning back to wrap itself around the both of them, forming an egg of glorious molten-gold fire, trapping them both inside.","Around the egg, the Abaddon Inn formed once more, feeding on Daekol’s vulnerable spirit, digging into the cracks that were beginning to form. Above the Abaddon Inn, a red moon shone down its ominous scarlet light, enforcing Lex’s Supremacy in the form of an artificial realm.","Within it all, Lex’s Dao Intentions began to resonate, infecting everything to the point where the Dream realm itself began to change its nightmares to mimic the battlefield where Lex and Daekol fought.","So many Dao Lords were no longer watching the fight, but Ballom could not help and turn his gaze back at the fight.","\"Was that... no, it can’t be... that can’t be...\" he whispered, but quickly his attention was pulled away.","\"Pay attention honey, let’s not die today,\" said Bridget as she stood behind him upon the Dream Arena.","Nuwa was looking at Lex, but her gaze seemed to be lost in time. Eclipse’s smile widened as she saw something extremely interesting. James, the human pretending to be the Timekeeper, looked at Morrow with a reluctant, resigned smile.","\"In our defense, we really tried,\" he said to the Timekeeper’s cane. \"I say we unleash all that Fractured time now.\"","The cane sighed, and just flew away to the bar.","\"You have to wait until the Nexus event or you’ll screw everything up. Now, we can only pray that ’Lex the Bombastic Bazooka’ doesn’t get himself killed.\"","Outside, Lex had not stopped breathing fire. His grip continued to crush Daekol’s neck. His sword intent kept cutting through his body. The two retributions and Abaddon Inn still tortured all of Daekol’s being.","Unseen and unknown to Daekol among all this was the Karmic Bead which hovered directly above the egg of molten flames, tying itself to Daekol’s karma incredibly deeply. There was also what remained of the Farham Primordial egg shell which had, at some point, appeared atop Lex’s heart. Oh, and the rest of the energy from the Double Yang Disaster Rose poured into Lex’s body, forcing his Rebirth by Fire to awaken.","An ever increasing amount of Dao energy gathered around the area as Lex’s Dao Intentions raged without control. A tremendous amount of pressure built up until finally... something cracked.","James had delayed Lex’s Dao Body tribulation because he didn’t want Lex to be occupied when the Nexus event came, but man proposes and Dragon-Lex screws up that proposal. Whatever ability he used to delay the tribulation shattered from the accumulated pressure of Lex’s Dao tribulations, and Lex’s Major tribulation mutated.","It gathered clouds pulsed, and all the lightning gathered and formed a rainbow colored sphere of Lightning Laws. Then the clouds, as if a massive eyelid, blinked.","The laws of the Dream realm groaned as an entity most ancient, forgotten by almost all appeared within the realm. Its appearance was not slow or gradual - it appeared within the blink of that cloudy eye, and its massive size blotted out the entire realm.","All Dao Lords within the Dream realm looked up. All Immortals looked up. All dreams and nightmares looked up as a memory long forgotten unveiled itself into reality.","The Timekeeper had told Lex that within a Dao Body tribulation, the recipient of the tribulation lives through the memory of a scene many thought was a real event that happened once upon a time.","However, Lex’s Primordial Dao Body tribulation did not bring him into a memory - nay, it summoned the memory into reality. Maybe it was the Primordial aspect of it, or maybe it was because the tribulation somehow fused with his Major tribulation, or maybe it was just because it was Lex’s destiny to get screwed. No one could say for certain what had caused it, for nothing like this had ever happened.","They could only look above at the memory older than even Eclipse herself.","A look of recognition flashed in Nuwa’s eyes as she looked at him - the progenitor of Jorlam, of Giants, of Mountain-men and all such races that boasted both size and power. A being so powerful and so ancient that even the few survivors of the Primordial realm did not know of him.","Eclipse, upon her throne, pulled out her Enigma Pillar and placed her hand upon it, searching through her archives of secrets as she tried to find any hints of who this was. Though there was no answer, there were rumors.","\"So that’s him... Pangu...\"","Lex sensed the danger above him, but all he could do was raise Daekol’s body above his own to continue using him as a shield. Even now, he did not stop his golden flames."]},{"number":2437,"title":"Chapter 2437: Axe’s descent","paragraphs":["Lex was hurt. He was genuinely hurt because at this point, he and Daekol were trading blows without holding back, and neither had the ability to dodge. They could only defend. Daekol kept taking on tremendous debt from his system to heal himself, while Lex relied on his excessive healing capability to keep recovering from the damage he suffered.","Even now, both of them were managing to keep pace with each other, despite doing so through incredibly different ways.","Daekol couldn’t make sense of it. He was a system user, a peak Celestial, a Sovereign, a Lord in Arch-Heaven and a champion of the Path of Chaos. His identity was so unique, there may never be another who could match him. It seemed impossible for anyone else to match him in his own cultivation realm, so then how could Lex do as much while he still technically wasn’t even a Celestial Immortal yet?","Meanwhile, Lex too had to admit that Daekol was genuinely an impressive opponent. Considering that he was still in his Dragon-Lex form, admitting as much was truly an incredible feat. To be able to keep up with Lex despite all the advantages he had was incredibly impressive.","It would have been incredible if they had not met as enemies. It was not often that Lex found someone who could go toe to toe with him. Unfortunately for Daekol, his greed got the better of him, and Lex wasn’t about to show any undue mercy.","Not to mention, at this point, Lex probably couldn’t show any mercy even if he wanted to. His doppelganger had told him that the average Dao Body tribulation was pretty easy. Considering that they had delayed his tribulation, it should be somewhat harder. Lex was actually prepared for that.","He was not, however, prepared for his two tribulations to fuse together to form something entirely new and completely unheard of. Suffice to say that no one in the history of history had attempted a Dao Body tribulation at the same time as a Major tribulation to the Celestial realm, if only because most who attempted to create a Dao Body were at the peak of the Celestial Immortal realm.","The few who weren’t at the peak... were at level 8 Celestial Immortal realm. There were no others, until Lex. Only he was crazy enough to attempt something like that and somehow survive the process.","Though Lex’s eyes could not see beyond the egg shell, his spirit sense reached out towards the sky, where Pangu’s visage was beginning to appear. Many had tried to learn more about the memory upon which this tribulation was based. There was finally an opportunity for them to do so now.","While only Eclipse uncovered the massive beings identity from among those who didn’t know, all who could see the tribulation could study everything about the tribulation itself.","Pangu’s massive eye seemed to lock onto Lex, and an intense emotion flashed through them.","The flicker of emotion, alone, was enough. Daekol’s spine shattered within his body, and the ligaments in Lex’s knees ruptured. He was forced out of his Dragon form, bringing him back to his normal human state. Of course, that did not stop him from continuing to breath fire.","The only reason Lex’s defense performed better was because of his partial Primordial Dao Body - the defense and strength of the body itself was entirely irrelevant otherwise.","\"Move out of my way, ****** . You will not survive my axe,\" said Pangu as he glared at Lex, his voice suddenly fading as he spoke some name.","Even though Lex’s mouth was busy breathing fire, he did not hesitate to use his spirit to respond.","\"Excuse me, massive sir in the sky. If you could just give me five minutes to move, I absolutely will. I’m kind of unable to move as I am right now.\"","He did not think pleading to the thing would work, but no one could blame him for trying.","\"Since you will not move, then DIE !\" the massive entity roared, and the eyes turned into that of anger.","The behemoth was too massive to truly see, far larger than what the mere horizon could hold. Yet upon seeing even a fragment of his enormous body, an image of his entire being automatically appeared in the observer’s mind.","Pangu raised his right arm above his head, holding a great axe, radiating a power that caused the universe itself to shudder. Before the axe could properly fall, the visage became smaller, weaker... more reflecting a tribulation of the level that Lex’s strength could actually trigger.","Of course, even so the descending force of that axe far outstripped Lex’s power. Daekol and Lex, both at the same time, felt that death had come knocking.","Daekol screamed, a massive body of a mythic creature suddenly appearing behind him. The creature seemed like it was still alive, but existed in some sort of stasis. Its body faintly gave off the aura of a broken Dao Heart. The creature was half Laoer, meaning it had half the bloodline of a Sage race.","Maybe Daekol had more measures, but he could not summon any of them in time.","At the same time, Lex too summoned his greatest defense. It was a shield made up of everything Lex had ever learned, all condensed together perfectly. It encapsulated his understanding of the laws of fire, of sword intent, of space, of defense itself, of physical strength and so much more. More importantly, it contained the law of karma - and all of Daekol’s karma that he had been able to get his hands on.","Yes, he was not just using Daekol’s body as a shield, he was using his karma too!","Then the axe fell, and honestly, even Lex himself did not know whether he was alive or dead, for with the descent of the axe, everything was extinguished. All light, all thought, all defenses, they all were cut down by the unstoppable axe.","In fact, in the absolute last moment, the Dream realm itself was about to be punctured by the axe, forever suffering permanent damage from that attack, until the Dream Master intervened. She did not stop the axe, only strengthened the Dream realm itself.","As for the area where the axe fell... no one could observe it any longer, for it no longer existed.","Even Daoflix, which had been streaming Lex’s fight even if all viewers had moved away, could not find any trace of the two.","Up in the air, slowly, steadily, the tribulation began to fade, with Pangu’s furious eyes the last thing to go."]},{"number":2438,"title":"Chapter 2438: The End - Recommended song Skyfall","paragraphs":["For the very short duration of Lex’s mutated Primordial Dao Body tribulation, no Dao Lords killed each other even on the Dream Arena. That felt a little ironic because now Lex felt like he was the one about to die.","Lex had always been proud of his defense, but today he experienced for the first time what it truly meant to have an overwhelming, unstoppable, irresistible attack. Whether it was the body Daekol pulled out as defense, Daekol himself, Lex’s defenses, or even his own body, not a single one of them had even slowed down the attack.","It wasn’t a hot knife through butter, more like a nuclear bomb eviscerating the butter itself.","The only thing that was able to resist the attack at all was the Primordial Dao Body itself, although Lex wasn’t quite sure how good a job it did because he couldn’t feel his legs.","To be more specific, as Lex lay inside a crater, his blurry vision looking up at what was probably the sky, he had no idea of anything. He didn’t know if Daekol was dead, he didn’t know if the tribulation was over, or what state his body was in, because he had not even a single ounce of spirit sense left to check up on himself.","He knew he was still alive, because, well, he was, and that about summed up the total extent of what he knew.","Somewhere on the fringes of his exhausted, weary mind, Lex knew that if something didn’t happen, he was going to die. Jack’s awareness could not help him at this moment because the moment the tribulation struck, Jack too fell unconscious. Maybe he too was on the verge of death, or maybe he was already dead - Lex had no way of knowing.","All he knew was that he was going to die if something didn’t happen.","\"Rebirth by fire... rebirth by fire... rebirth by... rebirth...\" Lex whispered in his croak voice, in the hopes that somehow the ability would activate. Shouldn’t this be the time it kicked in? Isn’t this what it was for?","Yet he felt not an ounce of fire, except the burning that was slowly building up in his spine as sensation finally began to return to him.","He blinked, and tears fell from his eyes, clearing up his vision somewhat. He raised his head... or tried to, and discovered that when his body weight was in tons, even lifting his head was a hard task.","\"Come on... rebirth...\" Lex muttered as he moved his right hand and discovered that... he still had a right hand.","Lex would have loved nothing more than to activate some healing ability at that moment, but he had no energy left in his body. Somewhere in the back of his mind, he could not help but wonder when the reward part of the tribulation would come. Even if the Dao Body tribulation had no significant reward, shouldn’t his Major tribulation reward him with an upgraded body and soul? Should it improve him? Heal him?","But there was nothing.","With his right hand, Lex grabbed onto his head and lifted it, finally allowing himself to see himself. His legs were gone, but his torso and head survived. Even though they survived, there wasn’t much to see.","He was mostly bones - black, burnt to a crisp bones, but bones nonetheless. There was some stuff that could have been muscle or organ, but now it was in such a state that Lex didn’t even know what to call it.","His heart, however, seemed entirely fine for some reason. He would have loved to investigate why that was, but he had no means. He let his head fall back on the ground, causing a small boom.","\"Last time I trust a damn phoenix,\" Lex muttered as he grit his teeth - hey, he still had teeth - and grabbed his heart. His vision was beginning to fade, his consciousness was beginning to weaken, and still the tribulation had offered him no reward, nor had the damn Rebirth by Fire ability kicked in.","But Lex refused to die. He had too much to live for. He had just decided to start dating again back when he was in the Hollow.","Lex squeezed his heart, though it was entirely unknown what he expected to come of that, there were no veins or arteries connected to his heart. They had all been burnt or destroyed. Even so, he squeezed. If his heart wouldn’t pump on its own, he’d pump it himself. If the damn Rebirth by Fire wouldn’t work, then he would just do it himself. This wouldn’t be the first time he’d recreated his body from mere remnants.","\"I will not die,\" Lex grunted through gritted teeth. \"Not today... I will... not... die...\"","He fought with all his might, but his self awareness continued to fade. No amount of will power could change reality. Without his Sovereign realm, he was not really a Sovereign. Without the energy to use Domination, he could not force his supremacy on anything.","His thoughts became blurred, and then faded altogether so that there was nothing he could do anymore.","Yet his body did not stop. Even when his mind shut down, and even when he could no longer think, his hand kept manually pumping his heart.","Jack had prepared a tremendous amount of divine energy to send to Lex for his final clash with Daekol, but the tribulation had changed too quickly. He hadn’t had time to send it.","Liz had made a deal with Oaka to allow her to go help Lex at a critical moment, but that had to wait for the tribulation to end first. Unfortunately, when the tribulation ended, no one could find Lex.","There were so many contingencies he’d made, but none of them could be used. There were so many people willing to help him, but none could find him. In this moment, where all of Lex’s power was gone, and even his thoughts faded away, the only thing left was a grim determination not to die that had seeped into his bones.","A suffocating silence threatened to blanket what was left of Lex, only the irregular sound of a forcefully beating heart keeping it at bay.","What no one realized was that Lex’s tribulation was not fully over. The last word spoken by the figure in the sky hung around Lex’s body like a curse, siphoning energy from the tribulation to stick around just a bit longer, with no other purpose than to usher him into death. But the curse, too, was quickly dwindling.","On the border of the crater stood a figure, watching to see which would give out first - the curse from an entity long lost and forgotten, or Lex’s bitter resolve."]},{"number":2439,"title":"Chapter 2439: Someone show him","paragraphs":["Anyone who knew Harriot knew that the number of things that he cared about besides Eclipses’ matters were very few, and the people he cared about were even fewer. His goals were always aligned to Eclipse’s goals, and his concerns were always his concerns.","Thus, the very obvious frown on his face would take many by surprise if they could see it, especially if they knew the context in which it appeared.","\"Are you sure you don’t want me to help him? He looks like he’s going to die any moment now,\" said Harriot as he looked down into the crater at what was soon to be Lex’s corpse.","\"There’s still a tribulation field all around him,\" responded Eclipse from her throne, even though it was far away. \"Do not, under any circumstances, interfere with his tribulation in any way. If he dies... then that is simply the consequence for his own actions. Neither he nor the Innkeeper can blame me for that.\"","Harriot turned to look at Eclipse, who also seemed to be watching Lex, and then looked back at the human. His hand was manually pumping his heart which was keeping him alive somehow. He suspected that it had something to do with the Primordial Farham Egg Shell that had become embedded in his heart and then fused with it, but he couldn’t say.","After all, he had a Dragonheart, and those things were notoriously difficult to stop.","\"If you don’t want to interfere with his tribulation, why did you have me bring him here from the Dream realm?\" Harriot asked as he narrowed his eyes and searched for any signs of vitality. Unfortunately, to avoid disturbing the tribulation field around Lex’s body, he could not use any of his powers to observe, so he genuinely couldn’t tell what state he was in.","\"It’s not the same,\" explained Eclipse. \"The Dream realm is connected to every other realm, and the literal fabric of the realm almost tore open. Lex would have ended up in the Void. You know what happens when Primordials enter the Void unprotected - we do not need a repeat of the Acorn realm. So, I just let him fall from the Dream realm into the Garden. You can blame the Innkeeper for being an absent parent - forcing me to act in his stead.\"","Harriot rubbed his eyebrow as he tried to accept that logic. To be fair, Eclipse was right. With Lex, more or less, being considered a Primordial now, entering the Void unprotected would have led to unpredictable results.","But just leaving him there also felt kind of bad.","\"I’ll be subtle about it. No one needs to know we helped. Watching him beat his own heart is just...\"","Harriot just didn’t want to admit that he was concerned about Lex, but Eclipse had already diverted her focus. The Enigma Pillar was where she hid all her secrets. It was a tool far more powerful than anyone could imagine, and it also held far more secrets than anyone could imagine.","Yet Eclipse was still limited by many things, as unbelievable as it was. During the early years of the universe, she was incredibly weak. In those days, she was nowhere near as strong as she was now, and there were too many people stronger than her. Thus, she did not know the fine details of many things that occurred before her birth in the early to middle years of her life.","For example, the name Pangu was one she drew from the memories of an enemy she had once slain. She knew almost nothing about him, save that he was apparently incredibly large and unbelievably powerful.","The problem with ’incredibly powerful’ was that it lacked a lot of context. How powerful was he exactly? Knowing that answer... would allow her to guess the strength of whoever had stood in Pangu’s path that fateful day.","As for what day it actually was, why they clashed, and what the outcome was were all things she did not know. The fact, however, that the universe chose to give it such incredible emphasis reflected just how important that confrontation was.","It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to say that the fight Pangu had that day changed the universe forever. It was just that no one knew how or why.","\"His pace is slowing down - if you want to do something, this may be your last chance,\" said Harriot, interrupting her reading.","Eclipse sighed, and then looked at her poodle. Sometimes, she forgot that it was in his nature to be cute.","\"Someone show him what’s going on,\" Eclipse said before turning back to the Enigma Pillar.","Harriot wasn’t sure who acted, but suddenly he could see the tribulation field around Lex.","The Dao Body tribulation was more than just a memory, or a test. The more severe the tribulation, the more realistic the memory.","Lex’s tribulation had summoned the figure out into the open, allowed it to speak, and to strike with his axe. Everyone focused on the attack from the axe, failing to realize that every single aspect of the memory was the tribulation.","The moment Lex looked up and spoke to it, he was not talking to Pangu, the ancient being, but he was entering a confrontation with the tribulation itself. It was just that the tribulation was using this particular memory to enact it out.","Thus, it wasn’t just the axe strike that landed on Lex that was a part of the tribulation, but the figure’s final curse as well. When he had yelled out ’die’ at Lex, it was not just simple verbal venting, but an actual, genuine curse.","That curse was still active now, all around Lex, using whatever energy was left from the tribulation to try to kill him.","In turn, Lex’s resistance so far was not just an attempt at continued living, but was direct resistance against the tribulation. Everyone thought that Dao Body tribulations had no feedback. Well, in Lex’s state, Eclipse wasn’t so sure.","\"Don’t take this away from him,\" she said to Harriot. \"If he can survive this on his own, then the significance of it will be far greater than you realize.\"","There was another thing that she didn’t mention. Inside the Primordial Garden, Lex would also remain protected from any chances that happened to the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum. That was significant because humanity seemed to be losing its position on that list, and fast. Celestial Immortals humans across the universe started to suffer from tremendously terrible luck, and while that sounded simple, in truth it was leading them to their deaths.","The human race was losing its position, and that was further causing the unlucky Celestials to suffer. The timing... could have been better. If Lex hadn’t entered the Primordial Garden, he would have likely already died."]},{"number":2440,"title":"Chapter 2440: A brand new tribulation I","paragraphs":["There were no thoughts running through Lex’s mind, but he wasn’t dead yet. He could still feel pain. He could feel his body - what was left of it - protesting aggressively against his every action, or rather his only action.","His right hand, repeatedly squeezing and relaxing, forcing his heart to pump. Things had not gone according to plan. He placed the egg shell on his heart expecting to fuse with it when his Rebirth by fire ability kicked in. But the ability wasn’t kicking in.","No wonder Phoenix’s were on the verge of extinction - their ultimate ability, which triggered upon entering a near death state, came with performance issues.","Thus, even with his mind shrouded in darkness, and even with all his thoughts disappearing, Lex could feel the pain in his body. Pain - it was so easy to ignore when he had a goal, a purpose, and some energy to pursue those goals. But when all he felt was pain, with no mind to understand context, it was not so easy.","In that case, existence became an endless abyss, without start or end, and only darkness and pain to keep company. What then, kept the hand moving? Kept the heart beating?","For some people, it could be a profound sense of purpose or meaning. But for Lex, in that moment, at the bottom of the crater, it was an overwhelming sense of pettiness. He refused to die out of sheer spite against the ability Rebirth by Fire, for which he had such great expectations, but it refused to activate. In his last moments, all he could think of was that if he wanted something done right, he had to do it himself.","So even when he felt nothing except pain, using whatever trace amount of energy left in his body, Lex refused to give up. He refused to give in. He kept his heart pumping.","Yet there was no blood left, so what was the heart even pumping?","Energy. It was pumping out trace amounts of energy so little, that the only thing it could fuel was his own hand.","The egg shell had protected his heart, but that did not mean Lex could automatically absorb or fuse with the egg shell. His heart wouldn’t suddenly gain the egg shell’s powers. The only reason Lex had been able to fuse with things for so long was because of his Empyrean bloodline, but mostly because of his cultivation technique.","At the moment, however, Lex was not using the technique so the heart couldn’t fuse with the egg. So where was the energy coming from?","It came from the heart itself, and whatever was left of his body. Much as what Lex experienced during the gluttony retribution, his heart forced some energy out of his body, bit by bit, piece by piece, giving him the ability to continue pumping.","Had circumstances been even slightly different, Lex’s excellent healing abilities would have long kicked in and started to heal him. But that last bit of cursed energy, trying to kill Lex, suppressed it all.","But ultimately, true power never came from hate. The hatred of a prehistoric monstrosity, empowered by two, mutated tribulations, clashed against Lex and tried to wear him down. It kept him from healing and tried to suppress him until those final embers of life were extinguished.","But while the energy from the tribulation waned, the intensity of Lex’s spite remained strong, keeping his hand pumping so long as it was not entirely deprived of energy.","Under Harriot’s concerned gaze, the tribulation field around Lex slowly weakened as its energy dissipated until at last, it vanished.","For one, brief moment, absolutely nothing happened. Then all the energy in the surroundings that had been pushed out by the tribulation field came rushing back in, flooding Lex’s body. At the same time, a thin patch of tribulation clouds began to form over Lex’s body.","\"Umm, is his tribulation supposed to start back up?\" asked Harriot as he stared at Lex.","Eclipse, who was reading through her secrets, paused and looked up.","\"I mean, this kind of thing has never happened before so it’s hard to guess, but I would have guessed that the tribulation should have ended after that,\" she said, looking towards Lex. Then she narrowed her eyes. She could not peer into what was happening with the tribulation laws since her abilities were sealed, but she could make an educated guess.","\"Or perhaps the Primordial Dao Body tribulation did fuse with the whole tribulation, and only occupied the lightning one, allowing the others to continue as intended. But that seems unlikely. Yet if it fused with the entire tribulation, and each one occurs with the same intensity, then this is no longer a tribulation. This is just a death sentence.\"","After a few moments of observing the clouds, though, another thing occurred to her and she shook her head. A certain look flashed through her eyes as a look of anticipation appeared on her face.","\"I have another theory though. Lately, the universe has gained a lot of energy, and many of Arch-Heaven’s laws have evolved. Maybe... what we’re seeing is a new, never before seen version of the tribulation.\"","Harriot was surprised by Eclipse’s words, but that didn’t ease his concern. Lex was on his deathbed right now, and he was in no condition to face anything.","In truth, Lex was already much better. When the natural, ambient energy came flooding back, his body rapidly absorbed it like a dried out sponge, allowing him to heal. Of course, his healing was by no means something that would be quick. Considering the state of his body, with no external help, it would take him anywhere between ten to twenty thousand years of healing before recovering to a moderate state. That would still not be close to his full strength.","He turned back around, but this time he didn’t see Eclipse busy with work, nor was she looking on casually. Instead, she was looking at Lex with a great deal of anticipation as if she knew what was about to come.","A stream of transparent energy flowed down from the clouds and wrapped itself around Lex’s body, slowly lifting him off the ground and bringing him up to the clouds."]},{"number":2441,"title":"Chapter 2441: Reason and logic be damned!","paragraphs":["A normal Major tribulation to the Celestial Immortal realm followed the same pattern as the one for the Heaven Immortal realm. There was the Lightning tribulation, the Fire tribulation and the Spirit.","Over the years, many researchers theorized that this form of tribulations was actually incomplete based on a simple trend. Generally speaking, as the cultivation levels rose higher, the corresponding difficulty and complexity of anything related to them also rose.","This was a simple law of nature.","For example, mining simple moral gold was pretty easy, but once certain types of golds corresponded to the value of certain Immortal realms, harvesting and purifying them became much harder. Harvesting a simple piece of cabbage was pretty simple, but picking up a Celestial Flight Cabbage was not just a matter of reaching down and picking up.","This trend could also be seen in the tribulation for the Heaven Immortal realm, which had one more trial compared to the one for Earth Immortal realm, specifically the Spirit tribulation.","The fact, then, that the Celestial Immortal tribulation added no new levels, and instead made preexisting tribulations harder seemed somewhat incomplete. They argued that there should be one more level to the Major tribulation, and that being tougher was not enough.","Of course, the foundation of the whole argument was that the universe was still not in a mature state, and that there was room for evolution or growth in the operations of the universe’s systems. There was no actual evidence that the tribulation should have another level.","Yet as Lex’s body rose into the sky, heading towards the clouds, Eclipse suspected that she was witnessing for the first time what would now be the final stage or step of the Major tribulations leading to the Celestial level.","She was not too concerned about Lex’s condition, though. She had a deep enough understanding of the functions of the universe that she could guess what was about to happen, and did not even need to rely on her abilities.","Lex’s body rose directly through the clouds and was brought to the edge of a small, circular pool of some unknown liquid. Around the edge of the pool was a natural formation, absorbing the energy of the tribulation and turning it into the liquid itself. The interesting thing was that the formation was atypical, in the sense that it was not made based on the environment or items or some specific arrangement, but that it was made entirely from some unknown language that had never before appeared in the universe.","Eclipse was not only certain that this language was entirely brand new, but she was also certain that this type of formation had never appeared before in the universe. The number of changes appearing in the universe was slowly and steadily rising.","Lex’s body hovered over the pool, his abysmal condition reflected perfectly in the still surface of the liquid. For a moment, nothing else happened. Then, without any semblance of ceremony or even an ounce of gentleness, he was dropped into the pool.","The stillness of the liquid was shattered, giving way to a great tumult. The dirt and char covering Lex’s bones came floating to the top of the liquid before being eviscerated, while great amounts of the liquid flooded into what was left of his body, nourishing him, strengthening him, ushering him into a new realm.","Eclipse felt a great temptation to grab a sample of the liquid, but since she had not interfered with Lex’s tribulation to help him, she would not interfere with it now to sate her own curiosity either. It was only fair. Since he earned this reward on his own, he should also enjoy it on his own as well.","\"Sometimes I think my heart is just too soft,\" Eclipse said with a sigh, attracting an odd gaze from Nulli, Harriot, and anyone else who heard. She had been called many things, Primordial Queen, Harbinger of Pain, Unstoppable Calamity, Living Calamity and several other versions of calamities, but never had she been called soft hearted. At least, not in their memories.","They did not interrupt her musings, and instead continued to watch Lex. This was something new for them too, and unlike Eclipse, the only way they could figure out what was happening was by watching.","\"Is that... liquid lightning?\" Nulli asked with a frown, feeling confused. How could lightning nourish and heal Lex, as it was clearly doing.","\"In some cultures and myths, lightning is considered the source of all life,\" Eclipse explained while she watched. \"Of course, myths don’t alter reality - instead they are often a reflection of what already exists. Lightning has a very extreme nature, yes, but it has traces of Life laws in them as well, originating from the yang nature of it.","\"But that’s not what’s happening here, because what Lex is submerged in isn’t liquid lightning. This is a smaller version of the Tribulation Pool - the source of all realm associated tribulations, found within the Arch-Heaven. The lightning, fire and spirit tribulations are all formed from this liquid in this pool, and this is also the reason why cultivators grow and are nourished after facing tribulations.","\"The very reason that Dao tribulations are considered death tribulations instead of nourishing ones is because they are not sourced nor associated with this pool. The fact that Lex is being directly baptized in this pool means that... actually, I can’t say for certain what it means yet. I doubt things are as simple as him just being rewarded. Let’s keep watching and see what happens. I don’t want to make a wrong guess and accidentally influence nature’s design.\"","The others just nodded and continued to watch.","The liquid in the pool began to decrease at a noticeable rate as it was absorbed into Lex’s body, allowing it to slowly regain its shape.","Still, it was nearly thirty hours before Lex’s eyes opened, and he gasped for breath. The moment he woke up, Lex was not flooded with relief at surviving, or surprised by his surroundings.","Nay, Lex was filled with extreme fury and indignation. The target of his extreme emotions? It was neither Daekol, nor was it the tribulation that nearly killed him.","\"Damn birds! I’ll turn you into fried chicken if I ever get my hands on you!\" Lex cursed at no one in particular, and focused on the entire phoenix race. In all his years as a cultivator, Lex had faced many hardships, tribulations and difficulties, but never had he been scammed to this extent!","In all fairness, there was a perfectly logical reason for why the ability hadn’t triggered, but Lex no longer cared. Logic and reason be damned, it was now his life’s mission to reveal to the universe the scam that was Rebirth by Fire, and the phoenixes as a whole!"]},{"number":2442,"title":"Chapter 2442: Because of course","paragraphs":["Only after his outburst did Lex realize that his surroundings had changed. That realization was quickly followed by an awareness of everything that had happened. That one axe attack had nearly killed him outright. Lex had rarely ever encountered such irresistible might, to the point where no defense or preparation mattered.","His mind raced, not only to observe his surroundings and understand his situation, but also to trace Daekol. An attack like that was more than enough to kill anyone, but Lex refused to believe that Daekol was dead.","Though his interactions with Daekol were limited, he understood enough about him to know that the guy was meticulous. If Lex himself had prepared contingencies in case he got in trouble, how could Daekol lack them?","Even in his weakened state, fully aware that the tribulation might not be over and that he might still have difficult trials to face, Lex did not fully commit himself to healing. Half of his attention - the part that he had originally used to assess his situation - was used to focus on healing and understanding the role this strange liquid played in helping him recover.","The other half of Lex’s attention was used to summon the Karmic Bead and leverage the deeply intertwined karmic connection he’d built with Daekol to find him.","At first glance, it seemed like Daekol was truly and genuinely dead. A simple search for his karma returned only traces of the past - no present. Yet Lex was not so easily convinced. Not only did he not give up the search, he increased the amount of energy he put into it.","In his current state, Lex did not have much energy at all, but that was also why he needed to search right now. If Lex was in such a state, he didn’t believe that Daekol would be any better. If he was alive, he would also be severely injured, which made this the best possible chance to find him.","Yet no matter how he searched or how he manipulated the karmic bead, he found nothing. For a moment Lex felt a hint of genuine doubt. Could he be overthinking things? Was he truly dead? Was Lex the kind of person who would buy a haunted house in a horror movie just because it was cheap, then go into the dark basement alone when there’s no electricity?","No way in hell! Even if the Karmic Bead did not give him any feedback, Lex trusted his own experiences. Even his instincts could be fooled by systems-","Lex’s eyes widened as he realized something. Yes! Daekol had a system! If he was using his system to hide or survive somehow, it would be much harder to find him! But now that Lex had an idea of what to look for, at least he had a direction to search in.","His instincts completely ignored systems, but he’d owned a system for most of his life by now. He was intimately familiar with the workings of a system, its aura and most other things about it which could be observed and sensed.","If Daekol’s system was weakened, or not operating at full capacity, then maybe Lex could still find him. This was an enemy he absolutely could not let escape, or else Lex would never know when he might strike again.","Lex closed his eyes and even reduced his focus on healing, instead concentrating all effort on the Karmic Bead to locate Daekol via his system!","In a state of such intense concentration, time seemed to lose all meaning. Whether he spent seconds searching or hours or maybe even longer, he did not know. What he did know was","that once he began searching for signs of Daekol’s system, he finally seemed to get a lead.","His Karmic Bead, which could find no trace of any active karma at all, suddenly seemed to sense something. It was like the kind of thing that was hard to notice at first, but once noticed was hard to ignore.","After a short while of searching, all at once the Karmic Bead turned into a thick, black thread and shot out into the distance, beyond the realm he was in and far, far out into the universe.","Lex nearly collapsed. Daekol was too far, he didn’t have enough energy. Yet now that Lex was awake, there was much he could do. Lex focused on Jack, and discovered that the fairy was not dead - he was merely in a state of shock due to the intensity of the Primordial Dao Body tribulation.","He forced his tiny fairy body to wake up and send over the divine energy he had accumulated. Though Jack too needed some time to recover properly, right now no time could be spared and extreme measures were required.","He forcefully sent over the item, causing much of the divinity to be wasted, but Lex couldn’t care at the moment. Using the divine energy that flooded into his body, Lex did two things.","First, he channeled a great deal of it into the Karmic Bead. If a miracle is what it took to reach out to that damn Sovereign, then a miracle is what he would perform!","The second thing Lex did was use the divine energy to try to forcefully remove whatever kept himself disconnected from the Midnight Inn System! As soon as the system came back to him, he could-","Lex’s eyes constricted the moment the blockade broke, and a barrage of emergency notifications flooded his mind.","\"LEX THERE’S SOMETHING WRONG WITH THE SYSTEM!\" Mary’s voice yelled in Lex’s mind, but he’d already figured that out by the time she screamed!","He needed to merely glance at the notifications to know that the system was prompting him that Primordial energy was leaking into the system, and that it was about 22% corrupted due to it!","However, even weakened as he was, Lex was a Celestial Immortal now, and his senses were far better than they used to - especially for something within his own soul. Although the system was showing him 22% corruption, the actual figure was around 93%!","It had absorbed far more Primordial energy than it was showing him, and already it was going against its programming, lying and deceiving him!","Lex could have been anywhere in the universe when he discovered something like this and it would have been a terrible and grave situation. However, since he was inside a tribulation, and more specifically inside a miniature Tribulation Pool, the situation automatically became a whole lot worse. Because of course, how could anything ever be normal with Lex?","<anno data-annotation-id=\"dddca98c-4f46-6fe2-20d3-b426d448f29a\" data-title=\"Within the Primary realm, the stele containing the Universal Mandates trembled.\">Within the Primary realm, the stele containing the Universal Mandates trembled. 1 </anno>","<annotations style=\"display: none;\">The Universal Mandates were mentioned and discussed in ch 1433 and 1584. Read both of them for context on Universal Mandates.</annotations>"]},{"number":2443,"title":"Chapter 2443: From bad to worse","paragraphs":["The tribulation was doing funny things. Lex didn’t know exactly what was happening, but he could tell for certain that something was going awry. At the same time, his system was going haywire, his divine energy was running out, Mary was screaming in his ear and Daekol was getting away. Oh, and his healing had also slowed down due to whatever was happening with his tribulation.","It was all a bit overwhelming, and yet... Lex adapted quickly. He was injured, weakened, borderline overwhelmed, but most of all, he was incensed. It was all those damn Phoenix’s fault... no wait, it was all that damn Sovereigns fault.","No matter what happened, he would not let him get away. But at the same time, this system absorbing Primordial energy was also not something he could ignore.","In truth, Lex was severely underestimating the seriousness of the issue, mainly because the malfunctioning system was not informing him that a Universal Mandate was on the verge of being disobeyed. While Lex himself did not know what the Universal Mandates were, his experience inside Abaddon where even the system gave him a notification proclaiming its adherence to the mandates let him know that it was not the kind of thing he could overlook.","Within the Primary realm, the stele upon which the mandates were written trembled, and that was enough to cause a universal emergency far beyond the scope of even what the ongoing war had caused.","Asux, the Primal Monarch, along with a few of the Primal Kings who were still around, immediately arrived around the mandate, trying to peer into who was on the verge of breaking a mandate! There was no question that as soon as they discovered the identity of the perpetrator, they would unleash any weapon they needed to so that he could be stopped.","The Primals exchanged no words, nor did they glance at one another. All their focus was on the stele as Asux tried to connect with the stele to learn the identity of whoever was about to break a mandate.","In a situation like this, even Nuwa dared not interfere, nor could she even if she wanted to. When Eclipse brought Lex into the Primordial Garden, she had made sure to give him the privacy he needed, which meant that Nuwa had no idea what was happening.","Eclipse did not have her powers which is why she could not see into the issue Lex was having, nor could the others who were with her. Yes, some of them, such as Nulli, sensed that a mandate was about to be broken, but she could not tell who was causing it. Naturally, she could not connect it to Lex since there were no signs just yet that he was the source of this trouble.","The more urgent the situation, the more calm Lex became. He reassessed his priorities, and barely placed addressing the system issue above hunting down Daekol, though he did not stop that either.","He connected with the system and, for the first time in so many years, sensed the condition of the Midnight Inn. Contrary to the mess his notification tab was filled with, the Inn itself seemed entirely and utterly calm, though he noticed many key members missing. He could not spare any thought to investigate their whereabouts right then, though.","A projection of the Innkeeper appeared within the Midnight Inn. He appeared without any fanfare at all, so at first no one sensed him - at least within the Inn.","Asux and the other Primals, however, locked on to an image of the Innkeeper who seemed to appear out of the darkness. He wasn’t quite the cause of the mandate break, but he was certainly connected to it.","\"Who is that?\" Asux asked, even as he prepared to launch an attack across the universe itself.","\"The Innkeeper - a mysterious Dao Lord, with little to no information about his identity or past being leaked. Even his race is not entirely confirmed,\" responded one of the Primal Kings. \"Even if he is not the culprit, the target is surely nearby. I say we eradicate the very realm he’s in for safety.\"","Asux did not respond to the suggestion just yet, although he was preparing to act as soon as he needed to.","From the moment Lex unlocked his system till now, half a second had passed. The liquid from the tribulation pool, which was until now healing him, suddenly became thick and viscous, trapping Lex within instead of healing him.","The tribulation was investigating, trying to understand what the cause of the anomaly was. Lex himself did not understand what was happening, but he could roughly guess that this had something to do with the Primordial energy.","He clicked his teeth, more annoyed than concerned by the situation. A mere system, one that was connected to him and largely under his control, could not cause him to be worried. Instead, he had another idea.","\"Mary, the system is not obeying its own rules right now,\" said Lex, his tone entirely calm despite the situation. \"I think this may be the perfect moment for me to remove your soul from the system itself. Guide me on how to do it.\"","Mary, who had been building her body for all this time, paused. Lex was right. This really was the perfect opportunity, but the danger...","\"Be at ease,\" said Lex, his presence and visage spreading the calm and confidence that had so long been associated with the Innkeeper. The difference was, this time, it wasn’t just the Host Attire causing that feeling. Lex himself had the confidence to deal with this situation. \"Just tell me what to do, and leave the rest to me.\"","As he spoke, Lex also unleashed his Sovereign realm, tightly wrapped around his main body so as to affect his body, soul, and most importantly, the system that resided within.","By now, one full second had passed by, and the tribulation was probing inside Lex’s body, yet seemed to be blocked by the Sovereign realm. Lex could not allow the tribulation to sense the system - his instincts told him that would lead to a very bad outcome.","Yet even if the tribulation itself could not directly probe him, the universe itself was in search of the criminal who dared even attempt breaking a Universal Mandate. While the culprit remained hidden, for now, much like Asux himself, the universe locked in on the appearance of the Innkeeper.","Suddenly, every Dao Lord in the universe, asleep or awake, free or imprisoned, learned of the Innkeeper as the universe spread the information in the hopes that someone could find him, and the criminal acting against the mandates.","This was no longer a projection in the sky or a vision from a tribulation - this was a direct message being sent into the minds of all Dao Lords! Unfortunately, since Lex himself was not a Dao Lord, he was not aware of the situation, and he continued to act as normal."]},{"number":2444,"title":"Chapter 2444: Holy sh-","paragraphs":["There were too many issues, so Lex simplified them. He made a list of issues that needed to be dealt with in the order of importance and urgency. The system’s absorption of Primordial energy was clearly a major issue based simply on the fact that it showed Lex a fake system report.","From the day he got his system, he’d been distrustful of it, but no matter its intentions, it always adhered to the rules and structure that governed its operations. He had not come to trust the system, for its intentions were to use Lex for entertainment purposes, but he had come to trust the holistic nature of the guidelines that governed the systems actions.","If by absorbing Primordial energy the system could bypass those firm boundaries, then everything he had built using the system was at risk.","The severity of the issue would cause anyone to panic, feel anxious, and treat it like an issue that needed to be dealt with immediately. Lex, however, had been dealing with life-threatening, urgent issues basically his whole life, so he did not panic.","He figured out how to deal with the system, and once that was done, found that there was room for him to take advantage of the system’s current state.","Yes, Daekol was a lingering issue, but with his connection to his system reestablished, he had every confidence that he could take Daekol down sooner rather than later.","Mary understood better than Lex how urgent the situation was, but she was also not some inexperienced amateur. Her understanding of Lex and his capabilities was perhaps second only to Lex himself, which is why despite what logic told her, she put her faith into Lex.","She also tested herself, and found that the restraints that the system had put on her for so long had all loosened by a lot.","In a single moment, she gathered all her thoughts and channeled them into Lex’s mind, which was much quicker than speaking.","\"Focus on the system core. Externally it seems like a single, cohesive entity, but in truth its structure is far more modular than you can imagine. You cannot normally see the internal structure of a system until reaching the Dao Lord realm, but that doesn’t mean you can’t interact with it.","\"Back then, I suffered an injury so grave it nearly shattered my Dao and my soul, and the system suffered alongside me. We were both critically wounded, but I realized something crazy. Even when damaged, the system followed a set of protocols, as if the creator had even designed what to do in such a state.","\"That meant that even injured, damaged and on the verge of being destroyed, the system already had the means to protect itself and recover. Considering the... unique nature of my location, and the injury I suffered, I had no delusions. I knew I would face death sooner or later, so I played a last, desperate gambit.","\"I used a treasure I’d gotten from the system before to preserve my damaged Dao, placing it inside the treasure as if it were some physical item, and attached a segment of my soul as well. Then I used that treasure and inserted it into the system as a temporary energy source.","\"That means, for all these years, the reason that the system has been able to operate above its grade and level is because it was operating on an energy source based on a genuine Dao - even if it was fragmented. But that energy source is also not originally part of the system, causing internal operation problems.","\"Preserving the energy source is a medium-priority task in the system’s internal operations directory, but if you can trigger a high-priority, self diagnostic and repair task, the ’battery’ will be officially detected as a foreign object.","\"That means when you scan the core of the system, you’ll be able to sense the core as one, whole item, but also a contradictory, foreign aura within it. You’ll need to lock onto that foreign aura and forcefully pull it out of the system immediately - or else the system will crush the ’battery’ and use it as a material resource to repair itself properly. In short... if you miss the timing, or are unable to do it, I’ll die\"","There was a pause in the message, as if to let Lex absorb what she had said, and let him evaluate whether or not he still had the confidence to go through with this.","Then she began to guide Lex on the intricate method by which he could force the system core to trigger a high-priority self-diagnosis. To be clear, this was different from the other self diagnosis that the system usually performed before telling Lex the percentage damage that it suffered.","The problem, however, that Lex immediately identified was that Mary’s method to trigger the self diagnosis might work while the system is working normally. Now that it had an issue, even the system itself seemed to have enough self awareness to try to hide its predicament.","In such a situation, why would it trigger a self-diagnosis? Because Lex would order it.","Lex wasted not a moment. As soon as he was done listening to Mary’s instructions, he unleashed his Sovereign realm to the best of his ability, and condensed it to only exist up to one millimetre outside his body - approximately the size of ten hundred dollar bills stacked atop one another.","He focused on the system deep within his soul, and inside the Inn, he used his projection to focus his power on the system panel as much as he could manage.","Across the universe, every single Dao Lord in the universe saw the Innkeeper. They knew that it wasn’t that the Innkeeper was the one breaking the mandates, but the stele singled him out nevertheless. Maybe he saw facing the one breaking the mandates, or maybe he was facilitating it. Maybe he was the only person who could hope to stop it. They did not know the details - they just watched.","The Innkeeper, appearing as calm as he always did, opened his mouth and uttered a single word.","\" Stop .\"","That was it. The vision ended. The stele stopped vibrating, and everything went back to normal, leaving all those who were watching stunned.","What had just happened? Had the Innkeeper stopped the mandate from being broken with a single word or... or had he directly stopped the stele from showing his vision?","For a single, unified second, all Dao Lords across the universe froze in shock as they tried to understand what had just happened.","\"Holy sh-\""]},{"number":2445,"title":"Chapter 2445: For her","paragraphs":["\"Holy shi-\"","\"NOOOOooooooO!\"","\"Why’d you stop? Show me more! SHOW! ME! MORE!\"","\"What happened? Quick! Someone put on Daoflix! Find out what happens next!\"","All across the universe, countless Dao Lords lost their minds when the feed suddenly cut off - especially because of the manner in which it was cut off.","There was a Dao Lord who flipped the table he was sitting at, but he didn’t even realize because he was extending his senses out into the universe to try to learn what was happening.","Another one smashed his face into the television, and then into a wall, and then into the surface of the planet he was on. But no matter where he smashed his face, he could not tune back into the feed because it had been cut off entirely.","Perhaps the only Dao Lord who couldn’t care less about the feed cutting off was Asux. He didn’t care that the vision ended - only that the stele stopped trembling. That was enough for him.","\"Someone, send the Innkeeper a box of chocolates from me,\" said Asux as he turned away.","Too many Dao Lords were in such critical situations that they could not afford to continue wondering what was happening with the Innkeeper - such as the ones on the Dream Arena - but there were also many who could think of nothing else.","\"This is so embarrassing,\" said Eclipse as she rubbed her eyes, trying not to look at Nulli beside her who had turned entirely pink. Even back during the Tea Party, Nulli had not turned as pink as she was now - and the sight was only made worse by her heavy breathing.","The sight of the Innkeeper halting the desecration of the Universal Mandate with a single word - it was too overpowering. In Nulli’s mind, there was no woman alive who could witness that scene without feeling thoroughly enamored. Eclipse didn’t count.","Afraid that Nulli might do something in her pink state, Eclipse had to summon some helpers to... restrain Nulli and help calm her down. She was only allowed to return when she returned to her normal, crystal blue appearance.","Only after Nulli was gone did Eclipse remove her hand and looked up at Lex reluctantly. She had almost considered having a private meeting with the Innkeeper after this, but now she felt like doing so was not such a good idea. Pink Nulliths were too unpredictable - she couldn’t risk it.","Nuwa, on the other hand, just sighed, closed her eyes and went to sleep. She couldn’t deal with this stuff anymore - best to just pretend like she couldn’t see what Lex was doing. She had to admit, though, that among any of the races she helped create, she had never encountered anyone with even 1% of the guts that Lex had.","The masters of the Sage races could not help but pay attention to this mysterious character. Up until now, everything they heard about him was in the rumors and hearsay. It was only now that they had, for the first time, properly witnessed his true, genuine prowess and found him to be incomparable.","The Innkeeper was truly a unique existence within the universe - an extreme rarity.","The problem was... the Innkeeper was considered a patron of humanity, but Destiny had covertly made arrangements for humanity’s destiny to be devoured. That meant that sooner or later... someone would need to deal with him.","But then they thought back to that one word ’stop’. That one word - was it merely meant for the criminal breaking the mandate, or was it also a message to Destiny herself?","Speculations and rumors were rife, and the chaos in the universe only continued to increase after that. Lex, however, neither knew about any of that, nor could he afford to care about anything else at that moment.","He’d seen how responsive his system was towards Sovereigns, and although he was not a genuine Sovereign just yet, he was the owner of this system. That had to make up for the gap.","Within Lex’s soul, under the joint influence of Domination and the Sovereigns realms enhancement of Lex’s status, the system truly and genuinely stopped. To be specific, the normal operations of the system did not stop - it was the further absorption of Primordial energy that stopped.","Had Lex still been at the peak of the Heaven Immortal realm, it may not have been so easy to achieve as much. But now, even though his tribulation wasn’t completely over, Lex was already more than halfway through to becoming a Celestial Immortal.","The change in Lex’s strength was not something that could be easily explained. The simplest way to describe it was that if he had fought Daekol in this state, the fight would not have lasted nearly as long - Lex could feel as much deep within his bones.","\" There is a foreign object interfering with your operations. Perform a self diagnosis ,\" said Lex, even as he manipulated his energy into the type of soul pollution that Mary had told him about, and condensed it all around the system, forcefully pushing it with.","He had also been specific in his wording - choosing to scan for foreign objects rather than Primordial energy. Doing as much would have caused much greater resistance from the system. For now, seeing that he had merely stopped the absorption of Primordial energy rather than withdrawing it, his system did not resist.","The system had a soul, which meant that it was a living being. It had a memory, and some form of spirit, even if those aspects weren’t pronounced. Up until the system could truly break free of his influence, it dared not underestimate Lex - he was the human who was meant to die along the way, but had overcome every single adversity he had ever faced.","The system began its scan, and while it did that, Lex briefly observed his situation. His tribulation had returned to normal, but perhaps something had been triggered, and now it seemed like the pool phase was about to end soo, and the next phase was about to begin.","He would need to finish all other matters before then.","Much more importantly, the more the tribulation pool healed and strengthened him, the more Lex’s own natural healing factor kicked in. Regardless of his feelings against phoenixes, the case was that the stronger his Celestial aura became, the more the phoenix aspect of his powers became active.","It was as if everything before this was fake - like he was running a car on cheap, knock off fuels, and now finally he was using premium fuel. Faintly, Lex began to realize that the Celestial realm was genuinely special, and that he could now do a lot of things - including finally making use of Lotus’ unique ability.","But none of that mattered for now. Though he was growing exponentially stronger with each passing moment, he did not delay at all. Getting his system to properly activate a high-priority self diagnosis was a complex procedure, but he followed Mary’s instructions to the letter, finally triggering it.","It was just one more notification atop the thousands that waited for Lex to check, but he didn’t bother at all. As soon as the diagnosis started, he dedicated 100% of his focus to observing the system. If he made a mistake, Mary would die, so he would not make a mistake. He could not make a mistake.","For the one companion who had been beside him from the day he got his system, the one who had guided him, taught him, teased him, had laughed with him, Lex would ensure that this went without a hitch.","Time passed by second by second, until an entire hour passed by. The high priority self diagnosis was not a quick or simple process, and it took far longer than even Mary had anticipated, but it didn’t matter.","For a brief moment - for a fraction of an instant, too quick to even be quantified with a unit of time - another aura appeared within the core of the system. Lex had no idea how long that aura was meant to appear, but he immediately recognized it as Mary’s, and grabbed a hold of it with his Domination and Spirit Sense faster than he had ever done anything.","\" RELEASE !\" Lex roared as he used everything - every single ounce of power, focus, strength and will power that he had - into pulling out the container of that aura.","It was easier said than done. Interfering with the internal workings of a system was something that even Dao Lords struggled with. It was just that the system itself was detaching the foreign entity as a part of its protocols, so Lex’s efforts coincided with its actions, allowing him to pull the treasure free before the system could try to recycle it for its own use.","From within the system in his soul, Lex suddenly pulled out a heart shaped pendant. He had no time to be surprised at the appearance of the treasure, for the moment it appeared, he felt his connection to Mary sever.","His faithful assistant, who had guided him from the moment he received his system, was no longer connected to Lex on a mental level.","Without wasting any time at all, Lex plunged that pendant inside the new body that Mary had been making. She had already told him what to do in case he was successful - now all that was left was to hope it worked.","No - Lex had no interest in hope. He would make it work.","\" Vinei ,\" Lex said, summoning the black phoenix in front of his projection, frightening it so much that it nearly shed its feathers.","For some reason, the black phoenix could not help but feel like the Innkeeper was looking at him... with an unusual look. But he had to have been mistaken. Why would the Innkeeper look at him with killing intent? Yes, there was definitely a mistake somewhere.","\"Help her with her rebirth,\" he said, sending the phoenix down to Mary’s body. In truth, Vinei was a Celestial Immortal, but he was too weak for such a task in Lex’s opinion. After all, now he knew that phoenixes were a scam. Temporarily, though, he’d still have to rely on him."]},{"number":2446,"title":"Chapter 2446: Should’ve killed me when you had the chance","paragraphs":["After seeing that the pendant was absorbed into the new body, and that a pulse of ’life’ seemed to emerge from the body, Lex allowed his projection to disappear. He did not bother giving Vinei any more instructions - what could one even expect from a phoenix? It would be good as long as he managed to help a little.","Lex turned his focus to his system. The warnings were abundant - don’t let systems absorb Primordial energy. Bad things would happen if he did. Honestly, Lex had no idea how long his system had been absorbing Primordial energy. Maybe it had been doing so far longer than Lex was aware of.","Maybe, back when he was too weak to sense it, his system was already secretly siphoning some of the energy. Then it could have shown him a low or small percentage whereas in truth it had absorbed a whole lot more.","Lex was curious why Primordial energy was such an issue for systems. In fact, Lex wanted a deeper understanding of Primordial energy than simply saying it was ancient energy and that it was powerful. Why was it powerful? What made it special or unique?","Ever since Lex became a Primordial, he noticed that his weight increased by a lot - not just his literal weight, but the weight his very existence put on the laws that interacted with him. Why did the Void react to Primordial energy in such unique ways? Why could the Primordials back in the day be so strong even without becoming Dao Lords?","Lex did not have the answer for that, but as Celestial energy filled him and fueled his Primordial soul, he started to feel like there was no upper limit to his power. While previous realms such as Earth and Heaven Immortal realms had a theoretical upper limit, the Celestial realm seemed to have none - at least for Primordials. It was curious, but unimportant at the moment.","For now, Lex looked within himself, his gaze falling upon the system. It was impossible to read Lex’s emotions, and just as difficult to discern his thoughts from the gaze alone. It felt detached and indifferent, as if the actions taken by the system.","His system - the one that governed a realm, controlled the Inn, and wielded such incredible power that even Dao Lords could not see through it - felt stressed under that unwavering gaze. The reason was simple.","All that power, all those abilities, they were not something that the system could do according to its whims. It could no more deploy the Butter Knife itself than a mortal human could choose to activate healing in a certain part of his body. Although mortals could heal their bodies from minor or even moderate wounds, that was done by the body itself, and the mortal could not control it. At most, the mortal could provide the correct environment and fuel for the body to perform its functions optimally.","\"I will allow you to keep 30% of the Primordial energy you’ve absorbed up until now,\" said Lex, as if a ruler issuing a decree. The system felt as if it had been pardoned, though the system itself could not understand why that was. A foreign sensation filled it that it could only define as... relief?","\"However, the moment I learn that you’ve exceeded that 30%, or that you’ve lied to me again, I will personally make sure you’re never able to absorb Primordial energy again - even if I have to hand you over to that glass orb called Regix to do it. Understand?\"","As if to respond to Lex, the system began pushing out a tremendous amount of Primordial energy - energy which was then absorbed by Lex as if it was the most pure healing elixir, allowing it to heal at a visible rate! His muscles started to reform, his bones started to regrow, and his skin began to appear once more.","In fact, his regrowth was so fast and intense that Lex even grew a small, wild beard.","Everyone had clearly warned him not to let his system absorb Primordial energy, but there was a reason Lex let it keep 30%. First, his personal experiences had led him to believe that not everything was as concrete as he was always led to believe.","Until he understood the story himself, he would not blindly rely on others. Second, as long as the system had Primordial energy within it, Lex could sense that it wasn’t nearly as cohesive and perfect as it normally appeared to be. At least Lex could now read the system’s emotions much in the way that he could read the emotions of his guests.","It wasn’t that Lex was being arrogant - it was that in this way, he felt he had more control over the system than less. After all, previously, all control over the system depended on the operations of the system’s design and the intentions of the creator. Like this, there was a wild element that could disrupt that design. Like this, his system was more like a living being, and Lex had plenty of experience in dealing with living beings.","With his Sovereign realm remaining constant, he could feel just how much Primordial energy the system had left, and the system had very faithfully released all Primordial energy up to 29%, not even risking that 30%.","As if Lex wasn’t scary enough, that mysterious glass orb known as Regix posed a far greater threat.","Lex did not reveal an ounce of emotion on his face, but internally he felt greatly satisfied. He had just learned that upon reaching the Celestial Immortal realm, Primordial energy had become a great tonic for him. He could heal directly using it, which meant his healing factor had improved many times over.","In truth, his healing ability had been improved due to him inheriting more abilities from Phoenixes, but Lex conveniently ignored that.","Instead, he opened his eyes and found that by now, the liquid in the pool was merely up until his ankles. When the liquid disappeared, the tribulation would enter its next stage. Before that... Lex summoned his Karmic Bead once more.","The Primordial energy released from his system had healed him even faster than the liquid in the pool, which meant that at the moment, he was close to his peak strength. He held out his Karmic Bead and placed it in the air in front of him, as if he had placed it atop an invisible Go board.","A Karmic string shot out from the bead into the distance, crossing an impossible distance, reaching to a hidden pocket realm somewhere out in the Void, and connecting to what appeared like a broken puppet.","The puppet opened its eyes, shocked, and discovered that he saw a projection of a human standing in front of him. It looked like Lex, but more rugged, and somehow more... defined.","\"You put up a good fight, Daekol. You’re a worthy opponent. But that is all,\" said the illusion of Lex that appeared in Daekol’s eyes.","Daekol had used a system ability called Debt Protection, which meant that since his debt to the system was so huge, the system was protecting its investment. The consequences of such an ability were, naturally, immense but it should have ensured his survival. It had managed to protect him even from that final tribulation strike, which is why he had no idea how Lex had been able to pierce through its protection.","\"You are not smart - you proved as much when you kidnapped Almira. You are not wise - you proved as much when you targeted me. Your sole destiny... the culmination of your entire life is nothing more than becoming a name I cross off my list. You should have killed me when you had the chance - I won’t make the same mistake.\"","Before Daekol could speak, before he could resist or employ some ability, the illusion of Lex disappeared. The karmic string from Lex’s bead reached the thick web of karma Lex had sowed with Daekol, and shattered it.","There was no build up, no suspenseful fight or struggle. Even though Lex had not become a full Celestial yet, he was no longer someone Daekol could resist even at his full strength, let alone in his current, weakened condition.","Not a trace of emotion passed through Lex’s eyes as he killed Daekol. Instead, he simply searched once more, scouring the universe for any sign of Daekol’s karma, but there was nothing.","Lex wrapped the puppet that was acting as Daekol’s body with his karmic string, as well as the system hidden within, and pulled it towards himself. Sovereigns were hunted even by Dao Lords, so Lex would definitely not give up this opportunity to get his hands on one.","As for making use of it, or trying to absorb the system into his own, those were things Lex would have to do later. For now, he had to face the final aspect of his tribulation, for the pool finally ran out of the tribulation liquid."]},{"number":2447,"title":"Chapter 2447: An era of progress","paragraphs":["Lex’s surroundings changed. He was standing within the empty pool, but the moment all the liquid was absorbed the pool itself disappeared. Instead, Lex found himself standing on plain dirt in the center of a grand structure. Right in front of him, roughly 20 feet (6 meters) above him was an imperial gallery with a thin veil across the front, keeping Lex from looking in.","Lex’s eyes narrowed, not because he disliked being looked down on which was literally what was happening, but because his surroundings felt oddly familiar. Clearly he was still within the Primordial Garden where the second half of his tribulation had started - Lex hadn’t questioned how he got here. That could be answered later.","But he also felt like he was somehow within Arch-Heaven, which was new. How could he simultaneously be in the Primordial Garden, and inside Arch-Heaven at the same time?","The veil rippled, and Lex saw a vague outline appear behind it.","\"Congratulations, Aspirant, for surviving your cultivation journey thus far, as well as all the trials and tribulations along the way. You have made it, at last, to the apex cultivation realm officially ordained by the universe itself,\" spoke a deep and powerful voice from behind the veil. Lex could physically feel the authority contained within that voice. Yup, he was definitely back in Arch-Heaven.","The strange thing, though, was that his strength was not limited like it usually was in Arch-Heaven. Also, why was the Celestial realm being called the last ’officially ordained cultivation realm’?","\"Your journey has been long, but along the way you have enjoyed the fruits of this universe, and have been nurtured by it. It is now time to return the favor. Kneel, and you may accept an official position in Arch-Heaven. Kneel, and you may be initiated into the army of Arch-Heaven. Kneel... and you may take the first step in witnessing the beginning of a new age.\"","Lex raised a single eyebrow, not intimidated in the least by the weight of the voice, or the promise of a new age. All along, he had been the one telling others to kneel. He had yet to encounter someone who could make Lex voluntarily kneel, and even if it was the request of the universe itself it would not be enough, let alone whoever was behind the veil.","\"And if I don’t?\" Lex asked, ready to face whatever retaliation would be targeted towards him. This was a strange tribulation.","\"That, too, is permissible,\" responded the voice, taking Lex by surprise. He was certain there would be a threat of death or something along those lines.","\"The universe is rapidly changing, and an era of progress is coming. The Arch-Heaven will no longer stand aloof, and let the workings of the universe go on unguided. The universe itself will establish the foundations, and the ministers, lords, governors, mayors and soldiers of Arch-Heaven will enact the will of the universe, and ensure stability.","\"It is for creation, made from creation. All those who reach the Celestial Immortal realm after effort and tribulation will be given an opportunity to enter those hallowed ranks. After 10 Dao cycles of service, they may choose honorable discharge, and regain their freedom, or rise in the ranks of Arch-Heaven.","\"Of course, should any choose to reject this opportunity, they need only endure the Blade of Severance. Should they survive, then the tribulation is complete, and they may return from whence they came.\"","There was a lot of information packed in that small speech. Based on what Lex understood, joining the ranks of Arch-Heaven was something only those who passed a tribulation to become Celestial would get. Those born in this realm would not get this opportunity. Then again, how hard was it for races who were born as Celestials to gain an official position in Arch-Heaven should they want it?","For now, it was pretty easy, but maybe things were changing. The Arch-Heaven had never really played a significant role in the universe before this, at least as far as Lex knew, but maybe that would not be the case in the future.","It was a decent opportunity, but serving for 10 Dao cycles before getting to retire was too much in Lex’s opinion. Considering that 1 Dao cycle was 231,000 years, 10 of them were over 2 million years of service.","That was quite steep in Lex’s opinion. But the question was, was there another way out? He had no idea what the Blade of Severance was, but it didn’t sound pleasant. Would those who just survived the difficult tribulation so far even have the energy to face this new and unknown danger?","\"Nah thanks, I was offered the role of Heaven’s Augur before and I didn’t take it, so accepting the rank of a soldier is definitely out of the question. I’ll just face the blade,\" responded Lex casually.","Behind the veil, the figure paused, as if stunned by what he heard. After a moment, a cane was used to push the veil aside, revealing a Karmari - a member of the Sage race. He seemed surprised by Lex’s words, and was even more surprised to see a human.","\"Are you sure? I’ll give you another chance to consider your options. In Arch-Heaven, you may be able to avoid the obstacles your race is currently facing.\"","That was, by far, the most considerate thing Lex had ever heard a member of the Sage race say, which was the real surprising thing.","\"Like you said, an era of progress is coming, and for my race, I am that progress,\" responded Lex with a faint smirk.","The Karmari simply nodded, and returned behind the veil.","Lex heard a sound behind him and turned around to see a white marble statue wielding a Cloud Head Saber. He stood still, though it was clear that he had locked onto Lex.","\"You may pray before your demise,\" said the white statue, looking at Lex as if he was a dead man. Yet Lex only found his words to be amusing, and did nothing.","A few seconds later, the white marble statue grabbed the hilt of the blade with both hands and struck. The slash was blinding, his speed far beyond anything Lex could have dealt with back when he was a Heaven Immortal. The laws contained within the strike were also unique, and aimed to sever the connection between his soul and Pulse, the ruling law associated with, among other things, life itself.","Lex did not move at all during the strike, and the statue and the Karmari both assumed it was because the strike had been too fast for him to respond. That was natural. The blade was designed specifically to be too difficult for a new Celestial.","Yet...","Lex looked down to the place where the blade was touching his chest. Let alone sever anything, the blade could not even leave a white line on his skin."]},{"number":2448,"title":"Chapter 2448: You can suppress humanity, but you can’t suppress me","paragraphs":["\"There’s no need to feel embarrassed. It’s perfectly normal to have performance issues the first time,\" said Lex as he grabbed the blade of the sword and moved it away from his chest, winking at the marble statue.","Before the statue, or even the Karmari behind the veil could respond, there was a clap of thunder above Lex’s body, and he began to fade away. Before he completely faded though, Lex left behind some words.","\"Arch-Heaven may feel like it can govern the universe, and that’s fine, but it will sorely regret it if it thinks it can control me.\"","Lex disappeared completely, leaving behind a silent gallery, for neither the statue nor the Karmari knew how to respond to what had just happened.","Lex’s tribulation ended, and he reappeared in the Primordial Garden. A yellow light shone down from between tribulation clouds as Lex received the final feedback from his tribulation. He had, formally, stepped into the ranks of Celestial Immortal - but he had done far more than just that. He had also survived his first ever Primordial Dao Body tribulation.","Normal Dao Body tribulations did not have any real feedback to give - allowing the targeted person to live in itself was the reward. Lex, though, was not ordinary by any measure or standard, and neither was his tribulation.","As his body and soul experienced the final baptism of the tribulation, his cultivation technique activated on its own, steadily advancing his Dao Body directly using the laws of the universe as a source. The highest level of the universe’s laws were nourishing Lex at the moment, and his cultivation technique was absorbing far more from them than any before him.","Every time Lex had a Major tribulation, the universe had experienced various phenomena. Each time, the reasoning was unique. This time, too, there had been a phenomenon. Pangu had appeared in the Dream realm, and all the Dao Lords of the universe had witnessed the Innkeeper prevent a Universal Mandate from being broken.","That should have been all, right? Even that much was too much. Under what circumstances could there be even more universal phenomena? Whether it was fortunate or unfortunate, Lex was about to find out.","Eclipse was already watching Lex, for this new portion of the tribulation had been very interesting for her to watch. Yet in that moment, she froze. Nulli, who a single moment ago was entirely pink, returned to her blue state as she unleashed her power, but she was a fraction of a moment too late. Eclipse’s unseen, mysterious bodyguard had acted first.","Destiny had decided that the time was nigh for the fall of mankind, and so she had unleashed her many means against them. Ill-fate, bad luck, vengeance, betrayal, accumulated negative karma - whatever one called it, the humans began to suffer from it. All Celestial Immortal humans became targets for assassinations, or impossible obstacles. Death welcomed them too easily, and life gave up on them too readily. Even their tribulations become infinitely harder - but Lex, whose tribulation had mutated, did not experience it.","He never visited the Obelist within the Spirit tribulation, where her traps lay. He also found himself in the Primordial Garden, where he was able to avoid so much of her influence. But her master stroke, the new curse that lay upon the position of the human race on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum, could not be avoided.","The moment he became a Celestial Immortal, he became a key figure in defining the destiny and status of humanity’s position upon the spectrum - as if he hadn’t been that already. By becoming a Celestial, however, he became a target for her curse as well.","Guided by the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum, which spanned the entire universe, the curse found him even within the Primordial Garden. If a special barrier had been erected to hide him, he could have avoided it, but only as long as he stayed within.","Blocked by Eclipse’s bodyguard, Destiny was unable to sense where exactly Lex was. While his location remained hidden, what was happening to him was not. She did not even need to specifically investigate him because...","His cultivation technique was resonating with the laws of the universe, connected in the most direct and fundamental way possible. Thus, when the curse arrived upon Lex, it resonated with those laws.","Lex was no normal human. He was a Celestial. He was a Primordial. Most importantly... he was the best!","Lex felt it like a punch in the gut. Something was trying to latch onto him - to infect his karma, distort his destiny, and drag him down to his nadir. This was not a result of Destiny acting directly - if it was, Lex would have had no recourse or chance at resisting. This was merely something she did indirectly so as to get what she wants, but avoid being traced or detected.","Unfortunately, she failed in avoiding detection because not only had Eclipse sensed her, a projection of Lex appeared all across the universe.","It was not the Innkeeper, nor was it some indistinct feature such as his eyes. A figure of Lex appeared in the skies everywhere any Humanoid race existed, and upon that figure shone a holy, nurturing light, as well as a dark, corrupting taint.","The universe was trying to nurture him, and Destiny was trying to corrupt him. Lex himself, however, was absorbing both forces unimpeded, and using them for himself with his cultivation technique.","The discomfort of the suppression made Lex frown a bit, but he quickly calmed down. Although he did not understand what was happening, he quickly managed to gather that he was being suppressed by a force - perhaps the same force that had been leeching off humanity’s destiny, or perhaps another.","Great. He had literally just finished dealing with Daekol, and now there was someone else waiting in line to mess with him.","\"You can suppress humanity, but you can’t suppress me,\" Lex said angrily, and forcefully accelerated his own cultivation technique. It seemed to be able to absorb the influence of the curse as well, so he might as well take that as fuel as well.","What Lex didn’t realize was that his simple words had reverberated across the universe... or that a much greater secret was being suppressed by Eclipse’s bodyguard, keeping it from being detected.","\"I suppose you were right,\" said Nulli as she looked at Lex’s body. \"The Innkeeper really is preparing to go to that place.\"","Eclipse nodded, though her gaze was fixed on the corrupting force trying to influence Lex.","Destiny... Eclipse had finally found her."]},{"number":2449,"title":"Chapter 2449: Wrong about one thing, kid","paragraphs":["\"You can suppress humanity, but you cannot suppress,\" said the projection of Lex, mocking Destiny to her face.","If at any other time, such a thing would have happened she would have immediately personally decimated the human speaking, but not this time. She knew what this really was - it was bait to get her to reveal her location, and it was poorly disguised bait at that.","She, instead, turned her attention to Bourdow. He had been lucky enough to find traces of the real Wu Kong, all without needing to fight any other Dao Lords on the Dream Arena. Soon, he would enter the core region of the arena, at which point it was only a matter of time before he stumbled onto its secrets.","She did not even need to steal the arena. Once she understood how it was formed, she could recreate it herself. Sure it would take a while, but time was no concern.","*****","Conquest realm","\"You can suppress humanity, but you cannot suppress me,\" said Lex, his words more intimidating than any actual threat. The entire Conquest realm was in chaos. The strategic strikes carried about by the Midnight Battalions crippled the entire realm’s ability to deploy their strength effectively.","In truth, more of the Conqueror’s forces had died from their own mismanagement than from the battalion’s attacks. That was because the Midnight Battalion did not come with the purpose of causing chaos and carnage. They wanted only to rescue Z, and they meant to delay the realms forces from mobilizing as best as possible.","But war was a game of information, and Velma was one hundred steps ahead. Though the battalion was outnumbered one million to one, their every action was measured and layered, revealing the true consequences much later.","Yet in the end, the war did not end quickly because of one piece of information that came to light. Z was not in the conquest realm. The Conqueror had sold Z to some unnamed party the very day Z triggered the heritage of an ancient Human King.","Now, the war waged on only so that they could extract who the buyer was, and where Z had been sent to. But there was one issue. Even as he was besieged, the Grand Conqueror remained confident in his defenses. Velma could neither harm him, nor could she extract any information from his mind.","It could not be helped - he was a cultivator of Regal Embrace.","Yet before he could gain his momentum, Lex appeared in the sky above the realm, his strength, his demeanor, his power absolutely unquestionable. While the Conqueror remained unperturbed, Velma could not help but laugh.","\"Do you know who that is? That’s Z’s teacher. Buddy boy, enjoy your defense for a little while longer, because after he gets here, the only thing your defense will do is make you into a better punching bag,\" teased Velma, even as she kept attacking.","Beside her, Luthor and Gerard also kept attacking the Conqueror, keeping the pressure on him. If they relented even a little, he could summon his forces from across the universe, and they couldn’t let him do that. For a brief period, it almost seemed like they wouldn’t be able to capture him, but now, as long as they could hold out until Lex got there...","The group did not doubt even for a moment that Lex was going to return, because Velma had received news that the Innkeeper had made an appearance inside the Midnight Inn. Now that the Innkeeper was also back, it was only a matter of time before everything returned back to normal.","The Grand Conqueror retained an indifferent expression, though his increased retaliation showed the pressure he was beginning to feel.","*****","Tyrannum realm","The intense attack on the protective formation by the countless Dao Lords paused ever so briefly. Alexander and the rest didn’t know why it had paused, but they were grateful for it. They had no idea that the pause had been because of the vision of the Innkeeper.","The pause, however, was too short. They could barely recover at all before the bombardment began again.","No one expected, however, that shortly after there would be another pause.","\"You can suppress humanity, but you cannot suppress me.\"","Those words, that voice, that appearance. Alexander and the rest had not expected at all that trapped within that formation, they would be able to hear Lex’s voice once more, or that they would be able to see his appearance.","They weren’t the only ones who were shocked - the Dao Lords watching outside were shocked too. Was there really a human who dared stand out and resist at this time? The downfall of humanity had already been decided. In as little as a hundred years, or at most a thousand years, there would be no more Celestial Immortals left among the human race.","At that time, the fall of this once great race would be final.","They increased their efforts in destroying the formation. They didn’t know what anyone else was doing, but they dared not get caught slacking in their efforts.","But they weren’t the only ones who were shaken by Lex’s appearance and vision. Deep within the formation, far beyond the point where Alexander and the rest had entered, sat a single man. His blonde hair, fair skin, and moderate build all gave him an impressive appearance, and that was before he opened his eyes to reveal his deep blue eyes.","The man looked up at Lex and marveled that even now, in this day and age, the spirit of humanity had not gone out.","\"Not bad at all. But you are wrong about one thing, kid,\" said the man as he held out his hand. The pillar that Alexander and the rest had brought to the formation appeared in the man’s hand, and started to repair itself, turning into a magnificent spear.","\"Even humanity cannot be suppressed.\"","The spiritual energy within the formation suddenly began to stir, and the laws of the universe began to writhe in a way all too familiar to the attacking Dao Lords.","\"Is that... what I think it is?\"","\"It can’t be?\"","\"What’s going on?\"","\"Why does this look like... the phenomenon caused by the birth of a Dao Lord?\""]},{"number":2450,"title":"Chapter 2450: She’s at it again","paragraphs":["Eclipse was unusually silent, but no one disturbed her. They all watched Lex as he absorbed both the tribulations feedback as well as the curse, and grew visibly stronger.","Lex himself closed his eyes and felt the changes taking place, for alongside his new cultivation realm, he also received a lot of information. The key detail his instincts told him was that he really needed to talk to Eclipse, and that their conversation would play a significant role in his future.","Besides that, he also felt oddly aware of how unevenly distributed his specialities were. For example, his array skills, sword intent and law manipulation were very high level, but his spirit and soul based arts were actually lagging behind.","He was also aware of the difference in level of mastery among the many laws he used regularly.","He wasn’t sure why, but he had a feeling that all of this had something to do with reaching the Dao Lord realm.","The tribulation feedback and cursing attempt didn’t last long, barely a dozen minutes or so, after which he was completely free. Lex flexed his fingers and tested his new strength and found that it was entirely incomparable. Before reaching the Celestial Immortal realm, he was already equal to some Celestial Apex.","Now... Lex could not gauge how strong he was at all. He simply felt that most of the fear in his mind disappeared, as if there was hardly anything left in the universe capable of making him afraid.","Even Dao Lords, while still far beyond his power level, seemed not as invincible as they always had. That particular illusion was because his Dao Body had jumped to 60% after the tribulation.","To be fair, a lot of his strength also came from the fact that there weren’t countless hidden curses on his body and soul, dragging him down. To this day, Lex had no idea where these curses came from, but that just went to show the true depth of this universe.","Confidence was good, but the moment he became overconfident was the moment he would seal his fate to be the same as Daekols. Even beings like Nuwa had to be careful, so how could he, a mere Celestial Immortal, claim invincibility?","Lex blinked, and then turned towards the garden. Though Eclipse was nowhere in his sight, he knew she was looking at him.","\"Thank you for saving me,\" Lex said with the humblest tone he could produce, and bowed towards the forest. He was not quick to rise either, for this was not a performance. He was genuinely thankful, for he knew Eclipse had no obligation to help him.","There was nothing he could offer her beyond the relationship that they already had, and that relationship was like that of a lost child being guided through the darkness by a caring figure.","Harriot appeared beside Lex and nodded at him, not revealing even a hint of the earlier anxiety he displayed when he felt Lex was going to die.","\"Come on. She has some words she wants to share with you,\" the poodle said before walking ahead. Lex silenced his mind, and did not at all notice that the poodle was wagging its tail happily.","Now, as a Celestial, Lex realized that the Primordial Garden was actually a whole lot scarier than he previously imagined, and that a lot of the scary parts were being held back by his escorts. His senses were sharp enough that he could realize that... just the beasts and creatures in this garden alone could probably conquer many realms if they were allowed to exit.","A few moments later, he found himself kneeling. Lex had no idea how that happened. One moment he was walking behind Harriot, and the next he was kneeling, and his gaze was fixed on the floor in front of him, as if his body dared not look up.","\"You put on a good show, Lex,\" said Eclipse from her throne, an amused smile on her face. She did not explain to him why he could not look up - his confusion was much too amusing. Beside her, Nulli looked at Lex longingly, as if she could somehow reach the Innkeeper through him.","\"Much more important than that, however, is that you showed me something new,\" she continued. \"I have witnessed two of your Major tribulations now, and both of them were quite enjoyable for me. I can scarcely wait for your Dao tribulation.\"","Lex recognized the voice, so he now knew that he was in front of Eclipse. That helped him calm down.","\"Thank you, I’ll take that as a vote of confidence. Actually, considering how notoriously difficult Dao tribulations are, I’d be quite happy settling for a normal one,\" he answered, a hint of resignation in his voice.","That caused Eclipse to chuckle.","\"You’re perhaps the first person I’ve witnessed who thinks fondly of a regular Dao tribulation. Then again, I suppose you have sufficient reason for that. But enough of that - I did not call you here today for casual conversation. I do not want to interfere in however the Innkeeper intends to train you, but I felt compelled to give you a hint of advice based on your fight with Daekol.","\"You have an acceptably adequate mastery of karma for your level, and it is far beyond most of the other laws that you use. However, while that appears good for now, I think it will cause you problems down the lane. When you reach the peak of the Celestial Immortal realm, you will automatically understand how to reach for the Dao Lord realm.","\"The only thing I’ll say is that... find alternative laws. Specialise in something else. You have quite a lot of potential - I’d hate to see you waste it on forming a Dao based on karma.\"","Lex paused, unsure of what to make of that. Was Eclipse telling him to avoid Daos related to karma? Wasn’t she, herself, an expert in karma? So why would she say that?","Instead of elaborating, Eclipse continued to speak.","\"The second piece of advice I’d like to give you is...\"","Eclipse paused her speed as she slowly turned to her right where Nulli was standing, a hint of exasperation and disbelief in her eyes. Nulli, oblivious to Eclipse’s feelings, was once again sniffing the air, as if she could smell something familiar on Lex.","\"The smell is stronger than before. Did you go... meet the Timekeeper? Is the Timekeeper hiding in the Hollow?\" Nulli asked, locking in on Lex.","As the Primordial Nullith, she was especially sensitive to the presence of the Timekeeper. Or, rather, his smell."]},{"number":2451,"title":"Chapter 2451 - 2nd piece of advice","paragraphs":["Lex did not want to lie. Actually, he was pretty sure that he couldn’t lie even if he wanted to at that exact moment, and even if he did it he would be caught immediately. Yet he also did not really want to admit that the Timekeeper was hiding inside Lex’s own forehead.","\"Nulli, now is not the time,\" Eclipse said, although she glanced at Lex for a minute. She almost considered asking him herself, but then shook her head. She couldn’t afford to get distracted.","\"Sorry about that, you’ll have to excuse me. Nulli is pretty sure she killed the Timekeeper the last time they met, so if he’s still around that would be very embarrassing for her,\" Eclipse explained, letting Lex know why Nulli was so curious.","This also allowed him to assess what he wanted to do in the future if he really was associated with the Timkeeper, because it would be quite stupid of him to keep appearing in front of Nulli if he had a relationship with the Timekeeper. That was like asking for trouble.","Lex was slightly surprised, though not from the news about Nulli and the Timekeeper. Two, powerful beings both of whom had an emphasis on time made it very believable that they would either be great allies or committed enemies.","No, he was surprised that hearing the news had no effect on him at all. He was pretty sure that was some kind of massive secret, yet he wasn’t pressured in the slightest. Had he finally reached the level at which he could comfortably learn the secrets he’d been learning all along?","He tried to remember the things he’d forgotten in Abaddon, but the fact that he couldn’t at least told him that he hadn’t forgotten them because his level was too low. Instead, there was some other reason entirely.","\"Coming back to the matter at hand, I can see that you have a lot of open karma out in the universe - many things that you want or need to do. I know this is short notice, but I highly recommend you complete all your tasks and return to the Midnight realm within 10 hours and twenty one minutes and fifteen seconds, standard Mature realm time.","\"Stay out any longer than that, and you won’t exactly die immediately, but a lot of bad things are going to happen. Immediate and unavoidable death are definitely a possibility among many other things.\"","Lex froze. This conversation took a turn he wasn’t expecting. A lot of questions came up in his mind, but so did a countdown. That was exactly 37,260 seconds left, and counting down.","Not a lot of time.","He didn’t question why that time limit, or what was going to happen. The timeline didn’t fit the timing of the Nexus event, but it didn’t matter.","\"Thank you for telling me. I should probably go,\" said Lex. He waited one second to see if there was anything else they wanted to say before teleporting back to the Midnight Inn.","Nulli frowned and looked at Eclipse as if she had been wronged.","\"Now is not the time,\" Eclipse said again.","Nulli only sighed, and then nodded. Eclipse was right. The Timekeeper wasn’t an enemy they could afford to face during this critical moment. Ten more hours...","A strange light flashed through her eyes, and a pink blush began to appear in her cheeks.","Lex reappeared inside the Inn and used a single second to orient himself. He thought through all his priorities, everything he needed to do, and then looked through his system notifications.","There were literally thousands of notifications, but most of them were emergency notifications about the Primordial energy. He directly skipped them and focused on anything that required urgent attention.","There were a few. For the first time in a long time, he failed a quest - to open a resort. However, instead of the quest being failed, the quest was updated into a new quest for reasons Lex did not know. The details for the change weren’t provided. He had his own suspicions though.","Chain Quest: Quest 3 Updated!","Updated Quest: Establish a Midnight Resort! -> Establish a Midnight Resort inside Arch-Heaven!","Quest time limit: 100 years -> 1000 years","Quest Reward: New worker race slot! -> New worker race slot + Hiring department building","Quest Failure Punishment: System shutdown for 5000 years -> No punishment","Remarks: The smart, handsome and charismatic system host can do the quest at his own leisure. No need to stress.","Besides that, there were a number of notifications for events that had already happened so there was nothing Lex could do. For example, there were notifications about the Inn getting invaded, but that was long over.","Then there were quests which had been activated due to ongoing universal events, such as the destruction of the realm. Those quests should have failed, but instead they were simply deleted.","Lex had a strong suspicion that his quests were kept from being deleted by one of two things: the system going dormant due to having no access to him for so long, or the system itself was preventing the quests from failing because it did not want to attract any attention to the fact that it was absorbing Primordial energy.","Even the happy remarks by the system quest now seemed like attempts from the system to placate and flatter him simply because it could not resist his influence at all.","In short, there were many things that needed his attention inside the Inn, but none that needed him to act immediately. No, the stage where he was most urgently needed was elsewhere.","Lex held out his hand and grabbed at a string of karma that danced in front of his eyes, as if specifically left there for him to find.","Within that string was a vision of Velma, looking directly at him.","\"Please don’t blame me for this, but I had to accept your sister’s demand. We all wanted to go save Z, and she insisted on coming with us through her mirror. But, I knew you’d be worried, so I put a tracker on the mirror in case anything happened to it. And if nothing happened to it, you can find a Devil called Ahjour in the canteen near the central Guild room building. He’ll bring you to the Conquest realm where we all are.\"","Lex smiled faintly, and appeared inside the canteen. Ahjour was a Devil Lex had met during the first Midnight Games, but that hardly mattered right now.","\"I heard you were waiting for me,\" Lex said to the Devil who had been eating a bowl of noodles.","Ahjour paused, and looked up with an expression of irritation. Yet the moment his gaze landed on Lex, he withdrew all his irritation and put on his best smile.","\"Not at all, not at all. We can leave whenever you want.\"","Lex nodded. 37,250 seconds until Eclipses’ deadline."]},{"number":2452,"title":"Chapter 2452: Grand a**kicking","paragraphs":["\"It’s pointless, you cannot win,\" said the Grand Conqueror arrogantly, looking at the group constantly attacking him. They had been at an impasse for weeks at a time, with a few small breaks in between when he managed to temporarily get away from them. Due to the difference in the flow of time, the war in the Conquest had been going on for months already!","This fight had been the most frustrating he’d had since he got his system because that woman from the Inn - the one leading the invasion - could do something he’d never experienced before. She could cause him to disconnect from his system!","In truth, even she did not know or understand what she was doing - that much the Grand Conqueror understood. However, she had an ability which interfered with all communication to cripple him and prevent him from contacting reinforcements. Whenever she used that ability, contact between him and his system would be severed too!","The issue was that while his defense was generally invincible, his attack was severely lacking. He normally made up for that by summoning the many soldiers and warriors that worked for him, not to mention his special bodyguards and assassins. Unfortunately, some of them had been killed, while others were out of reach because the system could not be used long enough to call them over.","None bothered to reply to him for they were too focused on trying to capture him. If they couldn’t defeat him, then capturing him for interrogation would be good enough. Yet it was not as if there was no response to his words at all.","There was a single clap of thunder high up in the sky above the Conquest realm so loud that it spread across the entire realm, causing not just the ground to shake, but the very laws of the realm. Shocked, they looked up in the sky and found that not a single cloud was left. Instead, all they saw was a clear blue sky.","But there was not a single soul across the entire realm, native or invader alike, who could enjoy the clear blue sky for what had replaced the clouds were cracks. Above the entire Conquest realm, in the sky, space had cracked.","That clap of thunder was not, in fact, thunder. Instead it was the sound of space breaking. There were too many who could only look up in horror and wonder what had caused such destruction, but the Grand Conqueror and the rest did not need to wonder.","Right above them, in the center of the cracks, stood Lex. By now he had somewhat trimmed his beard and cleaned up its shape. It didn’t look bad - though the only person in the entire realm noticing Lex’s beard was Moon. Everyone else was looking at his feet which stood upon the cracks spread across the realm.","\"I heard... that you folk like conquest,\" said Lex, his voice completely casual, yet it rang in everyone’s mind. His gaze wandered around the realm beneath him until his eyes finally locked onto the Grand Conqueror. A glance was all Lex needed to recognize the Regal Embrace, but the knowledge did not cause the slightest ripple in his mind.","\"I thought that maybe I’d try my hand at it.\"","Before the Grand Conqueror could even process those words he felt something hit him in the face. His body slammed into the ground with such force that the tectonic plate upon which he stood began to fracture.","Massive cracks spread across the entire continent, spreading faster than people could escape them. A soldier fell into one of the cracks and a deep, overwhelming fear gripped his chest as he looked into the darkness where he was falling. A moment later, when the warm glow of rising and erupting magma illuminated the crack, the soldier found that he had much preferred the darkness.","All across the Conquest realm, dormant volcanoes became active and new volcanos formed where there had never been any before as torrents of lava shot into the sky.","Lex turned to Velma and handed her a list.","\"You think you can get the devils to send me to these realms after this?\" Lex asked, skipping all the small talk.","Velma blinked as she looked at the list with over a dozen realms, most of them immature realms like the Conquest realm.","\"It shouldn’t be a problem, but why these?\" she asked, even as she began to arrange everything.","Lex glanced at the others and found that they were mostly unhurt, which was a relief.","\"I have about 37,000 seconds to retaliate for the invasion of the Inn. It’s not enough to track all the ones responsible, but it should be enough to let the Humanoid Alliance understand what happens when they mess with us.\"","Velma nodded, not asking any more questions. The time limit sounded urgent, and the fact that Lex wasn’t cracking any jokes showed just how serious he was.","Lex spotted the Grand Conqueror, using the fact that his body was buried deep inside the ground to run. Lex ignored him and pulled out the Innkeeper’s Business card and threw it into the air.","Far up in the air, at the very peak of the realms limits, a projection of the Innkeeper appeared with the business card as his core.","The Innkeeper, as always, looked particularly dashing, though his warm demeanor and soft smile seemed very misplaced given his surroundings.","\"If the alliance, or any Dao Lord interferes after this, then do not blame me when my reaction is not proportional. With so many Major realms disappearing left, right, and center, a few more missing realms won’t matter.\"","He was not looking at anyone in particular when he spoke, nor did he even try to send out his words to anyone. It was as if he wasn’t speaking to anyone in particular at all.","A few moments later, however, a vague figure appeared in front of him.","\"Are you trying to declare war on the alliance?\" he asked aggressively.","The Innkeeper looked at him with an amused smile, and then snorted, his figure beginning to fade away.","\"A mere alliance, can you even afford to pick a fight with me?\"","The Innkeeper disappeared, and though the figure tried, he could not trace or detect the Innkeepers power at all. It was as if what was in front of him was genuinely an illusion. But illusions did not have that kind of aura.","The figure looked down at the continent and found that the human Lex was looking up right at him. The figure disappeared, not doing anything.","Lex did not breathe a sigh of relief. He showed no signs of concern at all. Internally, however, he felt extremely relieved.","Then he turned back towards the Grand Conqueror. It was time for a grand asskicking."]},{"number":2453,"title":"Chapter 2453: Pathetic Mathew","paragraphs":["A hint of pity flickered through Velma’s eyes as she watched the ’powerful’ and ’mighty’ Grand Conqueror trying to crawl through the ground and evade Lex. Unfortunately, while his defenses were impeccable, all his other techniques were sorely lacking.","\"I’ve found a way to pass through the defenses in his soul,\" said Moon, who appeared right beside Velma. Or, more specifically, the mirror appeared beside Velma with Moon’s reflection in it.","\"To be specific, I can’t harm him, but I should be able to get you to infiltrate his memories through his soul rather than his spirit. Just have Lex continue to beat him for a while - the impact of Lex’s attack seems to break through all his defenses at the point of impact.\"","Velma nodded, and quickly slipped the information to Lex. The reason it was imperative to search through his memory was because that was the only reliable way of finding out Z’s location.","Lex held out his hand, and the Grand Conqueror appeared within it, held upside down by his foot. The man was bleeding from his head, and his armor had been torn apart. He looked up - well technically, since he was upside down, he looked down - at Lex with shock in his eyes.","Lex had teleported him over like it was nothing, and he hadn’t been able to resist even in the slightest.","\"I can read your karma like a book,\" said Lex, his voice completely plain and bored. \"You’re a former guest of the Midnight Inn. You lived as a refugee from Earth. Exactly what aspect of the Midnight Inn did you look at, and think it would be a good idea to mess with it?\"","Before he could answer, Lex slammed his body onto the ground, using the Grand Conqueror like a whip.","\"Or what? Did you think that because you got a few tricks, that you were suddenly all powerful? Or did you genuinely think that someone would defend you from the Innkeeper?\"","In truth, if the universe wasn’t in such complete chaos, Lex wouldn’t have dared behave the way he did. Any single Dao Lord could completely screw him over even now - such as the one who had interacted with the Innkeepers projection just now.","It was just that no one wanted to mess with someone with such complete mastery over teleportation at a time when they could not get any backup that Lex dared to behave the way he did. Moreover, he had a much more complete understanding of Dao Lords now.","They often thought in extremely complex and layered ways, such that every action hid many potential plans. They were far more careful than they appeared, and considered many factors that non-Dao beings couldn’t even consider. Thus, Lex was very blatant in his actions, and completely convinced himself that the purpose of his actions was to provoke any kind of reaction so that the Innkeeper could justifiably retaliate.","He was clear. Inaction was far more dangerous than action given his situation. The fact that the Innkeeper hadn’t reacted immediately was already incredibly dangerous, and Lex had thought of multiple possibilities to explain why that was. That was for later, though. For now, he would enjoy the part of his performance where he got revenge.","The Grand Conqueror grit his teeth and tried to activate his system, but he could not connect to it at all. Lex, however, noticed and immediately realized what he had been trying to do.","He lifted the Grand Conqueror and pierced his chest with his hand, except that there was no blood. Lex did not reach into his chest, but into his soul. Unlike Lex, the Grand Conqueror had fused the system with his own soul, making it much harder to separate or remove. Lex, however, would settle for simply stopping it from working.","\"How did you...\"","The Grand Conqueror’s eyes constricted as he realized what Lex had done, but for some reason he could not complete his words. Even Lex hadn’t really been stopping him from mentioning his system, but he just couldn’t ask the question.","Lex snorted, and then pushed the Grand Conqueror away and clapped his hands, as if cleaning them.","\"I’ll give you one last opportunity. Resist. Impress me. Show me what made you so confident,\" said Lex as he stood still. Internally, he’d already decided how many seconds he could continue to spend here. Due to the increased speed of the flow of time in this realm, he could do this properly and ensure they gained the information they needed on Z.","The Grand Conqueror looked at Lex, at the sheer audacity and arrogance of the man, and found that... there was nothing he could do about it. Was it really arrogance if he really couldn’t do anything against Lex at all?","Lex, in the meantime, couldn’t help but compare this guy to Daekol. They really weren’t even on the same level. It was such a tragedy that Regal Embrace had fallen into the hands of such a person.","The Grand Conqueror tried to teleport away, relying on some kind of escape talisman, only to find that he was slapped back out midteleportation by Lex. The shock of that slap gave Moon the opening she needed to access his soul, allowing Velma to begin reading his memories.","\"His name is Mathew Barn from Arizona state, developed male pattern baldness extremely early in life and only ever had one girlfriend who broke up with him because...\"","Lex glanced at Velma who realized she was speaking out loud and suddenly went quiet.","Lex groaned. He didn’t even feel like fighting anymore - this was just pathetic.","Before Mathew could recover from the shock that his memories had been read, Lex grabbed him and poked his forehead, causing him to get stunned. He could not think, he could not move, he could not resist. The Grand Conqueror, the person who received a legacy from an ancient Human King, and had received a sponsorship from the Humanoid Alliance, could not put up the slightest resistance against Lex.","\"You have about one hour,\" said Lex, calculating how many seconds that would be in a Mature realm. \"You need to read all his memories by then. If you’re not finished, you’ll just have to bring him back to the Midnight Inn with you. Oh, and have everyone evacuate this realm as soon as possible.\"","Velma looked away from Mathew toward Lex.","\"Why? Is something about to happen?\"","She had sensed it from his urgency earlier, and had avoided asking back then. Now that she saw how easily Lex controlled the situation, she asked him since she was sure it wouldn’t distract him from a fight. After all, if something bad was going to happen, she needed to prepare for it.","\"Yes. This entire realm is steeped in sin and negative karma, so I’m going to use it as fertilizer for my own realm. After about one hour... this place will be too unstable for most immortals to survive in.\""]},{"number":2454,"title":"Chapter 2454: Sin","paragraphs":["\"Sin?\" Moon repeated, looking at Lex as if he were unfamiliar to her.","Lex immediately picked up on what she was sensing and thought of a way to explain.","\"If the one being kidnapped was you or me, and Belle was the one who rescued us, what do you think she would do once she saved us?\"","The question wasn’t necessarily the best comparison for Belle had spent most of her youth trying her best to protect and save her younger siblings, largely unsuccessfully. It wasn’t her fault - she was just too weak, and her enemies too strong.","But assuming she was strong enough to save them from someone, what would she likely do? A scene flashed in Moon’s mind: Belle, with a neutral expression, killing everyone responsible while talking to them calmly as if to soothe their emotions.","It wasn’t like Belle was a genocidal maniac. It wasn’t as if she were a bloodthirsty demon either. She was just an extremely protective woman who didn’t know how to express her emotions and protective instincts in any way other than anger.","That, however, also made it very easy to imagine the kinds of things she might have done if she really did have the strength to save them.","Moon looked in Lex’s eyes to see if he really had it in him to do the kind of thing he was insinuating. She saw not an ounce of hesitation.","\"Are you sure you want to do this?\" she asked, unsure about how she felt about it. On one hand, these people had really provoked them. On the other hand, it wasn’t the people but their leader.","Lex shook his head, as if Moon was misunderstanding him.","\"This is not about revenge, or about venting my anger, if that’s what you’re thinking. It’s about establishing a fact - and the fact is that there will always be consequences of messing with the Midnight Inn. Besides, this realm really is steeped in sin - you just can’t see what I see.\"","Lex disappeared, leaving Moon standing there with Velma, though she didn’t brood for long. It wasn’t that she misunderstood Lex, but that Lex had misunderstood her. Would she care about the deaths of people who kidnapped Z?","No, she just found it hard to believe that Lex intended to use this entire realm as fertiliser. Since when had he become so strong? She really was wasting a lot of time just sleeping and processing her own realm.","But if Lex were now powerful enough that entire immature realms were things he could do with as he wished, maybe he could wake up her body as well.","Lex flew to the highest point of the realm and slowly began to unleash his Sovereign realm, overlapping it with the Conquest realm. His own realm wasn’t nearly large enough that it could encompass the entire Conquest realm, but he didn’t need it to be.","Everyone looked up and saw a red moon appear in the sky, and a feeling of bone-chilling dread spread to anyone and everyone who looked at it.","Lex had given Velma an hour to evacuate everyone because that is how long it would take him to completely deploy the Sovereign realm to its maximum without being interrupted. The extent of the realm at that point would be far beyond what he had managed to release in his fight with Daekol.","The full extent of the Sovereign realm deployed, utilised now that Lex was a Celestial Immortal... even Lex himself could not imagine what that would be like. He would need to find out.","Velma looked up at the red moon, and read through the information leaking from it, and could not help but look at Lex oddly. Here, she thought her powers at the Celestial Immortal realm were unusual. She should have known better than to compare herself to Lex.","She gave the order, and the Midnight Battalions began to retreat back to the Midnight Inn. They didn’t particularly go out of their way to loot dogs or grab any valuable resources. They weren’t lacking in such things, and more importantly, any loot they would steal would be less for themselves and more for the Midnight Inn.","Velma had informed them that Lex intended to kidnap the whole realm itself, so at that point, was there even a need to loot something as insignificant as individual resources?","They didn’t even need to question whether such a thing was even possible - there was a well-documented instance of Lex kidnapping a realm before.","Over the next hour, all of the battalion members evacuated, and the devils made countless deals, considering Velma hadn’t hidden Lex’s intentions from them. As allies, it wouldn’t do to withhold such critical information. She wouldn’t want them to think the Inn was stealing from them.","Thus, during this one hour, they made all the deals they wanted and harvested anything and everything they wished.","In fact, following up on Lex’s statement about sin, Velma even provided a list of residents of the realm who weren’t really stained by the sins of most of the realm’s residents, and told the, Devils that they would be ideal partners for deals. Even if they wanted to leave the realm, the Inn wouldn’t interfere.","However, the devils were expressly forbidden from taking any native of the realm outside if their name wasn’t on Velma’s list.","Velma herself used this time to extract as much information from Mathew as possible.","Unfortunately, there was a tremendous amount of useless information, not a single piece of useful information could be found.","Clearly he had other defences or mechanisms in place to protect critical information. Either he needed to be interrogated properly, or they needed more time to search his memories, thus Velma could only take the stunned Mathew back to the Midnight Inn with her.","Before leaving, she turned to take a look up at the blood-red moon once more. The path Lex was walking...would be far more difficult than her own. If he succeeded, however, then she could not even imagine what he would become."]},{"number":2455,"title":"Chapter 2455: Setting Foundations","paragraphs":["To say that the situation was not strange would be a lie. Lex had built a fake realm inside a necklace, and then fused with that necklace, moving that realm into himself. Thus, now, wherever Lex walked he would take the realm with him.","Yet no matter how strange it seemed or felt to think that he carried a realm inside of hímself wherever he went, that was actually quite common among Celestial Immortals. To be specific, it was quite common for Celestial Immortals to fuse an entire planet with themselves. and take it wherever they go. In the Origin realm, there was even a club of Celestial Immortals who used their fused planets like ships to travel through space.","Thus, to carry a small realm within oneself was not completely unusual or unheard of. But it was also not without limitations. The size and strength of the realm one could fuse with and carry around was limited by a few things, such as the strength of his body and his soul, as well as his familiarity with certain laws.","For Lex, that was not a major concern. He was very familiar with quite a few laws, and the strength of his body and soul need not be questioned. Thus, when Lex encountered a realm which had a history of cruelty and sin, and was occupied by those whose greatest contribution to the universe would be their deaths. He decided to make use of it. Much more important for Lex than the actual resources that filled this place was the set of rules that governed this realm.","What neither Velma, nor anyone else noticed about this place, was that the rules that governed the function of this realm seemed to leave space for administration, or some kind of control. It was so subtle that those who didn’t already know the patterns wouldn’t even recognise the actual purpose behind why the laws were configured in such a way. It was a sign that a system had played a fundamental role in the development of this realm, and in fact governed much of its function. Lex had witnessed such a thing inside the Midnight realm as well. To be specific, the way that the laws operated inside the territory of the Inn within the Midnight realm was similar to this.","When Lex was designing his own realm, his purpose had been to have absolute control over those laws so that he could force himself to become equivalent to a Sovereign inside. Looking at these laws now, Lex realised that this was a better way of doing things. Instead of absolute control over every law, which was both difficult and energy consuming, it was better to allow the laws to develop naturally in such a way that they would grant him access to manipulate them when needed.","If he was able to do this, then in the future it would not take him such a long time to summon his Sovereign realm, especially in the midst of battle. Of course, first he would have to ensure that only he could affect and influence those laws. Devouring this realm, and the template according to which its laws were built, would allow Lex to save a tremendous amount of time and effort.","Lex also had a feeling that he could improve his Lotus form to give himself even better and greater control over the Sovereign realm, but that was something he would need to experiment with and perfect. It wasn’t something that could be done at a moment’s notice. As such, the destruction of this realm was something that would need to be systematic. Instead of destroying the whole realm immediately, Lex first checked if the realm had a core or something akin to an Axis Eternum, lf he made one of those for his own realm, it would drastically increase his control over the realm. If this realm didn’t have one, that was also fine.","Once Lex returned to the Midnight Inn, he could read Taro’s journal to learn how to make one for his own realm. As it turned out, the Conquest realm did have a core, and it was connected to Mathew’s castle. Deep underground, beneath even the dungeon, was a hidden chamber within which was a stone pillar that seemed fused with the ground itself.","All the laws of the realm seemed to emerge from the pillar, and were clearly controlled by it. Lex placed his hand on it and, after extending his spirit sense inside to study it for a moment, expanded his Sovereign realm over it. Then he began to devour it!","A massive earthquake shocked the entire realm, and lightning started to flash in cloudless skies. The cracks, which still filled the space in skies above the realm, began to expand rapidly. A storm of energy began to travel through the realm, but none of it could shake Lex.","The weight of his Primordial self kept him anchored at his location even as the entire realm began to destabilise far too rapidly. Absorbing the realm like this would waste a lot of its essence and resources, but Lex was pressed for time. The important thing was to improve his own realm, while also leaving behind a message, The Conquest realm dared to enslave a worker of the Midnight Inn, and so it was conquered.","After this it would be nearly impossible to retain the Inn’s status as a neutral entity. Then again, Lex didn`t care so much about that anyway. While the system wanted him to maintain absolute neutrality so that he could accept all guests, it seemed that it just wasn’t meant to be. The laws of the realm began to rupture, and even more chaos began to spread, until at last the outer boundary of the realm burst.","The outer boundary of all realms, mature and immature, kept the realms separated from the Void, and purified the Chaos energy of the Void and processed it into stable energy to be used within the realm. The moment that boundary was damaged, the destruction of the realm became unstoppable."]},{"number":2456,"title":"Chapter 2456: Prelude","paragraphs":["Lex ended up spending more time in the Conquest realm than he originally wanted to, but it couldn’t be helped. While he could sacrifice the material wealth of the realm, the way in which the laws of the realm were set up was too useful and unique. Lex might never encounter another Immature realm with a similar law template again, he so absolutely had to harvest it.","But what did it even mean to harvest laws? It wasn’t like they were something physical that he could pick and put in his Sovereign realm. That is why he looked for the core of the realm - that really was something he could pick up and shift. However, it would never connect to the new realm. As soon as the Conquest realm was destroved, the core would be too.","He just did his best, using whatever little knowledge he had of realmscaping and realm processing for the Midnight realm, and implemented it. Of course, since the laws themselves were connected to the environment and things within the realm itself, Lex took special care to absorb them as well.","Whatever he could absorb himself, he did. But the realm was massive, and even at his greatest speed, he ended up using a lot of time. For the things he couldn’t absorb, or couldn’t be bothered to absorb since it would waste too much time, he grabbed them with his spirit sense and bundled them together. Thus, an odd sight of Lex floating around a collapsing realm, followed by a collection of random mountains, forests, lakes, mines and more could be seen. To those of the Conquest realm who survived long enough to witness such a thing, the scene was enough to frighten them to death.","When he returned to the Midnight Inn, Lex brought all those things with him, and just dropped them in the Chaos Sea. Whether they would survive, or be devoured by the sea didn’t matter to him. What was more important to him were the hints of certain valuable laws still attached to them, or the energy contained within them. For now he was not an expert on influencing the changes in a realm, so he would just settle for such a brutish way of doing things. Velma had already prepared a teleportation path for him to the next designated realm from the list he’d given her. The list was compiled by Lex by tracing all those responsible in Z’s kidnapping. While it was surely not all those involved, it was a start.","\"Is there anything I need to prepare here inside the Inn?\" Velma asked, still unsure of what trouble Lex was expecting.","\"Just find out where Z is as quick as possible, It would be for the best if we can rescue him before long,\" said Lex, not elaborating, With each passing second, his instincts also began to sense a growing danger.","If he, a Celestial Immortal could sense it, then the Dao Lords surely could as well.","Something big was about to happen.","He wasted no time, teleporting to each subsequent realm and eliminating all those responsible. He didn`t destroy the other realms for they weren’t nearly as corrupted or filled with sinners as the Conquest realm, but he did not spare a single person who played a role in Z’s kidnapping. His actions were a loud and resounding answer to the universe about the consequences of messing with the Inn. Unfortunately, no one was paying attention to him at the moment, not even the Humanoid Alliance.","The changes in Arch-Heaven were attracting a lot of attention, but much more important was a piece of news that had been published recently. In the last one century, about 50% of all Dao Lords in the universe had disappeared. They had either been killed, or taken to a place where they could no longer be sensed.","The sheer number of disappearances was extreme. A major organisation - one that used to operate on a universal scale - collapsed. With the downfall of one, others soon followed. By now, the greed incited by the Dream Platform was finally beginning to subdue. Too many Dao Lords realised that their emotions were unusual, but it was too late.","Even if they managed to escape off the edge of the platform which was easier said than done, escaping the Dream realm itself would be too hard","The Elder races and Sage races got embroiled in war finally, mainly because of a new alliance which had popped up which blamed all the universal chaos on the Sage races. It claimed they were the ones fanning the flames in secrets so that they could monopolise the universe in secret. Even if the conspiracy wasn’t true, and they weren’t responsible for everything, it was true that soon they would be the only ones left with any real power. The whole universe was theirs for the taking, for too many other organisations capable of resisting them had been crippled. Within the Folklore realm, Jack opened his eyes from his recent meditation session, it was done. His formation was ready. He could find the Nexus as soon as the event occurred. It was too dangerous to go out and do anything else, so he gave up on all his plans and decided to stay put and wait for the Nexus event.","He was blissfully unaware that his crew had started a revolution for the fairies, attacking all those who enslaved fairies and began to create a holy land for them where the fairies would be protected from the curse that affected their race.","How they managed to create a place which could save fairies from their curse was also quite a tale. They found a minor realm inside a massive boot, claimed that the boot kicked out all curses, and enough people believed it so that when the fairies entered they found that they actually felt freed.","Of course, that was not nearly enough to turn the tide on the fate of fairies, but it was a start. Somewhere in the Geb realm, Hemzy opened her eyes and looked out in disbelief. Did she finally manage to escape the Hollow? Before she could celebrate, a sword cut through her body.","Belle had no idea whether Hemzy was an enemy or not, but the weird look in her eyes was enough to spook her, and that was reason enough to act cautiously.","She looked around her surroundings, sword still in hand, and then quickly flew away. She needed to find a way back to Eden. Even if that place was in chaos, she would not abandon it. She would save it - she had to."]},{"number":2457,"title":"Chapter 2457: Prelude II","paragraphs":["By the time Lex returned from the third Minor realm, Velma had finally extracted news about Z’s whereabouts. That’s exactly why her expression was so grim. \"There’s an unknown group that’s targeting all humans who got their hands on any Human King’s heritage,\" she explained with a solemn voice. \"Their purpose is unknown, as is their affiliation. The only thing Mathew knows or cares about is that they paid a very good price for Z, as well as information about anyone who unlocked one such heritage. Speaking of which, Mathew himself also unlocked a heritage, but he wasn’t able to make use of it because it clashes with his cultivation technique.\"","It made sense. When cultivating the Regal Embrace, what other heritage would he even need? The only shortcoming he needed to make up for was his attack power.","\"Is there anything at all we can use to track them?\" Lex asked with a frown. He’d already checked, and Z’s karma was blocked, otherwise he would be able to trace him.","Velma shook her head with disappointed.","\"He either knows nothing, or his memories have been wiped. They’re very careful.\"","Lex frowned for a bit, but quickly recovered. He placed an item with Z’s aura within Obsidian and left a quest there to find Z. For now, that was the best he could do.","\"Don’t worry too much about Z, he’s tough. His situation may not be as bad as we imagine. I’ll keep visiting these realms and see if I can find anymore leads on Z. As for Mathew...\"","Lex narrowed his eyes and looked across the Inn towards the dungeon where he was being held. Removing his system without killing would be hard - fortunately, Lex didn’t care about preserving his health. \"I’ll strip the inheritance he received and place it in the inheritance lounge. After that... I’d say give him to Luthor. Killing him would be far too easy. I’d rather keep him alive as an example.\"","Velma nodded, but she didn’t look too relieved. \"I’ve been looking into things ever since I learned about what happened to Z. It seems like the humans are in a tough spot - they’re being targeted by too many forces. There have been over a hundred reports of human Celestial Immortals being targeted by assassins the past few months, and those are just the ones who have been reported.\"","Lex looked at Velma and understood the things she left unsaid. If humans were being targeted, it wouldn’t be long before they were being targeted as well. He was about to respond, but sensed that someone was spying on them. He looked over and found that Almira was peeking from behind a rock, her nervousness apparent on her face. For the first time since Lex returned to the Inn, his expression softened and he even let out a smile. \"You don’t need to worry. With the Innkeeper back, he won’t let anyone harm us anymore.\"","Lex teleported Almira over to them, taking the little girl by surprise. She let out a yell of surprise, and then suddenly turned red when she realised that she had screamed embarrassingly in front of uncle Lex. She buried her face in Velma’s clothes as she hugged her and tried to hide her embarrassment.","\"What are you doing spying on us?\" Lex asked as he squatted down and rubbed her head, messing up her hair a little.","\"Uncle Lex, you came back and you didn’t even come see me,\" she complained, her voice filled with a tone that demonstrated the great injustice that had been carried out against her.","Lex chuckled, finding her complaint cute. \"I have to go deal with some bad guys who tried to hurt uncle Z, which is why I couldn’t come see you. But I promise, once I’m done, I’ll come play with you properly. \"","Almira glanced at Lex, as if judging the reliability of what he said, \"Well, once you bring back big brother Z you have to come see me, OK? I’ll show you my newest record in the sandpit engine.\" Lex felt like an arrow pierced through his heart. Why was Z a big brother but he was an uncle? Of course, he didn’t let his thoughts show, although Velma saw through Lex’s feelings at a glance. \"I promise,\" Lex reaffirmed and then teleported away. Fortunately, there was a convenient outlet for his frustrations nearby.","Lex glanced at Mathew indifferently, none of his previous warmth still apparent on his face, and reached into his soul. Without any reservation, Lex searched for the human King’s legacy and found a dainty, glowing seed hidden within his soul.","Lex wasn’t entirely sure if that was the human king’s legacy, but it was definitely an inheritance of some sort so he grabbed it and tossed it into the inheritance lounge without any hesitation.","After that, Lex searched for the system. The system was entirely fused with the soul which made it much harder to locate.","Lex deployed the Sovereign realm and used it to influence Mathew’s soul, looking for any trace of the system at all. It took him quite a while before he found what he was looking for, and pulled it out of his soul.","Unfortunately for Mathew, the process was not as effortless as it felt to fuse the system with his soul. A large chunk of Mathews’ soul was damaged in the process, but Lex managed to pull out the system at least.","Lex fed the newly acquired system to his own. He still had to search Daekol’s remains for his system, but now was not the time for that.","With that done, Lex left Mathew to Luthor, and left the Inn to go to the next realm.","Besides hunting his enemies and searching for Z, Lex was also on the search for Damian. His instincts were warning him that this enemy, once so easily overlooked, was once again becoming a danger.","Unfortunately, he was unable to use his bloodline to trace him. Instead, he managed to track Belle who had reappeared in some distant realm.","Lex would have to find some time to go bring her back as well. That reminded him, Liz was in the Dream realm. He’d need to call her back as well. Time was short."]},{"number":2458,"title":"Chapter 2458: New Dao","paragraphs":["\"I can’t locate Lex, but it’s already been more or less confirmed that he is alive. Whether he won his fight or lost is unknown, but he clearly survived that... tribulation of his,\" said Oaka as he looked at Liz with an honest and straight forward expression.","\"That means our previous deal has become void. I can’t really help him out anymore, nor can I target his enemy. Naturally, that also means that your payment is not required, as per the agreement. I wonder, however, if you’re interested in another deal?\"","Liz looked at Oaka and her thoughts raced. She hadn’t even come close to completing the mission given to her by the Tower of Providence, but Nemo had been getting restless as of late. He’d been suggesting that they return to the Midnight Inn - just to be safe.","Liz, however, wasn’t the type to give up so easily. Just as she was thinking of using Oaka to contact some old acquaintances in Ventura, the merchant’s expression shifted slightly, and he presented Liz with a document.","\"What’s this?\" she asked as she glanced at it. Then her expression changed too.","\"Whats the meaning of this?\" she asked, looking up at the merchant.","\"It’s the bounty request I just got for all humans. Naturally, it’s quite the tempting price, but I did not take it.\"","Liz’s expression did not ease. That’s the part she didn’t understand. Why didn’t Oaka accept such a great deal? Such random kindness did not console her, but worried her that there was something even worse in store.","\"You don’t need to be concerned with this,\" Oaka said with a soft smile \"this is just a game.\"","Liz did not understand what he meant but the growing smile on Oaka’s face seemed oddly genuine... and creepy.","*****","Bourdow kept moving at a slow pace, whistling as he went, not at all concerned about being discovered. What he was concerned about, however, was how quickly all the luck he’d accumulated was being used up.","The Dream Arena was clearly extremely perilous. At the same time, however, he was also excited by how much luck was being used up because the reward would correspond to the amount of luck used up.","Over the years, Destiny had helped him accumulate a tremendous amount of luck from various declining races. The thing about declining races was that they still had a great deal of luck left, but not enough strength to defend it, not to mention no one would find it surprising that a declining race would continue to decline.","Whether it was the human race, the fairy race, various lizard races which leeched their luck off dragons, and so on. Any one of them had a great deal of luck that no one would notice if they disappeared.","As he was strolling, Bourdow finally spotted Wu Kong. Luckily, the monkey hadn’t noticed him. Now all he needed to do was use the monkey to find the great secret of this arena.","Along the way, he’d even found a whole lot of Dao Essence, so this trip really was turning out to be the luckiest trip of his life. He couldn’t wait to count all his harvests in the end.","*****","Alexander and the rest had blacked out. They neither saw, nor sensed in any way what was happening around them, and they weren’t the only ones.","All Immortals within the vicinity of the phenomenon had blacked out, but that was expected. But then again, such a thing was expected. How could mere Immortals witness the birth of a new Dao Lord?","Outside the formation, the other Dao Lords had stopped attacking. At this point, breaking the formation would be moot. What was important now was to observe who the new Dao Lord was, and what the level of his Dao was.","Although a Minor Dao was most likely, they couldn’t eliminate the possibility of a Major Dao as well. The difference between the two would be significant.","They did not, even remotely, consider the possibility of a Unique Dao for that was too unlikely.","Second by second, minute by minute, time passed and everyone waited patiently. As it happened, when only a few seconds were left before the deadline Eclipse gave to Lex, the figure deep within the formation stood up.","A bright light hid the outline of his figure, blinding even Dao Lords who squinted at an oddity. Why was there none of the Dao radiation that accompanied a new Dao Lord?","As if in response to their answer, an outline of the figure was finally seen. It looked like a man, donning heavy armor, carrying a massive weapon.","In the eyes of some he held a spear, and in the eyes of others he held a sword. What the weapon was didn’t matter at all, for his greatest weapon was not the one in his hand, but the oath that powered him.","The light dimmed, and the Dao Lords finally laid eyes on him. Blonde hair, blue eyes, a jaw so sharp it could cut through steel and a presence that weighed down on all who laid eyes on him.","This... was a human! Not only was he human, but his bearing... his aura... this was almost...","\"My name is David Paladin,\" announced the man, his voice carrying across not just the realm, but the whole universe!","Just as Lex had caused a phenomenon, so too did this man. The difference was that David’s phenomenon was filled with the invincible power of a Unique Dao!","\"The founder of the Paladin Dao, creator of the path of paladins, and the torch bearer of humanity’s glorious return to power. All those who have targeted humanity... prepare for your imminent demise!\"","The universe welcomed the birth of the unique Paladin Dao, and watched in stunned silence as humanity’s destiny skyrocketed.","At the exact same moment, several other races revealed Dao Lords of their own, as if they had been holding back for so long. Even though none could match up to David, their rise was unquestionable.","Within the Dream realm, Bourdow’s expression changed, but it was too late. He had, for the first time, triggered an Unlucky Break."]},{"number":2459,"title":"Chapter 2459: Don’t take it personally","paragraphs":["The Dao of Lucky Break was so immensely powerful and effective that ever since Bourdow had become a Dao Lord, he’d never really encountered any issues. That was because he was very careful about how he used it.","Thus, for so long, he was very calculative about the luck he stole, and how he used it. He always, always made sure that he had an immense reserve left regardless of his situation.","Even when the Dream Arena used up a lot of his luck, in truth it was only about 15% of his reserves. However, as it happened, the luck he used up was the one he created and accumulated himself, whereas the luck he was left with was the luck he stole.","Even though he stole the luck, he purified and refined it countless times until it was indistinguishable from his own. No one should have any claim left to it. Unfortunately for Bourdow, he had placed too much trust in that ’should’.","All his luck turned... there was no word for it except sour. Even if it had turned into bad luck directly, he might have been able to control it. He would have been able to keep it from triggering. Yet when it turned sour, the luck acted against him as if it held a vendetta. It was almost as if the luck had a mind of its own.","Just in the way he could occasionally trigger a Lucky Break, this time he automatically triggered an Unlucky Break, and its effects were instantaneous.","Not only did Wu Kong notice him, he triggered some kind of trap on the Dream Arena which launched a flare over his head, alerting everyone of his location.","As if that was not bad enough, his soured luck began to break down and devour his body like a greedy parasite. Bourdow coughed out blood as his internal organs were ruptured, and he had no choice but to burn all the luck he had. That was not an easy choice because without any luck to use up, he would immediately become the weakest he’d ever been since becoming a Dao Lord.","\"Are you following me?\" asked Wu Kong who appeared beside Bourdow, grabbing his body as if to steal something.","Either Wu Kong was extremely lucky, or Bourdow was extremely unlucky, for Wu Kong swiped the strongest protective tool Bourdow kept on his person to protect himself.","\"Oh?\" said Wu Kong, clearly not expecting to steal something so valuable so quickly.","\"Dammmit!\" exclaimed Bourdow as he pushed himself back and activated a teleportation device.","Yet it seemed that luck was not on his side because he tripped when he pushed himself back - something he hadn’t done in his entire life - and the device broke before activating.","Wu Kong became even more interested in this fellow for he couldn’t understand what was happening, but he could tell that it would benefit him. He swiped again, and this time he stole a whole lot of Dao Essence.","Bourdow, well aware that he couldn’t continue on like this, immediately decided to give up and contact Destiny to extract him, but it just wasn’t his day. For reasons he couldn’t understand at all, he was unable to connect to her.","\"What the hell is going on?\" he exclaimed, this time teleporting away with his own power. The reason he’d used his device before was because it had a fixed destination that even the Dream realm wouldn’t interfere with. Now, he was teleporting at random, and he didn’t trust his luck to guide him.","But he was forced to act, for wherever he would go would be better than being in front of Wu Kong, right?","Turns out, he was terribly, terribly wrong.","Bourdow appeared in the center of a massive formation, each and every ounce of it giving such immense Dao Radiation that he had no doubt that he had stumbled onto the core of the Dream Arena.","The ground beneath his feet was painted with a large and ominous pattern, one that frightened Bourdow even though he couldn’t understand the reason why.","If that was all, he would not have been nearly as afraid as he actually was. The thing that frightened him the most was not the core area, nor was it patterns on the ground. Instead, it was the sight of the Dream Master, standing there, waiting for him to gather his bearings.","What made the situation worse... was that he recognised the Dream Master!","\"You... what are you doing over here?\" he asked even as his mind raced and he thought of a way to escape. But it was no use. In the presence of the Dream Master, he could not muster any strength at all. It was as if he were a mere mortal.","\"Waiting for you, obviously, \" responded the Dream Master as she waved her hand, causing countless chains to emerge through the ground and pierce through Bourdow’s body.","The chains then withdrew, pinning Bourdow to the ground with taut chains.","\"You know, I’ve heard that you’ll be lucky for as long as you live,\" commented the Dream Master as she walked up to him and guided the blood on the chains onto the formation beneath him.","\"Seeing the state that you’re in now, I guess it’s time for you to die.\"","Bourdow trembled and tried to use any means at all at his disposal. Unfortunately, in front of her he had no means available at all.","\"No, please, don’t do this. I... I can pay you. I can pay my own ransome,\" he pleaded, but the Dream Master just heard his words with an air of indifference as she continued to do her work. \"Don’t take it personally,\" she said plainly.","\"A lot of races paid for too many years with too much of their luck to trap you here. It’d be a real disservice to them if I let you live after all the sacrifices they made for me.\"","Chills traveled down Bourdow’s spine as he realised that when he thought he was being clever, he was merely walking into a trap that spanned over an age."]},{"number":2460,"title":"Chapter 2460: The Nexus Event I","paragraphs":["Within the Folklore realm, Jack opened his eyes in shock as he felt his power skyrocket for no apparent reason. His Paladin powers became stronger on their own, and as they strengthened, so did his abilities and senses.","Before he could savor the feeling, though, the formation he was sitting in triggered, shocking him even more! The Nexus event wasn’t supposed to start yet, but it had. Across the entire universe, all destinies were being rewritten entirely. In fact, Jack even felt that the position of the fairies on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum had increased substantially.","Lex, meanwhile, had done his best to attack as many realms as possible within his time limit. Yet about 10,000 seconds before time was up, he discovered that there were no more devils who could help him teleport across the universe. Whether it was because their actions had been noticed, or because something else was happening, Lex didn’t know.","They all just disappeared, withdrawing even from the Midnight Inn. Velma told him that they had all gone back to their own realm, but even she didn’t know the reason why. Thus he was forced to stay inside the Midnight Inn until the time was up, using that period to process the growth in his cultivation and Sovereign realm.","When the time was up, though, Lex too flashed his eyes open. Not only had his own Paladin powers also increased, he received a strange system notification. Just as he was processing that notification, he felt the position of humanity skyrocket on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum in a way he’d never felt before!","The strength of his instincts grew exponentially, to the point that he sensed two significant things. First, there was something hidden within the Midnight realm that was dangerous, and had eluded his senses and detection so far. The second thing he sensed was that the seal on his forehead loosened on its own, and a flood of memories came rushing in. It seemed like the Timekeeper also knew a great deal about the Nexus event.","In the memories, Lex discovered that he was sitting across his doppelganger talking about it. \"The next Nexus event is going to be special,\" Said the doppelganger as he puffed his pipe. \"Unlike the previous ones, it won’t just be the trigger of the Nexus event which will wipe away all destinies. This time, the entire duration of the event will wipe destinies, which is an opportunity of a lifetime.","\"You see, I have a lot of time on my hands, and it needs to be released during the Nexus event. Doing so will give you a tremendous amount of positive karma, and improve your destiny, but despite what it seems like, that’s not such a good thing. \"With such a rise in karma and destiny, it will attract attention, and questions. Questions like where all this time came from - questions that neither you, nor I can afford to answer.","\"Half the time released can be used up by you however you wish, and only half needs to be released into the rest of the universe. With that, you can speed up the development of a valuable fruit, grow a treasure, expand a realm, whatever you want. It just can’t be used to increase the flow of time in a soul - besides that, it’s entirely up to you.","\"But, before the Nexus event, you need to discreetly release a bit of time in advance so that the universe can acclimatise to it. I have a few trillion years worth of time set aside, and the more of it you release before the Nexus event, the more effective the time you release during the Nexus event will be. It’s just a matter of how much of that time you can smuggle in using your soul.\"","After talking to his doppelganger a bit more, Lex had accepted the deal for two main reasons. The first reason was that the value of so much time could not be estimated, and it could help him a lot, even if he didn’t exactly know what he would use the time for just yet.","The second reason was that at the time Lex was extremely weak, and the mysterious Timekeeper was strong, so he didn’t dare refuse this deal. As soon as he was done viewing the memories, Lex knew exactly how he was going to use that time.","Around the same time, a veil seemed to be lifted across the universe, revealing many secrets. All at once, countless Dao Lords sensed that it was not just a few, but thousands of Mature realms that had been destroyed! Yet, oddly enough, the universe did not mourn the destruction of every Mature realm. In fact, it seemed there were actually very few realms the destruction of which caused the universe itself to shudder!","In comparison, the majority of realms that were destroyed relieved a tremendous amount of strain, and a separate kind of burden that gave off the feeling of wrongness.","None could explain it, for none could understand it, but what they all realised was that there was something wrong with those destroyed realms. Within Arch-Heaven, the dome which had trapped hundreds of Dao Lords shimmered, and its surface became transparent, allowing anyone to peer inside. Yet the sight they saw was terrifying!","Each Dao Lord lay on the ground, a painful expression on their faces. Black veins covered their bodies, as if poison coursed through their veins. Yet the most terrifying thing was that above each of the Dao Lords’ bodies, there seemed like a warped, terrifying soul, wrapped up in chains. The mere sight of those souls gave off a feeling of wrongness, as if they did not belong to this universe.","The agents left behind by the Sage races to watch and report the situation on the dome were horrified the most, for they realised what those souls were. They were parasites, occupying the bodies and replacing their original hosts! It was unimaginable that such a thing could happen to Dao Lords, which meant that all these people had been infected by these parasitic souls before they reached such a level.","They then reached the Dao Lord realm and began infecting the universe with their corrupted Daos. The question was... where did so many of such parasites come from? They certainly did not know. They tried to report it immediately, but the universe was far more tumultuous now than it had been in ages. It was also at this time that a wounded Romulus left the Gilded Hollow, and entered the universe once more."]},{"number":2461,"title":"Chapter 2461: The Nexus Event II","paragraphs":["When the Nexus event came, Vera felt it far more deeply than most - including Lex. The entire future became a blank canvas, as if destiny and fate did not exist at all, and no amount of probability could allow her to predict the future. In fact, probability itself became skewed during the Nexus event, and all sorts of unusual things began to happen.","That was because the standard probabilities that most were familiar with were merely a result of the normal function of the universe’s laws. Yet during the Nexus event, especially this one, too many unusual things began to happen.","This was something she had predicted. She had, long ago, held a meeting for oracles to determine what they should do during this time. Yet she had, by now, come to terms with the fact that her ability wasn’t nearly as powerful as she thought it was.","For some strange reason, though, almost as soon as the Nexus event occurred, her instincts improved. Since she wasn’t a practitioner of the True Path - what humans identified cultivating body, spirit and soul - her instincts weren’t particularly pronounced generally speaking.","Now, though, that had changed. Her instincts became active, and they said only one thing: there was something terribly wrong with her father. But the realization came too late. When she began to look for her father, he was missing. Not just that, but her mother was missing too.","On Earth, Robert Joel watched with kind, soft eyes as Kristine gave birth - this time to a son. The woman, despite being a powerful cultivator, was exceptionally drained after giving birth, becoming as vulnerable as a mortal woman. She could barely keep her eyes open, but she struggled on, wanting to look at her husband and her new child.","Robert took the child from the doctor and brought him to Kristine, the silver dagger floating behind his back completely hidden. When Kristine took the child, she wasn’t looking at him at all, and Robert flicked his finger, sending the dagger towards her neck. Yet at the last moment, right before the dagger touched her neck, it stopped.","During the Nexus event, Robert couldn’t see the future either, but his instincts had become much sharper. He could sense lethal danger in his near future if he killed Kristine. In comparison, leaving her alive only left a minor vulnerability - far less than the danger of killing her.","It wasn’t a perfect plan, but Robert was never too bothered with perfection. He found that those who obsessed too much on doing everything perfectly often missed out on other opportunities - just like Daekol.","His performance was, quite frankly, very disappointing. After all his effort to remove that dangerous element by his daughter’s side, the stupid Sovereign failed. No matter - keeping him occupied for so long was good enough. It had allowed Robert to move forward with his plans.","\"Sleep, darling,\" said Robert as he took the child away again. \"We’ll be right here when you wake up.\"","Kristine looked at him lovingly, and then finally closed her eyes. The same instant, Robert killed the doctor and everyone else, leaving the weakened Kristine behind.","Robert casually made his way to the same village where Bastet once resided - the very one she had protected for centuries, and the one that couldn’t normally be found by cultivators at all.","The smell of corpses was, thankfully, finally gone. He looked up and found the only other resident of the village standing at the base of Bastet’s temple, looking at him with a sombre expression.","\"Do you believe me now? If I hadn’t hidden you here, your beloved grandson would have already paid you a visit,\" Robert said. \"I suspect what would have followed would not have been a quick demise, but a prolonged life of pain and misery.\"","Damian pursed his lips, but said and did nothing. The ’man’ in front of him was far too mysterious, and far too enigmatic. Even Damian, after getting his hands on the lost legacy of the Sepore family, was nothing in front of him.","\"My end of the bargain,\" Damian said, and held out two vials of blood. One held Moon’s blood, taken long ago, and the other held Lex’s blood from before he became an immortal.","How did Damian get ahold of Lex’s blood, and even manage to keep it secret?","It had been collected by the insects that invaded Polebitvy, oh so long ago. Back then Damian didn’t even know whose blood was being collected, or why.","Now... even though he knew, he didn’t tamper with the blood at all. Though this man was mysterious, that didn’t matter. What mattered was that they could work together.","\"How long can I remain within this village before being detected?\" Damian asked, not bothering to inquire why the man wanted this blood.","\"A few centuries at most,\" responded Robert as he looked at the vials of blood and analyzed them. \"Definitley not more than 500 years. Best make the most of it.\"","Robert then turned around and left, not bothering with Damian anymore. He no longer needed anything from that man.","He soon appeared in a base he had prepared long ago, and placed the child in an altar before beginning to smear Moon’s blood on his body in strange symbols. Once it was all used up, he injected Lex’s blood into the baby directly.","\"Soul Genesis blood to strengthen the vessel, and Empyrean resonance blood to help it adapt to the upcoming changes...\" Robert muttered to himself before taking a seat himself in a separate part of the altar, especially prepared for himself.","Soon, the ritual began. A thin, silver stream of unusual particles began to enter Robert’s body from somewhere unknown, while a thin stream of blood red particles traveled from his body to the baby’s.","After a few hours, the baby opened his eyes, his gaze carrying a depth of emotions and wisdom that far surpassed its age. The Essence Wormhole would finally be his!","*****","Abaddon, Forgotten Forest","The two Kun Peng opened their eyes as if they sensed something they had been waiting for..."]},{"number":2462,"title":"Chapter 2462: The Nexus Event III","paragraphs":["Without wasting a single moment, the two Kun Peng began to wake up all the other residents of the forest, getting ready to, at last, leave this accursed place.","The process was not long at all, and took an entirety of two seconds, as if everything had long been prepared. Then... the entire forest itself disappeared, leaving the endless army on invading Dao Lords lost and without a target.","Within the universe, a new realm appeared called the Forgotten Forest realm, and it began to rapidly head towards maturity, as if time was passing at an exponential rate. Where all this additional time was coming from was something even the two Kun Peng did not know, nor did they care.","The reason they had hidden for so long wasn’t so that they could get caught up in minor, insignificant details. They didn’t even care if their realm reached maturity or not - that was simply something their collaborator had promised them. No, all they cared about was the impending war.","Soon, a message was delivered to them, detailing all the tactical information about one of the Sage races, from their realm ownerships, to their secret weapons, back up bases, hidden contingencies and so on.","\"To war,\" said the Kun Peng Little Blue called Mr. Big-fat-guy. Behind him, countless other Dao Lords echoed his call","\" TO WAR !\"","The Kun Peng released their wings and flew. They flew through their realm, through the Void, at a speed faster than light, or thought, or even teleportation, arriving upon the base of the Weaver race with a sudden ferocity that could not be contained.","The Weaver race, subjects of Destiny, and the best oracles in the universe, never saw this particular future coming, and so they were caught unprepared.","To make matters worse, at the moment of the invasion, a massive dream began to manifest above their realms, taking the shape of the Dream Arena, making all Dao Lords vulnerable. That included the Kun Peng, and the other invading Dao Lords, but they didn’t care at all.","They attacked with a ferocity that could only be cultivated by harboring a vendetta for over an age.","The attack came too suddenly and too strongly, making it impossible to resist in a short period of time, thus a few of the wiser Weavers escaped. Yet when they entered the Void, they did not find it empty as it usually was.","Instead, standing there, waiting for them, was Elizabeth the Wrathful. Behind her was an army of confused Primals.","An ominous feeling gripped the Weavers, but they tried their luck anyway. That was all they could do.","\"Peacekeepers! You’re finally here! We’re... we’re being attacked!\" said the leading Weaver, only to find that his body was slowly starting to disintegrate. The thing about Elizabeth - the thing that caused all to fear her - was that she never had trouble killing Dao Lords. She did not need the Dream Arena - wherever she stood became the graveyard for her enemies.","The Weaver never understood why he had been attacked, nor did the Primals behind her. The difference was that the Primals didn’t care too much either.","\"The day my father let me out, we stopped being peacekeepers for this ungrateful universe,\" she said in a hateful, angry tone.","The next moment, another war began in the Void, stopping all escaping Weavers in their tracks. During this Nexus event, the destiny of the universe was being rewritten.","*****","The Nexus","Jack activated the formation and finally, finally arrived at the Nexus. He had waited so many years for this moment. If his life were a book, then he would have been waiting for this moment for nearly 800 Chapters.","The journey was not easy, but he had made it here at last. But making it here was just the first step. He now had to begin construction of the Midnight Castle here, and then place the Chamber of Rebirth within. This was the ultimate contingency Lex had prepared for himself, and if his experience with the necklace had taught him anything, it was that he could never be prepared enough.","After gathering himself, Lex took a look around and immediately noticed the Nexus item! It appeared like a simple dagger, though upon further consideration Jack realized that nothing about it was simple at all.","The blade, at first, seemed to be made of a metal similar to silver, but closer inspection revealed that it was instead made of silver moonlight. The handle was made of a pure white material, almost like the purest of marble, but there was something off about it that he couldn’t discern.","The blade had no aura at all, making it perfect for assassination, but Jack had no doubt at all that it was far beyond his level. For a moment he considered taking the blade for himself, but discovered that he had some kind of internal inhibition stopping him from trying to take the dagger.","Jack had no idea if that inhibition was normal or not, but he quickly reigned in his greed and decided not to mess with anything. His goal was to create a failsafe for himself - a way to protect himself in case he ever faced death.","Jack looked away from the dagger and looked around to find that the Nexus was not too large. The ’ground’ was made up of some kind of metallic liquid, though fortunately it could not be entered, making it a decent alternative for the floor if one ignored the fact that it was constantly moving.","The boundary of the Nexus consisted of nine pillars, evenly spread to form a circle, with a transparent barrier between them. Beyond the barrier were endless clouds, hiding anything and everything from view.","The sky, too, had a limit and rose merely a couple of miles high. All in all, it was a small place, not even big enough to fit a whole town, but it was enough to fit in the Midnight Castle.","Jack immediately started working, entirely unaware that, at some point, the dagger disappeared from the Nexus, leaving it empty save him."]},{"number":2463,"title":"Chapter 2463: The Nexus Event IV","paragraphs":["Within the Midnight realm, Lex sat with his eyes closed, allowing the storm of time to erupt from his body. The place he chose to carry out this particular activity was the place he called the Valley of Time where he had previously made alterations to the realm to facilitate him in allowing time to move faster.","Now, the endless torrent of time that the Timekeeper wanted him to unleash was rushing out of his body in a massive yet consistent stream. Exactly 50% of the time unleashed was disappearing into the Void, its target unknown to him, while the rest that he could use for himself was being directed towards the Midnight realm.","Honestly, an upper cap of the Heaven Immortal realm was kind of low for him. It limited not just the resources that the realm produced, but also the natural level of the natives of the realm. Now that he was a Celestial Immortal, Lex had no fear of any native becoming too strong for him to handle, so he could allow the realm to grow in peace.","Lex was sure that even with all the time he released, it still wouldn’t be enough for the realm to reach maturity, but at least it would grow much stronger than it was currently.","While he was meditating, allowing the time to flow through him, Lex got a couple of notifications from his system. Lex glanced at them, and though their contents deserved some attention, he could literally do nothing else right now, so he could only ignore them.","Emergency Notification: Due to an ongoing universe-wide event, all system related quests have been suspended, and all system processes are being put into minimal activity mode. The host is recommended to remain inactive during this period to avoid unforeseen complications.","New Notification: The Midnight realm is undergoing rapid evolution, leading to quicker development of Midnight Realm Management alterations and additions. Corresponding quest disabled due to critical external conditions. Corresponding Inn growth temporarily suspended due to temporary system operation suppression. The realm will grow naturally in an unguided fashion. The host is advised to avoid undertaking any further actions to avoid attracting undue or potentially detrimental attention.","Both notifications simply told him to do nothing that would attract attention. However, considering that he was shooting time out of his body like a rocket out of a bazooka, that was basically impossible. In his defense, he had tried to use the Masterless technique to his utmost before he began.","He also activated an Innkeeper Business card to create an Innkeeper projection above him, as if he was looking down on Lex just in case he really did end up attracting attention. The rest could only be left up to fate.","Yet Lex was overthinking. The amount of things happening during the Nexus event far exceeded his imagination, and the reason they were all happening right now was because they basically couldn’t be tracked at all.","The extra time flowing out of Lex’s body was directly advancing the Forgotten Forest realm, which meant his own realm wasn’t the only one rapidly evolving.","Lex had spread his awareness out as far as possible so that he could view the changes in case anything went wrong. He also wanted to see how the realm evolved to increase his own understanding of it for his Sovereign realm. Thus, he witnessed in real time as the realm grew, and the Chaos Sea retreated.","None of the plants or residents were automatically becoming stronger as the realm grew, for the time was only affecting noneliving things. That did mean, however, that mountains rose, new metals and minerals were formed, the continents underwent massive changes and the realm itself began to evolve.","The boundary of the realm became extremely efficient in absorbing energy from the Void, thus causing a rain of spiritual essence across the whole realm to keep up with the rapid growth of the realm.","In the easternmost corner of the realm, the sea of lava grew and grew until it gave birth to a world of fire elementals and a terrain unique to itself entirely. In the center of the realm, a massive continent larger than all the other three combined began to morph and change, turning entirely into a mountain range, the center of which was one, single peak that rose high above everything else in the realm, becoming the zenith of the realm, almost as if it yearned to touch the Primordial Fire Crow in the sky.","The upper limit of the realm grew, inching closer and closer to the threshold of Celestial realm, while the actual size of the realm also kept growing, its boundary extending farther and farther.","But despite how glorious the scene was, it was nothing compared to everything happening across the universe. Every single second, a Mature realm was being devoured - not destroyed, but devoured by an unseen, unknown force, wiping them from existence.","The laws of the universe trembled. The armies of Arch-Heaven marched. The Void Dwellers went mad amidst anarchy. Blood spilled in greater quantities than water fell from the skies, and bedlam replaced sanity and coherence.","Amidst what could only be called an armageddon that spread across the entire universe, there was only one realm that remained entirely unaffected. Within the Primordial Garden, a melancholic expression covered Eclipse’s face.","\"It’s almost time,\" she whispered, sending a shiver down Nulli’s back as she resisted her natural urge to immediately turn pink. She said nothing, and instead increased her focus even more. Now, more than ever, she could not fail Eclipse.","\"Shall I send the order?\" asked Harriot earnestly. Right now, he cared for nothing else save the pain his master must be feeling. He would have borne it himself if he could. Alas, he was too weak to do so. Always, he had been too weak to truly carry her burdens.","\"Not yet,\" Eclipse said softly. \"I want to see him first, one last time.\"","Harriot nodded, and then used his power. Eclipse did not rise from her throne, nor did her throne move at all. Instead, the realm itself moved around the throne until Eclipse, Nulli and Harriot were within a sepulcher, in front of a great statue that marked a tomb.","None of them said anything. They all waited in silence. This was the first time since this tomb had been made that Eclipse had visited, and the significance of this visit was not lost on any of them.","A shiver of excitement ran down Nulli’s back as she used the entire breadth of her willpower to contain herself from turning pink. The thing that Nulli loved more than anything else - the very thing that aroused her like nothing else could - was power. To be more specific, it was a powerful person, unleashing absolute, unquestionable might.","There was no one in the universe who could do that better than Eclipse, which is why Nulli tried to hard to contain herself. She was about to approach that one moment she had experienced countless years for. She could have traveled through time to that exact moment - as a Nullith, it was within her capability. Instead, she savored each moment, slowly building that anticipation, spending each moment by Eclipse’s side.","Her investment of experiencing so much time by Eclipse... was finally about to pay off."]},{"number":2464,"title":"Chapter 2464: Why was Eclipse...","paragraphs":["Harriot and Nulli said nothing, and simply allowed Eclipse to have her moment. Even now, though, there wasn’t any sorrow or regret on her face as she looked, only resolve.","\"Harriot, send word. It’s time to start,\" said Eclipse calmly, and the poodle quickly nodded.","The poodle was about to speak but paused, looked at Eclipse, and then ran off a certain distance before passing his orders.","\"The Primordial Queen has given permission. This time, they’re going to get fu-\"","*****","Dream realm, Dream Arena","Bourdow looked pleadingly at the Dream Master, but it was for naught. She had not spared him so long because she was merciful, but because she was making preparations.","\"The Human race, the Fairy race, Sloths, numerous lizards, the serpentine races, and countless natural treasures and plants such as Four Leaf Clovers, the Holy Basil, the Primordial Lotus series and so many more... you have leeched the luck off of so many and never felt an ounce of pity for them, so why are you expecting pity in return?\" the Dream Master asked as she slowly worked.","Bourdow would have answered, but he no longer had the energy to say anything. All he could do was look at the Dream Master and hope that she found mercy in her heart... or that Destiny could save him. But it was not to be.","Thick lines of karma began to emerge from Bourdow’s body, each one so massive that the sun itself would have dwarfed in its presence. Naturally, Bourdow alone could never devour all the luck, fortune and destiny of even one of these races, let alone so many of them.","He simply harvested a chunk of their luck, gaining much in the process while making it easier for others to steal the rest.","The karmic lines emerging from his body now represented those tiny chunks that he had stolen... and then there were even more lines coming out of his body, from races he had never even heard of. Why did he care where the luck came from? As long as Destiny gave it, he took it.","For all his bluster, he was nothing more than a glorified waste disposal unit for the luck Destiny did not harvest herself. At least, that’s what it seemed like in the Dream Masters eyes.","The Dream Master held out her hand and a dagger of moonlight blade, and a handle of white karmic strings appeared. She used it to make a single cut of Bourdow’s body, using the blood to write an ancient character on the Dream Arena beneath her.","\" For those who keeled for the sake of honor,","For those who sacrificed to right a wrong,","For those who endured though they saw no glory,","For those who died... to be a part of this story... \"","The Dream Master recited a few lines that sounded like poetry, but her each line was written in Bourdow’s blood, becoming a part of the ritual itself.","\" A pact in blood and a fate of decline,","An impossible oath for freedom eternal,","Rise guardians from races untold,","Witness the deliverance of a legend of old. \"","As soon as the Dream Master finished her chant, the karmic strings rippled, spreading across the very foundation of the universe until finally it touched the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum.","From there, all the concerned races were affected, though unfortunately, many of them no longer even existed.","The Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum trembled, and so did the Dream Arena, but it did not last long. Barely anyone noticed, and those who were in the position to notice chose not to interfere because they had already been warned not to.","A thick, grey fog began to appear all across the Dream Arena, causing all Dao Lords to get lost within, losing even those they were fighting mere moments ago. For some that was a grave loss, for others a great relief. For Bourdow, it signaled the end.","Surrounded by fog, he let his gaze wander into the distance instead of looking at the Dream Master. It was so unfair. If it were anyone else, he would have found a way to escape, to survive. So why did it have to be her? Why?","He got no answer to that question. He did, however, see the figure of a very confused fairy in the fog.","Jack looked left and right, and discovered that it wasn’t his body or even soul that had been transported, but a portion of his awareness. In fact, he hadn’t even been transported anywhere - he was merely witnessing something.","Funnily enough, to his left, he saw Tinker, the fairy he had rescued from a Hell.","The two did not talk, for both of them were incredibly confused about what was happening. They got no answers. Instead, more and more figures began to appear all throughout the fog. Each race had a few representatives, each one a crucial member and leader among their race.","It was only a matter of time before Lex, too, found himself standing in the fog, though Jack was nowhere in sight. He looked to his left and was surprised to see Cassandra! His teacher looked at him too, clearly just as surprised as he. Lex suddenly felt something, and when he looked to his right he saw another human - one he, oddly enough, recognized.","How could Lex not? He had seen statues of him back inside the Midnight Inn, within the village of Paladins. This was David Paladin, the founder of the path of paladins and... apparently a Dao Lord!","Shock appeared in Lex’s eyes as he realized that he was standing next to a human Dao Lord! He could not sense the aura, but his instinct told him as much.","David, in exchange, merely looked at Lex and gave him a nod of approval. He was glad to see that one of the leaders of humanity - as recognized by the universe itself - was also a practitioner of the paladin path.","This was the path he had created to save mankind, to save those who were not lucky enough to cultivate the True Path. He himself had walked the path to its very end to prove its feasibility, so now no one would be able to question, nor stop the paladins.","More and more figures began to appear in the fog, Lex noticed, and they all seemed to be looking at the same thing.","He followed their gaze and witnessed...","Lex’s heart stopped as he stared dumbstruck as the Dream Master looked up at him and waved.","Why was Eclipse... outside the Primordial Garden?"]},{"number":2465,"title":"Chapter 2465: I wonder who said that?","paragraphs":["Lex’s brain froze because he was trying to figure out what he was seeing. Considering she waved at him, he was pretty certain he was looking at Eclipse. No, scratch that. Based solely on the fact that no one would have the guts to impersonate Eclipse, Lex was sure that was Eclipse.","So if she was outside her realm the entire time, did that mean that the story about the evolution of the universe connected to her was a lie? Or was there more to it?","Lex didn’t have time to figure that out because Eclipse looked from him towards Jack with an unusual expression on her face, as if she had just realized something. Of course Lex couldn’t keep a secret from her.","Jack waved meekly. Eclipse chuckled and waved back with a dagger in her hand before turning her attention back to Bourdow.","In the fog, there were very few Dao Lords, but many Celestials and even more Heaven Immortals. These were not all the races that had their luck stolen by Bourdow - these were the races that had their luck stolen, and the ancestors entered into an agreement with Eclipse.","Romulus also appeared in the fog, uncertain of what was happening. He seemed to spot Lex in the fog, though, and calmed down. It was too bad he couldn’t move, or else he’d gone and sat next to him. Was that powerful looking guy next to him the Innkeeper?","He would have loved to ask, but he was unable to do so.","Eclipse waited, standing above Bourdow’s body until, at last, all the representatives appeared. A little over one thousand three hundred races had appeared - which was quite sad because originally over ten thousand had entered the pact. Those were the races that had died... to become a part of this story.","\"Guardians, protectors, leaders of these various races, you are here today because once, long ago, your ancestors entered a pact, and I made an oath,\" said Eclipse, her voice carrying to each and everyone in the fog though she spoke calmly. \"For two ages you have suffered, but today I will fulfil my oath, and deliver you from the chains imposed upon you by someone else’s design.\"","Bourdow just looked up at Eclipse. It was so unfair. If he had faced anyone but her... anyone but her...","Without explaining further, and without any further delay, Eclipse stabbed Bourdow in the forehead with the dagger, instantly killing him and shattering his Dao. Yet his body did not disintegrate due to the force of the attack.","Instead, it began to morph into someone else entirely. Something happened that Lex had experienced before. Eclipse was so powerful that Lex could not actually see her. The figure he ’saw’ when he looked at her was merely an image his mind projected knowing that there was a powerful figure there. Her actual appearance was unknown to him.","The figure that was stabbed in the head was a Dao Lord, but once it began to morph, Lex sensed that he was no longer seeing the real body. Instead, he was seeing a projection conjured by his brain so that he was saved from the real sight.","Yet while he was saved from the sight, he was not saved from the sounds - though for some reason he felt no pressure from them. Maybe the fog was protecting him somehow.","\"Huh? What the hell?\" said Destiny as her actual, main body suddenly appeared in place of Bourdow, wrapped in chains, covered in characters written in blood, with a dagger stuck in her head.","How was it possible? How could she be moved from her place without her noticing, let alone being able to resist?","She looked up to see Eclipse, and was even more shocked!","\"Eclipse? What the hell are you doing outside your realm?\" she asked, unable to process what was happening.","She tried to move her hand to her forehead - tried to remove the dagger - but found she could not. The weight of the chains... the weight was too great!","Shock! Disbelief! Horror!","\"How is this possible?\" she asked, trying to lift her hand once again, only to discover that she was not mistaken. She, Destiny, was being constrained by simple physical force. Such a thing could not be. Such a thing could never be! She was no mere Dao Lord! She could not be contained!","Destiny was suddenly infuriated, and she activated her power - her true, genuine power - without concern over the fact that the universe would immediately punish her for revealing her strength.","Yet there was no thunder - no calamitous roar of the sounds of chains breaking and the realm rupturing. Nothing happened. The chains... they bore even her full strength, and all they did was move slightly, allowing her to lift her hand towards the dagger. Yet she could not reach it.","\"Destiny, why are you in such a hurry to leave? I put in so much effort to host you,\" said Eclipse as she held the woman’s chin and turned her face towards her. The two ladies locked eyes - with Destiny’s eyes burning with uncontrollable fury, while Eclipse’s held nothing but an untouchable calm, the kind born only from absolute confidence.","\"Eclipse, why the hell are you outside your realm?\" Destiny demanded once again, her voice filled with a madness that threatened to destroy reality itself. \"Why can you exit the realm without affecting the universe?\"","Eclipse raised a single eyebrow, as if curious.","\"Oh? Why would my location be any concern to the universe?\" she asked oh so innocently.","Lex had no idea who this Destiny was, though he could guess. The only one worthy of Eclipse’s attention - the only one confident enough to even call out her name like that - would be a being above the Dao Lord realm. That was a kind of entity Lex could not even imagine challenging, and here Eclipse was, casually teasing her. It felt so... great!","Although Lex personally had nothing against Destiny, he decided that if Eclipse was teasing her and treating her like this, she probably deserved it.","\"What do you mean why is it the universe’s concern? Everyone knows that your realm is the only thing keeping your power in check. The moment you leave your realm, the universe should be affected and begin its transition!\"","Eclipse showed an exaggerated look of surprise upon hearing that.","\"Everyone knows? I wonder how everyone found out such a thing,\" she said, almost as if she was musing to herself.","\"Your told everyone yourself-\"","Destiny just paused, and looked at Eclipse with a shock that rocked her to her core as she realized something. Why did she believe this rumor, just because Eclipse herself claimed it to be true? Wasn’t it possible she lied, or misled everyone? Yet for billions of years, Destiny had never questioned such a thing.","It obviously wasn’t because Destiny was incapable of spotting such an obvious flaw. It was much more likely because... she, like everyone else, was affected by Eclipse, making her incapable of thinking otherwise.","\"Oh? Did I say it? Then I guess it must be true,\" Eclipse said with a nod. \"It’s a good thing, then, that I never left the Dream realm, my seat of power, for so long. Right?\""]},{"number":2466,"title":"Chapter 2466: Should have killed me when you had the chance II","paragraphs":["\"Damn, I didn’t see that one coming,\" whispered Lex as he tapped Cassandra with his elbow and pointed towards Eclipse’s revelation. Lex found that his status as a Primordial kept him from being as suppressed by the fog as everyone else.","It had nothing to do with power or cultivation level - since he was a Primordial, he got some extra benefits. Cassandra looked at Lex and could not muster the energy to be surprised at Lex’s oddities. She had become used to him being different back when she trained him.","She shook her head and then looked towards the Primordial Queen once more. This was a historic event that would be remembered for all of history. It was a tremendous honor to be a part of it. She did not want to miss anything because Lex distracted her.","Destiny’s mind raced, no longer wasting any energy on being shocked at Eclipse. Her situation was abnormal - she had never encountered nor heard of anything in the universe which could chain someone of her status. Now that she had finally come across it, she needed to figure out how it worked and stop it.","The chains restrained her, whereas the dagger restrained her grasp over destiny, making her suppression twofold. She needed to keep Eclipse talking so she could get more time to figure out a way to get free.","\"If you’ve been inside the Dream realm all this time then... who is in the Primordial Garden?\" asked Destiny. \"Don’t tell me it’s a clone. Each and every one of us probed the Garden - a mere clone, even if it’s yours, is not enough to deter us.\"","Eclipse seemed unconcerned entirely by her attempts to drag things out, and answered.","\"Oh come now, do you want me to tell you all my secrets?\" Eclipse asked as she strolled around Destiny, observing all the characters to make sure they were intact. Then she tapped on the chains wrapped around Destiny, and each of them began to slowly glow with a soft, white light.","\"Oh alright, if you insist ,\" Eclipse suddenly said, before Destiny could say anything herself. \"The one inside the Primordial Garden really is a special clone of mine. I had Life help me make it. It’s basically indistinguishable from myself. But the clone naturally doesn’t have the same strength as me, which is where my bodyguard comes in. But that... is a story for another time. We have much more important matters to attend to right now, don’t we?\"","Destiny had, one by one, tried to activate her powers and contingencies, but discovered that the pressure on her being caused by the chains kept her from using any power at all. As such... she had to do something incredibly desperate. She had to ask Death for help.","That at least did not require anything special. As long as she kept thinking about that moron in her mind, he would sense it. Of course, there was a huge probability that he might not respond. After all, it had already occurred to Destiny herself that she could merely be bait for Death himself.","But at this point, she could not be too concerned with that. She would do anything to get free of the chains, or the dagger.","\"Do you recognize the observers?\" Eclipse asked, turning her gaze from Destiny to the figures in the fog. They were not really here. Instead, they were just here to witness her keep her end of the oath.","\"Probably not. The ones here... you’ve never met them before. But there was a time, long ago, when you knew the ancestors of their races,\" Eclipse said, her voice drifting off, as if she looked back in time. The Dream realm, as if responding to her thoughts, conjured up an image in the air above her, showing a Primordial wasteland.","It looked like the most devastating warzone to have ever existed - one so terrifying that its memory itself had been wiped from history. On the border-","Before the image could show more, the laws of the universe rippled and wiped the image, hiding whatever it had wanted to show. Destiny, however, understood what Eclipse was getting at.","\"It’s been two ages... you’re still hung up on that incident? You stupid spider, you should have just died back then and spared the universe your drama!\" Destiny screamed, and once again tried to force her hands up, but they failed.","She needed to pretend like she was getting angry, like she wasn’t summoning Death. It was not hard.","Eclipse, on the other hand, merely nodded, almost as if she agreed with Destiny.","\"In the aftermath of that war, and your rise to power, their ancestors made a noble sacrifice,\" Eclipse continued to speak casually, as if she had no idea at all that Destiny was trying to summon Death.","\"They knew their future was being written by a hand not their own, that their destinies had been defined by a greater, corrupted power. So they came to me, one by one, and asked me to ensure that their suffering served a greater purpose. Instead of resisting, they gave in, condemning their own races to endless, incalculable suffering, so that some good may come of it. So that the wrongs of history could be corrected.","\"In return, I swore an oath. On the day when their suffering would pay off - one the day when I held you responsible, I would summon the representatives of their races so that they could witness themselves the fruits of their sacrifice.\"","Eclipse bent down so that she was at eye level with Destiny.","\"Eclipse, I don’t know what you’re planning, but you better think carefully about the consequences of continuing to offend me,\" Destiny said gravely. \"You are strong, but that does not mean that I am weak. If you think dealing with me will be so simple, then you are sorely mistaken. You have no idea what I am truly capable of.\"","Instead of feeling threatened, Eclipse chuckled, as if she found the situation genuinely amusing.","\"Are you regretting it now?\" Eclipse asked softly. \"But it’s too late for regrets, Destiny. You should have killed me when you had the chance. After all, you know what they say: Karma’s a bitch!\"","Eclipse grabbed the handle of the dagger in Destiny’s forehead and pulled out a thin, white thread of karma. Beside herself, she summoned an Eclipsecrawler’s Sentinel and tied the thread of karma to it.","It was only then that all the other karma attached to the sentinel became visible. They were no longer threads, but countless massive red chains, each of which carried a blood-debt so thick Lex could smell the blood from where he stood.","Destiny’s expression fell as she realized what those chains were. They were the karma... of destroying a Mature realm, and the only thing separating her and the chains was one statue, and one, thin line of white karmic thread."]},{"number":2467,"title":"Chapter 2467: He broke into my house once","paragraphs":["\"Eclipse what the hell are you doing? Do you want to destroy the universe?\" Destiny roared as she looked at the thousands of red chains on the Eclipsecrawler sentinel! Thousands of chains! That meant that Eclipse had destroyed thousands of Mature realms !","How was such a thing possible? How could such a thing escape Destiny’s notice?","She looked at Eclipse horrified, unable to understand what was going on. This was far beyond just a simple scheme. This was no longer even about Destiny herself! There was something else going on, but she had no idea what.","Eclipse didn’t answer, and instead placed a hand on the Eclipsecrawler Sentinels face, caressing it as if it was an old friend. In truth, it had been. Every single member of her race had been turned into these sentinels back during the Primordial Age. As the foremost race concerning matters of karma, their race had been refined one by one, while they were alive, turning them into the perfect tools to wield karma.","Destiny herself had acquired a few, absorbing their destined mastery over the law of Tether, turning that mastery towards destiny rather than karma.","Only Eclipse herself had escaped back then. Not a single other member of her race had been born since, for their entire destiny, fate and even karma had been devoured. Of course, after Eclipse reached the pinnacle of the universe, she could have brought back her race any time she wished. But she hadn’t.","One would think that after such a history, Destiny would anticipate that Eclipse would target her, but that wasn’t true. Back during that chaotic age, there were none who were sinless, and there were many others who had provoked Eclipse even more. Heck, Eclipse had just as much reason to attack Fate as Destiny, for she too had been guilty of creating a few of those sentinels.","When Eclipse withdrew her hand, the sentinel shattered, and the red chains of karma attached to that thin thread, and found their way to Destiny. The chained woman screamed, not just because she was being infected by such intensely dangerous karma, but because the chains that were binding here had begun to shine brightly.","Originally that shine did nothing to her, but as soon as the karma was connected, Destiny felt that all the destiny she had absorbed for countless years was corrupted - as if it was tainted somehow.","She didn’t understand... until she did. Countless races had come to Eclipse. Countless races had willingly accepted sacrifice. That wasn’t so that Eclipse could use their luck to trap Bourdow - that was merely a convenient coincidence. Eclipse had, with their consent, corrupted and tainted the very destiny of their race. Moreover, she had done it in such a way that the taint would not reveal itself until it interacted with the light in these chains!","Destiny opened her mouth to scream at Eclipse, but the only thing that came out was a wild, echoing scream! She still did not understand what these chains were, nor did she know what that light was, but she couldn’t take it anymore.","\" DEATH WHAT THE HELL ARE YOU DOING ?\" Destiny managed to roar, not bothering to hide anything. Eclipse was mad - totally mad - and Destiny was beginning to feel a hint of fear at whatever she had planned.","But it was too late to stop now. The moment the karma and the chains interacted, the preparation Eclipse spent two Ages setting in motion was triggered. The Dream Arena appeared above everything.","All across the universe, across the Void, and even Abaddon, the Dream Arena appeared up in the sky. It was entirely out of reach, but its presence could be felt across the universe. Countless mortals began worshiping the arena. Countless Immortals began worshiping it too. All Dao Lords stopped and looked up at it, feeling only a sense of helplessness and weakness they had not felt since they became Dao Lords.","Within the Origin realm, Vaelgorith looked up at the Dream Arena and knew it was time. He finished the process, letting the third Dao Lord die, automatically triggering the tribulation for the Origin realm itself, letting it transition from an Immature realm to a Mature one. This had been a long time coming.","That left only the seven other beings above the Dao Lord realm, who looked up at the Arena with a solemn expression, not expecting things to have taken such a drastic turn. The moment Destiny appeared on the platform, many things were revealed, and they all learned that Eclipse was behind this all. They just hadn’t thought that a mere Dao Lord... could make them feel so oppressed.","Within the Folklore realm, Bob looked up into the sky at the Arena and wiped his tears. He didn’t know what that thing was, but he was sure that the captain was up there. All cool and impressive things inevitably involved the captain.","\"Oh lawd,\" he said with a trembling voice, barely stopping himself from crying out of sheer pride.","The enormous torrents of Dao Essence that Eclipse had gathered over so many years began to fuel the Arena, drying up at a pace that would astound any who knew about it.","Destiny would have screamed again, would have cursed or yelled at Eclipse, but she couldn’t. She finally realized what these chains were... or at least why they were so heavy, to the point where she couldn’t raise her hands at all.","The light in the chains... was the strain of the universe. Destiny was literally, with her body, tied down to the strain of the entire universe. Pure dread filled her being as she looked at Eclipse, oddly reminiscent of how Bourdow had looked at Eclipse when he had been chained up.","’What... the... hell...’","Destiny tried to think, but even her thoughts were weighed down as more and more of the universe’s strain was pressing her down. If her mind were working normally, she might have thanked Eclipse for destroying so many Mature realms and reducing the strain on the universe so much, or she might have already been killed!","Just as Eclipse was about to continue, she paused, and looked behind her. There, right at the edge of the fog, stood Death.","\"It has been a long time, Eclipse,\" Death said calmly, though he kept his distance, his gaze falling on Destiny. \"What are you doing over here, if you don’t mind me asking?\"","Lex began elbowing Cassandra again.","\"Hey, I know that guy,\" he whispered in her ear. \"He broke into my house once.\""]},{"number":2468,"title":"Chapter 2468: Archon","paragraphs":["Cassandra rolled her eyes. She may not know who the new figure was, but she recognized the Primordial Queen. Sure, she was going to believe that someone who could stand up to the Primordial Queen had really broken into Lex’s house.","Lex, meanwhile, watched whatever was happening with a relaxed demeanor. In this situation, he was either safe or screwed and there was no in between. If Eclipse won, he’d be safe. If she lost, then whoever was capable of facing her would surely kill everyone who saw their confrontation, and there was basically nothing Lex could do to stop him.","But he wasn’t too worried. Lex had a lot of faith in Eclipse.","On the Arena, Eclipse didn’t stop whatever she was doing to Destiny, but her gaze was fixed on Death.","\"Obviously, I’m using Destiny’s body to bear the strain of the universe, Death. Anyone with two eyes and a functioning brain can see that. I think the real question here is what are you doing here?\"","Death stood about as physically far as he could from Eclipse without entering the fog, which made his caution abundantly clear. It was not just Eclipse who made him cautious, but the Arena itself. Nothing like this had existed in the universe before, and he couldn’t quite risk underestimating it.","Death looked from Eclipse towards Destiny. So far, they all maintained a non-interference policy with each other. All eight of them were unable to display their full strength, which is why they could not fully gauge the strength and condition of the others.","Thus, under ordinary circumstances, Death would never confront Eclipse face to face - especially within her own Seat of Power. The circumstances weren’t ordinary, however. Death was not entirely inclined to let Eclipse complete whatever task she was working on. What if she gained a significant advantage against them?","It had to be emphasised that Destiny wasn’t the only one who had bad blood with Eclipse - so did he, and a few of the others. For that reason, letting her grow considerably stronger was not in his best interests.","\"I am here to see if we can settle things calmly,\" Death said, his eyes finally falling back on Eclipse. Despite his subtle probes and investigation, he found no weak points in the chains. He wasn’t sure how resilient they would be, but his gut told him that no simple attack could break them.","\"I can arbitrate between you two. You let her go, and I’ll ensure you’re properly compensated, and we put this matter behind us. The universe cannot afford a fight between us all right now.\"","Eclipse, to Death’s surprise, looked at him with pity in her eyes.","\"You know such a thing will not work. You’re not here to arbitrate - you’re here to see if you can fight me and possibly affect my plans during the fight. But Death, think about your actions carefully. If you cease your actions now, then we can put this matter behind us.","\"The moment you take action, however, there’s no turning back. Ask any of my ex-husbands, I know how to hold a grudge. You will regret your actions right up until you’re unable to do anything.\"","Eclipse was not mincing words today, it seemed. Death looked one more time at Destiny and weighed his options. As much as he hated to admit it, compared to the other seven who were all restricted in how much power they could reveal, Eclipse was a much greater threat. He could not let her do whatever she wanted to do.","A scythe appeared in Death’s hand and placed its long pole over his shoulder casually.","\"I don’t think such words suit you, Eclipse. Do not mistake my courtesy for weakness. Stop now, lest I remind you that at the end of the day, you are a mere Dao Lord in the presence of an Archon. You cannot fight me and hope to win.\"","Lex felt a chill crawl up his spine, not because he heard something he shouldn’t have. No, the chill came from the grin on Eclipse’s face. He had a feeling that the emotion that the grin hid... wasn’t exactly joy.","Eclipse raised her right hand and a sword appeared in it, and then she raised her left hand and a double sided axe appeared within that. Then, she raised six more hands, each one wielding a different weapon.","\"This is not the Primordial Age anymore, Avernus,\" Eclipse said as she held Death’s gaze, her entire body beginning to radiate with power she had held in for too long. \"Let alone a single Archon, I can take on all eight!\"","The fight began before Lex realized it, and it occurred in a place of existence he could not comprehend. He saw neither Eclipse move nor Death, but he felt reality fold in on itself. He sensed that, somehow, somewhere, time rippled.","The entire universe itself stalled as the strain on it increased sharply, causing Destiny to unleash another, heartwrenching scream as her body was pressed into the ground.","The fight, it seemed, had not stopped Eclipse’s plan. Or maybe it was a part of her plan to begin with.","Somewhere Lex could not sense, Eclipse and Death clashed and Death was pushed back. Not only was he pushed back, he sensed that somewhere in the universe, one of the Major realms he controlled had been destroyed.","His pupils trembled as he tried to fathom what had happened. Had Eclipse destroyed a Mature realm with a single attack that wasn’t even focused on the realm?","Before he could get another answer, she attacked again and Death realized that he could not hold back at all. The backlash from the universe be damned, if he didn’t unleash his power then he would have no chance at all.","While the two of them were fighting, another person Lex was familiar with appeared on the Arena. Nulli appeared, garbed in armor that made her appear far more regal than Lex had ever seen her.","The moment she appeared, hundreds of thousands of other portals appeared behind her. One by one, more and more Nulliths began to emerge. For the first time since the Primordial Age, the entire Nullith race had congregated all within the same period of time.","They did not talk. Instead, they began to arrange themselves around Destiny, holding hands and channeling their power into the ritual that Eclipse herself had set into motion.","Lex sensed the familiar feeling of time gathering around the Nullith - he knew it well, because so much of it was coming out of his own body."]},{"number":2469,"title":"Chapter 2469: Too difficult, even for Eclipse","paragraphs":["\"You know, Avernus, I’ve always wanted to ask you a question,\" said Eclipse as she ignored the fact that Death was unleashing his power. A black mist spread out from his body, pushing away the influence of the Dream realm and even the universe, establishing his Caelum. Of course, the mist did not spread too far before it was cut down by Eclipse’s relentless assault.","\"What the hell is up with your obsession with death anyway? Did you enter a goth phase in your childhood and just never leave it? Or do you just like acting so edgy?\"","Eclipse cut down Death’s spreading Caelum as if it was nothing, infuriating him. Death, disregarding the consequences, removed all seals on his power, finally managing to push Eclipse back a little - while also managing to keep one of his realms from being destroyed in the clash.","Considering the Dream realm was Eclipse’s Seat of Power, that was already impressive enough.","\"Watch your words woman,\" said Death, his voice far deeper and filled with his increasing wrath. But no matter how deeply he spoke, or how intimidating he tried to be, it made no difference to Eclipse at all.","\"I mean, death itself is a concept that first depends on life to even matter. Without life, death can’t even exist. So like, what, are you trying to court Life? Was that the plan?\" Eclipse asked.","Death was enraged and attacked again only to discover that Eclipse was no longer even clashing with him, but instead infecting him and his worlds with tainted karma. He clicked his tongue and began killing the karma itself as he glared at Eclipse.","\"Of course, jokes aside, I know why you’re so obsessed with death. Maybe I know about it even better than you. Would you like to see?\"","Before Death could answer, Eclipse pulled out the tip of her Enigma pillar and pulled out a black slip. The scene around them changed. In fact, Eclipse and Death too disappeared, leaving behind only a scene of a child lying at the feet of a female corpse.","The scene showed nothing else before Death exploded in anger, unleashing an air of corruption and death, eating away at the scene.","With blood red eyes Death stared at Eclipse. If she were any other Dao Lord, that look alone would have been enough to kill her.","Eclipse only smirked in response, as if she was pleased by his reaction.","\"There’s no need to glare. I warned you. I told you - stay out of my way, and it’ll be better for you. But you were too full of yourself to listen. No amount of angry glaring, scythe slashing or screaming will change that. Live - live in regret knowing that after living for so long, you finally made a mistake you cannot recover from.\"","A throne appeared behind Eclipse, just as a gravestone appeared behind Death, their clash escalating to the next level.","Atop the Dream Arena, Destiny screamed again and again, the pressure on her body ever increasing beyond anything that any of those observing could understand. With every attack, every move, every display of power conducted between Eclipse and Death, the strain on the universe escalated, and thus the strain on Destiny escalated.","The absurd thing - the thing that would have shocked Destiny if she could clear her mind from the pressure it was under - was that the strain from Death was akin to a dozen Mature realms or so, but the strain from Eclipse was nearing a hundred. How could she be ten times stronger than Death?","The answer was that she couldn’t. So the question remained... what was it about her that caused such an immense strain?","Across the universe, the remaining 6 Archons watched the clash, and watched Destiny scream, but none of them intervened. Each of them watched with different thoughts running through their minds, but only Chaos knew that Eclipse was still baiting them.","He had glimpsed a hint of her plan, and knew that this was far from the extent of her power. She was merely portraying herself as having an opening, testing the resolve and positions of the Archon to see whether they would mess with her.","He could not speak for the others, but his personal plans lay not here, but in the next Age - nay, the next Era.","Divine didn’t even open his eyes. He simply remained in his sarcophagus, playing dead. There were too many people who wanted him dead for him to mess around in something like this.","Fate simply watched from within the Void, staying far away. She had no interest in getting involved in anything and compromising what she had been doing, so she merely watched.","Oblivion, naturally, would not interfere. Back at the tea party he had already confirmed that Eclipse was not against him, which automatically meant he was not against her. Besides, with Death finally occupied, he could complete his plans involving the Origin realm without attracting any attention.","Spirit was gravely wounded, but ironically, he was the one watching with the greatest intensity. If Eclipse wounded Death sufficiently, Spirit would not give up the chance. If he could get his hands on a wounded Archon, then it would do wonders for Spirits recovery.","That left only Life. Although she did not know the details of Eclipse’s plan, they had been aligned together for a very long time already, so there was no chance of a confrontation.","That meant that as the hours passed by, no one interrupted Eclipse and Death. Yet not only did Death not gain any advantage, he discovered that Eclipse had studied him thoroughly.","She was familiar with his every move and intention, and she already had a counter for it. He could do nothing to her.","What infuriated him most of all was that he could do nothing to her realm either. By showing him a glimpse of his own past, Eclipse had managed to steal some of Death’s karma, weakening him when he faced her.","The fight could have gone on much longer, but the universe would not allow it. Finally, the strain which Destiny had been shouldering alone suddenly fell upon Death as well, suppressing his ability and nearly causing him to collapse.","Without a word or exchange of any kind, Death disappeared. He could not face Eclipse in a weakened state - that would be akin to death, and not the kind he could recover from.","Eclipse only smirked before teleporting back to the Arena, finding that everything was going as predicted - meaning that Harriot had activated his ultimate illusion so that Nulli hadn’t been able to sense the fight at all.","If Nulli knew that Eclipse was fighting Death, she would have immediately turned pink, and what would have followed would have been too difficult to control even for Eclipse."]},{"number":2470,"title":"Chapter 2470: Gratitude","paragraphs":["\"I swear on the graves of my ancestors, if I miss this because of you Erlang, I will repeatedly rob from your entire bloodline for all of eternity!\" Wu Kong cursed under his breath as he used his spear like a walking stick, trying to make his way through the fog he had discovered.","He knew there was something amazing on the other side of the fog - he just needed to get there somehow. It was just easier said than done, and with all the time he had wasted with that nincompoop Erlang, he wasn’t sure he would make it to the other side.","Meanwhile, on the other side of the fog, Lex watched with great interest as the Nullith race worked together to carry on the mysterious ritual. There was just one thing he didn’t understand.","\"Hey, you’ve experienced Nexus events before, right?\" Lex asked as he leaned close to Cassandra. \"Do they usually last this long? I thought that they lasted only for a very short period of time.\"","This time, Cassandra did not dismiss Lex. Instead, she merely nodded, and then nodded again. She had experienced Nexus events before, and they did only last a very short time. This was clearly some kind of anomaly, but it was one she could not explain.","The reason was naturally that without Destiny to arrest control of the destinies of the universe, the Nexus event could go on until naturally interrupted. Right now, with Eclipse acting, the Nexus event would go on as long as she needed.","\"Your networking ability is quite poor,\" Eclipse said to Destiny as she walked up to her. \"I was hoping for at least a couple more Archons to show up, but I guess we’ll just have to settle for Death. With him shouldering a bit of the universe’s strain for you, maybe you’ll live long enough to do your job. Just to make sure, though, I took this from Death. It’s neat, right?\"","Eclipse held up a tiny string of karma which, upon undergoing a small change from Eclipse’s power, turned into a tiny scythe.","\"I got this from your pal. It should negate your death for a while. Hopefully you’re strong enough that you won’t need it.\"","Nulli looked at Eclipse and sniffed suspiciously but before she could speak, Eclipse took a step back. If, after all this, Eclipse’s plan suffered a problem because of Nulli’s bloody nose, she didn’t know how she’d cope with that.","Eclipse clapped her hands and suddenly a number of Dao Lords appeared behind her, all of them getting into position and kneeling behind the Nullith. More and more kept appearing. At first there were hundreds, but quickly the number grew. One thousand, two thousand, three thousand...","A total of five thousand, five hundred and fifty four Dao Lords appeared all kneeling, shocking all those who watched! These were Dao Lords all from different factions, different races, different organizations, but right now they all worked for Eclipse, revealing just how deep her network went.","For the first time in history, the entire Dao Congress appeared all at once - an organization that was previously thought to only include a few Dao Lords that had grown out of the Primordial Garden.","\"Members of the surviving races, descendants of heroes whose names history has forgotten, it is time for you to witness me completing my oath,\" Eclipse said out loud, looking at all the figures in the fog. \"Before I do that, I would also like to thank you. The sacrifices of your people... have allowed me to fulfil my dreams. The Dao Congress will never forget this debt.\"","The Primordial Queen, the Dream Master, the Living Calamity then did something that stunned everyone - those watching from afar, those watching from nearby, and even her own people!","Eclipse bowed towards those in the fog. It was not a soft bow either, but a complete, ninety degree bow, as if to demonstrate her utmost gratitude.","Lex felt an unusual aura wrap around him. It made no significant impact to him or his destiny or anything like that - it was just a mark made on his very being, as if to show that he had once received a bow from Eclipse, she who had been recognized by the universe itself.","After a full ten seconds, Eclipse finally stood up straight. When she rose she wore a soft smile on her face - a kind that Lex had never seen before on her. It was as if a great burden had been lifted from her heart. No wait, that wasn’t it.","Lex narrowed his eyes, and then dismissed the idea. No it couldn’t be. That was impossible. With a sceptical expression he turned towards Cassandra to consult her once again, and then froze when he saw that even she seemed doubtful. It seemed she had noticed as well.","Eclipse turned back to Destiny and clapped her hands one more time, activating whatever ritual she had spent so much time preparing.","Suddenly, a deep and intense feeling of suffocation descended upon the entire universe, as if the universe itself had become hostile towards something. Yet try as it might, it could not locate whatever it was that it was looking for.","While the fog protected them from being affected by what they were seeing, since the entire universe was subjected to that suffocation, Lex suddenly found himself unable to move, or do anything at all really.","The sense of suffocation then began to increase drastically, as if something terrible was happening. If the Nexus event weren’t happening, the most profoundly sinful karma would have fallen upon Eclipse at that moment, or at least on Destiny who was shouldering this ritual.","Then Lex finally felt it. There was one law in particular being affected. Out of all laws in existence, out of the eight ruling laws, for as long as Lex had cultivated, there was only one law that neither he nor anyone with any sense dared to mess with. It was the law of time, and it was the most fundamental core of this universe.","The history of the universe, the continuation of all that existed, and the future that had not yet arrived all depended upon, and were connected through time.","Underneath the suffocation, Lex sensed that the law of time was not just stirring up. It was being grabbed and being manhandled the way Eclipse had manhandled Death.","<anno data-annotation-id=\"37147b1f-17ce-efaa-1fdd-58e41402573a\" data-title=\"Eclipse turned slightly and glanced at Lex. Suddenly, he could not help but remember a conversation they had when they first met. He had made a joke about how it would take someone more powerful than the universe itself to turn back time.\">Eclipse turned slightly and glanced at Lex. Suddenly, he could not help but remember a conversation they had when they first met. He had made a joke about how it would take someone more powerful than the universe itself to turn back time. 1 </anno>","The joke was meant to be that it was impossible to turn back time. After all, they had been talking about things that were impossible to do. That’s when Eclipse told him what it would actually take to turn back time, and that it would only be impossible until it was done the first time. She had told him so clearly, as if she knew just what it would take.","It would take someone to bear the entire strain of the universe upon themselves.","Lex’s pupils constricted as he seemed to realize something."]},{"number":2471,"title":"Chapter 2471: Gates of Adol","paragraphs":["The sense of suffocation that blanketed the universe, ironically, affected the stronger beings more, and the weaker beings less. The more that one could sense laws, the more they felt the absolute danger that the laws seemed to carry right now.","By now, the other six Archons also realized that Eclipse was about to do something absolutely crazy, and that they should try to stop her. No one knew what the consequences of messing with time would be. No one could afford an accident that affected the whole universe.","Unfortunately, at this point, there was no one in the universe who could stop Eclipse either. In fact, Eclipse was looking forward to them trying to stop her, because then they could share the burden of the universe’s strain.","After all, once Death unleashed his power, the universe punished him by putting a certain amount of its strain onto him. The rest was being pushed onto Destiny. If they attacked, they too would need to unleash their full strength, at which point Eclipse needed only to survive until they were punished by the universe.","By that point, the strain would be divided among all of them, making her task even more likely to succeed.","In hindsight, so much made sense. The reason Eclipse had been hiding, keeping the universe from maturing, was simply because at that point the strain would become too great, not to mention that the laws of the universe would become far more complex. It would make her attempt to turn back time even more difficult.","That also explained why she had been destroying Mature realms lately. The more realms that were destroyed, the less strain there would be left on the universe. Eclipse must have calculated exactly how much strain she needed to remove for her plan to work.","The deaths of so many Dao Lords also served a similar purpose. She could eliminate them, reduce the burden on the universe, while also eliminating the chances that her enemies could retaliate against her.","The effectiveness with which she infiltrated so many organizations and gathered such a large army, all without alerting most of them was entirely unprecedented. Not a single one of the Archons had deduced that Eclipse was behind everything happening, or what her goals were.","Truthfully, even now, all her goals may not have been revealed, and she may have countless cards waiting to be played. Thus, despite the abundantly apparent danger, not a single one of them stood out against her now. Neither did the Sage races, or even the Primal race attempt to stop her.","At this point, could they even do anything. Even Asux, the Primal Monarch, was helpless when confronting Eclipse, not to mention... Elizabeth seemed to be secretly helping Eclipse as well. What could he even do?","Thus, when Eclipse took the next step, she did so without any obstacles whatsoever.","More and more power gathered within the Arena, and the universe became even more suffocating until, finally, Eclipse took out a sundial made entirely of gold.","Lex merely looked at it and recognized that it had a subtle hint of the Timekeeper’s aura. Lex wasn’t quite sure what was happening, because the stream of time rushing out of his body and the sundial with the Timekeepers aura suggested that he was working with Eclipse.","However the fact that Nulli thought that she had killed the Timekeeper suggested otherwise. Moreover, there was something definitely off about that guy when Lex had seen him inside his forehead back then, not that he cared too much.","The massive torrent of time rushing out of Lex’s body was also rapidly increasing Lex’s insight and understanding into the law of time at a rate that was basically impossible to replicate. Besides, Eclipse probably had things covered on her end.","Eclipse connected the sundial to the ritual, and almost immediately the universe shuddered. Destiny looked up and screamed, but at this point no sound came out of her throat. It wasn’t that her throat was too sore, but that she could no longer control her body at all at that point.","Her very existence had become the pivot upon which Eclipse used her technique, with Death sharing a small amount of her burden.","Faint grains of sand rose from Destiny’s body, each one cycling through the colors of the rainbow before dissolving into the air.","Meanwhile Lex seemed to feel like the universe had stopped. It was like he was in zero gravity, except it wasn’t just gravity that seemed to have stopped working. Everything seemed to have become weightless, and for a brief time, Lex was incapable of having any thoughts at all.","Above the sundial a small, black hole appeared, connected to absolutely nothing just yet. Eclipse, slowly, cautiously, reached out to it and blanketed it in her hand while channeling a thick, highly concentrated stream of Primordial Energy into it.","Lex watched, his mind empty of all thoughts, as the Primordial energy grew the black hole larger and larger, causing various colors to finally appear within it.","The universe shuddered once more, and this time even more violently. Cracks appeared on Destiny’s body, causing more and more grains of sand to fly up into the universe. Lex could not think, but he instinctually felt like those grains of sand were healing any wounds or injuries the universe suffered at the cost of Destiny’s health.","Meanwhile, Eclipse kept growing the hole larger and larger until it became as large as a person. Within it was an abstract mix of colors, forming nothing yet hinting at the possibility of something.","Eclipse paused for a moment, as if even she needed to gather herself before what she was about to do.","Nulli turned around and glanced at her. Although she did not break off from the ritual, there was no way she was going to miss the sight of what Eclipse was about to achieve. She could watch recordings of it later, sure, but there was nothing that could replace watching it with her own eyes.","A feat that even she, as a Primordial Nullith, could not achieve, was about to be done by Eclipse.","The two friends locked eyes for a moment, as if only they could understand everything that had brought them here. While the weight of the moment could be felt by all beings immortal and above, only they knew the actual cost of turning it into a reality.","\"Today my dream... will become reality,\" Eclipse announced to no one in particular, but Nullith nodded, as if confirming it.","Eclipse took out a small, purple orb. The thing was tiny - too small to even act as a jewel on a wedding ring - yet the aura it contained was more powerful than even the Dream Arena. If the fog had not been protecting the observers, mere exposure to that orb would have killed most of them, and crippled the Dao for those that survived.","She brought the orb to the hole, and the universe seemed to come to a halt. Destiny froze, light froze, laws froze. Only Eclipse, Nulli and the hole remained unaffected. But the hole was no longer just a hole - it was a doorway to an instant long past.","*****","Though he was bleeding golden blood, and though there was a sword of silver sticking out of his chest, struck from the back, Lunareth did not waver. He slammed down with both his hands clasped together, using them as a hammer to destroy the corrupted totem!","Behind him someone screamed, and more blades found their way into his body. By now, after facing war, after facing betrayal, after facing the death of all hope, he should have been broken beyond all doubt, yet even in reality even his back did not bend.","\"You will find no salvation in the Chalice, remember that,\" said Lunareth as he channeled pure moonlight into a single javelin. \"The Well, too, is a path to corruption. The only chance left is for you to imprison all that are corrupt beyond the Gates of Adol, and turn it into an eternal prison.\"","No one seemed to be listening to his words, for they were all furiously attacking him, but that did not stop Lunareth in the slightest. He lifted his javelin, aimed it far beyond the borders of the Primal realm and at the thing known only as Entity.","It was a massive city, larger than many realms, made entirely to devour Vaelûn and everything it held, empowering only the system host within its center - a mere puppet at this point.","Despite the torrent of attacks falling down on him, he threw the javelin with his full might, distorting reality and ushering into reality new universal laws to facilitate the flight of his javelin, thus giving rise to the concept of unreasonableness.","An axe cut Lunareth’s neck before he could see the javelin land, finally causing his knees to buckle.","As his vision dimmed, and his consciousness faded, Lunareth began to hallucinate, or else how could he at this moment see the little lass Eclipse, smiling at him as she reached out."]},{"number":2472,"title":"Chapter 2472: The Queen","paragraphs":["Up until Eclipse pulled up that tiny purple orb, Lex watched everything she did, even if he could not think about anything he saw deeply. He still watched. He was still aware. Yet from the moment that orb came out, he became entirely overwhelmed.","Even with whatever awareness he had, he could not perceive more than the presence of that orb. That, alone, consumed the entire processing power he attained as a Primordial Celestial Immortal.","The fact that the universe itself seemed to freeze, and the laws appeared to stop working, did not help the situation either.","Yet when the orb connected with the black hole, even what little awareness existed ceased. Time, it seemed, had stopped. Everything came to a halt as the universe entered an extremely precarious situation - one which threatened to unravel all of reality, and destroy everything in a profound, yet extremely horrifying way.","If the past was changed whatsoever, all of reality would have to be rewritten. The universe did not have enough energy to rewrite all of reality, especially from a point so far back in the past. That was like asking an architect to change the foundation of a building after constructing a skyscraper - except this was infinitely more complicated than that.","Thus, neither Lex, nor Cassandra, nor even the likes of David and the others, were aware of what happened after that point.","They also didn’t see the massive fracture that seemed to appear in Destiny’s body as she was split diagonally, rainbow sand rising from her wounded body.","The hole that appeared, linking to a moment far in the past, and it existed merely for the tiniest possible iteration of time. The duration was so small that it bordered on non-existence, and even that consumed all the energy Eclipse had accumulated for two ages. Moreover, the strain of doing such a thing ripped Destiny’s body further, making it seem like she was made of paper.","Within the Primal realm, Death too lay on the ground, wounded beyond anything he had felt since the Primordial Age, with no hope of recovery in sight. Let alone recovery, he could not even say for sure he would survive.","His mind was blank at that moment, though deep in his being he knew that if he managed to survive this ordeal, he would need to go hide immediately. He would be weakened beyond what could be explained, and even if the other Archons didn’t take advantage of the situation, there was no way Eclipse would let him be. She had said as much already.","The Dream Arena itself seemed to have suffered a great deal of damage as well, though the time was too short for that damage to become apparent yet.","Eclipse didn’t care. As tiny as the time was, it was enough for her. It was more than enough. She had been preparing for this moment for nearly as long as it had been from the moment she looked back to.","She saw him - Lunareth Selaryn. Most living beings in the universe did not know how much of their reality had been shaped by this one Celestial. Although his Dao was that of Moonlight, ushering into reality something so beautiful, he was responsible for the birth and creation of countless concepts that were common now in the universe.","He was considered one of the first heroes to exist in history. The concept of valor itself came into existence when Valor Borne, an Elf back in the Primordial age, tried to replicate what he had learned from Lunareth.","There were countless other examples, but it did not matter. The universe had forgotten. Everyone had moved on - everyone except Eclipse.","She opened the portal back in time, using Destiny and Death to bear the strain of the universe for that one fraction of a moment, and saw how even in the midst of the most heartless betrayal, Lunareth had not given up his mission.","That the universe was safe today was as a result of his sacrifice back then. The fact that the Celestial race retained some semblance of honor was based on how they idolised Lunareth’s sacrifice that day.","The fact that Destiny... and perhaps even Fate, and a few others were able to reach the ranks of Archon may also be tied to that one instant. As much as Eclipse wanted to, she could not rob the universe of Lunareth’s death.","Too much was tied to it. Even she, as strong as she was, could not achieve such a thing, now or in the future. That didn’t mean she was ready to let Lunareth die. It just meant she needed to get creative in her approach.","Fortunately, she had all the time in the universe to prepare for this moment before this.","The instant that the portal was open, Eclipse watched Lunareth fall, watched his body begin to die, his spirit begin to fade, and his soul begin to extinguish.","She needed to let him die. More specifically, she needed to retain the direct consequences of his death, whether in terms of how people reacted to it, or in the karma that was sown, or how destiny and fate were affected, and how the laws of the universe were affected.","She needed none of that. She only needed... him. She reached out, her hand encompassed in the power of dreams, making it so that all those who were awake at that point in history could not sense her at all. Considering that back then, all beings were so innately powerful that there was no need for sleep, that included everyone.","She touched, with the tip of her middlefinger, Lunareth’s soul, and channeled into the perfect substitute. It was a clone she had made herself, studying the technique used by Life to create Eclipse’s own clone.","This substitute immediately took on all of Lunareth’s karma, all his destiny, and even his fate, effectively replacing him in every sense, while the tiniest wisp of ’life’ that was left in Lunareth in that moment was taken away from the body, completely untraceable to anyone and anything as Eclipse wrapped it in the power of dreams.","The timing was perfect. It coincided perfectly with history. Lunareth ’died’ exactly at the moment he was supposed to, and history was preserved perfectly with none the wiser that anything had changed at all.","Eclipse had set a precedent. By perfectly preserving all subsequent actions and consequences to an event, she actually changed history without any actual consequences whatsoever.","Yes, there was the tiny matter of the fact that by reaching into the past, she created karma between the past and future - a tiny error that should have been enough to cause the laws of the universe to implode, or at least rewrite themselves, ultimately changing history.","But was that also not the reason that she had spent so much time learning about and mastering karma? So that she could avoid this one, unavoidable mistake?","Thus, through means and sacrifice that none other than Nulli knew, Eclipse had perfectly preserved history without leaving any mark whatsoever. She saw with her own eyes how Lunareth ’died’. At the same time, she pulled out that one wisp of ’life’ from the past and brought it to the present.","The whole thing happened all at once. There was no room for errors or mistakes. Fortunately, there were none. Yes, many suicide warriors had tried to attack Eclipse at that time. Yes, many weaker beings and forces tried to interfere in the present to stop her, even though the most powerful did not. But she had prepared for all of that.","Thus, with her own hand, she preserved the life she had mourned the loss of for so long, and brought Lunareth back to life.","The moment the portal closed, Destiny’s body exploded. There was no other word for it - there was a massive explosion of rainbow dust, resulting in the unquestionable demise of an Archon.","The universe greedily absorbed all that rainbow dust, or at least it tried to. In the past Eclipse was restricted, but in the present, she was a Queen.","With a wave of her hand, she gathered that rainbow dust and channeled it into that single wisp of fragile life, on the verge of being extinguished. But when it was nourished by an energy so potent it ought not to exist in the universe, how could it die?","Yes, that energy would have been too much for anyone to normally absorb, but wasn’t that what Eclipse was there for? She filtered and purified it into the gentlest form of energy so that the life was preserved, and then slowly, in front of the eyes of so many witnesses, she recreated the body of Lunareth Selaryn.","The Celestial looked blankly at her while he recovered, and for a moment even he could not understand what had happened. He only sensed the foreign and unfamiliar laws of the universe, brushing up against him, while he looked down at the expectant eyes of Eclipse.","His first thought was not that he had somehow lived, but that...","\"You look tired,\" said Lunareth softly, as he lifted his hands to Eclipse’s cheeks, and saw through the most powerful Dao Lord in the universe.","She said nothing, and let him caress her, as she felt the touch she had longed for, for over two ages."]},{"number":2473,"title":"Chapter 2473: Excuse me?","paragraphs":["Romulus wiped the sweat off his brow and did his best to appear as inconspicuous as possible. He used to think he was the strongest Dao Lord in the universe, but that beautiful lady up on stage could probably kill him with one hand. It seemed he really needed to go meet with Lex and the Innkeeper as soon as possible lest he accidentally commit some faux pas.","Eclipse did not care that everyone was watching them. In fact, this tender moment between them would not last long anyway. The whole point of summoning everyone here, of fulfilling her oath to them, was to show them the return of Lunareth.","Why else had so many races accepted such a sacrifice, if not to save Lunareth? Even if that sacrifice ultimately resulted in the destruction of their race, they were willing to make it for the whole reason their races had been saved was due to Lunareth to begin with.","\"This place feels foreign. I don’t recognize the laws,\" said Lunareth finally, his gaze shifting from Eclipse to the various figures watching from within the fog. His gaze seemed to pause on Romulus for a moment before continuing.","\"It’s because you have traveled through time. A lot of time,\" explained Eclipse patiently. \"I have prepared a place for you to acclimate to the state of the universe. It’s called the Primordial Garden - it should be quite familiar to you. Your Dao, your understanding of laws, your application of power, getting used to your new body, all of it will take a lot of time as well.\"","Lunareth did not immediately respond, taking in everything as he looked around once again, this time taking in the faces of all those watching. He noticed which races were present, and got an idea of what might have happened.","Currently Lunareth was incredibly weak, with his Dao barely existing at all, which is why his thoughts weren’t running as fast as Dao Lords normally did.","\"What about-\"","Before Lunareth could continue asking, Eclipse put a finger to her lips.","\"Some things can no longer be mentioned casually. Wait till we’re in the Garden, I’ll tell you everything. But to answer your question briefly, yes, we won the war at great cost. Many people died along the way... many more were corrupted.\"","Lunareth sighed as he heard the answer, his most important concern addressed. He feared that he had been rescued because the war had gone terribly wrong, and that his help was needed.","With that concern finally gone, and with Lunareth no longer concerned about the larger affairs of the universe, he finally turned his focus solely on Eclipse.","\"You should have moved on,\" he said softly. \"You must have suffered so much for this.\"","Eclipse smirked, as if she was anticipating Lunareth’s reaction to what she was about to say.","\"I tried. I got married eight times - twice to the same guy. Didn’t work out.\"","Lunareth, who had been looking at Eclipse with such care, suddenly widened his eyes in shock, causing Eclipse to burst out in laughter. Even Lex could not help but grin, though of course he dared not laugh at the future Mr. Eclipse. It was at that moment Lex realized that he didn’t even know if Eclipse had a last name, not that it mattered.","\"But no matter what I did, I couldn’t forget you,\" said Eclipse as she took a single step back and took a look at Lunareth in whole. \"Don’t rest your laurels just yet. Just because we won the war back then doesn’t mean that the problems have been solved. There’s a whole lot left for you to do as well.","\"To say nothing of anything else, we still need to deal with the repercussions of bringing you back from time, not to mention to ensure that no one else can mess with time. The list of things I have for you to do is very large - don’t think you can get out of doing work by being cute.\"","Lunareth smiled and could not help but laugh. His adaptability was quite strong. Mere moments ago - at least for him - he had been betrayed for reasons he did not understand. He had been stabbed in the back, and effectively killed.","Yet how could he dwell on that when he could see hints of what Eclipse had been through to rescue him. At the time he was supposed to have been killed, Eclipse was quite weak. She was nowhere near being one of the strongest, so he could only imagine everything she had been through to achieve what she had done.","Even the pain of being betrayed was overshadowed by the feeling of understanding what she had done for him.","\"Ah little lass, to think, after all this time, you have not changed,\" Lunareth could not help but say, and then froze. No, wait, that wasn’t right. Compared to him, compared to the life he had lived, she was not so little anymore.","Before he could dwell on that, Eclipse turned her gaze towards the fog.","\"Be serious, Lunareth. We have things to do. The figures you see before you are the descendants of those who have sacrificed much for your return. It is not I alone who have brought you back.\"","Lunareth’s expression turned solemn. He was having trouble wielding his power, but he could see hints about any of the races he saw. For example, the humans no longer seemed as glorious as they once were, and that Qilin didn’t seem right either.","\"There will be time to address them all later,\" Eclipse said before Lunareth could even consider saying something to them. \"For now, we have things we need to do. We are on the clock.\"","In truth, one of the reasons Eclipse did not want Lunareth to speak was because he knew secrets, but he did not yet understand they were secrets. Not everything could be revealed so casually. Even she, while gossiping, knew when to draw the lines.","Lunareth nodded, though he still wanted to express his gratitude.","\"Thank you, all, for what you have done. I will not forget it,\" he said as he committed each face to memory, and found that there was no real consequence of doing so. How strange.","Eclipse was about to dismiss the fog, for there were genuinely a lot of very important things that they still needed to do, and needed to do urgently. She was interrupted, however, in a very unexpected manner.","\"Excuse me,\" yelled out Lex as he waved his hand in the air. \"Before you send us away, could I talk to you for a moment?\"","Cassandra did her best to keep herself from facepalming, and David looked at Lex as if he was very impressed. Romulus, meanwhile, decided in that instant that he was going to latch on to Lex and the Innkeeper no matter what."]},{"number":2474,"title":"Chapter 2474: Missing work without leave","paragraphs":["It was a solemn affair. An Archon had been crushed to death. Even though none of those observing from the fog had any real context for how powerful an Archon was, it was obvious at sight that she had not been an ordinary person. The very fact that each grain of sand that emerged from her body felt more powerful than most Dao Lords was a clear indication of just how powerful she had been.","Beyond that, Eclipse had achieved the impossible. She had brought back the dead by opening a portal into the past. There were, no doubt, countless complexities involved in the process beyond what those in the fog could see.","Heck, the very fact that the portal to the past had been shut, but the Nullith continued to work on the ritual clearly indicated that things were far from over, or nearly as simple as they appeared.","Although most had no context for the oath Eclipse mentioned, for it was so long ago that no record of it had been kept, the mere fact that she mentioned it was enough. That she honored that oath was extremely noble. The fact that she valued this man... meant that he must be extremely honorable.","After all, though Eclipse had a history of her own, and that history was not always pleasant, she had always adhered to her principles, which made her incredibly well looked upon - even if most were too frightened of her to show it.","She was the Primordial Queen, strongest in the universe, vanquishers of Archons, and the author who rewrote history. Who dared to talk to her so casually?","Lex, apparently.","Lunareth looked at the human with incredible surprise, seeing how casual he was in his request. It was clear that he must have some history with Eclipse, which made Luanreth even more curious about the human.","\"Who’s that?\" Lunareth asked Eclipse as he assessed the human. He was quite decently strong, even by the standards of the Primordial Age. Going by the traditions of the human race from back then, he must have sired a large and noble cultivation family by now, and would be a respectable patriarch. To be able to behave so casually despite such heavy responsibility demonstrated the strength of his character and inner self.","\"The son of a friend, although I like chatting with him myself from time to time,\" Eclipse told him. \"He has a knack for being a nuisance to others which is very entertaining to watch, but when he starts being a nuisance to you it’s a sign that the conversation should end soon.\"","Lunareth nodded.","\"Yes, friend. How can we help you?\" he asked the human, wondering about Lex’s parent. To be qualified to become Eclipse’s friend, he must have a very interesting personality himself.","\"I realize you probably have a lot that you need to do, and I don’t mean to take up your time, but I was wondering if I could ask for a small favor since I’m already here. You know, considering your expertise in karma, and the Dream realms extensive reach.\"","Eclipse raised an eyebrow as she listened to the request, and could not believe that the first thing she was going to do after reviving Lunareth... was this . Never in a million, trillion years could she have foreseen it. But it was exactly for that reason that it was also perfect.","*****","\"You!\"","Bang!","\"Shouldn’t!\"","Bang!","\"Have!\"","Bang!","\"Spoiled!\"","Bang!","\"The!\"","Bang!","\"Ending!\" Z roared as he smashed down the rock one more time, finally killing the jackal that had been acting as his prison guard.","Upon seeing that the task was done, Z allowed himself to fall down and rest, his body covered in blood and wounds from the fight he had just been through.","\"I can’t believe you did it,\" whispered one of the slaves who was a part of Z’s slave legion. They had been sold alongside Z, which is why they were altogether. For months they had suffered, thinking that they had no future, all the while Z was silently and quietly training.","Although his primary purpose in this prison was to translate the legacy of King Zarek, that did not stop him from using it for himself. His captors didn’t stop him because that would only make Z a better fighter for them.","But now, today, Z had finally managed to break free of his imprisonment and kill all his guards. Considering that most of them were peak Heaven Immortals, with one Celestial Immortal meant that he should have had no way of defeating them, but he did it.","The fact that they had spoiled the ending for one of his favorite shows may have had something to do with it - he honestly didn’t know, he had blacked out during the process.","\"Yeah, it’s about time,\" said Z as he picked himself up and began unlocking the rest of the legion. \"If my boss was here, he’d probably give me a very low evaluation in performance. Kidnapped for so long and I barely managed to free myself.\"","The other slaves looked at him dumbstruck, unsure how to respond to that.","\"Don’t be ridiculous. No one could have done any better than you. But the task is not over. You may have defeated the guards, but we still need to escape this realm, or else we’ll end up right back here, and in worse conditions.\"","Z nodded, and began coming up with a plan as he freed everyone. Using some tricks he’d picked up, he began healing the slave legion before connecting them altogether so that the entire force of the complete legion could be utilized by him. There was no other way of escaping.","Z took a deep, long break before kicking down the door to his prison, ready to face an immediate retaliation.","What he saw, instead, was Lex sitting on a pile of corpses waiting for him, with two unknown figures standing behind him.","\"You’ve been missing work without leave,\" said Lex, looking very upset as he looked down at Z.","Lunareth, from behind him, opened up a dictionary given to him by Eclipse and looked up the concept of a ’leave’."]},{"number":2475,"title":"Chapter 2475: Should have killed me when you had the chance III","paragraphs":["Convincing Eclipse to help out had been a whole lot easier than Lex expected. He naturally had Mathew, the ’Grand Conqueror’s’ karma recorded on hand, so he thought he’d just show it to Eclipse and she could point him in the right direction. He could not have anticipated that not only would she help him, she’d escort him personally to the location where Z was being held.","He was being held by some kind of cult dedicated to the revival and glory of humanity who believed that humanity was, in fact, the most superior race and so on and so forth. Lex did not believe for one moment that these were the true people who had managed to buy Z from Mathew.","It made no sense. They were strong, yes, but not nearly remarkable enough to hide from Lex’s own senses. There was clearly some deeper ploy, but now was not the time to dwell on that for one very good reason.","Eclipse had not just a projection or clone alongside Lex. No, she had emerged from the Dream realm with her main, actual body. There had been no major reaction just yet, but Lex understood what the action signified. She was ready to allow the universe to progress.","She was either holding back from triggering it immediately due to proximity to Lex, or perhaps the process had already silently begun. It wasn’t necessary that everything needed to happen with a bang.","After Lex killed all the cult members - and he did not hesitate to spare a single one since they had gone as far as kidnapping Z and making use of him - the trio waited for Z to finish his own fight. Lex could go help, but since he had already started the fight, it would be too anticlimactic if Lex didn’t even let him vent his emotions. That untimely spoiler seemed to hurt him more than his time as a slave.","\"So now that I’ve brought you here, I have a question I want to ask you,\" said Eclipse as she looked at Lex, sitting atop a pile of corpses, getting ready to pose in front of Z. \"Finding this place wasn’t so hard. Why didn’t the Innkeeper just bring you here? Or better yet, why didn’t he just rescue his worker himself?\"","The question did not alarm Lex, nor did it take him by surprise. He didn’t even need to come up with a convenient lie, because he merely needed to answer truthfully.","\"The Innkeeper is... a protector of the Inn,\" Lex answered slowly as he thought about all those that depended on the protection of the Innkeeper. \"He is a positive force, an encouraging personality. The day he is forced to drop that role, that identity, the day he is forced to transition from a protector to an avenger, the universe may never be the same. That warm, calm smile is something he must never lose. As much as all the workers of the Inn are protected by the Innkeeper, we in turn wish to protect the Innkeeper from the day he is forced to replace that smile.\"","Lex’s reasons for wanting to protect the Innkeeper from facing such a reality were complex, but he hadn’t lied in the fact that this was how most of the Inn workers genuinely felt.","Lunareth put down his dictionary and looked at Lex for a moment, absorbing what he heard about this Innkeeper. He was intrigued, and would love to meet him one day.","Eclipse did not push further. She was not like what Lex had seen her in the Primordial Garden. Her powers were no longer suppressed, so she could see that the power keeping others from peering into Lex’s mind came solely from Nuwa, and not from the Innkeeper at all.","She had some thoughts on the matter, but did not pry or comment. Instead, she gave Lex a piece of paper with all the listed mental weaknesses he had that she had discovered. If he did not address them, they would definitely become Heart Demons during his next major tribulation.","Chief among them was Lex’s attachment issues. No one extremely close to him had ever died. They had suffered, yes, but they had not died. Even so, Lex’s emotions became extreme every time he dealt with their perceived suffering. Unless he managed to reign in his extreme emotions, they would come back to haunt him sooner or later.","There were also a few other items on that list. Finding out he had so many weaknesses put him in a bad mood, but before he could go through the rest of the list, or come up with countermeasures, Z emerged.","\"You’ve been missing work without leave,\" said Lex, venting his negative emotions towards Z, causing him to freeze and his comrades behind him to freeze.","But Lex did not let the mood linger, immediately smiling as he jumped off the corpses and came to inspect Z.","\"I’m kidding. You did a good job surviving despite the difficulties you faced. Let’s go home - you’ve earned yourself a proper break. Naturally, your friends can come along if they wish to as well.\"","Z shivered. The sound of Lex praising him caused Z to shiver as he felt like something was terribly wrong, and that Lex was trying to lure him into an even more desperate situation, like the time he made him manager for the Gamer’s Den!","Before they could continue the conversation, however, Eclipse intervened.","\"While we’re on the topic of heading back home, you should probably call back all the Inn workers and everyone else you know back to the Midnight Inn. The universe is going to be a very unsafe place for the next few centuries, and as admirable Brenda is with her shenanigans, I don’t think she’s cut out for intense survival circumstances.\"","Lex froze. Z froze. They both locked eyes, realizing that compared to the two of them... perhaps poor Piere had a tougher time.","But Eclipses’ words reminded Lex that there were still many out there he had been trying to reach or contact.","Chief among them were Liz and Fenrir, but that also included Belle, Brenda, as well as Alexander and the others. The problem was... they all weren’t so easy to locate.","*****","Death pushed himself up off the ground, a deep, intense hate boiling in his eyes.","\"You should have killed me when you had the chance, Primordial bitch, because I’m going to make you regret leaving me alive,\" he said through gritted teeth. He was no longer inside the Primal realm - he had already retreated to his most hidden and secure hideout to recover from his injuries.","Unfortunately for him, it wasn’t as secret as he had assumed.","\"Do you really think that the Primordial Queen would make such a basic mistake?\" asked a familiar voice, sending a chill down Death’s spine. He looked up into the darkness and discovered that he recognized the face.","\"You? How can it be you?\"","Whether he got the question to his answer or not was entirely unknown, for above the building where Death hid, the Enigma Pillar revolved silently, shrouding in secret whatever happened within."]},{"number":2476,"title":"Chapter 2476: Not the kind of danger you expect","paragraphs":["Lex was bonded with Fenrir, allowing him to pull his wolf back from across realms. That was not all. In fact, Lex and Fenrir both benefited from each other’s strengths, providing each other feedback based on their own strengths. It was just that Lex was so much stronger than Fenrir, that his feedback to Fenrir was more pronounced than the other way around.","Lex didn’t mind. Fenrir, to begin with, was originally meant to be a protector of the Midnight Inn. It was just that he was generally too weak to adopt that role in most high stakes situations. But sooner or later, he’d rise up to that role, Lex was sure of it.","There was just one problem. Since before Lex had been attacked by Daekol, Fenrir had been baited away, and had gotten lost somewhere in the Dream realm. Now, he was no longer there.","Lex couldn’t well ask Eclipse to help him with every minor matter - even he wasn’t that shameless. The problem was that every time he tried to summon Fenrir, he could feel Fenrir resisting the call, as if he was caught up in something important.","Then there was the matter of Liz. She was pretty easy to find - as it turned out she was within one of the cities in the Dream realm run by Eclipse. As for others...","Lex glanced towards Z. It would be too much to put him back to work immediately, but a minor task couldn’t hurt.","\"Z, I want you to go back to the Midnight Inn immediately. You can take your friends if you want. Once there, I want you to tell Velma to redeploy the Dream tavern and use it to call back all members of the Midnight Inn still within the Dream realm.","\"Let everyone know that it is extremely important that everyone urgently return to the Midnight Inn for safety. There are a few people I’ll need to go and bring back personally, so I’ll join you all shortly.\"","Movement in and out of the Inn was still restricted for all others except through taverns. Lex felt like now, he could finally completely take control over the Inns teleportation capabilities regardless of anything else, but he didn’t have the time to get into that. The system had too many notifications he needed to deal with, and he’d get to the teleportation issue once things calmed down.","As for his current predicament, fortunately, with Eclipse right beside him, it wouldn’t be difficult to send Z and the rest to the Origin realm from where they could return to the Midnight Inn.","As for how Lex would go about rescuing everyone... he hadn’t quite figured that out yet. He would need to forcibly recall Fenrir to the Inn, and Liz he’d grab on the way. Belle though...","Lex could sense her clearly now. But traveling without being sent by the Inn, and without devils was tough.","Lex resisted the urge to sigh. Why was it that no matter how strong he became, his problems elevated with him? How nice would it be if occasionally his problems stayed at easier levels?","\"How much time do you think I have before it becomes dangerous to stay out of the Inn?\" he asked Eclipse.","\"It’s already dangerous, but I think you’re misunderstanding where the danger is coming from,\" said Lunareth who glanced at Lex and found it so amusing that such a weak little creature could be so at ease while talking to Eclipse. Had one of his descendants already achieved the Dao? Only with such an achievement under his belt could a mere immortal maintain such a stable bearing in front of two Dao Lords.","\"The danger is not the typical one of bandits or marauders, or of Vaelûn spontaneously manifesting a heinous fiend in your path. You don’t even need to fear that one of the laws you’ve been using will suddenly rupture and be eradicated from the framework of the universe, leaving you injured and permanently scarred.","\"No, the dangers abound in the universe are all uniquely singular in nature. Vaelûn is maturing, transitioning from an immature period to a mature one. During this time, mature and relatively mature realms are the safest places to be, for anything and everything even relatively unstable can be utilized by the universe in the process.","\"For example, what if Vaelûn decided that you perfectly personify the law of humanity, and decide to turn you into a law? Doing so might help it transition into a mature state. At that point, you can neither resist Vaelûn, nor escape your fate. You’ll be dead - or alive in the form of a law that can do nothing but act as it is meant to - and no one will be able to do anything about it.","\"Athough what I said is merely an example, that is the kind of thing that can actually happen. So during the transition period, it’s best to stay inside a safe place. No one can predict when you may become a part of the universe’s foundation. Of course, if you have a Dao Lord escorting you throughout, you may be able to avoid such a danger, but Dao Lords themselves have to face a different kind of threat during this period. So, whether anyone likes it or not, the universe is finally going to see some peace.\"","Eclipse could not manage to hide her smile. Lunareths Dao was currently almost in a dormant state, so he wasn’t as in tune with the universe as he normally would be. So, while he got the gist of the issue right, he still made some minor mistakes.","\"Not a single law has ruptured since the end of the Primordial Age,\" Eclipse told Lunareth, resisting the urge to chuckle. \"But yes, theoretically, that could still happen right up until the universe matures. You don’t need to worry because even though your Midnight Realm is not fully mature, I’m sure that the Innkeeper has taken precautions to prevent it from being used up by the universe.\"","Lex gulped, and smiled weakly."]},{"number":2477,"title":"Chapter 2477: Hidden amidst the chaos","paragraphs":["Lex immediately scrapped all his plans. Finding Belle, saving Fenrir, rescuing Giselle, going on a date...","None of that was on the immediate agenda anymore because his first priority was ensuring that the Midnight realm didn’t get swallowed up by the universe. Fortunately, his real body was still inside the Midnight Inn so he wouldn’t need to waste any time moving.","The fact that his Primordial aura had empowered his projection to not only be able to talk, but fight and kill everyone who had captured Z was quite convenient. In truth, the fact that he could kill them all with his projection alone was another reason Lex was sure that there was some kind of conspiracy afoot.","He would also check out Z’s body and soul once he returned to the Inn to be safe. But before any of that, he had to make sure that the realm could survive.","\"I’ll be closing the Primordial Garden off for a few centuries,\" said Eclipse as she looked at Lex. \"I’ll be looking forward to your progress in the meantime. Just so you know, once the universe matures, reaching the Dao Lord realm with a Minor Dao will become much easier. Anything beyond that... will become much harder.\"","She and Lunareth waved at Lex before they disappeared, taking Z and the others with them. Lex, meanwhile, processed what she had just told him. He wouldn’t be seeing Eclipse again for at least a few centuries, which was a shame. As for the stuff about becoming a Dao Lord, Lex wasn’t bothered by it in the slightest. When had anything been easy for him? Besides gaining weight, of course.","Lex’s projection disappeared. Meanwhile, within the Dream realm, somewhere in the dense fog that was now empty, Wu Kong frowned as he looked ahead and found nothing but fog. He then looked behind, and saw only fog. He was lost.","Dammit, Wu Kong swore to dedicate the next ten Dao cycles to making Erlang’s life miserable once he was out of here!","What he had not realized was that Eclipse had long dismissed the fog from her realm, and thus Wu Kong as well. He was no longer inside the Dream realm. What exactly his location was, no one could say for sure.","Romulus, meanwhile, had no idea where he was or where he should go. He could track certain fortunes to find enemies or friends, but he was no longer certain about the state of the universe. The feedback he was getting from the universe was strange and unlike anything he had anticipated, which revealed that the universe had begun its maturing process.","During this time, it would be best to lay low and establish himself. To do that, he wanted to find the Innkeeper, but that was easier said than done. Fortunately, by now, the name of the Midnight Inn had become relatively well known across the universe, so it didn’t take him long to find out how he could reach it. He needed to find the Henali first.","Within Arch-Heaven, there were even more changes taking place. Many new ministries had appeared, among which was also the Ministry of Dreams. As it happened every single one of its members was also a member of the Dao Congress.","Vox, the half Laoer, half Jorlam Dao Lord who had helped Lex out, also gained a massive promotion, going from being a minister to being a Royal Chancellor!","Mango, too, seemed to get some kind of promotion, though he couldn’t be bothered to care about it. He also didn’t care about the fact that his limiter percentage had somehow shot through the roof!","But they were not the only ones inside Arch-Heaven. Serene and Leon Williams had long been hiding inside Arch-Heaven, yet something strange was happening to them. Ever since they saw the phenomenon of the massive warrior striking at Lex, they had entered some kind of trance.","Sometimes, hints of lucidity would flash through their eyes, but most of the time they appeared to be in a daze, as if some kind of internal battle was being fought within both their minds.","What was most strange was that neither of them were ordinary. Leon’s sword intent was unknown because he never fought and never stood out, but it was certainly one of the best among his realm across the universe. Meanwhile, Serene held some kind of secret heritage that allowed her to alter talents of those yet to be born.","Yet no defensive or protective measure was triggered during this strange event, as if there was nothing wrong at all - or that whatever was wrong could not be detected.","Elsewhere in the universe, in what was meant to be a battlefield between dragons and phoenixes - a bitter, broken land containing only death and destruction, there was a hidden temple. Within that temple, a golden dragon and a white phoenix worked together, using their own blood to nourish a single egg. All around the egg grew Helix Petal Roses - the same kind that had been used to create Lex’s physique.","Hidden amidst the chaos of the universe, many powerful races and beings were secretly preparing for the new coming era, and leaving behind what would inevitably be called the Age of Dreams.","Among those powerful races, there was also a weak race of fairies. Tinker had found a tool linked to karma and the moon, and discovered a hint that Eclipse had purposefully left behind to see if anyone would find out.","While she did not uncover the mystery, she did use that mirror to pledge fealty to the moon, and thus Lunareth. As such, when he returned, the fairy race officially broke off from the Humanoid Alliance, and became vassals of the moon. Though their curse was not lifted, since Destiny was not the one who placed the curse on them, they discovered that the chains of destiny no longer bound them as tightly as before.","They had lit the sparks that would, hopefully, one day turn into the roaring flame of fairy glory.","All of this, and more, Nuwa saw from within her chamber, but she did not react at all. She no longer placed her faith in entire races. Instead, she had chosen to invest in individuals. Wu Kong was one example. Lex was another example. There were many more as well, all hidden.","Perhaps it was now time... to start revealing her own hand, and set her plans in motion.","Slowly, Nuwa stood up from her throne, and walked into a certain chamber with her temple, each step causing her momentum to rise.","Just as her momentum reached its zenith, Nuwa opened her walk-in closet the size of a realm and began the most important task of all: deciding her fit for her return!"]},{"number":2478,"title":"Chapter 2478: Forbidden History I","paragraphs":["\"Twinkle, twinkle, little star, how I wonder why you’re free and I’m not,\" said Bastet as she lay on the ground looking up at the countless stars within the sky above her. Beside her, Falak merely glanced at his mistress but did not comment.","The fact that she had been asleep for over a hundred and fifty years, and then just lay where she sat for another fifty years after waking up may have held the reason for why she wasn’t free! The answer was that she was just too lazy to pursue it!","The two of them would probably spend the next few centuries sitting on this hill, not doing anything at all. He didn’t mind. He had long learned a technique to put himself in stasis, allowing him to not feel the passage of time. How else was he supposed to survive? Even Demi-Dao Lords could get bored!","Just as Falak was about to enter stasis once again, a Henali guard came to call them.","\"The Governor is summoning you. It is a little urgent, please make your way to him immediately,\" he said politely.","In truth, Bastet and Falak were political prisoners, but they’d been given a lot of freedom. At least they weren’t deprived of energy like they were back on Earth.","Falak immediately adopted his original form - that of a bull - so that his lazy mistress could sit upon his back and be carried to their destination.","Thus, a black cat and a white bull followed their guard all the way to the Governor’s mansion.","Within, they found that the mansion was not empty. In fact, the governor had summoned many other Demi-Dao Lords as well.","Falak immediately noticed what they all had in common, though. They all were born in the earliest days of the Origin realm. Heck, two of them were even surviving Mythical beings born at the creation of the Origin realm - specifically, the Golden Dragon Vaelgorith, and the Holy Doe, Aurelia.","\"It seems everyone is here,\" said Hiran with a pleased smile as he looked at the group. The Origin realm was in the middle of its tribulation, but it would surely succeed. What they had to do now was take advantage of this opportunity to finally begin working on the true reason that the Henali had conquered the Origin realm so long ago.","\"Bastet, how have you been?\" asked Aurelia, her voice sweet and gentle, causing any who heard to feel utterly relaxed and at ease - anyone besides Bastet!","\"Imprisoned,\" Bastet responded lamely. \"First by my father, and then by the Henali. Sometimes I thank the stars that my mother was more of a concept rather than an actual being, otherwise I assume she would have imprisoned me too.\"","Instead of being surprised by Bastet’s reaction, Aurelia chuckled softly.","\"It is good to see that you haven’t changed. There are so few left who can cause me to reminisce about the good old days.\"","Bastet looked at the Holy Doe - basically a doe with a white, glowing light all around her - with a strange look.","\"You call that the good old days? Do you remember what happened to Ophelia?\"","Aurelia shook her head, as if disregarding what Bastet said. She no longer mourned the losses of days so long passed - it was pointless.","\"Everyone, please, pay attention,\" said Hiran as he clapped his hands. \"I have just been informed by the Divine Ruler. The maturing process of the universe will last anywhere between five hundred years to a thousand years. That is a very small window in which we must operate.","\"If we can successfully gain control of the Glatictus Necropolis, and carry out our plan, the Origin realm may become the one and only realm across the universe where true, genuine reincarnation may become a possibility. Yes, that’s right! Life after death may become a possibility within the Origin realm!\"","It seemed none in the room shared the same enthusiasm as Hiran - perhaps because they didn’t believe as strongly as he that they could succeed. Hiran smirked, as if predicting that they would react like this.","\"You all don’t believe it because you’ve been hearing stories about reincarnation for billions of years. Time and time again, various forces have tried to discover what makes the Origin realm unique, but have been unable to discover it - and you yourselves may have searched as well.","\"You all probably feel it better than anyone else. The Origin realm is not normal. There is something different about this place. It has something to do with Glatictus Necropolis, you’ve all figured out that much, but you don’t know what exactly. Well, today, I am going to tell you all at last.\"","All the Demi-Dao Lords paid attention, if for no other reason than to finally understand why the Henali had been after the Origin realm for so long. They had faced no shortage of opposition in the process - they knew that better than anyone else.","The number of wars fought over control rights of the Origin realm were not few. The actual natives of the realm had long accepted that they could never take control of it, and thus they had all allied themselves with the Henali who treated them fairly.","\"Long ago - long before the Origin realm even existed, and long before the Age of Dreams even began, there was a war,\" said Hiran as he chose his words carefully. Some things could not be revealed, but certain things needed to be explained. In truth, Hiran himself did not know much. All he knew was what the Divine Ruler had told him.","\"Vaelûn, our universe, was invaded by another, dying universe known as Pentagal. Or, to be specific, certain forces within Vaelûn summoned Pentagal in the hopes of devouring it and speeding up the growth process for Vaelûn. Little did they know, their actions caused the growth of Vaelûn to slow down tremendously.","\"Regardless, that doesn’t matter. Pentagal was dying anyway, and it was eventually destroyed. Vaelûn devoured much of Pentagal, but ultimately it was a new universe and could not completely process it properly, resulting in various remnants of Pentagal to be left in the universe - various treasures, laws and artifacts that do not belong to our universe, but to a universe that had already previously entered maturity.\"","There was a fire in Hiran’s eyes as he spoke, and enthusiasm and excitement rolled off him in waves. In fact, even the Demi-Dao Lords who were listening could not help but get infected by his excitement as their minds raced to understand the implications. Did that mean that the artifacts of Pentagal contained fully formed, fully matured laws?"]}]);
